</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"9d2df459-cb87-4225-83b3-d216b5ba9d8e" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-PerformanceConsiderations">Performance Considerations</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"3bbd14f1-79b8-4f04-8614-f858e1e19f98">
<li local-id=3D"583d552f-367a-4a33-958f-70b4de07a097">
<p local-id=3D"45e33a2b-1281-4345-afc6-1a7a81985c68">Enhanced initial flowa=
bility</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"64bacadf-b8f1-4f1a-869a-98f3f52a31c7">
<p local-id=3D"8fea2053-a77f-4d91-965f-5ae2f01ec0cd">Careful monitoring of =
water resistance</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d734b133-8ff5-4cca-925c-2e4f6349e485">
<p local-id=3D"f64885ff-2748-4705-8499-6f8ac997f5ae">Potential subtle chang=
es in green body properties</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2e1c0887-6a44-448b-9ad6-071f0cfc53ef">
<p local-id=3D"d19c8f01-fec2-4a5c-865b-7fd3acb27bad">Thermal debinding perf=
ormance</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"2b917646-ad52-43ae-8db2-ae2fc6f5d3b2"><strong>Caution</stron=
g>: Contains reactive chemicals. Use appropriate personal protective equipm=
ent.</p>
<p local-id=3D"31865448-6730-42a8-8ee6-2c3a735ab082"></p>
<p local-id=3D"4a41d83d-5b92-459e-82f7-2a5b739b4559">2025-03-26</p>
<p local-id=3D"7db3e31a-30ff-4232-ba5c-0043621bb842">PXL: Received Unit 5 b=
ack from Bodycote. It only leaks in one spot, but more leaks may be opened =
after machining.</p>
<p local-id=3D"259d22a0-a8a2-4215-9d65-6f2e4857ff6d">HOPPER: Working on ins=
talling HOPPER V3.4 in PILOT 2. Ben removed the mist box and heater to clea=
r up some space for installing the hopper without being space constrained.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"181d9baf-16dd-49d8-ad7a-3637f4a84dfb"></p>
<p local-id=3D"202223a8-8918-4bb4-87ee-4f81d75448e7">2025-03-27</p>
<p local-id=3D"b7e3ad30-af80-4613-a9ad-82697979317b">PXL:</p>
<p local-id=3D"a53dfa3c-55d6-4934-a44c-b3e7bba3c83f">Electron beam welding =
meeting w/ Matt Wade at Electron Beam Engineering. The combination of braze=
 filler material and electroless nickel plating is likely to cause cracking=
. Even welding it without BFM would be unlikely to succeed. Starting and st=
opping a weld can cause cracking so it is beneficial to weld around the ent=
ire cell in one shot and do a power taper off as ending the weld. They regu=
larly weld assemblies that are then brazed later. The corners of parts butt=
ing together should be as sharp as possible, burrs can even be beneficial a=
s they act like filler material.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2b86dab3-5a76-4f35-ab31-1e67cc874348">Meeting with AEM. Crai=
g is interested in EBW. They tried soldering stainless steel to copper and =
had difficulty getting the solder to wet to the stainless. They did some re=
search that suggests that solder joints between stainless steel tend to be =
weak.</p>
<p local-id=3D"177a606f-faf4-420a-8e58-2bd6c7d92990">HOPPER: Assembled and =
installed in PILOT 2.</p>
<p local-id=3D"164dc8a6-34e4-43c8-b392-ed48d71229b9"></p>
<p local-id=3D"46875bfa-bf75-428e-8568-7fd88284dc69">2025-03-31</p>
<p local-id=3D"183db063-82da-42f2-bca8-7fcdef86f97f">HOPPER: Working on des=
ign of benchtop testbed for HOPPER/spreader technologies that would enable =
motion in one axis with total access to the HOPPER and spreader from the to=
p, bottom, and sides. Working on integrating a sealed solenoid into the HOP=
PER 3.4 design to act as a tapping mechanism.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4b194a46-0c48-42a9-a642-bb79f5322449">PXL: Meeting on next s=
teps for the various PXL assemblies. Removed as much epoxy as possible from=
 Unit 3 in preparation for a debind cycle that is being run tonight in one =
of the CM (hydrogen) furnaces. The nominal plan is to BAg-7 braze the leak =
points and install a new copper part in the pocket whose copper part Craig =
removed.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c509a418-9e83-4bd0-b160-d8e2570d5431">REDRESS: The powder fo=
rmulation tried over the weekend made brittle green parts that were not wat=
erproof. I made a new batch of 500g of powder with the last of the PMMA and=
 added back the plasticizer. I am also trying to make a batch of binder usi=
ng amorphous polypropylene by dissolving stearic acid and amorphous polypro=
pylene granules in ethyl acetate. N-heptane would work better, but we are c=
urrently out of it. The polypropylene granules are very slow to dissolve in=
 ethyl acetate, so I have increased the mixing plate temperature to 50C.</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"4f89f88b-a564-46ee-ac60-6772e3f4a5bb"></p>
<p local-id=3D"eb3335c4-a8f0-4e49-83b5-ca7596d097bb">2025-04-01</p>
<p local-id=3D"c4ba129d-ab11-4572-8810-c6de42ebea37">HOPPER: I am working o=
n modifying the HOPPER V3 design to fit through the opening in the PILOT ba=
se plate and to have a larger dispense line of 140mm (5.512=E2=80=9D, I wen=
t with 140mm for the sake of clean metric dimensions). This entails a redes=
ign of all components, so technically I should=E2=80=99ve increased the ver=
sion to V4. The hopper version has been incremented to V3.5 to mark the new=
 design as being distinct.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b7d7b538-aa21-4acd-855a-ae785539a06d">PXL: Removed Unit 3 fr=
om F2. The cleaned grooves seemed similar to the way they had appeared befo=
re the cycle. The only noticeable change to the plate was that the copper a=
ppeared to be less oxidized. Whoever removed the plate from the pressure te=
st fixture last failed to remove the o-rings, so they were decomposed and s=
ome pieces of the large o-ring fell off at several locations around the fur=
nace heat bricks as I was removing the plate. The o-rings held their shape =
but had turned gray and broke apart into dust when force was applied. I use=
d compressed air to remove the remaining o-rings and o-ring fragments befor=
e preparing the top surface for brazing. I cleaned out the two grooves and =
the empty pocket with acetone and a stainless steel wire wheel in the rotar=
y tool in the heavy R&amp;D lab. I applied BAg-7 paste to one groove immedi=
ately after cleaning it to protect it from oxidation before the brazing cyc=
le begins, and the other groove has BAg-7 wire tacked in place at the ends =
with BAg-7 paste. Sean gave me a chamfered bare copper FG2 heat exchanger t=
o install in the empty pocket. It seemed to fit well. I applied BAg-7 BFM p=
aste to the corners and BAg-7 wire to the sides (1/32=E2=80=9D diameter, th=
e same as we use when brazing with BAg-8). I worked with Mahmood to generat=
e a brazing cycle for the plate based on BAg-7 experiments I had run previo=
usly. The cycle goes to a peak temperature of 730C with a hold time of 30 m=
inutes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7003b130-f055-46e8-bd63-5598cd47a004">REDRESS: I am having s=
ome difficult dissolving amorphous polypropylene in ethyl acetate, so I am =
trying to</p>
<p local-id=3D"3a1c70c9-c879-4f3b-935b-90ba9e60cdb8"></p>
<p local-id=3D"7c47160e-225f-44e8-ac35-9c6097f3e180">2025-04-02</p>
<p local-id=3D"e8bf8789-b276-4970-b747-10610aaeeebe">PXL: Meetings, assembl=
y, repair</p>
<p local-id=3D"3ea701d6-0fd0-4077-a471-ed95289ff958"></p>
<p local-id=3D"69c3c77b-1fab-44ec-9143-2ee2fba8fa22">2025-04-03</p>
<p local-id=3D"6021e172-6968-4244-8f11-7ea7fff7e886">PXL: Meeting w/ AEM. P=
repared Unit 6 for BAg-8 rebraze. Soldered Unit 5 on hot plate. Prepared Un=
it 3 for 2nd BAg-7 braze and started cycle in F2 with a peak temperature of=
 710C (previous peak temperature for 1st BAg-7 braze was 730C).</p>
<p local-id=3D"859dd101-9bb4-405e-a3d6-6f21b9eb37c9"></p>
<p local-id=3D"399659a4-14f9-4698-938b-b2ccf2d10e92">2025-04-04</p>
<p local-id=3D"930f26af-61c6-40ba-a160-7eccf3da78ee">PXL: 5 and 6 leak, 3 i=
s sealed before machining. 3 leaked after machining, so I grooved the leaki=
ng joints and filled the grooves with BAg-7 paste, trying to keep the level=
 of the paste flush with the level of the plate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2e128535-9949-4bd8-8fe5-c31fe8f6f4d9">To Do Next Week: Insta=
ll and wire HOPPER V3.5, redesign for tapper, add vibrator, spreader bar fo=
r V3.1. Try fly cutting with Stepcraft.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ca6d0b2a-0d04-4dd6-bb46-7746400410ef">NOTE: Goal is to have =
some hopper in PILOT 2 to run prints to be able to show the board, explicit=
ly not to create an optimized hopper before starting to print with it. Opti=
mal process would be to determine the quantifiable specs of the function an=
d performance required from the hopper, then design and test prototypes to =
meet those requirements, then integrate that into the machine.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2397ed6c-c6c5-48ce-accf-1ebc1fe0e431"></p>
<p local-id=3D"0f248c09-4369-4234-b06a-ba7e1a179d7d">2025-04-07</p>
<p local-id=3D"b25b6214-23e2-4a72-b5a0-48b3913ca2ec">PXL: Came in on Saturd=
ay and removed plate 3 from F2 and leak checked it. It was sealed, so I cle=
aned it up a bit with a diamond stone and it stayed sealed. Today Unit 6 wa=
s minimum cleanup machined, leaks were marked, and I cleaned the leak point=
s with acetone and a wire wheel, and applied BAg-7 BFM paste, left it on th=
e hot plate at 40C for a few hours, then loaded it into F2 and started cycl=
e 13, which is the BAg-7 braze cycle currently set with a peak temperature =
of 710C.</p>
<p local-id=3D"df255e11-4adf-40e3-b6bc-5afc25b0c274">REDRESS: Having diffic=
ulty with making a PMMA-based binder that produces strong green parts after=
 curing. I am experimenting with: Poly(methyl methacrylate-co-ethyl acrylat=
e) <a href=3D"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/182249" cl=
ass=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/p=
roduct/aldrich/182249</a> which forms the strongest powder cake I=E2=80=99v=
e ever seen when dissolved in acetone and mixed with powder, but doesn=E2=
=80=99t bind back together well after grinding, sieving, and curing. Althou=
gh to be fair, I was only able to get ~1/3 of the cake to grind into powder=
 because the remaining chunks were too strong to grind.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f7cedbd6-c67f-4860-ae41-e73cfab0716c"></p>
<p local-id=3D"9c4c3b67-5b31-47ba-b391-1910d7ada0ad">2025-04-08</p>
<p local-id=3D"8ccd0351-02f6-4160-a04b-3bd005c4234d">PXL: No word back from=
 AEM on Unit 3. After removing Unit 6 from last night=E2=80=99s BAg-7 brazi=
ng run in F2, it only leaked on one side of one unit (2 points) before and =
after machining. Some porosity is visible where the BAg-7 BFM was melted in=
to the grooves.. I grooved out the leaking joint, then grooved it deeper pe=
r Marcus' request at the exact location of the leak to get a better view of=
 the leak point.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bdc2984b-8a18-466b-b9fa-9e0413ab5d9d">HOPPER: Working on a n=
ew motor mount for the stepper motor that drives the dosing roller; mountin=
g it to the end cap doesn=E2=80=99t provide reliable belt tension. I am als=
o working on mounting a stepper motor to act as the impact doser roller cle=
aner; a solenoid is difficult to integrate given the dimensional limitation=
s and has limitations on the frequency and amplitude control. I am printing=
 a new hopper that has mounting holes on the front and back to enable mount=
ing of the roller and tapper motors on one side of the hopper and the vibra=
tor on the other side.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7c750f9a-61b6-4dfc-a18b-1e893506f2bd"></p>
<p local-id=3D"c5007786-3503-4076-ad43-55dfc5192530">2025-04-09</p>
<p local-id=3D"35291374-1c6c-4903-8e23-0eb42c0e98a8">PXL: Cleaned groove on=
 Unit 6 and applied BAg-7 braze paste using the final Unit 3 method: I inje=
cted paste into the groove to fill it as well as possible, then scraped off=
 the excess with a razor blade held at an angle to hopefully push the braze=
 paste into the groove as much as possible and reduce the excess paste left=
 above the surface.</p>
<p local-id=3D"de7ee79a-3997-4f47-8a3b-ac7bd1d3c17c">REDRESS: I have a batc=
h of 1 kg of powder coated with 28g PMMA EA and 2g silane coupling agent. I=
 am working on a batch that will have 1g of 3-(trimethoxysilyl)propyl metha=
crylate dissolved in 100g IPA, allowed to hydrolyze for 1 hour, then mixed =
with powder and dried to pre-treat it, then it will be blended with 36g of =
PMMA-EA dissolved in acetone combined with 1 g of dibutyl phthalate. I have=
 also been omitting TEG-DMA in recent formulations, which may be a mistake =
because TEG-DMA is apparently acting as the crosslinking initiator. Here is=
 a possible recipe: 1000 g powder to 20g binder, 17g PMMA, 1g AIBN, 1g TEG-=
DMA, 1g Silane</p>
<p local-id=3D"fd393395-ac82-45c0-b1a7-581ffe8ec223">HOPPER: Assembled a HO=
PPER V3.6 for PILOT 2 with a shorter belt that moves the stepper motor clos=
er to the shaft and a new stepper-tapper design that has a brass bolt on th=
e end of a carbon-fiber reinforced plastic arm to tap the shaft without dam=
aging it. This would enable precision control of the frequency (by setting =
number of stepper moves per second) and the amplitude (by controlling rotat=
ional velocity) of the tap impulse. I also began working on using an Arduin=
o to control HOPPER functions (doser roller rotation, vibration of doser ro=
ller with stepper motor, stepper-tapper, and vibration motor). Controlling =
these functions with an Arduino would enable more advanced control of funct=
ions independently of simple gantry motion. Per Payman=E2=80=99s request, I=
 removed the stepper-tapper and replaced it with a traditional solenoid, an=
d abandoned the advanced control system in favor of simple Duet control thr=
ough the PILOT printer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e5e9eb4f-2d35-4a67-97f4-d1675c018f6a"></p>
<p local-id=3D"768e812b-4a5f-47d0-8a20-eee1be5f09d6">2025-04-10</p>
<p local-id=3D"3dcf7d57-722f-4cff-8edc-0b1cf7923c68">PXL: Weekly meeting wi=
th Craig at AEM. Shipping the unit to TSMC has been delayed, so they didn=
=E2=80=99t actually need it on Friday. They pressure tested Unit 3 to 80 ps=
i for several hours and it remained sealed. They have been simulating the p=
erformance of fully machined copper heat exchangers that have solid outer w=
alls and are therefore brazed with a full-height vertical braze joint. Thei=
r simulation results suggested that the performance of machined heat exchan=
gers would be lower than 3D printed lattice heat exchangers, but may be acc=
eptable for their application. They are also looking into reducing the tota=
l height of the PXL assembly by 1-1.5mm to compensate for changes that need=
 to be made elsewhere in their hardware stack. We are not attempting any fu=
rther repairs of the plates that we have in our possession. The BAg-7 leak =
repair completed last night on Unit 6 was not successful; one key differenc=
e between the repair protocol used on Unit 3 and that used on Unit 6 was th=
at Unit 3 was initially BAg-7 brazed with a peak temperature of 730C, which=
 Unit 6 was always brazed to a peak temperature of 710, the temperature pro=
file that was used for rebraze attempts on Unit 3.</p>
<p local-id=3D"52a70d9c-751b-4a74-8baf-6cc72ffc2b1f">HOPPER: HOPPER V3.6 is=
 assembled and installed in PILOT 2, waiting for Pourya to finish wiring an=
d programming. I am working on printing a new body for HOPPER V3.1 that has=
 spreader bars attached. I am also working on HERMES, a simple testbed for =
testing the hopper outside of the printer that can also be upgraded to be a=
 full printer when used with pre-coated powder with the addition of a laser=
 or projector to cure the layers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f1ae3423-2912-47de-b357-681bb63fc066">REDRESS:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"c4b13919-3caa-4fde-8be4-bd57d4346b1e" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-AquaMold=E2=84=A2BinderRecipeforWater-SolubleMoldMetalForming(Adjusted)"=
>AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Binder Recipe for Water-Soluble Mold Metal Forming (Adju=
sted)</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"535d6f8d-d1df-452e-ab48-ca0d3e3da6fb" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"64e99f00-ae8f-40f4-a9e6-8ac98e2d55e6" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1280gFinalMetalPowderMixture(98%Metal,2%Binder)">For 1280g Final Meta=
l Powder Mixture (98% Metal, 2% Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"3695a7d9-e4da-43b5-ad5e-c427bf46f343"><strong>Metal Powder</=
strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"67b65086-f9b1-42a6-8263-421295427154">
<li local-id=3D"c5cdd6ea-00ac-40a9-b269-9e86655390da">
<p local-id=3D"fbaf4074-4c04-47c2-bcaf-89ad52427195">1254.4g of metal powde=
r (17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e310a2db-5618-4786-9742-bfd0cbf55d05"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (25.6g total)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"4b4d0777-59d0-4f59-bd0c-83d93f16dc69">
<li local-id=3D"106e0eae-365f-457f-a918-16f8234e2e11">
<p local-id=3D"bdab839c-7ef1-48e0-a16f-ab6feff4e343">22.5g Poly(methyl meth=
acrylate-co-ethyl acrylate) (88% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"405457b4-e34a-48d2-a696-1863ee8c8b39">
<p local-id=3D"e1a11682-6fb6-4ed4-9c7a-b617b8f453e3">1.54g Triethylene glyc=
ol dimethacrylate (6% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c339a962-13d3-474b-9438-1662cbc4e56d">
<p local-id=3D"dc7d779d-f4a7-4905-87af-6b2c8a265f51">1.02g 3-(Trimethoxysil=
yl)propyl methacrylate (4% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bad74cb4-3aa7-46bc-8b93-fbc4f2690d64">
<p local-id=3D"1b09ae83-8eb3-4cc8-98c1-bf8b53133561">0.51g 2,2=E2=80=B2-Azo=
bis(2-methylpropionitrile) (AIBN) (2% of binder)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"cdb907c4-14e8-44dc-823f-b2eed4c44e6f"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"8ae574e6-c4fe-4d19-9b62-bfbd5516adfc">
<li local-id=3D"bf8aaa3f-c029-40bd-b4e5-1a6a452b9fd7">
<p local-id=3D"faf366fb-177e-461f-9745-6489e06796a4">230-256g Acetone (9-10=
:1 ratio with binder solids)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"2174f123-7453-45d5-bd7b-57a6a1dc7e88" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Equipment">Equipment</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"f7ba59b2-2696-4260-825d-63f417780afb">
<li local-id=3D"040342ee-a306-463a-bdd0-f2ade45289c6">
<p local-id=3D"d60c2b24-f4d0-4c1d-906c-001405bc4f5d">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bb1cb9f0-2d70-4521-aed9-36b531be256d">
<p local-id=3D"26513bf9-1c2c-4c38-be59-440ac9414064">Glass containers with =
tight-fitting lids</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"463e299f-5319-41df-b5f1-57d4eb8eeb9e">
<p local-id=3D"ea0324bc-af32-4d84-aacd-4b8cc41d5f38">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c3652d09-9e5a-4796-a9d0-ed7244848a95">
<p local-id=3D"f7446f50-9c37-4114-8488-bc1bd16bd4ef">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"455ba822-fbc8-4104-a2b0-f49669e52efc">
<p local-id=3D"61a892f8-190c-420b-b3af-9c24e7f5d43b">Controlled temperature=
 oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5bde00bc-77e8-4d1a-8bad-82dfd21e17af">
<p local-id=3D"90bd3d3e-f3a1-4fec-9f4a-68b4ea436d69">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"31d2fbb1-47c1-4696-98f6-971da0d10538">
<p local-id=3D"239da5a7-c710-4e6a-8330-c696c3f3af6d">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d8572200-8cc7-4afb-bf6e-f0399dc506b0">
<p local-id=3D"6407c83b-cf7c-41bc-a88c-362943f7961e">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"661192c5-b971-420b-bfc7-0514011cc776">
<p local-id=3D"a03167ae-163e-41bf-9224-f7898b7b4e6d">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"c4fd6ee5-fc50-4b3c-9a70-0082b56cfa09" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"ba5027d9-20e7-422a-93c3-8d38e7111d55" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.BinderPreparation">A. Binder Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"f9ac5206-840f-40c1-bddc-5db725d94de0">
<li local-id=3D"b98c6786-763c-49fd-934a-3a470cb3176a">
<p local-id=3D"c59e4ef7-ffa3-420f-844b-209819b5dbf1">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 230g of acetone into a glass container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"81c99137-0f45-4e43-8007-55b0deb2d296">
<p local-id=3D"d0905b0a-0f41-4981-9bf1-32e475a369cc">While stirring, slowly=
 add 22.5g of PMMA-co-EA to the acetone. Stir until completely dissolved (a=
pproximately 30-60 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1a2a023f-8728-41b3-900f-e8c5205ec1c3">
<p local-id=3D"4e094394-830d-4134-8cc2-9f291635c28c">Add 1.02g of 3-(Trimet=
hoxysilyl)propyl methacrylate to the solution and stir for 15 minutes.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"066d3c9e-608c-43da-83e2-f738b0b268c1">
<p local-id=3D"47efe479-940f-462a-8859-65ae88d28027">Add 1.54g of TEG-DMA a=
nd stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f8ae2429-ec9a-4972-aa1f-a73d74653c40">
<p local-id=3D"5fd9a5eb-4ba1-4f31-8fdf-ee36559c2f86">Finally, add 0.51g of =
AIBN and stir gently until completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6770e964-020d-43c4-ae93-05de865fc401">
<p local-id=3D"10c40ee6-6936-4d28-974a-72b7544f6a79">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation. The binder solution =
is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"1f1967ba-c941-41c5-9050-cc6683b136c5" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.SlurryPreparation">B. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"4a279366-d348-42e5-b925-a0a37a8f740d">
<li local-id=3D"1cb90a2d-2c6e-4acd-9191-19b8fdf83419">
<p local-id=3D"ae4ad316-8688-47b1-8a69-4c51e5c710fe">Place 1254.4g of metal=
 powder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f2606535-3e7f-4b6a-880d-0ab3fd5107c0">
<p local-id=3D"abba4bd4-d416-4a3a-b274-5497efb74ff5">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the metal powder.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"3ab905b9-ef64-49cc-b220-909c4801bc98">
<p local-id=3D"00b0f1e6-6ef8-4951-b1ea-d22a247af9f5">Continue mixing for 30=
-45 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"84d77018-d701-4b7b-9cab-2391e65c0ea7">
<p local-id=3D"e84d45f6-ef98-4f56-be7d-c8c690b36338">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 26g) to achieve p=
roper consistency.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"5403c887-df06-4a8f-9eab-c86a0d2cad22" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.Drying">C. Drying</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"3141d803-b774-4a3b-9851-195986c5ff77">
<li local-id=3D"dbef5ec0-c066-4c7b-857a-635e9dca11b6">
<p local-id=3D"a87f5323-a417-483b-826c-ca124ce6ec55">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1314940e-b6f8-43ca-8e19-9fbe12cba2c0">
<p local-id=3D"7b8ba08f-d921-4fdd-8952-3cb0c9373531">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature in a well-ventilated area for 12-24 hours.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"02a542fd-663d-49f0-964e-08224fdbab25">
<p local-id=3D"76bafabb-4796-48ec-8cf2-ecfe0f5c2990">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 50=C2=B0C for 4-6 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"80c773da-c8de-46aa-8e54-02e273dce403">
<p local-id=3D"56a6c509-04ea-44e1-b31c-6a95f15f1e2f">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 60=C2=B0C for 2 hours to ensure complete solvent removal.</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b7adf080-7721-43d9-ac3c-30130fe1832f">
<p local-id=3D"b2b4f139-d113-4ed5-8b37-e2951e5cfe21">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid cake.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"39c87313-f20e-496c-95d3-b22f10cc8fd0" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.GrindingandSieving">D. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"3e8e9145-1d10-4d4d-a720-011764b43ecd">
<li local-id=3D"5b76a010-ba18-4a67-84c6-13e2cb162394">
<p local-id=3D"06524f34-073b-44a4-9822-bd02d9511285">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b657ea77-2f1d-42aa-9133-bfec9efb50f8">
<p local-id=3D"24e764cb-0151-4104-8a30-d24361fee389">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill under controlled temperature conditions (below 40=C2=B0C=
 to prevent premature crosslinking).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1b637a19-1b48-430c-bbbf-cef741f397c3">
<p local-id=3D"49c3948b-b51f-409a-9855-892a8862ae46">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
 for application).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e6e634cf-3e86-42e0-9b29-14b03ee63c4b">
<p local-id=3D"9381d5f1-80db-4c74-ad86-c1c489d1fc39">If necessary, add 0.06=
-0.13g of fumed silica (0.005-0.01% of total weight) to improve flowability=
 if the powder still appears damp.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"8adf213c-d9db-4385-8809-1996e8ebeb57" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.TheAquaMold=E2=84=A2Process">E. The AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Process</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"596dea87-2ee2-48bb-895e-599894287ad0">
<li local-id=3D"1343d49f-f3c0-418d-ad26-1e4fdd069f7c">
<p local-id=3D"b227b81f-0622-42ad-92ec-69775e207e2d">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"07eebfe7-2be6-42c4-9b5f-ff7c90deb3c6">
<p local-id=3D"1ed1741c-aca7-45b8-83ec-44ec0e766380">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0effef6f-f1a7-4dbd-8cc1-4c6bf6dd6761">
<p local-id=3D"e7b85108-b146-49bd-8a96-1637c37c564d">Heat the packed molds =
to 80=C2=B0C and maintain this temperature for 1.5 hours to activate the AI=
BN and crosslink the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f79d1923-5c6d-4ecc-a8fb-4d5b1c03a082">
<p local-id=3D"8cfcf615-9636-4f4e-a627-2e543342c3eb">Cool gradually to room=
 temperature (approximately 1-2 hours).</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"98630cf3-42e4-4ecd-acc8-90059013ca98" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.DissolutionandGreenPartRecovery">F. Dissolution and Green Part Recover=
y</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"9967c44b-f210-4924-8596-f704b626c36d">
<li local-id=3D"e713aace-55c2-44bc-89c4-d65551b04745">
<p local-id=3D"e04b1cb9-faaa-4e49-821e-9a47b5d97d2a">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in warm water (40-50=C2=B0C) to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"eb74f5de-4437-4527-9a03-016247b9ec27">
<p local-id=3D"e5a92b13-40a5-4d3a-9f2e-57be02040d59">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh water as needed until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"42fc50d0-f9fc-42f5-816f-34048ce465b4">
<p local-id=3D"7f1a55f2-7fb0-4eff-a1d7-7c4ade6bfbc7">Carefully extract the =
green part from the water bath and allow to dry completely.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0f19521e-aca4-4cd4-a1a0-b862355cf75d">
<p local-id=3D"2e56beb7-8d93-41ea-81dc-8d5027667cc4">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to your standard protocol for t=
he specific metal alloy.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"8fac2616-2f75-4f61-8bd1-78ccd77b5f35" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Notes">Notes</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"963039ed-e705-4a00-a5d8-340d68cd723c">
<li local-id=3D"8808c23e-a52c-4061-8a7b-323cf9bb57e0">
<p local-id=3D"47bf8f51-db29-4b90-832a-11177804ab1b">Store the AIBN in a co=
ol, dark place to prevent premature decomposition.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"76dd97fe-e274-42d1-a83e-5311a055fff8">
<p local-id=3D"53a06a1f-972f-4e85-8365-98d6c602cd37">All mixing containers =
should be clean and free of contaminants.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"504a6983-7002-4272-8c98-d6bfb4a4db67">
<p local-id=3D"f0289cc9-6ee8-4661-970e-3fc2ca1015fb">Perform all solvent ha=
ndling steps in a well-ventilated area away from ignition sources.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0d3a35f6-5894-422a-b0f6-cc9f7823d0b6">
<p local-id=3D"bcaad30c-1450-49f5-a792-0a53490aee28">The binder formulation=
 can be adjusted slightly based on the specific metal powder characteristic=
s and desired final properties.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"12b97c3d-1fa1-4f64-b863-ec8e77af73be">
<p local-id=3D"f7a4e076-a4ec-43c6-a51f-27ae87dd6f90">The water-soluble mold=
 geometry will determine the final shape of your metal part - ensure proper=
 mold design for complex features.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"ad2e173a-6d38-44d5-be7a-7e7b01862bd1"></p>
<p local-id=3D"efecd482-886b-448f-81dd-7de93c893f76">2025-04-14</p>
<p local-id=3D"df33c314-dfb7-4e61-b0eb-ce2a42ea7cf7">REDRESS: I came in ove=
r the weekend to grind and sieve the latest batch of powder (the recipe abo=
ve, but with the powder pre-treated with the silane coupling agent before b=
eing blended with the binder). I loaded it into a mold and tried to run the=
 PMMA crosslinking cycle in the lower Keith furnace, but the powder seems c=
ompletely unbound this morning so I suspect that the furnace did not actual=
ly heat up. I have been seeing it have some issues lately with not heating =
at all, so hopefully that is what happened and it wasn=E2=80=99t an issue w=
ith the powder not curing at all. I am trying the same powder batch in a ne=
w mold tonight with a different thermal cycle. I have historically been hea=
ting the molds to 250F, but Claude suggested that a temperature that high c=
ould cause issues with particle binding because it would cause the AIBN to =
decompose too rapidly and PMMA can degrade at temperatures above 100C. Look=
ing at the PMMA-EA I have been using <a href=3D"https://www.sigmaaldrich.co=
m/US/en/product/aldrich/182249" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">ht=
tps://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/182249</a> it says in the =
information that the glass transition temperature is 104C (219.2F). I had p=
reviously assumed that heating the PMMA above its glass transition point wo=
uld be necessary to bind the particles, but I may have been wrong about tha=
t. The cycle I am using right now is 70F-160F ramp at 120F/hour, 30 min dwe=
ll, 160-180F ramp at 120F/hour, 90 min dwell, cycle end.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8c39e6c2-cac3-4c7d-8b5c-dc5ba0782176">HOPPER: Working on des=
igning a HOPPER V4.0 that uses an aluminum doser roller modified from a pie=
ce of timing pulley stock.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4a8157ce-2f5f-4406-96d9-e53b5ed8266b">HERMES: Designed belt =
drive system and just need to print various components and assemble them. I=
 also need to cut the 4040 stock to the right lengths to put together the c=
ore frame.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8ea40cb4-3321-415f-ad3f-a123bf6ae4db"></p>
<p local-id=3D"28b42180-a7db-4709-ae93-0bfd8af9295f">2025-04-15</p>
<p local-id=3D"901b01a2-909a-4e62-83e1-82443ea8911a">REDRESS: The mold I co=
oked last night was no better, so I ran the same mold through a fast ramp c=
ycle set to 300F (it probably overshot that by a bit because of the ramp sp=
eed) and the part came out better. Still not strong enough, and it seems to=
 be still breaking apart when I am dissolving off the mold, but my sense is=
 that it is significantly stronger. I believe Claude may have been wrong ab=
out staying below the glass transition point of PMMA, and when I confronted=
 it it changed its mind and said that heating above the glass transition po=
int would be beneficial for green part strength.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8aff5166-7d78-478c-9051-5959e3463a62">HOPPER: I made an alum=
inum roller for HOPPER V4.0 by turning down the ends of a piece of timing b=
elt pulley stock. I also designed and generated a drawing for a mount to mo=
unt Payman=E2=80=99s HOPPER V3.1 to the blue and silver gantry.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d1f24fdb-8c9d-4ff3-9b38-65d94161af94">HERMES: I mounted the =
main carrier mount to the two linear guide bearings and installed the motor=
, idler pulley, and belt. I still need to cut down a piece of 4040 extrusio=
n to fit the front of the frame so the frame has not been aligned and the s=
crews tightened, but the bulk of the structure and functionality is ready. =
It does not have a good cable management solution yet, which I may need to =
work on or possibly ignore for the time being.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b4b6b426-2796-48b0-b5b0-92208476b6c5"></p>
<p local-id=3D"29151673-25b6-4757-9a4f-ded81b1802d1">2025-04-16</p>
<p local-id=3D"0b8b6615-3298-404d-be72-3988bdc566f5">REDRESS: I put two mol=
ds in the new higher temperature curing cycle (peak 300F), one filled with =
the latest batch of powder and one filled with the same powder that had bee=
n mixed with fumed silica, and the one that had been mixed with fumed silic=
a came out stronger and held up to mold dissolving much better. Some bits o=
f it still broke off, but it mostly held its shape. I think the issues with=
 structural weakness at some points are due to uneven fumed silica coating.=
 I am currently drying a new batch of powder that has some dibutyl phthalat=
e added to give it a bit of flexibility:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"0b53b472-1a9b-4508-99eb-2fec412cd220" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-AquaMold=E2=84=A2BinderRecipeforWater-SolubleMoldMetalForming(OptimizedV=
ersion)">AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Binder Recipe for Water-Soluble Mold Metal Formi=
ng (Optimized Version)</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"c3bfbd80-e2d5-45da-bf92-cc4a790e7d53" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.1">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"1e29e4fc-4121-4309-a9d8-9105a651fb30" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalPowderMixture(97%Metal,3%Binder)">For 1000g Final Meta=
l Powder Mixture (97% Metal, 3% Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"d6fb6b74-6adb-43d1-b42f-f3a0685f94da"><strong>Metal Powder</=
strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"bae4df73-392d-4c82-8d4b-58002d577a5e">
<li local-id=3D"fecf1559-d87c-4426-bc12-619743d37b92">
<p local-id=3D"e782ba8d-3656-4f6f-85f8-922acf42a4f9">970g of metal powder (=
17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"22090245-497e-4c81-94b3-315d02933f88"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (30g total)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d8e0c7fd-1411-4aeb-a33e-88372bcfca3e">
<li local-id=3D"27f13345-1308-427e-b528-e6dbcb7df177">
<p local-id=3D"4fc79a35-9406-4215-a2cf-14812a346196">25.2g Poly(methyl meth=
acrylate-co-ethyl acrylate) (84% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"201e9547-aa50-4d7b-917b-67765bc23eb5">
<p local-id=3D"0e835b79-d425-400c-ba61-96cb3e14d972">1.8g Triethylene glyco=
l dimethacrylate (6% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6d1b30b7-1317-4330-b74b-9874845ea02d">
<p local-id=3D"c61c11fc-a3ed-4d07-891f-9eb1ebbe8564">1.2g 3-(Trimethoxysily=
l)propyl methacrylate (4% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"73c1383e-48ea-4924-b967-abdfd1710e99">
<p local-id=3D"84e1cdc5-4e5a-46ff-9805-30bec0ef0d76">0.6g 2,2=E2=80=B2-Azob=
is(2-methylpropionitrile) (AIBN) (2% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c8fc8a83-9b05-4389-a381-d4ff9d857dd7">
<p local-id=3D"32d0daf4-3a7c-4e1d-8c06-e6e0ab27f6a7">1.2g Dibutyl phthalate=
 (4% of binder) - <em>new plasticizer component</em></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"89c7d1b4-6dd3-4858-9dc2-63ed1b06d9c5"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"4baf39ba-ab9d-412d-9ad5-53ca0ceaad23">
<li local-id=3D"737f2be4-0ce4-46a2-8c84-71e1418afd06">
<p local-id=3D"8182316c-c5c2-4856-af8a-1cb8ff8e3dd6">270-300g Acetone (9-10=
:1 ratio with binder solids)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"52068a32-3882-453c-8e32-efaaddd88276" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Equipment.1">Equipment</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"994a7b43-1386-45de-9466-1e24d0e398cf">
<li local-id=3D"cc9117ba-4904-4c20-b1f6-337422e3cc79">
<p local-id=3D"aa813ccb-622c-46da-be76-08baeb5facce">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"efb3db04-4116-4ed6-8ec0-aa6004862d32">
<p local-id=3D"d576aa20-7020-45e2-b9b4-55aad2c64fb7">Glass containers with =
tight-fitting lids</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b1feef26-7589-4b6a-81b5-ab4bd59c18d4">
<p local-id=3D"e73b1065-a70e-4b9d-9336-3cedf59f014e">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"657bccc6-a2de-415e-8214-c125ded94a34">
<p local-id=3D"99898d2f-dd91-497a-b87d-b7fb4a6cd61c">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e53521c2-fb95-4db8-95bd-0d21bfc3776d">
<p local-id=3D"76e024ee-423e-44b3-a182-503812c3aa5f">Controlled temperature=
 oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6cf96ebf-8622-4a1f-8298-30f068a2bf9c">
<p local-id=3D"d980896a-47b0-490e-be3e-41614caccdd8">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cb11562d-0dfc-4405-a1da-4afd34a4a756">
<p local-id=3D"9f7f8808-867d-41af-8448-06777c8e9794">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b622b81b-4605-46b2-aff1-c2c87ef4e90a">
<p local-id=3D"601959af-ddf3-479e-ad80-b826fd81b5f5">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"97dc8dfb-080b-4f1b-a688-1ef50fcec4a5">
<p local-id=3D"1692c2eb-b1e6-4ef5-9351-9c15f778f2b1">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"8e922197-6e46-4a09-bc14-8c6456b5b4cf" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.1">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"788bd675-3065-4fb7-87ad-7685252d2beb" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.BinderPreparation.1">A. Binder Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c67003be-ede5-465a-b9b0-bf7be21b4bfb">
<li local-id=3D"69d7ccf8-2c84-451f-b179-cf2cceaf37b5">
<p local-id=3D"eb4dd4d6-2ff9-4947-af55-bbc2aaf9f0cb">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 270g of acetone into a glass container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f52230e2-99e1-4981-ac47-65c55bc2297d">
<p local-id=3D"7f299602-7e01-43ee-995a-ea05b0d35260">While stirring, slowly=
 add 25.2g of PMMA-co-EA to the acetone. Stir until completely dissolved (a=
pproximately 30-60 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"60ec5315-05e9-43fc-9b6d-a75bd6db97ee">
<p local-id=3D"a2e1eb8b-04b8-4da7-9f6c-48370eb194cd">Add 1.2g of 3-(Trimeth=
oxysilyl)propyl methacrylate to the solution and stir for 15 minutes.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"1a75e1a2-729a-4787-ab9d-0486aa012772">
<p local-id=3D"8d93bbd6-823e-4344-bcc0-01dfcbb4698c">Add 1.8g of TEG-DMA an=
d stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"debec377-63b2-41d6-af08-dc430b1652af">
<p local-id=3D"967f7a34-ee60-4323-8b66-7353576ba758">Add 1.2g of dibutyl ph=
thalate and stir for 15 minutes to ensure complete incorporation of the pla=
sticizer.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c67fe145-f6ff-4e09-a777-a3cda93c9790">
<p local-id=3D"37b466c6-5d8e-4fb0-bb88-d3dc4c53f152">Finally, add 0.6g of A=
IBN and stir gently until completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fed11675-bec2-47b5-9f80-253f25c52178">
<p local-id=3D"5ce89975-ea5f-4a73-ad67-aa76f4a32f27">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation. The binder solution =
is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"e955d194-cf69-4fa8-acd9-e726b25151de" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.SlurryPreparation.1">B. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"40ff0d14-c34d-4e94-96b1-d9f23aa82ad3">
<li local-id=3D"f32d43d5-b57a-484b-ac71-c1a9bd173e99">
<p local-id=3D"35dcdfc2-efdb-4fd3-9632-adb7b9064fd9">Place 970g of metal po=
wder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0d9e42a8-9eb9-4af1-9017-8f6fe47aecdb">
<p local-id=3D"854fae87-79f9-4e8d-8d65-ec26b0eaf3f0">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the metal powder.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"43634fb1-eec5-4f41-b41b-ddcc2e3c51d9">
<p local-id=3D"d0c2eb37-ca5c-4a32-9aa5-90d82d22b1f0">Continue mixing for 30=
-45 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aed447f6-f0bf-4f07-8c04-d6da1fd042a5">
<p local-id=3D"db2d7930-2908-4a0c-9eb5-e537ba139c73">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 30g) to achieve p=
roper consistency. <em>Note: The plasticizer should improve flowability, bu=
t monitor consistency carefully.</em></p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"6962766c-1ae3-4bc0-9c9c-29a1a5a2351b" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.Drying.1">C. Drying</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"62de34d2-2ab3-4270-9b17-57dab2b0d89d">
<li local-id=3D"f42624df-fa17-44eb-902d-f45153384150">
<p local-id=3D"831ceb98-900c-4350-bafb-c5ac17459c33">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d4115660-b8cb-450d-8ea8-972054b51191">
<p local-id=3D"6a37cd1e-3b5e-42ba-907e-ecb72225bc3d">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature in a well-ventilated area for 12-24 hours.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"509e2971-6bfb-4583-8a67-e7a493d6c7dd">
<p local-id=3D"cbcbb32d-acf4-445f-a5c6-108457e59a39">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 50=C2=B0C for 4-6 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c6f14a12-26cc-4058-8b9a-08e7e78f1602">
<p local-id=3D"b78a0961-b1f9-4f7a-a987-31d0f823d1f0">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 60=C2=B0C for 2 hours to ensure complete solvent removal.</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ddd88af9-d6f9-4cdd-8387-7b41d30c7d06">
<p local-id=3D"f753d84b-d663-4718-9342-2cc3fb8e8f9d">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid cake.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"ab4406e7-a818-431d-a069-67b29f9f0b08" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.GrindingandSieving.1">D. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"210684e1-9dfc-4eac-8457-cf18fa8b3b34">
<li local-id=3D"258f7009-645e-48b7-877a-ce0ad27c89e9">
<p local-id=3D"db5e292e-18b7-4080-b9ea-357b8b45f603">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"749994f9-a839-465c-9897-cbbe8ef33fd9">
<p local-id=3D"c7af3299-bedf-4e50-9ec9-907a69a07ce8">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill under controlled temperature conditions (below 40=C2=B0C=
 to prevent premature crosslinking).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3f732de0-e5f0-4f1d-9032-47ba009c4d15">
<p local-id=3D"54e62427-fdc9-4e15-898e-a194b25b3eff">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
 for application).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f5503b6d-4adc-4740-9b63-20b89debe46d">
<p local-id=3D"35a4b164-7395-4f8e-93eb-b22fc5410e26">If necessary, add 0.05=
-0.1g of fumed silica (0.005-0.01% of total weight) to improve flowability,=
 though this may be less necessary with the added plasticizer.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"5c8ab3cf-4f92-4210-89f5-961398dac455" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.TheAquaMold=E2=84=A2Process.1">E. The AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Process</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"0c27cede-ed22-472d-b148-7c4800b02a37">
<li local-id=3D"c15095f5-222d-4bee-9a40-83c975615507">
<p local-id=3D"eeb27218-ce13-4440-a318-bde89209709f">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"13b54002-0c8a-42d4-bbe7-e105dcb6908b">
<p local-id=3D"773b5653-de45-42e0-8c63-2faf96f3f473">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"98a93dee-386b-4a43-85cd-100858c3a8b3">
<p local-id=3D"280a20a2-764d-4f57-8ea6-9540b2c67f7e">Heat the packed molds =
to 80=C2=B0C and maintain this temperature for 1.5 hours to activate the AI=
BN and crosslink the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aff67c40-eda4-46f9-9a81-5eebc01f43e0">
<p local-id=3D"6c0b8062-00f7-4b44-986f-c9892a6a4f8e">Cool gradually to room=
 temperature (approximately 1-2 hours).</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"4bc97e16-5cf4-4387-bd99-6bc397c93a91" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.DissolutionandGreenPartRecovery.1">F. Dissolution and Green Part Recov=
ery</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c581ccbd-efdd-4ed0-8d3e-9ca599972f63">
<li local-id=3D"a47b715c-16ba-4274-9aeb-8b8626d2bef4">
<p local-id=3D"66dad2b5-2989-4a6d-999d-c96c275be38e">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in warm water (40-50=C2=B0C) to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"d1d07d22-2572-4ac5-8754-73e1a2b450cd">
<p local-id=3D"91ecd743-9949-4d65-ba18-4c7fcaddb746">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh water as needed until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"919eba51-744f-4c51-881c-82368e76cceb">
<p local-id=3D"fe0042fe-155d-4d83-be58-0f0a26b54cfd">Carefully extract the =
green part from the water bath and allow to dry completely.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0198f4a4-3cd5-4883-8cba-8ee7a16213c5">
<p local-id=3D"130b29cf-7bee-48df-8193-e5437373f7fb">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to your standard protocol for t=
he specific metal alloy.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"18d95815-3be5-4294-8127-e7e2693c5be5" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Notes.1">Notes</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"54734851-ab43-42e3-a8c8-acb993c2c26c">
<li local-id=3D"29502bfc-62da-4c7b-b3b2-b990e728176b">
<p local-id=3D"5147b9d4-0d1b-4b8c-b000-6fcfa2ab5948">The addition of dibuty=
l phthalate as a plasticizer should improve the flexibility of the green pa=
rts and potentially improve packing density during molding.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"23c2d96e-bbe4-4c1d-b1c7-3516a2b1cc5c">
<p local-id=3D"191669ed-5936-4603-87c2-304e82b44093">You may need to adjust=
 the debinding cycle due to the increased binder content (3% vs 2%) and the=
 addition of the plasticizer.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a46c91b3-3da0-41b4-b54e-b7945c0415ff">
<p local-id=3D"cf561572-275b-451f-a8f9-6f83160755f0">The plasticizer may sl=
ightly lower the temperature at which the binder softens, which could be be=
neficial for molding but requires attention during handling.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"41a50be4-994c-456c-8478-b95314ba7535">
<p local-id=3D"a83713b4-8939-41de-92fd-856a4609907f">Monitor the first few =
production runs closely to ensure the modified binder system maintains stru=
ctural integrity during the molding and dissolution steps.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"afccb6c3-d937-4250-b20d-38d8c240db99">
<p local-id=3D"0ab1eeb2-fcfd-4630-95eb-6ebc6e9e7428">Store the AIBN in a co=
ol, dark place to prevent premature decomposition.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0acf7ea6-ddf7-4ec9-b6c1-51acbf53bce9">
<p local-id=3D"b31e6b0c-86bd-4306-b432-c8ed1b3090cc">All mixing containers =
should be clean and free of contaminants.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"446bed59-ddf4-4e77-8301-c918b3c27e59">
<p local-id=3D"697686f5-3f40-4bbd-990a-cf2e8fb8b0f1">Perform all solvent ha=
ndling steps in a well-ventilated area away from ignition sources.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d298449c-86de-4db6-946f-0f906d9281fc"></p>
<p local-id=3D"3b84f86c-85f7-4657-afb6-76db54f5e79b">I deviated slightly fr=
om the recipe by pre-treating the powder with the silane coupling agent ins=
tead of mixing it with the binder. I also tossed the pieces of the last thr=
ee batches of powder, some of which had not been ground and sieved, into th=
e v mixer with a bunch of fumed silica. Hopefully this will mix the powder =
with the fumed silica while also breaking apart the unground chunks so that=
 it is easy to sieve the final mixture.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9d38f296-914d-442e-911a-c3a48892e44b">HOPPER: The HOPPER V3.=
6 is installed in PILOT 2 and is wired up and running. There is an issue wi=
th the solenoid sticking to the roller shaft and therefore not tapping, whi=
ch per Pourya and Mohsen is due to the solenoid being too close to the shaf=
t. I will reprint the solenoid mount with greater spacing to (potentially) =
alleviate this issue. Worked with Payman to support his continued developme=
nt of HOPPER V3.1 on the silver and blue gantry. I am printing a new HOPPER=
 V4.0 body that hopefully will fit the aluminum doser roller better; the on=
e I printed today was still a little too tight to be useable. The one print=
ed today was printed with PETG-CF while the one I am printing tonight is PE=
TG Basic, which is the material I printed it with initially when I tweaked =
the dimensions to get the doser roller to fit.</p>
<p local-id=3D"59c9294f-c19f-4692-9365-994278834c5f">HERMES: I installed th=
e hopper mount, which because of the hexagonal cutouts I designed it with i=
s too flexible to be useful in final testing, but it should be fine for ini=
tial motion testing. I got a DUET 2 board connected to it and got the main =
axis homing sensorlessly.</p>
<p local-id=3D"be8330d8-98a4-4949-be0f-579786f5a5d0"></p>
<p local-id=3D"930ea9e5-985a-4546-84f4-cf9eee4dc660">2025-04-17</p>
<p local-id=3D"4a509efa-2c3f-4bcf-8341-b232ad00a518">PXL: Meeting with AEM.=
 They still haven=E2=80=99t mounted Unit 3 to their test setup, so apparent=
ly they didn=E2=80=99t need it when they said they did. They haven=E2=80=99=
t abandoned working with us yet, but they do seem to be exploring the possi=
bility of brazing in billet machined parts. They have a monolithic plate th=
at has a single piece of machined copper on the top with a single part stai=
nless steel base that have been brazed together. Apparently there are conce=
rns with crosstalk between the cells, but it is unclear if that has been te=
sted and whether it matters. They are also having a brazing company in Finl=
and conduct brazing experiments; they first brazed 9 machined copper heat e=
xchangers into an unplated 304SS base and were successful. Next they are go=
ing to try the same with 3DEO printed parts. The company won=E2=80=99t disc=
lose the exact process and alloys they=E2=80=99re using, so presumably they=
 have some secret sauce, although we have also had success with brazing mac=
hined copper before.</p>
<p local-id=3D"db06a273-d0eb-4574-85d9-c868222b0471">HOPPER: Assembled a V4=
.0 hopper with an aluminum roller and a stepper tapper. I still need to mak=
e a new mount for the solenoid for the V3.6 hopper in PILOT 2, but other th=
an that it should be ready to begin testing. I want to make some vibration =
damping mounts by printing them from FormLabs elastic material instead of u=
sing springs; the springs isolate the hopper vibrations from the mount well=
, but do a poor job of locating the hopper.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6ae3169e-61be-4ab9-b3c6-f64c056505b0">REDRESS: Mixed up a ba=
tch of PVP-VA powder to try to form layers with heat application. Ground an=
d sieved a batch of powder with the advanced blend with no plasticizer, and=
 ran yesterday=E2=80=99s batch of advanced binder powder with plasticizer i=
n the v mixer for 6 hours. I then filled a mold with the non-plasticizer po=
wder and one with the plasticizer powder. The mold with non-plasticizer pow=
der is the V8 mold design, which has thicker reinforcing gussets. I am runn=
ing both molds through the PMMATEGDMAAIBN cycle on the upper Keith furnace.=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"c82fd513-9e9c-4189-a585-039f3f9a533c">ULTRA: Printed a mist =
box for Payman=E2=80=99s ULTRA setup that is derived from the standard HOPP=
ER design but has straight sides and no opening for a doser roller.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4b93d6d4-29b0-41bd-9bea-b785a0ca49cd"></p>
<p local-id=3D"3e43716a-51f8-4601-af45-306702e974ee">2025-04-21</p>
<p local-id=3D"98083d52-ce17-4b8d-9695-ee3cf4a04f08">To Do this Week:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"ff1658e8-3d8a-4a0b-8915-ac84d023d86e">
<li local-id=3D"1b4b6884-ab8f-40af-bc4b-bab17cf5e831">
<p local-id=3D"eb5d3752-853e-4100-86e3-618aa04d6d7c">New solenoid mount for=
 V3.6 - DONE</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"64c13008-4563-468d-920a-b67802f1fe7d">
<p local-id=3D"a72f9cfe-286c-420f-ba1b-5f64f8ea7253">Stepper tapper testing=
 - DONE</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ed044aa-03ed-434d-943b-5f044614f424">
<p local-id=3D"baca9947-6061-4681-a6fd-a6a6a8331855">New V3.1 hopper with l=
arger width aperture and roller lowered to minimize uncontrolled powder cap=
acity - DONE</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7e62ba98-4078-4612-8531-fdbbe75a2207">
<p local-id=3D"cdc3a8bc-ca2a-47d4-96bc-d74403bc437d">Micro Drop mount - Mou=
nt complete for Pourya=E2=80=99s gantry, not ready for installation on PILO=
T yet</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c0c80643-02da-4a32-89bd-f18db7264e47">
<li local-id=3D"bbace1bc-d791-497a-8bca-5ba8324f467b">
<p local-id=3D"e7f850f2-e1ca-400f-bb5d-e70391640034">Mount on reaming gantr=
y first then move to PILOT by end of week</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"245a9a46-1577-460a-a550-d4be8e2fadf7"></p>
<p local-id=3D"cf14ad13-7aa1-4a1d-9a5f-f1f849cacc92">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"4f16e7aa-53e3-407f-8b19-d5ad236bdc58">PILOT: Designed and or=
dered sheet metal panels for laser protection on PILOT 3.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8a6adcea-75e7-4c23-8bf4-4c142e19bc20">REDRESS: Ordered 10 kg=
s of MIM feedstock from <a href=3D"http://www.ryerinc.com/" local-id=3D"471=
66464-7f28-4167-a6a8-217d94159b40" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" class=3D=
"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">http://www.ryerinc.com/</a> (5kgs 1740-901=
6AA, $53.00 per kg, 5kgs CUMI-9016OS, $75.00 per kg)</p>
<p local-id=3D"ece08867-5d95-4b68-8638-b466e4fafe02"></p>
<p local-id=3D"c75def18-af17-4f3e-a075-d06c92bf0cba">2025-04-22</p>
<p local-id=3D"ae6a748d-b825-4ceb-948e-8eb6cd33ae2e">REDRESS: Mixed up a ba=
tch of powder using a new recipe that eliminates the plasticizer and increa=
ses the TEG-DMA content:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"78ded6e3-fd04-4886-a81a-c39be10c5317" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-AquaMold=E2=84=A2BinderRecipeforWater-SolubleMoldMetalForming(OptimizedV=
ersion).1">AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Binder Recipe for Water-Soluble Mold Metal For=
ming (Optimized Version)</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"a3977fb5-170d-47bb-ab19-9cd40c7830c0" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.2">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"aade2c50-7618-4be4-99f6-b0e99833907c" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalPowderMixture(97%Metal,3%Binder).1">For 1000g Final Me=
tal Powder Mixture (97% Metal, 3% Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5b0d82e8-583d-49cd-ba0e-b67afebd0332"><strong>Metal Powder</=
strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"233e997d-1752-46f6-bd5b-40094c7ae2d4">
<li local-id=3D"340b7a6e-f07b-4987-aa31-2d5c8cb6e9f9">
<p local-id=3D"cb222119-76e4-40a4-9289-90c0624f25e4">970g of metal powder (=
17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"490ece06-c499-4c1b-bff0-4fd809018e11"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (30g total)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b964f85c-5f2e-4e6e-bf98-d87a95bbb56c">
<li local-id=3D"0dd00a92-5aaf-4c7a-9172-487915806233">
<p local-id=3D"6f396c23-cfdb-4155-a6b2-a4b243360df7">25.2g Poly(methyl meth=
acrylate-co-ethyl acrylate) (84% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4d5f4db2-3c01-4fe3-b6c9-2751cc11bac2">
<p local-id=3D"20d241eb-a662-4d96-bca0-a82654c80f8e">3.0g Triethylene glyco=
l dimethacrylate (10% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"280bf59b-72ca-4ede-8be1-4e78326b3f76">
<p local-id=3D"f32dd0fe-58a2-4481-834c-4f487b531637">1.2g 3-(Trimethoxysily=
l)propyl methacrylate (4% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"05b67129-74f2-46fb-9e5b-7f49657e4cfa">
<p local-id=3D"9b9bd3a5-92d7-489f-8e02-7118233de6ef">0.6g 2,2=E2=80=B2-Azob=
is(2-methylpropionitrile) (AIBN) (2% of binder)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"24bb81e3-e481-4891-8744-6746b634e9a6"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"2b511ebe-7739-4222-8b9b-63a61bbb01e4">
<li local-id=3D"1756315d-3c01-4222-a53c-9eb4886ed82f">
<p local-id=3D"42819be8-de6d-4aa9-a86b-1a54f752e0ea">270-300g Acetone (9-10=
:1 ratio with binder solids)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"1982d67f-f1cb-4bee-8936-62fdbbbde9e6" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Equipment.2">Equipment</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"aa4491b8-5d22-4571-a22f-84b864314594">
<li local-id=3D"878e37ba-f9d8-4d6d-a562-4ffd28f89508">
<p local-id=3D"b45dd9bb-59e5-41f6-a55c-75cbe99eba74">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"59e7f9b4-deb5-417a-a588-750e2624e350">
<p local-id=3D"f7274e27-6a56-45e0-ab67-9aa225937060">Glass containers with =
tight-fitting lids</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"37d595bc-ed26-4f8c-b92f-57fe03eeff01">
<p local-id=3D"9c15d41b-e57e-4de4-a9a5-4ca3fb038e99">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"24afdce4-48e4-4324-9156-073294518675">
<p local-id=3D"f26074b6-10f9-4a38-89f9-2fb437f2bb80">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8f16584b-10ee-4507-99f3-cd8520004bc9">
<p local-id=3D"2e2b67c7-3277-4b9b-a625-40d917dbba18">Controlled temperature=
 oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"37a42934-c7ed-453b-ba16-c0430528ec21">
<p local-id=3D"0fddf04e-6b1b-4eff-93d0-ec7e7d2ab47f">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a2f47a50-3786-43c0-ba84-b545a0c6fe31">
<p local-id=3D"0973b61c-99c9-4c12-a4a9-7b0927f2fecb">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"90a891ab-e12e-4477-98fa-eebf03820eda">
<p local-id=3D"afc08aae-a131-42ba-a0d6-db083e959295">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2e15b17f-6820-4674-8ad5-7efe1b4e868b">
<p local-id=3D"4878e9dd-468e-4f8a-9b2b-ec213df7de67">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"dd950d70-ca9e-4128-886a-258982c52d78" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.2">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"844bd19a-530f-4656-955b-1ac7a3e731d6" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.BinderPreparation.2">A. Binder Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"1e2f244e-4896-499d-b06a-540636e64619">
<li local-id=3D"6eddcfa1-ef42-4833-ad66-1ae2b6483ddc">
<p local-id=3D"3a0a743c-9da6-46cd-afb0-5570cf04501e">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 270g of acetone into a glass container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"23231413-afcc-46a2-a541-978058977e69">
<p local-id=3D"b672c0f0-ec11-48ce-9d07-f75862607d6a">While stirring, slowly=
 add 25.2g of PMMA-co-EA to the acetone. Stir until completely dissolved (a=
pproximately 30-60 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ed2d42e1-3c3a-464e-b61c-c97d07f13035">
<p local-id=3D"4bbf006b-a93c-4630-98bc-1be56527f839">Add 1.2g of 3-(Trimeth=
oxysilyl)propyl methacrylate to the solution and stir for 15 minutes.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"f4488cc5-efd8-4751-9c1b-bccaa165ca06">
<p local-id=3D"b348876e-8a11-442e-8e9d-a59797b4b64f">Add 3.0g of TEG-DMA an=
d stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dc4135ea-4972-4978-a6b6-7d35f5e70c69">
<p local-id=3D"c6e39e69-8028-4151-b415-85c05f53a690">Finally, add 0.6g of A=
IBN and stir gently until completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3507a771-5469-4561-a98e-f0bba9bf8ae9">
<p local-id=3D"c1ae476a-f04b-4d9e-8df1-fffe65976f18">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation. The binder solution =
is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"fcd1080c-8388-4e88-8e8c-38956cb753e2" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.SlurryPreparation.2">B. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"d3154708-3739-4f5d-9b25-677db80b00a9">
<li local-id=3D"cc148bb6-553f-4ed3-9e13-6e3034fb109f">
<p local-id=3D"ec2badc0-354e-40ae-9c93-ca26107888bf">Place 970g of metal po=
wder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"17a96532-32cd-4249-8403-3edc2a7896c2">
<p local-id=3D"17d8efaa-d003-46ed-b093-f5ed6b7a463a">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the metal powder.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"14991280-f02d-4fdc-90a1-88146ea09de7">
<p local-id=3D"931d0e48-ce75-4d85-af4b-44383a8f590e">Continue mixing for 30=
-45 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0d91192e-0c24-47d1-915f-a7f4b59abd38">
<p local-id=3D"5b9df3ea-b1c8-4201-8f7e-a8ac99bc5f5d">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 30g) to achieve p=
roper consistency.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"585673c2-3c14-4281-a3c8-b392bfce61df" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.Drying.2">C. Drying</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"70c4b724-cebf-4ba8-b58e-f9d4b16c7a7f">
<li local-id=3D"32ce8643-ad43-4b64-8bff-16516898ce8c">
<p local-id=3D"5d76fb23-46e3-492a-afcc-bb283392e61a">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bbe504bc-43eb-4d35-b08f-a00ea4dd9bd6">
<p local-id=3D"048d7641-8780-4e0b-83bb-53fa11d997e7">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature in a well-ventilated area for 12-24 hours.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"0581d9c8-93c9-4a9d-b6f0-46a154fc94ce">
<p local-id=3D"1db0df27-b94c-4da1-a3a6-fd25f714ddf9">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 50=C2=B0C for 4-6 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"23226309-37e8-4708-b5c3-d9ea9bc47878">
<p local-id=3D"5c49ca80-29ec-431b-af8b-5f52b94d4dd0">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 60=C2=B0C for 2 hours to ensure complete solvent removal.</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3f748dac-560b-4273-ab39-2ca769eb8a1b">
<p local-id=3D"09f31f07-1091-4fa1-9db0-39776643c9f1">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid cake.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"8d9c3e2d-9a37-45ae-a31c-cfbd254a3cde" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.GrindingandSieving.2">D. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7aa49990-b3bf-47ea-a191-ddbc7d5c13f3">
<li local-id=3D"60111b7f-dcb7-4b08-938c-d96d18a7d530">
<p local-id=3D"3414badf-6955-44de-a58e-ee799a693b89">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"03ca9d5e-9bf6-4450-9ebb-c128c680635b">
<p local-id=3D"9755a9bc-695e-4039-a55c-8b8f1f6192e9">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill under controlled temperature conditions (below 40=C2=B0C=
 to prevent premature crosslinking).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"647e9be2-1c7b-4eb2-836d-c4462b514a87">
<p local-id=3D"6f40350a-b4aa-4092-91d8-6bda28837413">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
 for application).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6facf186-995b-46f0-955d-b66369eef04b">
<p local-id=3D"58c301d8-2695-4609-8181-2d8e321d4b71">If necessary, add 0.05=
-0.1g of Aerosil (0.005-0.01% of total weight) to improve flowability.</p><=
/li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"41bd9072-1164-40d9-a868-e5d5caee7e43" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.TheAquaMold=E2=84=A2Process.2">E. The AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Process</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"8664dced-79c3-437c-949c-4d2a8b32b788">
<li local-id=3D"d265f654-7407-45b2-b2e8-f8d7543195ee">
<p local-id=3D"ce413b00-36bf-4fbb-b143-6ba385ebbff6">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8c0dd01a-a4bb-4d22-9c0c-4b127b26474a">
<p local-id=3D"2c87e375-e57a-4063-8011-98bd26529060">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"332ba053-c334-47eb-8aa5-cd4cb6399cd0">
<p local-id=3D"74b46033-d4e5-438c-9a30-e9eb116cc699">Heat the packed molds =
to 80=C2=B0C and maintain this temperature for 1.5 hours to activate the AI=
BN and crosslink the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d9141b4f-88b0-422e-a632-3ca22e467fa5">
<p local-id=3D"fd954228-1c31-4c53-8085-c9e833c8f100">Cool gradually to room=
 temperature (approximately 1-2 hours).</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"81b02d9c-017a-4aaa-bcb1-fc095eae46a5" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.DissolutionandGreenPartRecovery.2">F. Dissolution and Green Part Recov=
ery</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"74a0409e-bd3e-4d74-bd5d-c281d5205503">
<li local-id=3D"d8023a13-1ae5-4f50-b5f3-930870e79069">
<p local-id=3D"4a023000-270b-4b0e-aa2f-13866b41b0da">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in warm water (40-50=C2=B0C) to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"636e3879-be6a-4d21-bb2e-5db419117c11">
<p local-id=3D"55066a72-ff05-431a-bc98-46432dc25a23">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh water as needed until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"710acdb2-36d2-4606-bb7d-088f7cc8d72b">
<p local-id=3D"8a0ddb6d-f036-49e3-a8a6-6d4edb319b2f">Carefully extract the =
green part from the water bath and allow to dry completely.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ba9c6a62-21e0-4632-ad3a-98bd676eff1f">
<p local-id=3D"2fc66503-f65b-457a-89eb-3cae4fecc256">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to your standard protocol for t=
he specific metal alloy.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"eb400bfc-0b90-42c8-ba77-3672c36c4e0f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Notes.2">Notes</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"1dab2868-1458-408c-bcd0-c7c8782508b2">
<li local-id=3D"e239e6c9-0e98-4a25-9f3d-5523a2709b65">
<p local-id=3D"f331628e-1663-4c1d-9672-b94ae76372e4">The increased TEG-DMA =
content (10% of binder vs previous 6%) will create a more highly crosslinke=
d polymer network, which may:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"439806b4-abcc-4be8-ba82-badbae5a36b4">
<li local-id=3D"eca2e23d-69e8-465c-9827-1f29096f384c">
<p local-id=3D"0d8e1e3c-7724-4565-bf36-7062be65bed1">Increase green part st=
rength</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e7e86915-ce9c-42cc-a781-5a842685d190">
<p local-id=3D"48855c90-1adc-493c-acd3-235eecb99a35">Reduce flexibility com=
pared to the plasticized version</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1ed3aca9-cffe-4d4b-abfb-0a810154db0c">
<p local-id=3D"af22c389-844d-417c-9442-d6094edbfc85">Potentially increase r=
esistance to deformation during handling</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a2fbaa9a-4062-498f-9ce5-d522d63d0051">
<p local-id=3D"02165e1f-6f9f-4e10-bdd1-604e8465562e">Result in slightly dif=
ferent debinding characteristics</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"91e6fdd4-4710-402e-8875-145f152f6fbf">
<p local-id=3D"6cf4ab89-1907-41e2-a00b-7cf0f7e54b96">Maintaining the full 4=
% of silane coupling agent ensures good adhesion between the metal particle=
s and polymer binder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0a4b872c-0e36-414b-91f3-da8473f93baf">
<p local-id=3D"edd7b4f8-c911-47c4-8ab4-8e235322215b">The removal of the pla=
sticizer and increased crosslinking agent will likely create a more rigid g=
reen part</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ff5b0a62-7488-4053-a734-0f18f94d55e4">
<p local-id=3D"20cd32c9-dfdd-4b44-ba86-0c7a15e0738b">You may need to adjust=
 packing parameters to ensure uniform density with this more rigid binder s=
ystem</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"71bafd0a-d314-458c-83a7-6aa1e9654e13">
<p local-id=3D"4a12cd87-470a-4aa8-80ec-dffa343e44f1">The higher crosslink d=
ensity may affect the debinding profile - consider a more gradual temperatu=
re ramp during initial debinding stages</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"abf0ef03-2533-441c-ac82-4de706e580b3">
<p local-id=3D"e097bb34-45a8-4ebf-8c0f-4f70e7de1a33">Store the AIBN in a co=
ol, dark place to prevent premature decomposition</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3d7eaf9a-429e-40b9-9e75-97b2177e169f">
<p local-id=3D"08698e5f-fdd4-481f-81ee-e885c062b649">All mixing containers =
should be clean and free of contaminants</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a3f74e6-f82c-4320-8699-31adebcfd7ea">
<p local-id=3D"58a360c5-e9e3-48b7-b21d-d64c43ff0c71">Perform all solvent ha=
ndling steps in a well-ventilated area away from ignition sources</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"5f20709f-55ef-4386-a884-4950e064af92"></p>
<p local-id=3D"38d2231e-8b81-4c14-a0e4-b3d2e2ef5bf8">I am also continuing t=
o experiment with the batch that I made 2kg of (I think it might be a combi=
nation of several previous batches that I had made? I=E2=80=99m not 100% ce=
rtain of the additive composition, but it is definitely PMMA-EA based). Las=
t night I mixed some hydrophobic aerosil with the powder in the v mixer and=
 had Nick resieve the powder this morning, then filled a water-soluble mold=
 and a ceramic crucible with it. I am currently running the PMMA cycle in t=
he upper Keith furnace, but I reduced the peak temperature from 300F to 275=
F to minimize mold distortion. The powder flowed really well when I was fil=
ling the two receptacles, so I think adding Aerosil and in particular mixin=
g the powder well makes a big difference.</p>
<p local-id=3D"489afe8f-9a58-4d7e-b0bf-d7718fe2d0aa">I am also drying the 2=
kg cake I made with PVP-VA in the oven in the materials lab. I want to try =
it in PILOT 3 using the laser to cure the desired part outline. PVP-VA coat=
ed powder did very well in producing strong heat cured green parts, but it =
was not compatible with my Aquamold process because it is water soluble. Ho=
wever, it should work well with the laser curing process because the parts =
do not need to be waterproof. The laser curing process should eliminate the=
 need for spraying or cutting and will not produce debris that would need t=
o be vacuumed up like laser cutting the outlines of a part. It would also e=
liminate the need to cure the entire layer (although this could be done usi=
ng the standard heater if necessary).</p>
<p local-id=3D"c61cd111-b4e7-4cf1-83ee-c1d8f1989258">HOPPER: I have printed=
 the parts for the update version of Payman=E2=80=99s hopper design. There =
are some McMaster parts I need to order tonight to be able to assemble it, =
and I am still waiting on more stepper motors from StepperOnline, but I can=
 install the heat set inserts today. The heat set inserts have been install=
ed, so I should be able to reassemble</p>
<p local-id=3D"831ebc52-8900-44e6-a177-5b15626faf5b">NEXTGEN: I have design=
ed and printed the gantry mount for holding the spindle and Micro Drop wax =
dispenser, although Sean and Pourya are encountering issues with getting th=
e Micro Drop system to dispense drops of paraffin, so it is unclear when th=
e mount will become necessary.</p>
<p local-id=3D"78c2aa79-229e-4333-ae9a-dd4d84775e4e"></p>
<p local-id=3D"64ec65c7-17e5-474d-934f-24814f459c4c">2025-04-23</p>
<p local-id=3D"8dd2662e-0b6d-4cb3-b133-418315d4585e">HOPPER: Assembling Pay=
man=E2=80=99s hopper. I have the bushings installed (I am switching from be=
arings to bushings on the hopper to reduce cost and volume of the rotating =
component support element. I am also switching to larger timing belt pulley=
s to increase the number of teeth engaged at any given time and hopefully r=
educe belt slippage. Since we don=E2=80=99t have enough geared NEMA 8 stepp=
er motors around I am going to scavenge one from Payman=E2=80=99s current h=
opper, but I am holding off until Payman demos the hopper for Scott.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2eb8c233-972a-4191-81e7-683521b01df6">I am continuing to dev=
elop the stepper tapper system. I have it working with one of the 19:1 gear=
ed NEMA 8 stepper motors, but it is limited in the speed it can move the im=
pact arm and I am concerned about tearing up the gear box since the stepper=
 tapping cycle involves stalling the motor to home the arm and every time i=
t impacts the shaft; the way the cycle works it drives the motor slightly p=
ast where it contacts the shaft. I found a NEMA 11 motor around that seems =
to be functional so I have designed a mount for it and a new stepper tapper=
 arm to use with it. Hopefully this new system will enable a higher frequen=
cy of impacts and greater impact force with less likelihood of damage to th=
e stepper system because there is no gearbox. Assembled the new motor and s=
tepper tapper arm on HOPPER V4.0. The NEMA 11 motor seems to work as expect=
ed. It does protrude farther from the hopper than the NEMA 8 motor does.</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"734b3000-93bb-4954-b9d1-c1b9fc46703c">REDRESS: I have tasked=
 Mohsen with trying out a batch of PVP-VA coated powder in the laser-enable=
d PILOT printer (PILOT 3). He is trying various laser parameters to try and=
 selectively cure the powder where we would want a part to be if we were pr=
inting a part.</p>
<p local-id=3D"041e3a15-0c8e-4b0e-9ac1-490ec3e60024">The batch of PMMA powd=
er I mixed up yesterday dried on the hot plate overnight, and after running=
 it in the v-mixer for a while I am drying it in the oven in the materials =
lab. The reason it had be dried initially on the hot plate is because it us=
es acetone as a solvent, which would be unsafe to vaporize in the materials=
 lab oven. Once it has dried sufficiently (likely this afternoon) I will gr=
ind and sieve it. Since it has twice the TEG-DMA that the previous batch di=
d, I am hopeful that it will produce stronger green parts (I dissolved off =
the mold I filled yesterday and the green part mostly fell apart). I put 30=
g of this powder into a ceramic crucible and tapped it, then crash heated i=
t to 275F (it usually overshoots with crash heating so it may have gone ove=
r, on the other hand I only gave it 30 minutes to get to 275 so it may have=
 undershot the temperature). The green part produced was still not as stron=
g as I=E2=80=99d like, but it is considerably stronger than the previous ba=
tch while still being fairly flowable. I have a suspicion that at least som=
e of the =E2=80=9Csticky=E2=80=9D powder I have seen in the past was simply=
 not sufficiently dried and/or did not have sufficient flow aid added.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6847e7d3-cf8f-4ab6-8015-b7ea89bcf6e6"></p>
<p local-id=3D"39a6f944-bb09-46b2-a525-e78ee9fda83f">2025-04-24</p>
<p local-id=3D"23458a27-0797-45af-a174-5522b6d04884">AEM PXL: Meeting with =
AEM. There wasn=E2=80=99t anything they wanted us to do on the project, so =
at the moment we=E2=80=99re trying to move forward with some low-cost IR&am=
p;D projects, including initial in-house brazing with BAg-7 braze alloy (wh=
ich is in theory compatible with bare copper and bare stainless steel), ele=
ctron beam welding of bare copper coupons to stainless steel (we may need t=
o do a shrink-fit of the copper parts to get the zero gap that electron bea=
m welders prefer), and also experiments to confirm that the vacuum impregna=
tion resin is compatible with the HFE coolant that AEM wants to use.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5dd0932d-464b-41b2-b959-92ab63712a61">HOPPER: Continued test=
ing of stepper tapper with NEMA 11 motor.</p>
<p local-id=3D"209a14f1-0d23-480d-8647-e85c83347a22"></p>
<p local-id=3D"48f54132-1ac4-4d68-bb26-303a9f9f7922">2025-04-25</p>
<p local-id=3D"735bd7fd-f466-48eb-9f37-940e74154fef">HOPPER: HOPPER V3.5 ru=
nning on PILOT 2. Dispensed a layer of powder. The stepper tapper is not ru=
nning yet pending Pourya wiring a new expansion board, but even without it =
the powder was flowable enough to dispense reasonably well.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ff2bf6f4-c491-4a2f-817b-3994ae37558c"></p>
<p local-id=3D"e6a7f11f-db7b-41f9-86c8-58a66a901626">2025-04-28</p>
<p local-id=3D"7b97f031-258f-4f0d-8e27-3b01684ec636">R&amp;D Meeting</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4d923448-cb96-4368-952c-b7a9a52e12c8">
<li local-id=3D"62861708-0bc6-451e-a382-0afae6ce2c63">
<p local-id=3D"42aa703c-2d03-4410-a9cf-657439e78f6b">HOPPER: HOPPER V3.6 ru=
nning in PILOT 2. Stepper tapper is installed but not tested with integrate=
d control system.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7d8b1be0-ac13-4681-aa2d-08d006cfdb22">
<p local-id=3D"ae3635d1-fdb8-4110-8b02-a44aff8d1c26">NEXTGEN: Ordered laser=
 safety windows for Ultimaker hopper. Micro Drop wax dispenser received and=
 Pourya is in process of testing it on the old reaming gantry. Mohsen is co=
ntinuing experiments with the xTool F1 Ultra laser in PILOT 3.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ee205d0-c1cd-4250-ae0e-8784949e02a5">
<p local-id=3D"04f58b07-3457-4965-b0d9-bfc4c3e5ff7e">PILOT Ultra: System ru=
nning on old reaming gantry (blue and silver, rollers on frame. Sean is wor=
king on building the same system</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d687be43-f4ce-4f51-8a65-56418465e9ee">TO DO:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4127721a-a27f-4213-a0d1-fc1000d47396">
<li local-id=3D"5e622db6-2621-41d8-85d4-ef7b79203275">
<p local-id=3D"8cee40b9-1dad-4f14-8e96-721ed80d7346">Assemble HOPPER V4.0 a=
nd install in PILOT 2 replacing V3.6.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"aee0effb-6b1c-46d7-a5a0-f3773b132a2c">
<li local-id=3D"18fb81e8-c731-486e-b5b0-dae0cbb568b0">
<p local-id=3D"a44fa816-c179-4597-87dc-2651d79a3e65">Installed in PILOT 2, =
but the dispense rate is too high with the machined timing belt pulley roll=
er so I am printing a new roller that should dispense at a lower rate.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3c6e6be5-0383-4da3-824f-0751ef047d9f">
<li local-id=3D"2996060b-3830-4883-bb7d-81ec775f33bb">
<p local-id=3D"7992c116-55b1-47ab-9e13-dff86d27ee2a">Roller dispense rate i=
s high and uneven due to discretization of dispensing regions (</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"d3535cba-aa55-4c79-a1bb-d44e379e4756">
<p local-id=3D"8ec8acb1-beca-4183-b099-7a2d7d19aa93">New mount for laser on=
 PILOT 3.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"77012f5d-5345-4302-96ac-bb6c4c41398d">
<p local-id=3D"15b12e5f-56b5-4e69-af96-63124638d4bd">Once sheet metal has b=
een received, paint and install.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c765c7c9-da19-4e0c-9c89-b1a52a114424">
<p local-id=3D"370dd42c-8fe0-4ad6-8ef2-22a568ae7880">Make new HOPPER V3.1.1=
 with smaller valve - DONE</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"54ed05cd-a054-4793-a4df-2ff0b60a31cf">
<p local-id=3D"d35d5c8e-8cf6-40fb-a59a-a8250bd2f70a">2 new mist boxes with =
a smaller length of mist deposition to match the spreader bar on the HOPPER=
 - DONE</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"99fbb141-760b-4fe8-a490-148102b377fc">
<p local-id=3D"1e19c8eb-20f4-45a8-9855-25a8d48a47df">New stepper motor moun=
t that provides adjustable belt tension</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"331a6988-736b-4bed-99d1-933ad3e1a22a">ULTRA: Designing 2X ne=
w mist boxes for the blue gantry ULTRA system: one has the mist chamber len=
gth reduced from 130 to 125mm to match the spreader bar on HOPPER V3.1.1 (t=
he line of dispense on HOPPER V3.1.1 is 130mm but the spreader bar is 125mm=
 long, I don=E2=80=99t recall a good reason for that being the case so I pl=
an to modify that in the future). The other mist box has the same dimension=
s but the width of the mist chamber is increased from 35mm to 75mm.</p>
<p local-id=3D"edc10dc2-bc94-4359-a910-3a98153e1cd6">Need a picture of vari=
ous HOPPER iterations for the board meeting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e51a54de-ad55-4af0-8a94-c38e102c177f">REDRESS: Making a new =
batch of powder by pre-treating 1 kg of 17-4 powder with 2g of silane coupl=
ing agent, drying it, then mixing it with 15g PVP-VA dissolved in 200 ml of=
 water. I am also seeing some promising initial results from the latest adv=
anced binder batch; this one used 26.4 g PMMA-EA, 4g TEG-DMA, and 1g AIBN. =
It seems to form the strongest green parts of the PMMA batches so far, alth=
ough the powder is stickier and less flowable with the higher TEG-DMA conte=
nt.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1cd4e888-2558-4a36-a1ea-590f9a338f71"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1e6b47a3-655a-4687-b6cd-55ba275cc313">2025-04-29</p>
<p local-id=3D"831eb8c7-120d-4258-ba26-bf07d42e4b5e">ULTRA: Completed post-=
processing of 2X mist boxes (V2 and V2.1) and installed heat set inserts, t=
hen gave them to Payman.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"cbbf1267-9cbe-4418-90ce-391a13eb3d13">
<li local-id=3D"c98151c9-dbbe-438b-b23b-b518f85ae691">
<p local-id=3D"58c38c5a-7410-4b84-81e5-b6dfac90f9ac">Make duplicate HOPPER =
V3.1.1 for the Ultimaker ULTRA printer</p>
<ul local-id=3D"e62ab2be-0d73-4608-8f9d-92bb14a699e4">
<li local-id=3D"72be7260-1d35-4632-85e7-70b336f48ee4">
<p local-id=3D"afbece60-97c9-48ac-b1ef-fcee85126601">Body</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5ab3566a-730a-4b25-b235-5dda03b4425a">
<p local-id=3D"79871754-9310-4a9f-a035-bd6937c134c8">Valve</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3fdd169f-4263-40af-8f54-827be2445caf">
<p local-id=3D"41048988-6d07-45a3-a285-a773eae89842">End Caps</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"de329363-d22b-4bdc-a980-5e33a4478ea9">
<p local-id=3D"2a697434-d2c9-4777-9a93-c6d0fb350770">Motor mount</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2b96d533-fbde-46b3-9e25-70e83a397131">
<p local-id=3D"13974b7e-abfc-48d7-a93d-f2d6b9a528f9">Order timing pulleys a=
nd belt</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"9ac0fe18-7cd7-420a-bff8-1f3a4ad08a32">HOPPER: Installed new =
PETG-CF printed roller in HOPPER V4.0 and reinstalled the roller drive moto=
r and stepper tapper. Since I do not believe the tapper system to be necess=
ary or even beneficial, I am adding a vibrator motor per the suggestions of=
 Dan, my experience of controlling powder flow for the robotic cleaning sta=
tion, and the design of every commercially available hopper on the market (=
to the best of my knowledge; I will admit that I don=E2=80=99t know the det=
ailed design of every hopper that is commercially available). Reinstalled H=
OPPER V4.0 and loaded it with powder after mounting the vibrator motor. The=
 vibration is strong enough and the powder flowable enough that it will flo=
w around the doser roller even when the roller is stationary; this effect c=
ould be useful or detrimental. Either way, it is likely caused by too large=
 of a gap between the roller and the body.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d377991a-e2b5-4242-9a3d-141678dc89a2">REDRESS: I demolded th=
e part cured last night using the latest formula, and it only lost a bit of=
 material on the top and bottom. I have also cured another part with the sa=
me powder after it had been dried overnight in the oven in the materials la=
b and had .1g more Aerosil R 812 S added to it. Either or both of those mad=
e it much more flowable when filling the mold, and the part being demolded =
looks promising so far. I also used a slightly different procedure to demol=
d the second part; I clamped it so that it was immersed in water up to ~2mm=
 below the top of the part until the mold had mostly dissolved into strings=
, instead of immediately dunking it in water. I believe this may reduce str=
ess on the top surface of the part by allowing the porous part to fill up w=
ith water more slowly as the mold dissolves.</p>
<p local-id=3D"10521807-067f-4cd3-aa79-e38f5a9373ad"></p>
<p local-id=3D"eb87d449-2e44-4bee-bf7f-a4e5dc1c547e">2025-04-30</p>
<p local-id=3D"e93d2d1e-2660-4219-b4f7-04ffbaa62bab">HOPPER: Tested HOPPER =
V4.0 with new doser roller. This is an octagonal faceted design; it dispens=
ed less than the aluminum doser roller but dispensed in pulses when the fac=
ets were aligned with the output region. I am printing a new doser roller t=
hat has a large number of very shallow grooves (5mm dia, .3mm depth cut int=
o roller).</p>
<p local-id=3D"a2aaa500-9f17-4b40-b153-0a4bfe7807de"></p>
<p local-id=3D"55de22cf-a7de-4bcc-9fd9-cb49aac03f94">2025-05-01</p>
<p local-id=3D"0be91a7a-f719-4f36-a4e8-b15e9bb54ab3">HOPPER: Removed facete=
d roller and installed grooved roller, then reinstalled HOPPER V4.0 in PILO=
T 2. I also showed the system to Mohsen and described the macros that show =
how to trigger the roller (A axis), stepper tapper (B axis), and vibrator (=
M42 to trigger GPIO pin 14, I think). I also renamed some of the macros to =
be less confusing, because I am using the output that Pourya had previously=
 wired up for the solenoid tapper.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6e26aacc-e9ff-4336-a0df-c53e46aee2e7">PILOT 3: Painting 4X s=
heet metal panels and plastic panel to cover the end of the machine that is=
 not shielded by the control cabinet. All 5 panels are painted, although th=
e finish is not completely uniform; you can see lines between paint passes =
and the paint on one of the panels was damaged when it fell onto asphalt be=
cause it was resting up against a box at an angle to dry both sides and it =
was a windy day. Once the panels have dried, I will smooth out that side wi=
th some steel wool and add another coat of paint.</p>
<p local-id=3D"90b0b806-9010-43ca-bdf0-25cbe9754f28">REDRESS: A part came o=
ut of sintering this morning, and looks pretty good. There are regions on t=
he top and bottom that are missing, but that occurred when dissolving off t=
he water soluble mold, not during debinding or sintering. The part did not =
collapse or crack, however, there was some distortion of the base, which ma=
y have been due to the fact that it was not resting level on the ZTE setter=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"17d4c513-2e9f-4441-9f15-2cbedfe42094">AEM PXL Meeting w/Crai=
g: They haven=E2=80=99t officially severed the relationship with 3DEO, but =
they are pursuing making another monolithic machined unit (1 SS part, 1 Cu =
part) and a P52 with 52 machined units. These may perform worse than PXLs m=
ade with 3DEO printed copper parts, but they may be willing to take the per=
formance hit if brazing works more reliably. Also, the thermal conductivity=
 of billet machined pure copper parts will be slightly higher than 3DEO=E2=
=80=99s parts, which will help to offset the loss of performance due to sub=
-optimal geometry.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6061cc64-f5e0-413e-b70e-dea2b8319ffe"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1429cdc9-040f-43d5-ba5b-700935dcdffd">2025-05-02</p>
<p local-id=3D"76e49d11-0c31-4e30-8a1c-1021e3d9aa9d">PILOT: 5 panels are pr=
inted and ready to be installed on PILOT 3. In process of printing the lase=
r shielding window frames.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c84f81e3-e275-4415-b902-27cbeb398241">HOPPER: HOPPER V4.0 is=
 running on PILOT 2. The dispense is uneven long the dispense line, so I am=
 going to print a new hopper body and roller that should dispense more even=
ly. The body that is currently installed was printed in two stages because =
it ran out filament halfway through the print, and the second half of the p=
rint seems slightly shifted from the first.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0e71f788-5ebc-476f-b27c-10f570569a3c"></p>
<p local-id=3D"171ecff8-4503-48aa-87e6-e2a97b4e5547">2025-05-05</p>
<p local-id=3D"21a9f4a1-2f0b-492f-892a-e1c7fea4c98c">PILOT: New HOPPER body=
 (v4.0) printed to install on PILOT 2 along with a new roller that is small=
 enough to spin freely. Designing mount for extra Z stage for the Micro Dro=
p head on PILOT 1. Mount is currently printing on the Bambu printer from PA=
HT-CF (CF nylon). There is a modified version of the cable carrier tower th=
at the 2nd Z stage mounts to, and a 3D printed part that mounts to that sta=
ge and to which the Micro Drop head is mounted.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f63bd11a-e196-4b99-8c78-96c055d1e0a9">ULTRA: Painted clear p=
anels on Ulimaker S5 cover black to block laser light during operation of t=
he Ultimaker-derived ULTRA printer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bf2ef2d4-a70e-4427-be00-02483d78cf71">REDRESS: Dissolved the=
 mold off of a green part over the weekend; the mold is the older style wit=
h the thinner fins but it seemed to come out pretty well regardless. The to=
p partially dissolved off; I think the may have to do with oxygen exposure =
during thermal curing so I am going to try placing a ceramic sheet on top o=
f the mold the next time I cure one to protect it from the atmosphere. I am=
 also working on grinding MIM feedstock pellets into a finer powder that my=
 extruder can handle using a coffee burr grinder. The pellet extruder mount=
 I am using melted from the heat of the hotend, so I am going to design and=
 print a new one from a higher temperature resistance SLA material. I am cu=
rrently printing it from PAHT-CF as part of the same print as the two Micro=
 Drop mounts; this should have a higher temperature resistance than the CF =
PLA I used previously. I also intend to attach the cooling fan to the heat =
break, which I failed to do previously (intentionally; I wanted to heat up =
the entire heat break to help soften the MIM feedstock, but this meant the =
heat break got hotter than it would otherwise, and when the heat was conduc=
ted through the shaft collar it softened the PLA mount to the point that th=
e force of the feedscrew pushed the two bolts holding the shaft collar thro=
ugh the PLA part). I have redesigned the mount to be stronger around the tw=
o mounting screws, and printing it from a higher temperature material shoul=
d help. I also have two new coated powder formulations I want to try. One i=
s similar to the previous one, but the powder is pre-treated with silane an=
d the binder load is reduced to 1% and the AIBN is replaced with a UV-activ=
ated photoinitiator:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"c96bb3f8-ef78-46a7-9b33-ec51b445de80" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Silane-EnhancedUV-CurableAquaMold=E2=84=A2BinderRecipeforWater-SolubleMo=
ldMetalForming">Silane-Enhanced UV-Curable AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Binder Recipe =
for Water-Soluble Mold Metal Forming</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"a9a9b2fb-6a76-4c7f-ada0-e52da1a3fad7" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.3">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"b962e4ce-505a-4b86-a870-21c1d92fd787" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ForMetalPowderPre-Treatment">For Metal Powder Pre-Treatment</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"d9164033-c02a-43f3-8b50-bbb66f8c62d0">
<li local-id=3D"92ee7714-e914-414d-a571-d278f9ad531f">
<p local-id=3D"64c5fa33-ef26-4d8e-a786-9d41452c9eb8">990g of metal powder (=
choose one: 17-4 PH stainless steel, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"edba1356-f837-4347-9f7e-6c3c2f5c09d0">
<p local-id=3D"cf9ad8fc-4084-4526-90a5-5fc06c9f6fdc">1g of 3-(Trimethoxysil=
yl)propyl methacrylate (=CE=B3-MPS)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"190ed052-08b5-4af2-8b35-defbef2cb687">
<p local-id=3D"9618d279-d607-41e6-802d-7b904dc17085">100mL of Isopropyl Alc=
ohol (IPA)</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"817cbbb1-758e-44c8-9442-a60f1f16c2f1" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalPowderMixture(99%Metal,1%Binder)">For 1000g Final Meta=
l Powder Mixture (99% Metal, 1% Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5d065761-386a-4ebd-b4cc-e081b9ff061b"><strong>Pre-treated Me=
tal Powder</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"19a31ed6-9980-444e-812c-fe8b18308db7">
<li local-id=3D"b1b27639-2325-446f-b726-310b837cd831">
<p local-id=3D"ab1453bd-0e42-4ebe-9966-32767a860c04">990g of silane-treated=
 metal powder</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"ba2f5b89-737a-4757-9622-a0f35269eb13"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (10g total - 1% of final mixture)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"1b055ef3-0651-4653-9094-e8bda7fa495b">
<li local-id=3D"0f53ea11-82e9-4fef-aca6-e215d2fbed15">
<p local-id=3D"1ea69662-c53d-40de-9076-a48ea9c56e5a">8.2g Poly(methyl metha=
crylate) (PMMA) (82% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cf510f87-e83c-49be-97cb-9787aa1b3670">
<p local-id=3D"32f735f3-7af8-4c38-af18-134adb790020">1.5g Triethylene glyco=
l dimethacrylate (TEG-DMA) (15% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3aed3ab3-4a75-4dc0-8147-601199e8b322">
<p local-id=3D"a9fe1ac1-ac89-49be-8181-00f248396fdc">0.3g Phenylbis(2,4,6-t=
rimethylbenzoyl)phosphine oxide (TPO) (3% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7d2a3fbd-aabe-49a8-a728-8c9f93486d1a">
<p local-id=3D"543dbe5a-cfcf-4753-814b-b03a24db3f41">0.2g Aerosil R 812 S (=
to be added after grinding and sieving)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"29600b6a-e715-4cc2-b612-bcf1adccfe27"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d290d4ca-8e5c-4c9b-acd9-c7f37db41148">
<li local-id=3D"aa7066cd-ac50-4de9-82c2-df25f73a4cf7">
<p local-id=3D"ff4bc804-eef9-409f-b45e-5b8fdd991b27">90-100g Acetone (9-10:=
1 ratio with binder solids)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"44044e4e-eab5-472b-9f1d-035dbd64ecbc"><strong>Equipment</str=
ong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"acaa0da8-a949-4596-81a5-3a4f05fd68b5">
<li local-id=3D"377d3bc1-7aab-4166-8e08-c0c8d5a806a7">
<p local-id=3D"365265a9-6ced-4c4c-a59b-a7b57de0920c">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fb94b8cd-1c63-4f02-8168-76829a819ed3">
<p local-id=3D"a97291ed-9898-4e97-921f-05f481e8b7e4">Glass containers with =
amber/dark tinting or aluminum foil covering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8a9c5016-2e97-4131-a3d3-66f9e0becf4b">
<p local-id=3D"8098ce38-ec85-4889-8a77-4f3daf908c4a">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"da529660-9de9-445a-ac95-8355c9ae2328">
<p local-id=3D"f3d791a0-4185-477c-aed6-9317f8f74552">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6e6f0d33-9d65-45dc-9870-825ad44eb403">
<p local-id=3D"6aeabb5b-a267-4d7a-88c9-263e5faa0f68">Controlled temperature=
 oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b4191513-de66-44ec-a4ff-97c0470aa0ff">
<p local-id=3D"6c622a9f-b643-4eed-a695-ac59cc4e580b">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"658b6856-6646-4ac0-afb8-300622b29049">
<p local-id=3D"d9ad6fad-765b-4272-b917-5dcbba255258">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b7089933-828e-4921-9dc0-7af433ea4f05">
<p local-id=3D"c884db89-ad6f-4bbf-9ca5-aa3ee117f7d4">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"168e198a-b747-4d86-b5f5-a9eaea3ce982">
<p local-id=3D"d0cb5ee8-3594-4aad-8e94-bceaeee86e1c">UV light source (365-4=
05nm wavelength)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"524d00d2-3005-428d-860a-acb145982491">
<p local-id=3D"c5e0eb14-29a6-4dcb-bd62-67ff3b60728a">UV safety equipment (U=
V-blocking eyewear, gloves, covered skin)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9bdee2bc-9dc6-45ad-9634-f5030a2933e9">
<p local-id=3D"01b7ed93-8c77-4aa7-8735-b8c598aa0aa2">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"ec937dcc-5277-4185-80f6-fdd8189a09ec" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.3">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"105dda9f-ad8d-49f1-a487-38c2f901bb64" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.MetalPowderSilanePre-Treatment">A. Metal Powder Silane Pre-Treatment</=
h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b98411e2-9d31-445c-b9b3-2d1b5b9e6cc1">
<li local-id=3D"e73a6a90-6d48-4d76-9fec-f57e96bf36ff">
<p local-id=3D"779cb776-58af-474b-8608-7217b7a4fed7">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, add 1g of 3-(Trimethoxysilyl)propyl methacrylate to 100mL of isopropyl=
 alcohol in a suitable container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"39afcb5a-d893-4c62-8ea5-bed3ec23d16b">
<p local-id=3D"cf8834f8-1745-44e2-97f9-7f237a8f5f3a">Stir the solution gent=
ly for 5 minutes, then let it stand for 30 minutes to allow hydrolysis of t=
he silane coupling agent.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"33833559-dfd5-42cf-9281-3b3288d3a19e">
<p local-id=3D"7d49d76d-95ca-43df-84d4-91c9770df105">Place 990g of metal po=
wder in a large mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d0074d19-6fd7-48fc-81cd-45a831ca8f49">
<p local-id=3D"b0a1d8f7-a3c8-4edd-b77f-271d4e6a547f">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the hydrolyzed silane solution to the metal powder.</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ed487e8-2019-424b-92c1-b009f4c3260b">
<p local-id=3D"af7e4750-33f0-4e97-9c82-056210c120d5">Continue mixing for 15=
-20 minutes to ensure even distribution of the silane solution over all met=
al particles.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"27e561c6-43af-47e1-a06a-b48fb73a6be0">
<p local-id=3D"ef158885-a660-49f1-b48d-83ef800feac6">Spread the treated pow=
der on drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a7fcf29f-6ddf-4eb4-af1e-1f6f6cf67bcd">
<p local-id=3D"603a46c9-2826-4e9f-af55-5d000f0c44ab">Dry at 60=C2=B0C for 2=
-3 hours to remove the isopropyl alcohol.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c89ff4b2-208b-4374-9347-56a030a54233">
<p local-id=3D"330c738c-e2b6-42ed-baa3-61b423fe608e">Allow the treated powd=
er to cool to room temperature. The silane-treated metal powder is now read=
y for the binder application.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"d95a4af1-1b8e-4783-90cb-ac47ec8b1efe" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.BinderPreparation">B. Binder Preparation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"a732b780-9f18-4c5d-a7ff-28834c287897"><strong>IMPORTANT: Per=
form this step in subdued lighting or yellow lighting to prevent premature =
activation of the photoinitiator</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"0b1e4b6b-8d23-4efd-b9cd-4784205b1dea">
<li local-id=3D"1d2cab8e-d620-48ba-a18c-4b022c5be3ed">
<p local-id=3D"86f2e57b-a2f7-4f3d-8f43-8dd2ce95b426">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 90g of acetone into an amber glass container or a container wrap=
ped in aluminum foil.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e7336894-1f80-4a8f-8b46-ff030adf12ec">
<p local-id=3D"af5060e2-ec1b-4acc-a529-9e91d08da38f">While stirring, slowly=
 add 8.2g of PMMA to the acetone. Stir until completely dissolved (approxim=
ately 30-60 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"82cd0d29-ca32-4463-bdb5-23634c2150ca">
<p local-id=3D"2c03efa0-bd6a-4404-8ced-d03ccd70610d">Add 1.5g of TEG-DMA an=
d stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"78507d14-9233-4c98-9305-c9b3eb4566ce">
<p local-id=3D"081276a9-0193-47e6-aa17-e70c98e37e2f">Finally, add 0.3g of P=
henylbis(2,4,6-trimethylbenzoyl)phosphine oxide (TPO) and stir gently until=
 completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3500f9fa-c9d0-4b09-94ee-a0eaf6eb05f3">
<p local-id=3D"720eb7f1-5156-4fc9-b893-0ff6b6096b33">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation and protect from ligh=
t exposure. The binder solution is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"17370a01-c3de-48c7-a9c0-452732627df4" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.SlurryPreparation">C. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"daa3501a-3783-44a8-a20a-a13813ba77f2"><strong>Continue worki=
ng in subdued lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"3b9dfc90-19ab-46b8-8f7e-0714e08740e2">
<li local-id=3D"528cc921-7275-4323-b941-762fb6344d94">
<p local-id=3D"6c712949-5074-4544-be02-96f4e498faa6">Place the 990g of pre-=
treated metal powder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3b45a231-b317-45d5-9da1-5758af382700">
<p local-id=3D"095dcf93-8a53-4e70-9ad7-f63ddcc78f35">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the pre-treated metal =
powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cbd118f9-8a8d-4103-806c-ec4b6adaf45b">
<p local-id=3D"a43a840e-95f4-47dc-825a-35f51b9c7fb4">Continue mixing for 30=
-45 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder throughout the=
 metal powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3724301e-5130-4421-81ff-8d44c6652523">
<p local-id=3D"043449f7-824f-4167-977f-c661101fbca2">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 10g) to achieve p=
roper consistency.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"476deaac-1b15-4255-8d84-06272c4b9df6" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.Drying">D. Drying</h3>
<p local-id=3D"2cf4c15f-fdb8-4314-b64f-c8c052e8bce1"><strong>Protect from d=
irect UV light exposure</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b3d35028-be29-4d3d-a015-2e6f51061ba0">
<li local-id=3D"6fda7955-a773-47cc-820a-1c3fc4fcccea">
<p local-id=3D"6a0e4527-e837-47f7-96a5-cdcb8613c743">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cf8d08f1-860a-41a0-946a-c69edeb329d1">
<p local-id=3D"bf0632bc-9e22-4e3c-93fe-e909898caeb1">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature in a well-ventilated area with subdued lighting =
for 12-24 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e33315d0-c5eb-48b7-977d-b0a71219aa96">
<p local-id=3D"adfe22ba-29f5-49c3-a8b5-2192acaf3ea7">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 50=C2=B0C for 4-6 hours (ensure oven does not emit UV light=
).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"61ee7d4f-4555-410f-a179-e67e9b030965">
<p local-id=3D"d940b5d2-cb30-4682-b9fc-c3d6fecc746e">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 60=C2=B0C for 2 hours to ensure complete solvent removal.</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1afb84dc-f95c-4f6d-9be9-486716deb2e0">
<p local-id=3D"7c9f49ac-f298-4639-aabf-26e7aecd6047">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid cake.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"24fa075d-b025-4eaa-ac28-fa38afa4d89b" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.GrindingandSieving">E. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<p local-id=3D"657bce81-d9f6-4499-9b1f-7ca72d8201de"><strong>Continue worki=
ng in subdued lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"e39a77f6-6e56-4c43-af9c-818bdb644d8d">
<li local-id=3D"77622633-03c2-4c7f-ae7a-307f9c52393d">
<p local-id=3D"a4aeb7b9-ab05-4363-ba0c-65e4d6ee2f0d">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"518ac8e8-936d-4769-8b1b-a5f17985eb59">
<p local-id=3D"b8bc9c24-fa6f-48a9-822d-cebafcaee4c6">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill (ensure equipment doesn't generate significant heat or l=
ight).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"13a9bb51-22b0-407d-8d18-6fb650467624">
<p local-id=3D"d38b6fb2-369c-4358-bb3e-4a4c77ffbab5">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
 for metal powder applications).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"df3e25ed-a28d-4e9b-a998-5996f31a85f0">
<p local-id=3D"3b04f4ce-f028-49d2-aa50-b1a16eb926cc">Add 0.2g of Aerosil R =
812 S to the ground and sieved metal-binder powder mixture. Mix thoroughly =
to ensure even distribution and improved flowability.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"685e062f-1971-4b5d-9d29-4b57b4ccfb8c">
<p local-id=3D"95eb6d74-ac00-4dde-8a0b-7a0a45615b71">Store the powder in li=
ght-proof containers until ready for use.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"b2793f99-42f2-43d4-a535-ba400f2a4b3f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.UVCrosslinkingProcess">F. UV Crosslinking Process</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7348b026-a949-4ab4-b72c-f435c2e0b7d0">
<li local-id=3D"e6f658e0-b004-4469-b8fb-ceaae03718b7">
<p local-id=3D"1f626664-ce68-4a5b-83c4-36f766969e13">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1e24ce5a-f0f1-4857-8290-d86fb35b35ca">
<p local-id=3D"19686004-9123-486b-8815-c765f0ea1fae">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d9ffe33b-d487-4840-8a25-63755fd86b31">
<p local-id=3D"e11a4053-9dfa-408a-95e0-f2a91b1484a4">Expose the packed mold=
 to UV light (365-405nm wavelength) for crosslinking:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"eb474dd0-abc0-42d1-9c5c-e7e58abf942d">
<li local-id=3D"466f77cc-2e54-4f24-9c82-b0a61abf2374">
<p local-id=3D"b1aa0862-848d-4d9e-8563-e32ca904d154">For thin sections (&lt=
; 5mm): Expose for 2-5 minutes at appropriate intensity</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f2a7d260-a260-4b0e-87bc-a47958ef38e1">
<p local-id=3D"1ce71099-b103-4dcd-a623-2deee7f86112">For thicker sections: =
Increase exposure time accordingly or expose from multiple angles to ensure=
 complete curing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"59155f9c-e025-41b1-a8ce-35920b3ebd2a">
<p local-id=3D"c9575c42-d4e6-4669-9660-173437811654">Consider using a UV li=
ght with penetration appropriate for your part thickness</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"3e4a8a84-1709-4eff-871e-97e05d9e3002">
<p local-id=3D"6e4f2798-d4be-4a8f-8fe3-2536033e482c">Allow the part to cool=
 if any heat was generated during the UV exposure.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"b0952f98-880e-4a70-a6af-37677b97e4b9" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-G.DissolutionandGreenPartRecovery">G. Dissolution and Green Part Recover=
y</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"b02633bd-936d-45fd-a47b-fa0fa403a491">
<li local-id=3D"06de001e-79eb-4e99-b4db-c5008f643c53">
<p local-id=3D"a52be5a0-b281-4c99-89fe-aa55d38b7cb4">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in warm water (40-50=C2=B0C) to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"e2b21298-97ae-4885-b3af-5d31f8416540">
<p local-id=3D"1d9d72d2-9e89-458f-93f5-74922211f48a">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh water as needed until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6585abbc-086b-4194-9479-e9ad73b550ad">
<p local-id=3D"872d0313-9cf6-4e88-9289-16c569a06cb7">Carefully extract the =
green part from the water bath and allow to dry completely.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"357db5f5-1c8a-4198-ae0b-510e431468fd">
<p local-id=3D"b65cdc65-b1db-446e-ab5d-4e8c596e2eda">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to the standard protocol for yo=
ur specific metal alloy (17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr).</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"5f204f23-640e-4528-8abe-c2838ef44e80" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Notes.3">Notes</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"c0265b0f-182e-4386-96cb-3934d6100fa6">
<li local-id=3D"89e469cf-e933-4c97-bb18-6def0725ed82">
<p local-id=3D"a9ef2ca8-d4d6-4136-b5ac-039e1ec9d128"><strong>Benefits of Si=
lane Pre-Treatment</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"56a6c342-1df6-4129-a672-5b6af4bdb90c">
<li local-id=3D"ca94e770-2aed-403a-b7a7-a18a4c86d8c3">
<p local-id=3D"7cef89f6-84b1-4acf-bf70-b83f2636b25b">Creates covalent bonds=
 between metal surface and polymer binder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2c719d28-01f8-400e-95b0-9a69b6965d09">
<p local-id=3D"311d75b1-fae0-417b-9bea-99a7f904cccb">Significantly improves=
 metal-polymer adhesion</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e2543efb-55e0-4ee6-8519-032b7e72097f">
<p local-id=3D"97a4fd77-14ee-40c7-8ce0-fb815e204098">Enhances green part st=
rength and handling durability</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a3ba9784-c05e-48b7-a528-1a4ff4c2467e">
<p local-id=3D"5e9643dd-dfd8-4b33-821e-148e60e2b586">Improves dispersion of=
 metal particles in the binder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a29ab62f-ecd3-4efe-b298-e208487484a1">
<p local-id=3D"9fbc81e7-7bbe-4ac8-8553-38b6c5b7e0fd">Potentially allows for=
 even lower binder content while maintaining adequate strength</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"24c3391c-4f45-4e06-9436-2622aaa77304">
<p local-id=3D"bdf0e383-ea73-4f73-9ae2-5b4c7aec7f57">Reduces the risk of de=
lamination or cracking during handling</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"464d12cc-e6c5-41b6-a928-24c7853285cf">
<p local-id=3D"b4b46709-3b2c-400d-9766-7835280e395e"><strong>Silane Couplin=
g Mechanism</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"8b888a22-fe06-46c4-bb8c-aa2006d81615">
<li local-id=3D"762ea654-4ec6-4ff4-9fbd-465ed8e6676a">
<p local-id=3D"6cd18898-d3a3-4dc7-9135-ee2f66338112">The methoxy groups on =
the silane hydrolyze in the IPA solution forming silanol groups</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"51f74d76-f2af-45af-90c3-5d503d23316f">
<p local-id=3D"711d6106-bd50-4013-8fc0-efc2964878c1">Silanol groups react w=
ith hydroxyl groups on the metal surface</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"91923ac9-c47b-427a-953f-e89ecb1f6cbd">
<p local-id=3D"6385efc5-c760-4a4e-b364-9cac4844b541">The methacrylate funct=
ional group on the silane remains available to copolymerize with TEG-DMA du=
ring UV curing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7e2ae544-62fd-4bbf-a1bb-0d9c8f0426d6">
<p local-id=3D"c7c24c72-e63a-45cd-a173-06894f00d39f">This creates a chemica=
l bridge between the metal surface and polymer network</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"0fd09efa-4994-43c5-9928-93c5c6f30b3a">
<p local-id=3D"68becc0a-2abc-4fbe-b960-e2b1ed9f9209"><strong>UV Curing Adva=
ntages</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"ae3c6eab-3c28-4c3d-bf52-f1eddad11e7d">
<li local-id=3D"e0af75d6-c10b-4d38-a9aa-f548228e7b46">
<p local-id=3D"f8463228-7273-4485-b193-8869e4a20529">Room temperature proce=
ssing (no thermal activation required)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bf38287c-58be-4332-89ad-9a64d0162f48">
<p local-id=3D"43e46148-e5c6-4c54-9406-57d7e486a3c5">Rapid curing (seconds =
to minutes vs. hours)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"11d0fc4e-4c9f-4e33-b2f7-0710acebf74e">
<p local-id=3D"29a16eca-5c80-4053-a273-d8c39f1a0ea4">On-demand curing only =
when exposed to UV light</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"60c99909-7aab-45e0-9d24-7a726c88875e">
<p local-id=3D"c2d36eed-f788-430f-a2e6-4d944a1b4f2e">Potential for selectiv=
e curing of specific areas</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"43d8dc73-c45a-49ca-9476-f451a6d59e27">
<p local-id=3D"50c74d20-e6da-4ce6-b714-35eb3315a73a"><strong>TPO Photoiniti=
ator Characteristics</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"cc3653a8-51f8-48d4-b482-de296d8931b8">
<li local-id=3D"4b48bdb0-698a-4214-8d23-117bfdcd6321">
<p local-id=3D"2815a458-1d27-4854-95c0-d12df0b98ddc">Absorbs light in the 3=
65-405nm UV range</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f69d07f3-7a9b-4d95-8183-fcf4d07f5f76">
<p local-id=3D"9e5d9497-f80f-47cf-b7ee-641465ed1f89">Generates free radical=
s when exposed to UV light</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6716498d-5253-472b-b209-00a4ab1ac5c8">
<p local-id=3D"8cc40ae3-6477-45b3-af8b-30fa4bc04fa4">More effective for thi=
cker sections than many other photoinitiators</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9f74e862-5ca8-4f88-a199-704e8ce6f65a">
<p local-id=3D"5c4ca56e-33c9-420b-8089-a064a77e370a">Yellow color may affec=
t aesthetic appearance of green parts</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"071d656f-47cf-416a-9e7d-09bb371c32ce">
<p local-id=3D"b77eba4c-1150-46ce-9884-b2d4943bdc6c"><strong>Important Prec=
autions</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"e17e9653-c26c-4c53-832f-24994f8f583d">
<li local-id=3D"c7c93d1c-118d-4e26-82bf-034d950953c9">
<p local-id=3D"a4cb9451-e3f3-41d9-bee2-5e0b115cad3e">Protect the binder sol=
ution and mixed powder from UV light/sunlight until ready for curing</p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"f309c3c3-16d7-409d-a4c8-c2f3523efeca">
<p local-id=3D"4b1770de-53d2-41a8-8798-f9402e6bef43">Use amber containers o=
r aluminum foil wrapping for storage</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"eff3daf2-b7d7-4648-8485-141cc3fca41b">
<p local-id=3D"4074c884-1253-48bf-b7b2-03c10cbbb5f3">Work in subdued lighti=
ng conditions when handling the material</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"de462578-0b93-41c1-88af-b5f521d53208">
<p local-id=3D"3a02dfe8-1ba6-4677-9f9d-b771370e3979">Wear appropriate UV pr=
otection when operating UV light sources</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"725c0591-be05-45cc-97c0-9992f812b654">
<p local-id=3D"ebe3a430-2daa-44e9-803a-9b04e4b759ae">This formulation uses =
a reduced binder content (1% vs typical 3%) which will:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3f8a9eee-5b02-4843-a353-1a024fd29078">
<li local-id=3D"885bb826-85a7-474c-8c23-9e3adcf58aea">
<p local-id=3D"6b10a07a-f054-4b0c-b795-ba41d430f283">Result in higher green=
 density</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"54e40ada-d6b8-4ea5-9d03-e1a49d933604">
<p local-id=3D"3744076a-46a4-417e-bb7c-ef55306a75c7">Lead to lower shrinkag=
e during sintering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ea418181-b996-425c-a002-19d821700c3d">
<p local-id=3D"265ea1c8-e13a-45f1-afc3-e15371a08cd5">Potentially limit comp=
lexity of possible geometries</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cc92d3cf-ebcb-4a83-992f-953c1d5b5784">
<p local-id=3D"1a79368e-8e09-405d-b438-d41cdb95f580">These limitations are =
partially offset by the silane coupling enhancement</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"0c58b54f-a158-4f7a-866d-f25af5149de5">
<p local-id=3D"77505035-c0ef-4fd0-8343-4b87ff525cbb">The increased TEG-DMA =
content (15% of binder vs traditional 10%) will:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"d35dda96-2b82-426e-9b70-f7c93cb841b2">
<li local-id=3D"82e2dd5b-cc61-4dd5-8ebe-17721e218632">
<p local-id=3D"3a96053f-84c2-40a7-a16e-f3613791dd5f">Create a more highly c=
rosslinked polymer network</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1d356c77-fbff-4b39-9870-a6054fbf8d85">
<p local-id=3D"f5caf576-6080-458a-bb06-8dd0123a8e22">Provide reactive sites=
 for the UV-initiated polymerization</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9789d012-3d5b-471d-b237-c2457f5149b1">
<p local-id=3D"2830c6ad-0c8f-4694-a24e-4d3266af7680">React with the methacr=
ylate groups on the silane-treated metal surface</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"ba1e401c-3e9c-4ef7-80e0-acfaff2ba24e">
<p local-id=3D"425db3a5-f7b7-4f22-a17b-60f2cc026f57">Depth of cure will be =
limited by:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"733ee5b2-2809-4393-9247-889665e30289">
<li local-id=3D"b2a03d2b-694c-45c6-873b-a628c3fced5a">
<p local-id=3D"b02f6e02-19a2-43ff-92ef-314c9947a9dd">Metal powder shadowing=
 effect (metal particles block UV penetration)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1c59fe74-6f0a-4ab3-a599-565540d11549">
<p local-id=3D"3f9a6cb5-e270-4768-94b6-9688d4f61f72">TPO concentration and =
efficiency</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7f804bd9-a5c3-45de-8b79-50211c9e5405">
<p local-id=3D"5052412c-4d66-4a91-b32f-7388d8d7316f">UV light source intens=
ity and wavelength</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d526aa1d-4b82-4c8e-bc98-ec8b0e392d76">
<p local-id=3D"4621de59-79f4-4f0f-a043-aaf50d561373">Part thickness and geo=
metry</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"10d54abe-7485-4117-9a8b-ce1e7467c385">
<p local-id=3D"93710ee2-db14-4ed4-9d53-b04ac7a3b585">For thicker sections, =
consider:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"5fba8bf0-87ed-4056-ad50-41199f587c3a">
<li local-id=3D"24d05339-b710-4c40-87f3-e975b9e297a1">
<p local-id=3D"fd43c39c-ef6f-495d-be18-5944907338fd">Staged packing and cur=
ing of layers</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"135e132b-cd3f-491a-a5c3-e8652d2fcf35">
<p local-id=3D"6562c5b5-112e-4bac-816e-dba41e2e27d6">Using multiple UV ligh=
t sources from different angles</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5a903ed7-54dc-437e-8ad9-0ee9f7b82561">
<p local-id=3D"fbaa699d-7c2e-415c-bc4a-0d3aac85ae09">Longer exposure times<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a08fd8cd-03a2-491d-9485-7943390156f8">
<p local-id=3D"46b7a701-ead0-4fb1-bcf2-ed04c6df1da0">Higher TPO content (up=
 to 5% of binder) for deeper penetration</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"4ffdd1c0-63c6-4490-b120-9a3d58407979">
<p local-id=3D"ecbada77-e231-499c-a978-81ebb106874b">Store all components i=
n cool, dark places to prevent premature activation</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e4c3e248-0207-4222-aac3-a2da74833392">
<p local-id=3D"ed2ee885-46eb-4fea-8533-06f2370a4a4b">All mixing containers =
should be clean and free of contaminants</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6700fa27-0279-417d-a69f-cadc2d0629ce">
<p local-id=3D"e88ec17d-eb85-49d6-b5bb-26beb40a9f2f">Perform all solvent ha=
ndling steps in a well-ventilated area away from ignition sources</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"b6183a80-d995-4191-bd63-024a6808225a">I am also working on a=
 recipe that is similarly photoinitiated, but has both water soluble and no=
n-water-soluble binder components so that it can be poured into the mold as=
 a slurry, UV cured, and the mold can be dissolved off while at the same ti=
me debinding the water-soluble components to yield a porous green part that=
 is only loaded with the non-water-soluble components. The binder load is a=
lso increased to 3% for this formulation:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"56672078-14a2-492a-9162-f5eb1a994a0e" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-UV-CurablePourableMetalSlurrywithWater-SolubleComponent">UV-Curable Pour=
able Metal Slurry with Water-Soluble Component</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"5af228d6-5c9a-4dbd-ac0c-f0104a9513b1" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.4">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"03871065-c625-4c96-a5a7-da686f14710e" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ForMetalPowderPre-Treatment.1">For Metal Powder Pre-Treatment</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"8d1ca7f4-14ab-476a-954c-c92ab8a1baee">
<li local-id=3D"6a28b817-dd0b-4408-bf31-4304a611df8a">
<p local-id=3D"ef53158c-75a6-475a-92d0-2c5dbcc413fa">970g of metal powder (=
choose one: 17-4 PH stainless steel, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4d96d190-b7a4-4d97-80b0-a075173fbe95">
<p local-id=3D"18c88d8a-543a-470d-966a-48696295a164">1g of 3-(Trimethoxysil=
yl)propyl methacrylate (=CE=B3-MPS)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a0f8440-a796-41e8-965b-b37b151645bc">
<p local-id=3D"f100742f-25ba-4349-bc87-3a0a0da85f26">100mL of Isopropyl Alc=
ohol (IPA)</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"0d7b9925-7b7f-4819-83a8-5bda10e22deb" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalSlurry(97%Metal,3%TotalBinder)">For 1000g Final Metal =
Slurry (97% Metal, 3% Total Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5bb0a7f4-8cf1-40d7-92fd-0d2fcecbe75e"><strong>Pre-treated Me=
tal Powder</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"a39178c5-97b6-40e6-965a-b81fc83654ac">
<li local-id=3D"f0bc4c01-fb17-4274-bbc8-17a34ab86004">
<p local-id=3D"b51dcae3-4e2a-4e70-b86b-839656c3a297">970g of silane-treated=
 metal powder</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"721270ae-d2f1-412d-a97e-235377789ae8"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (30g total - 3% of final mixture)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"91226b94-c7d8-4370-9d1a-93f7755e59b8">
<li local-id=3D"578c0b37-ad29-4156-9695-6a4198366103">
<p local-id=3D"f639f9f2-2448-40fa-a3fa-0dfcc6065d71">9g Polyethylene glycol=
 diacrylate (PEGDA, Mn ~575) (30% of binder) - <em>water-soluble component<=
/em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"55b3d997-8854-4fd1-be39-aaa8b611fc90">
<p local-id=3D"8c3dcf35-0b6f-419e-b691-fa73d3718ed4">6g Poly(vinyl alcohol)=
 (PVA, hydrolysis 87-90%, Mw ~30,000) (20% of binder) - <em>water-soluble c=
omponent</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"beca4056-32e7-467d-9ebd-3c8630611477">
<p local-id=3D"6b366d6c-571f-40be-81d0-7c006eddae1e">6g Triethylene glycol =
dimethacrylate (TEG-DMA) (20% of binder) - <em>non-water-soluble component<=
/em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cc2dba5c-07d9-4a60-a43b-30cd9614ea15">
<p local-id=3D"118eb322-96b1-4e0a-b62b-98caf89698f7">7.5g Polymethyl methac=
rylate (PMMA) (25% of binder) - <em>non-water-soluble component</em></p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"932941ec-b0de-40e0-8bb7-b520d184a9de">
<p local-id=3D"4aafceb9-74bf-4505-90ff-519247ba1cc9">1.5g Phenylbis(2,4,6-t=
rimethylbenzoyl)phosphine oxide (TPO) (5% of binder) - <em>photoinitiator</=
em></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"c6742857-01e9-4379-a602-9b80f6fa840a"><strong>Solvents/Dilue=
nts</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"6f17957e-e0c1-41dc-94ae-83e74af61b43">
<li local-id=3D"01f912fc-fda6-49e5-8619-92b04d9c032a">
<p local-id=3D"fb3b310e-05bd-4f89-90a2-7d395b22842d">30g Deionized water</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"647c6727-2192-4bf9-a1e9-bb8317db8eb3">
<p local-id=3D"2483d193-b43c-4ced-82b2-ec0c2ad8df50">30g Ethanol (or Isopro=
panol)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4dadd386-6253-4d15-8a3b-20e62bb1fb7a">
<p local-id=3D"1873ac6c-8422-47fc-b4d6-85319588bb06">0.6g Dispersant (e.g.,=
 Darvan C or Dolapix CE64) (2% of binder weight)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d7e9b749-b4af-4da2-9f43-2e664c8e2363"><strong>Equipment</str=
ong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"6ec11279-ee3f-4e6f-a1e2-7d31c8e8dc38">
<li local-id=3D"3c194bcf-4693-4f85-b7dc-68d96ad81043">
<p local-id=3D"da32673e-4e78-4640-8291-93dae1a20344">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ef998c08-8f49-4f0c-94c9-81b69b01ef41">
<p local-id=3D"bdd2e17d-1bfb-4891-a4bf-ca7a88009bb0">Glass containers with =
amber/dark tinting or aluminum foil covering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"954e72b8-bf30-4149-b88e-e67088d411f9">
<p local-id=3D"6fedb34c-8c1f-46fa-b081-e0133aa32f50">High-shear mixer or ul=
trasonic homogenizer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2d12eea1-88c5-46c2-b243-be25e86b8f3f">
<p local-id=3D"4a0e1a73-382e-4b6f-825b-023896743649">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"39815a4d-35c6-4686-92f9-92e21a58badb">
<p local-id=3D"718cd99c-21ce-4a32-90d9-8db55febe7f5">UV light source (365-4=
05nm wavelength)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"734c8f7d-23c5-4b2f-8899-611a0a2c34f7">
<p local-id=3D"3fc49a5c-32ab-4a32-9cd2-cebbb526ec69">UV safety equipment (U=
V-blocking eyewear, gloves, covered skin)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b6500f79-01f4-4e29-a374-1b8d5ec1a738">
<p local-id=3D"801b4581-b2eb-426c-a720-3709c3921c9b">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"678b8439-2e26-43a2-93d8-14f08e11a605">
<p local-id=3D"61b794db-4498-4f75-abad-9e64af5e6a4c">Viscometer (optional b=
ut recommended)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"3043ebc3-2a7b-416d-a61e-6fd32e6d6194" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.4">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"75d42949-348f-4eb7-b835-07c5358af99f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.MetalPowderSilanePre-Treatment.1">A. Metal Powder Silane Pre-Treatment=
</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c63d635d-77ea-4b47-bd71-e0046b560df0">
<li local-id=3D"104730cf-397a-45f4-a5f0-3eb9ce461474">
<p local-id=3D"9bf6e6cc-6c04-4d92-8335-d214909a20d0">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, add 1g of 3-(Trimethoxysilyl)propyl methacrylate to 100mL of isopropyl=
 alcohol in a suitable container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0e785f19-5c3b-4a05-af6a-4cac862f03e6">
<p local-id=3D"a4b9590d-63a4-42f6-9e89-1cd8b7b46ece">Stir the solution gent=
ly for 5 minutes, then let it stand for 30 minutes to allow hydrolysis of t=
he silane coupling agent.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b54211bb-c393-41fd-858a-b68cffbb836f">
<p local-id=3D"02105d2a-f914-4785-b38c-600c4b4d6549">Place 970g of metal po=
wder in a large mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5ea7a19e-8dfe-43b4-81ae-975d04eb6843">
<p local-id=3D"0b4b60ac-0fe9-4197-bfb1-e49d2082846b">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the hydrolyzed silane solution to the metal powder.</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"090ebef7-e08c-4717-abfc-0f5d365c9aaf">
<p local-id=3D"1f5d0ba9-a03d-424f-9337-cd701c3b9c8b">Continue mixing for 15=
-20 minutes to ensure even distribution of the silane solution over all met=
al particles.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7496abec-0f9d-448b-ba7b-bb7f80eed6f6">
<p local-id=3D"5f0011e8-0110-4437-87d6-147f7cc4bd3a">Spread the treated pow=
der on drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"74a847c8-8d31-4507-b025-e0716fb7e175">
<p local-id=3D"57ab97f2-cb79-4da9-8a9e-f5255dcb3cc7">Dry at 60=C2=B0C for 2=
-3 hours to remove the isopropyl alcohol.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"84e6e1cf-6de7-4c45-8b14-4cb4242a20e4">
<p local-id=3D"0447401b-cc83-4b3a-9733-4928cde92fdc">Allow the treated powd=
er to cool to room temperature. The silane-treated metal powder is now read=
y for slurry preparation.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"944604e9-3a7c-41a1-beb5-23e9c87e1005" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.Water-SolubleComponentPreparation">B. Water-Soluble Component Preparat=
ion</h3>
<p local-id=3D"c634cf61-32dc-4436-9e1d-70a017755f0f"><strong>Work in subdue=
d lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"9bbb87ac-3e12-4618-b16d-2400f7147f5b">
<li local-id=3D"94369f19-2b2b-459b-9818-765d5c0b93a6">
<p local-id=3D"eaa0ec4a-b86b-4ab3-b054-97180ecd07b6">In a suitable containe=
r, add 30g of deionized water.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"af5080d2-c09e-4a4e-8175-713818083e40">
<p local-id=3D"ef1376b0-a970-41c6-b95e-9adff4f122f0">Heat the water to 80=
=C2=B0C and slowly add 6g of PVA while stirring.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"213a25d2-3850-4753-a2be-6c847e9dc4fa">
<p local-id=3D"a5c3f465-404a-4964-abe2-2a7ad3612086">Continue stirring unti=
l the PVA is completely dissolved (approximately 30-45 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fc621200-67eb-4eef-bfaa-00362cf968ed">
<p local-id=3D"4c2a8cf2-2b1d-40d7-bf75-4ad647fee50c">Allow the PVA solution=
 to cool to room temperature.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"a4640989-085f-4b90-a1ce-f347288fd463" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.UV-CurableComponentPreparation">C. UV-Curable Component Preparation</h=
3>
<p local-id=3D"33712bdd-d4b2-4bcc-939e-d2f35f4381a7"><strong>Work in subdue=
d lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"80dae45a-33b5-466f-9459-bebb34a8b8f6">
<li local-id=3D"72eb197b-42d4-454b-abab-66dd167b61a3">
<p local-id=3D"5003cd94-5289-45d7-965c-360e0c543556">In a separate amber gl=
ass container, mix 30g of ethanol with 0.6g of dispersant.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b081ef85-ed77-4032-ab26-a82546d923be">
<p local-id=3D"1314547d-0c85-48bd-ba5b-63b0205e39b2">Add 7.5g of PMMA and s=
tir until completely dissolved.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d9fd08c9-138c-4c7f-b62c-905f5175b39f">
<p local-id=3D"b6d33653-778c-4ac9-963d-62b89f394f09">Add 6g of TEG-DMA and =
stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"19a822d3-b438-433e-a926-58b5307185c1">
<p local-id=3D"4670bfca-f7cf-42c2-872d-9e8aa635171e">Add 9g of PEGDA and mi=
x thoroughly.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"010efdc4-6f9d-4899-9e9c-ace5024451a8">
<p local-id=3D"20d57f4e-a085-430a-bc77-7f108d915bca">Finally, add 1.5g of T=
PO photoinitiator and stir gently until completely dissolved.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"87fd60ca-dd96-40a9-a379-53cbdf85780f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.SlurryPreparation">D. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"0135ed8a-f721-46ac-b030-2db40bd26ef3"><strong>Continue worki=
ng in subdued lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"19ab0c6b-b785-4e57-9400-253d153857c8">
<li local-id=3D"149f54e6-8c5b-4e0a-b961-2bf81d4ddd87">
<p local-id=3D"af487e06-4571-4965-bc72-a65a5ec0e268">Combine the water-solu=
ble PVA solution with the UV-curable component solution and mix thoroughly.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8934a024-3cab-4bfa-bc3e-f1d913c980b1">
<p local-id=3D"47ab2fe3-ccfb-47eb-853e-5c992fc404d1">Place the 970g of pre-=
treated metal powder in a high-shear mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c7df1123-7965-4112-85ff-cf79bb43edcf">
<p local-id=3D"f3f80fd1-7932-4bb1-8071-f7b24db0d5af">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the combined binder solution to the pre-treated metal =
powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2fd242b8-305e-4119-8c36-5d95d2433c13">
<p local-id=3D"3f39b075-9795-419a-80da-4f17c67edd6f">Increase to high-shear=
 mixing for 15-20 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder =
throughout the metal powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"25463e92-acca-4626-bcd4-bfdacbbe0176">
<p local-id=3D"cf213691-aa09-4246-be70-3c22c1245c9f">Check the viscosity of=
 the slurry - it should be pourable but not too fluid. If needed:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a0443a48-1207-4e7f-9979-d31ecb877f89">
<li local-id=3D"ddc973a9-be61-446b-b6fb-60c6e6327cc5">
<p local-id=3D"9aa06d08-4092-467b-87b2-c057d261c428">If too thick: Add smal=
l amounts of additional water/ethanol mixture (1:1 ratio) in 5g increments<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2ef03fca-2414-4fda-a88a-409ae9d2303d">
<p local-id=3D"51101b14-57be-4426-85ac-fa6faa8a54c1">If too thin: Add small=
 amounts of PVA solution to increase viscosity</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"3faaf173-ab76-431a-9d90-9821af0ee2cd">
<p local-id=3D"a236cf9e-fc47-49ef-90af-82c39038d25a">The slurry is now read=
y for pouring into molds.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"71f92e88-7953-4a85-b35d-5028787c9c24" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.CastingandUVCuring">E. Casting and UV Curing</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"db52d0b9-3ee8-483f-a230-65dee5438650">
<li local-id=3D"d6d6095d-c82b-439b-bd5b-0e2717e1eea5">
<p local-id=3D"c1d09678-2971-489e-832e-9622aef7c5cd">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b0df2077-e301-4bd9-8c70-5af6c7bddcb0">
<p local-id=3D"a4fd728e-a923-4507-801c-c8b265793065">Pour the prepared slur=
ry into the molds. Consider using vibration or vacuum to remove any trapped=
 air bubbles.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ac86d929-ce39-4c12-bbe5-92ae029ed69b">
<p local-id=3D"38f61051-3e4b-4d30-8616-f7c1f4a76c77">Allow the slurry to se=
ttle for 5-10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f3842d24-dfee-41c7-b6be-4e286a032715">
<p local-id=3D"5dfd2956-b830-4f0b-83af-0d877ba08422">Expose the filled mold=
 to UV light (365-405nm wavelength) for crosslinking:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"29515a72-d371-40e4-8dc1-60a6df5d2a54">
<li local-id=3D"79c66c85-b4dd-4889-b7d2-e2d695a7ce97">
<p local-id=3D"9b9ef773-1bc3-4dea-823b-2fbd2a21b138">For thin sections (&lt=
; 5mm): Expose for 3-6 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cda722cf-1f37-4bbb-8624-5d7a24c0b6fc">
<p local-id=3D"dd33df44-3ee8-4c18-b191-454555afa623">For thicker sections: =
Use a staged approach with multiple shorter exposures from different angles=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"44ceadfe-35cb-43ec-86e2-af60e7072e39">
<p local-id=3D"132920a1-986b-4476-b60f-891a3a63dc8e">Allow 30-60 seconds be=
tween exposures to prevent excessive heat buildup</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"5c528e70-f036-4773-8590-7436f8ad8709">
<p local-id=3D"fe81ad9b-7ddc-422b-9683-7198b70a3a4c">Allow the part to cool=
 completely after UV curing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"fb524105-e925-4b3a-806b-7fa9e7bc77af" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.PrimaryDebinding(Water-SolubleComponentRemoval)">F. Primary Debinding =
(Water-Soluble Component Removal)</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"f70f21fc-0a24-43ea-8822-8ec29f5a94dd">
<li local-id=3D"47ab8452-d150-45bb-8310-653a74a73d31">
<p local-id=3D"816f9d43-f3f7-44a5-95d1-2d1f5a617254">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in warm water (50-60=C2=B0C) to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"f2192fdf-592c-4cc9-aa51-eacdde668c6e">
<p local-id=3D"ab8980e5-9bec-4dc2-8f90-9dba3f1983a3">After the mold is comp=
letely dissolved, continue soaking the part to begin dissolving the water-s=
oluble components of the binder (PVA and PEGDA).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a1f7abf8-b0b1-4dfd-882e-7b571b259845">
<p local-id=3D"ab4f3f11-0565-4dc3-a2fd-aee8e76ae44a">Change the water every=
 2-3 hours to facilitate faster dissolution.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c892710c-5963-41b4-bec2-b01cf8982302">
<p local-id=3D"18186da9-057c-41eb-88bf-910e761a7b79">Total immersion time w=
ill depend on part thickness but typically requires 12-24 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"37deba84-96c8-4fd3-adbb-dedaeffa87d9">
<p local-id=3D"82e624ee-b8dd-4410-a317-dcdd5cbe6288">Once the primary water=
-soluble components are dissolved, carefully remove the part and dry it at =
room temperature for 12 hours, followed by gentle heating at 40=C2=B0C for =
2 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"229f0f11-cc51-47cb-973f-5c40b637496a">
<p local-id=3D"ea005cce-d5a8-49b6-a207-4ce4dd7c852e">The part is now partia=
lly debound but still held together by the non-water-soluble components (PM=
MA and TEG-DMA).</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"e70fa871-34a3-4308-85ee-0e83526cbcb9" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-G.SecondaryDebindingandSintering">G. Secondary Debinding and Sintering</=
h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"2265f455-cda2-4d35-9117-f270b046242f">
<li local-id=3D"31cd6ba3-d406-46fa-ba2d-d114de8b049f">
<p local-id=3D"07b0c0ea-80e4-4b51-9ac7-68ab31551919">Follow standard therma=
l debinding protocols to remove the remaining organic components:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"15a9673f-9541-4390-bad1-8efe9a24b5b7">
<li local-id=3D"58134396-6aa8-4ffd-960c-6721694c6f42">
<p local-id=3D"753aca27-791f-4a72-8778-0a14a1762b3a">Slow heating rate (1-2=
=C2=B0C/min) to 300=C2=B0C with appropriate hold times</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7e30d0ee-c414-41bc-b176-4e4b570a3c35">
<p local-id=3D"ff0bfa98-e4c2-45a5-8eff-3b9a5f1c64d0">Continue to final debi=
nding temperature based on the specific binder components</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"5a5d58f3-4402-412f-af38-fcf9bbee15d7">
<p local-id=3D"32639251-c866-42e1-852f-8a8eb1623be0">Proceed with standard =
sintering protocol for the specific metal alloy (17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or C=
uCrZr).</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"dcb16188-5b27-4c36-aac6-99f0461767da" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Notes.4">Notes</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"8f85abef-0cb8-44fb-8a2d-9f5bd0e6b128">
<li local-id=3D"1ac646e6-382e-490e-90dd-61ef2bd1565f">
<p local-id=3D"15628568-8cd9-440d-8a0d-754a4fa1a2a6"><strong>Dual-Component=
 Binder System Benefits</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f9be2871-2e34-438c-bbd0-d72158085ba3">
<li local-id=3D"f36e248e-ce49-4866-9cb4-e185b1ddb03d">
<p local-id=3D"bfba535e-766c-4eec-a7ef-793bae4c59c5">Water-soluble componen=
ts (PVA and PEGDA) allow for primary debinding via water immersion</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a418c770-8f7b-45b6-b0fe-697321fa4fe2">
<p local-id=3D"3590a0ea-c753-455b-aac9-61738505d742">PMMA and TEG-DMA provi=
de structural integrity during the water debinding step</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aad8ff4b-f32a-49f6-978d-6cf5fffe4e80">
<p local-id=3D"d7f690bf-5735-48b7-acf6-a2877f4abc10">The combination allows=
 for lower total organic content during thermal debinding</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e6cb52f3-1168-4b9b-a27c-d28394dd6ce2">
<p local-id=3D"44251ee8-fb7f-40c1-aff7-17e61dc2a3f7">Reduced risk of defect=
s from rapid gas evolution during thermal debinding</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"1dd1f95d-b97b-4826-824d-ddc635b1b5f3">
<p local-id=3D"601e3299-ea87-44ac-846c-543815b65d5f"><strong>Slurry Propert=
ies</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7ee42440-3736-4077-a7b4-09e2d175c253">
<li local-id=3D"63fda8e7-7c03-413b-bdd4-fdad6e177ed4">
<p local-id=3D"1947d664-db76-4a2e-b17c-1c5ba3808e45">The ethanol and water =
create a homogeneous system that will evaporate slowly, giving good working=
 time</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6a185604-c374-4da2-90de-3ccb6045737c">
<p local-id=3D"816e9880-4079-4567-81ab-77fa82b8360e">PVA acts as both a bin=
der and a rheology modifier</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6b715e70-a742-48a0-8b70-874f54b41f86">
<p local-id=3D"d124ee0a-30bd-40d5-b998-1ed5f8d1b522">PEGDA provides both wa=
ter solubility and UV-curability through its acrylate groups</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ebdb5998-5c73-4fa7-9e44-4af9231b3076">
<p local-id=3D"75907e45-e0b3-4cab-99bc-91d9e5d37c7e">The dispersant is cruc=
ial for preventing metal particle agglomeration in the slurry</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"1153a324-c9c1-4445-a553-9cd21dc74f59">
<p local-id=3D"03b2e397-7d27-499d-a928-e133d1b681ae"><strong>Key Process Co=
ntrols</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f6e176b3-fefd-4c4d-982f-c42154450ce2">
<li local-id=3D"c42787c4-7de3-447f-9ff9-840e77ad3aa9">
<p local-id=3D"44287bfe-037a-46ae-9638-6856043bb088">Viscosity is critical =
- too thin and particles may settle before curing; too thick and pouring be=
comes difficult</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e90a5f8f-96f0-4798-9f5a-11433784bd1b">
<p local-id=3D"c7f6cd5c-7d06-4499-83a4-32ab6feb4e43">UV exposure time must =
be sufficient to cure throughout the volume, not just the surface</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2925b46d-819e-4105-b059-0a1d70966ed3">
<p local-id=3D"7c300c42-f12c-430e-b542-6ff69cbeb2c6">Water temperature duri=
ng primary debinding affects dissolution rate and potential distortion</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"6dfb545f-c2e1-47a9-9b48-b6ba645da859">
<p local-id=3D"920b04d8-5828-430b-a220-b1bfed4a60f0"><strong>Metal Loading =
Optimization</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4076d178-7ad8-45a8-8c91-09b74b99819c">
<li local-id=3D"259bfb01-a5f7-4889-b53c-77a83a99f0cb">
<p local-id=3D"633f036a-3a87-4e90-a4ae-aca6f9686321">This formulation uses =
97% metal loading, which is high for a pourable slurry</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ccb0ec8f-d215-4ffe-af29-263870d0a610">
<p local-id=3D"64131dd6-d6a5-48f3-9a3a-1af2b223d37b">The silane treatment i=
s essential for maintaining flowability at this high metal content</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f2a51606-ef56-4105-a849-08ab08b2aa19">
<p local-id=3D"e473efaa-f373-4958-ad63-a32338388696">If pouring issues occu=
r, metal content can be reduced to 95-96% by adjusting the formulation</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"be462fb6-03c5-492f-ae08-232808553113">
<p local-id=3D"c1f79abc-3713-4029-b94b-b55d9a624ec0"><strong>Potential Chal=
lenges and Solutions</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c60e5bab-e4df-4c0c-acca-4f127232715e">
<li local-id=3D"0acb1951-f7b3-44be-8d51-ce6ad12ded9d">
<p local-id=3D"c662a738-947d-43f6-a27e-da5b47d75c38"><strong>Sedimentation<=
/strong>: If metal particles settle too quickly before UV curing, consider =
adding 0.1-0.2% xanthan gum to the water component</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bdaf07a8-6f9f-4ce2-87a0-2964c682cbc5">
<p local-id=3D"dce91ea4-9c1a-4a62-ac91-a13eb68ece52"><strong>Incomplete Cur=
ing</strong>: For thicker sections, consider adding a secondary thermal cur=
ing step at 80=C2=B0C for 30 minutes after UV exposure</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"96d6006d-2950-4c64-b8f2-b0ec6edc927c">
<p local-id=3D"5733ad01-a443-4ea3-925a-58edacdf3711"><strong>Poor Surface F=
inish</strong>: If surface definition is insufficient, increase the PVA con=
tent slightly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a98251a3-738c-4e9d-b330-7d7b84d3c7e1">
<p local-id=3D"ad67b8a7-51b9-4882-878f-fa87b3932038"><strong>Cracking Durin=
g Drying</strong>: Slow the drying rate after water debinding by using a hu=
midity-controlled environment</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"196ec108-b468-46c5-82d9-0695dc0ddfc8">
<p local-id=3D"e9ff7358-9b3c-4aa2-afd3-f29ca235bf48"><strong>Storage Consid=
erations</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f246e5f5-7bcd-45b0-9f99-dce442d9cea7">
<li local-id=3D"8e55ae20-a542-4c69-8e09-61ae7d20a1aa">
<p local-id=3D"4dccf5be-1026-49d6-8072-1155417074dc">The prepared slurry ha=
s limited working time (4-8 hours) and should be used promptly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a4aaace-df40-46b3-a1fa-d968b148f743">
<p local-id=3D"e1a92535-b19c-4495-8c5c-9734ede8df16">Store any unused slurr=
y in light-proof, sealed containers in a refrigerator (4-8=C2=B0C) to exten=
d working time</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3b8e8a52-6a34-46e2-8c56-809786b649c2">
<p local-id=3D"fec10dfa-a8b9-4b15-94ce-1f67f97fa89d">Allow refrigerated slu=
rry to return to room temperature before use and check viscosity</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"69242aef-318f-41be-bc53-340061e1db26">
<p local-id=3D"5f9995e2-4646-4907-858b-a46ba4ab6649">Perform all steps invo=
lving solvents in a well-ventilated area away from ignition sources</p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"ce734146-61ce-44e4-a600-de3b1a04c375">
<p local-id=3D"6f922db6-17a8-49b6-a05d-a8e6053458e7">The water-soluble comp=
onents also make this process more environmentally friendly</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"4ff0a2f8-7fa0-41c8-a30c-871fd90974e1"></p>
<p local-id=3D"8370b0a6-eadf-4576-8d52-5d211c408448">Bambu Printer: I remov=
ed the updated roller from the printer this morning, and I am going to try =
printing a Benchy test part using PAHT-CF, a material that I am completely =
unfamiliar with. Okay, apparently PAHT refers to a polyamide, which in this=
 case is likely some formulation of nylon. I printed the Benchy and it came=
 out pretty well; the surface is a bit rough but other than that it looks g=
ood with no stringing or sagging.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f82c728f-7b01-4470-b56e-0a4c87d8382c"></p>
<p local-id=3D"af78a97b-eb3d-4b5a-9525-26d28935fedd">2025-05-06</p>
<p local-id=3D"32206fb4-e55f-4b7d-80f7-e66b8480ab89">PILOT: Printed opaque =
guards for PILOT 3 windows. Iterating on Micro Drop mount to mount the Micr=
o Drop head to a linear stage of the same type used for the spindle Z axis =
on the PILOT printers and the BETA printers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"86e924d3-4cf4-41d1-9dea-bad7a3121b5a">PILOT ULTRA: Repainted=
 and installed the 5X acrylic windows on the printer cover and painted the =
clear doors. Installed 1X laser guard window on the left hand door.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1bf2996d-a872-4f8e-bfae-51d5b413ab4e">Ultimaker issue: One o=
f the Ultimakers kept being unable to extrude filament about 10 minutes int=
o a print; I believe this is due to the hot end heat break cooling fan not =
functioning correctly and allowing the filament in the heat break to soften=
 and expand, jamming it in place. I blew out the fan and it seems to be wor=
king now, but it should be replaced before too long.</p>
<p local-id=3D"63cd15ae-ef94-4ff1-a215-b2573463792d">PERPLEX: I am working =
on setting up the Prusa to print with MIM feedstock by installing an update=
d version of the pellet extruder.</p>
<p local-id=3D"abd4eb36-1726-4c60-ad08-171345184f2b">REDRESS: I mixed up a =
batch of powder with a binder with a photoinitiator added. In theory, once =
the powder is fully prepped and loaded into a mold, it should be possible t=
o cure it with UV light instead of heat. I also ground and sieved the batch=
 of powder I made with a 1% binder load, and it is currently curing in the =
upper Keith furnace. It did not seem quite as flowable as I=E2=80=99d like;=
 I would like to run it in one of the tumbling mixers for a while to see if=
 that helps to break up agglomerations and coat the powder more evenly with=
 Aerosil. When I pulled the ceramic crucible out of the oven while it was s=
till at 275F, the powder did not seem well bound. This may be an artifact o=
f the reduced binder load, but I also believe that this batch was made with=
 silane pre-treated powder, which may have inhibited the bond between parti=
cles. Fortunately I have another batch made with 3% binder load that is als=
o silane coated; if it has similar issues with binding then that would sugg=
est that the silane coupling agent is detrimental to my process.</p>
<p local-id=3D"625ce557-05c1-45e1-b25f-de59e99c3499"></p>
<p local-id=3D"2d9c094d-ccef-476c-8de8-45ec03979102">2025-05-07</p>
<p local-id=3D"113e9638-8f71-4f68-afa6-db80b9038e1c">HOPPER: Designed and p=
rinting a new mount for the stepper tapper. The previous mount broke becaus=
e of the print orientation and design of the mount; it was essentially an L=
 bracket with the stepper mounted mounted to one side of the L, and it was =
printed so that the bending stress is applied to a joint held together by Z=
 axis layer adhesion.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b051b788-2069-4735-84b4-b351e62337f6">REDRESS: Attempted to =
print using MIM feedstock (17-4 PH Aquamim from Ryer Inc) in the pellet ext=
ruder that was previously used for paraffin printing. I was unable to get i=
t to print well; there seems to be a narrow band of volumetric flow rate wh=
ere the feedstock will extrude and adhere well (to the build plate as well =
as to other layers) and I was unable to force the Prusa to extrude at a con=
stant volumetric flow rate. The extruder stepper seemed to slow and stop at=
 the same point when printing certain perimeters; this may be due to the sl=
icing or because the Prusa control system is not rated to provide enough cu=
rrent to drive the extruder stepper while it is completing that section, po=
ssibly because other axes are drawing current instead. It also seemed that =
the hot end was struggling to maintain sufficient temperature to get a good=
 extrusion; the first few layers would come out well but the extrusion got =
more and more spotty as it build up layers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2609f55f-e022-4c27-a665-a367653b98c1">I loaded a ceramic cru=
cible with UV photoinitiator sensitized powder, and first cured it in the E=
legoo curing chamber for 30 minutes, then in the Formlabs curing chamber fo=
r 60 minutes with no heat, and I am now curing it in the Formlabs curing ch=
amber for 60 minutes at 60C. The two UV-only curing cycles had minimal effe=
ct, however, the batch was not very well mixed (a skin of dried binder was =
left on the surface) and ground (most of the cake was not rendered into pow=
der and was also used with silane pre-treated powder, any of which may have=
 contributed to poor particle adhesion.</p>
<p local-id=3D"41aaf684-5ebf-4a4f-88e8-c1154c96854f">To test the theory of =
silane pre-treatment causing poor adhesion, I have filled a water-soluble m=
old with the latest batch of powder with a 3% binder load. I also had that =
batch of powder mixed for 15 minutes after grinding and sieving with a smal=
l amount of Aerosil R 812 S added, but the final powder was still not as fl=
owable as I=E2=80=99d like. I dried out the powder in the oven in the mater=
ials lab before grinding and sieving it, but I then left it out for 24 hour=
s, which may have allowed it to pick up atmospheric moisture.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0c056622-2e21-43c8-a063-b4c4c02b60d8">I dissolved off the mo=
ld that I cured last night filled with 1% binder load powder and it fell ap=
art during the process.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5abd81f9-5c5b-4769-8e18-8d67605b545f">HOPPER: I tried out th=
e new stepper tapper mount, and the clamping feature I modeled in did not f=
it the NEMA 17 motor well. I</p>
<p local-id=3D"5c4de752-5461-4f31-9f5a-a6f4d54f70af">ROTSPRAY: I ordered 6X=
 new pulleys (McM #6495K745) and 4X new belts (McM #6484K241) for the rotar=
y sprayer assemblies.</p>
<p local-id=3D"51e9dca8-4b2c-4105-9788-8623c0ff433e"></p>
<p local-id=3D"7ddd281b-2b29-4bf0-b3b5-6b2713913c5b">2025-05-08</p>
<p local-id=3D"faa680b8-ea3c-4696-9114-7cbcb45ec0bc">PILOT: Assembled the n=
ew mount for the stepper tapper. This mount has an added clamping feature t=
hat was printed in an orientation to make it as strong as possible, so it s=
hould be more resistant to breaking as compared with the older mount. The s=
tepper tapper is ready to be installed, but because the hopper is currently=
 installed in the printer and the stepper tapper is hopefully not necessary=
, it will not be mounted until the hopper is next removed from the printer.=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"032fe25e-8523-4129-9c0c-e97d1115887f">Working on a new mount=
 for the Micro Drop for PILOT 1. This mount needs to have a limit switch ri=
gidly installed, as well as being compatible with the limit switch currentl=
y used elsewhere in the PILOT printers, which is backordered for a month so=
 the mount also needs to be compatible with the standard inexpensive limit =
switches that are used on the rotary spray heads.</p>
<p local-id=3D"18a934e8-1eef-4ae4-b69b-24646d8c5757">REDRESS: Attempting to=
 print with 17-4 AquaMIM feedstock still. I believe that if I can get the p=
rint file to maintain a constant flow rate and match that flow rate to the =
print speed in X and Y as well as the maximum continuous flow rate capabili=
ty of the extrusion system, it may be able to make good parts.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0258a653-4950-4ad2-bc2f-d2dea6a813e7">I have mixed up a new =
batch of powder following this recipe:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"6babd96f-a914-4a83-8c85-83c2012cb426" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Thermal-CurableAquaMold=E2=84=A2BinderRecipeforWater-SolubleMoldMetalFor=
ming">Thermal-Curable AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Binder Recipe for Water-Soluble Mol=
d Metal Forming</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"16b90669-1b44-40e3-a208-62e6f79116ce" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.5">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"d192aca4-5e7e-467d-bc5d-bbec76c066e4" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalPowderMixture(98%Metal,2%Binder)">For 1000g Final Meta=
l Powder Mixture (98% Metal, 2% Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"6f093b37-dce1-4a6d-81e7-ab2fb986f801"><strong>Metal Powder</=
strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"57252154-cbb4-4b44-9ed3-7655c6ff15fd">
<li local-id=3D"5616022b-977c-458c-808a-05e533d208c6">
<p local-id=3D"1ad44b52-3e76-4b33-8b33-5fad730061e7">980g of metal powder (=
choose one: 17-4 PH stainless steel, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"7e2cde43-4f9b-4a96-94e6-2371623d9d1e"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (20g total - 2% of final mixture)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"1cbde12b-991b-4353-960c-fd5b16af8257">
<li local-id=3D"8826ee16-f5ce-4069-869f-8d508a5ab5da">
<p local-id=3D"486bd944-75ad-4de4-9c87-9664d26a690c">15.4g Poly(methyl meth=
acrylate) (PMMA) (77% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5747de96-1e39-4a9a-bba2-84eb5c9d9500">
<p local-id=3D"96239a1b-b61c-433e-a6d8-8a90a1156506">3.0g Triethylene glyco=
l dimethacrylate (TEG-DMA) (15% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"de4391b6-2f88-4610-92d3-c0ee75da0b72">
<p local-id=3D"2398b453-3398-424b-ae3c-217c482a7bcd">0.6g Azobisisobutyroni=
trile (AIBN) (3% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2484a016-94ec-41fa-a6ca-e9e2648501de">
<p local-id=3D"07101629-a029-4a44-b973-aa4a786c435b">0.6g Dibutyl phthalate=
 (DBP) (3% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7474fad3-f8cd-415e-8cb9-141299cf0c3b">
<p local-id=3D"fd8db3db-0bfc-4563-bb2e-16b6b101115f">0.4g Aerosil R 812 S (=
fumed silica) (to be added after grinding and sieving)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"fd3ada7d-873d-495b-9bbe-1d8fed3ddf5b"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"ad7555f8-3932-4b25-ab4e-7c675281206d">
<li local-id=3D"65f80012-a5ce-496c-987f-80d489bf0cbd">
<p local-id=3D"246a072c-e177-406c-b022-748d66c221dd">180-200g Acetone (9-10=
:1 ratio with binder solids)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"48523015-a2f5-451e-bfa6-5a8dc54b518a"><strong>Equipment</str=
ong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"8848a9bf-0399-4bb2-aa08-87378d1f59dd">
<li local-id=3D"acfc9f2d-0fb6-43d7-b298-edc94b177d21">
<p local-id=3D"2b42d87e-fee1-4dcd-aca3-7ce8ae577677">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"64b2fc37-dd4b-4a6b-8c3b-dd3738fd8649">
<p local-id=3D"18b5cfef-fef4-4e91-8132-c823a072e462">Glass containers with =
amber/dark tinting or aluminum foil covering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"68ec17c7-bcdf-4cc1-bcd3-75d36942695b">
<p local-id=3D"dd7f48c4-abb8-4b14-a332-6d04270f4740">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"583adb56-3097-4758-bf2e-a30b1719ba58">
<p local-id=3D"edfa1521-3851-46c1-b20e-565f48f2690e">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f6b76ef8-e978-42de-86cb-e2a53c673369">
<p local-id=3D"1158d5b1-8925-408d-aaff-325ab930e96b">Controlled temperature=
 oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1e882291-4de5-4a12-bd58-868293389bc6">
<p local-id=3D"71739d83-4cde-47fb-9d11-85ce632fb267">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"816d5473-925f-4db3-ac76-95398df3ac6b">
<p local-id=3D"ffc5d187-7b3b-4cd8-a08d-d2643331042b">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9083ec9c-b365-47e2-95c3-9a7466ca76a8">
<p local-id=3D"aa6e44fb-5e63-429a-ae13-799de85bc46a">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8256b8e9-9dbf-4968-8f42-65b006c13d7e">
<p local-id=3D"134b1092-bf42-49de-8f8f-37a4de60e491">Thermal curing oven (c=
apable of 80-90=C2=B0C)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"94bd1ece-d4f1-4025-a796-ff4214fa0818">
<p local-id=3D"0d8bb92b-8bba-46d6-b7d4-c9a0e9282646">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"7e25bae3-7d2c-4bb9-ba24-d67565095afd" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.5">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"b553410d-f755-4c69-b5fc-c5072d14622f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.BinderPreparation.3">A. Binder Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"9d31ed47-1031-43c9-8ad2-efc027a317d4">
<li local-id=3D"fc6eaec8-842b-4d2a-9459-422c6877bf5c">
<p local-id=3D"1775f124-d3da-49b1-a7fd-2dfd91e7364a">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 180g of acetone into a suitable container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"026c91c6-7cc8-4e3d-b15c-b98c5686266c">
<p local-id=3D"b669d675-1f3f-4ca7-aae5-cdbdc7fe0c83">While stirring, slowly=
 add 15.4g of PMMA to the acetone. Stir until completely dissolved (approxi=
mately 30-60 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f2ee5007-95e3-4ad8-b900-56336e36a9e0">
<p local-id=3D"23c07416-55dd-488a-9c9c-805d158fd0b0">Add 3.0g of TEG-DMA an=
d stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ea6e50a4-b124-4292-8b37-44a099021de0">
<p local-id=3D"8ab97701-2aba-4c01-8491-d992c3706d45">Add 0.6g of dibutyl ph=
thalate (DBP) and stir thoroughly for 5 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fc5c58fb-2738-4926-b076-ad9b625ecaae">
<p local-id=3D"17e32079-5ec4-4182-900e-5af421629f18">Add 0.6g of AIBN and s=
tir gently until completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5a72b48b-c515-40ad-9349-e138ba33aab0">
<p local-id=3D"9231318d-3974-4171-bb8f-e5967a5a54f0">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation. The binder solution =
is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"3d263ef8-3990-4a7e-baec-1c6ae68f0e68" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.SlurryPreparation.3">B. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"d415705c-75aa-45dd-bc42-af7d0cd4cd48"><strong>Maintain tempe=
rature below 30=C2=B0C</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"c3645da3-0db7-40c0-bec9-727667341b82">
<li local-id=3D"4f8aeaca-73b3-4326-b073-f7b00264ba02">
<p local-id=3D"120faaf4-bf39-4558-a1be-c4365e9e77b2">Place the 980g of meta=
l powder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b8166907-6e4e-4319-97a4-cdae7716ed2a">
<p local-id=3D"e1ecede8-a271-441c-a1fa-2c67e9d96020">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the metal powder.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"d25a15a5-06af-4922-a96b-325cb964197f">
<p local-id=3D"a9bfb6d6-926a-4b66-b686-a73c9b196f1c">Continue mixing for 30=
-45 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder throughout the=
 metal powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"87af28cb-5717-45ce-8460-599486727aff">
<p local-id=3D"cfb2e1d1-12d1-4801-899b-e07bc093d723">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 20g) to achieve p=
roper consistency.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"af559626-ed5e-4f80-9869-63f377a53741">
<p local-id=3D"2a2dff0b-60d8-4adf-a83e-1dfc9ae9610b">Keep the temperature b=
elow 30=C2=B0C during mixing to prevent premature activation of the AIBN th=
ermal initiator.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"992e12d5-64f7-43f5-a63b-5a1d79cb70cb" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.Drying.3">C. Drying</h3>
<p local-id=3D"804b4edd-47ae-4b14-9cc0-4d17bde1bdba"><strong>Maintain moder=
ate temperature</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"30559803-17cc-41cc-a662-4d13bb57f715">
<li local-id=3D"efe00312-9b51-436f-8e7e-04514a08fffa">
<p local-id=3D"957cf84f-74ea-44bc-a4b4-4c10eea3d523">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9cc091c0-b450-4d43-a1cd-b075b32f6e43">
<p local-id=3D"e22c6020-8edd-4cfe-8a91-6793da83bd06">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature (20-25=C2=B0C) in a well-ventilated area for 12-=
24 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e222cb63-e0ae-4cd0-9bf3-c129fb9a56f3">
<p local-id=3D"baba326c-bd76-452c-985e-6d0f7d2f5b26">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 40=C2=B0C for 4-6 hours (temperature must remain below AIBN=
 activation temperature).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"34dea188-5ce5-4346-b5fb-f9e52d03f7ad">
<p local-id=3D"99663fc8-223c-4c12-b661-413f6ff3a8aa">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 50=C2=B0C for 2 hours to ensure complete solvent removal wi=
thout activating the AIBN.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b03c7139-11a7-4561-bba8-3a740906c05e">
<p local-id=3D"30624aeb-5584-41c8-bd9e-f6be814c2bb6">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid cake.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"a4bd2b47-ba86-4fb6-abe4-0bd1fc034836" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.GrindingandSieving.3">D. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<p local-id=3D"9851cf8d-38c9-4cce-8251-394187ea87e1"><strong>Maintain cool =
conditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"5fe526ba-3224-4e8a-afbe-b20571024280">
<li local-id=3D"0d525c35-061d-407e-ac9e-372f5ca6cf13">
<p local-id=3D"15efb8f0-a5d5-4978-83d9-0a8d9a4ce8e4">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"799c2ad3-9c3c-41cf-9b6a-089f6bd99a29">
<p local-id=3D"f32ae08b-d385-4458-a851-2d274c11130e">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3ba9101f-58c8-4818-995d-5a0d2539d791">
<p local-id=3D"5819570e-e690-4f0f-8070-c81d2048456d">Monitor temperature du=
ring grinding to stay below 60=C2=B0C to prevent premature AIBN activation.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"564cf9a8-a1bd-45da-a05c-e9125ca8c241">
<p local-id=3D"a7be0f14-2658-4852-88ac-03ffc8c496b1">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
 for metal powder applications).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b2b88971-4e4e-4f46-9108-7cf198e8f3d7">
<p local-id=3D"f998620d-86dd-4c2d-a3e2-10994ece2f39">Add 0.4g of Aerosil R =
812 S to the ground and sieved metal-binder powder mixture. Mix thoroughly =
to ensure even distribution and improved flowability.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3146c91e-c976-46af-bfd7-57f71d3fd89c">
<p local-id=3D"640fb72b-8040-403a-9ac9-13ed1095cb12">Store the powder in co=
ntainers at room temperature or below until ready for use.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"56a0187a-7c70-46f1-bc8f-1616078e43ba" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.ThermalCrosslinkingProcess">E. Thermal Crosslinking Process</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7264e3ca-513e-4647-b2b6-397ab2c5f45a">
<li local-id=3D"73549607-63ab-4d00-92ab-5fcb8b697cea">
<p local-id=3D"a3c0a60d-43e9-4332-9ba8-b4d7ec4cdaed">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer that can withstand 90=C2=B0C).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ef18b5c6-b508-4edb-9b91-8be4defd94df">
<p local-id=3D"d1077c71-b407-42df-a16f-b85fce59dca2">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"da709a06-25b6-4ab5-a51d-a30321a3d58e">
<p local-id=3D"d6b3b28e-7744-4ff0-8094-94d8450d2895"><strong>Thermal Curing=
 Step</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"0bc2dd1c-7f6a-4533-be30-d5349331771f">
<li local-id=3D"08faec48-6570-4e33-8be4-8201fe1a264f">
<p local-id=3D"636b1221-9f13-4e82-b3b2-7784cf328bb3">Place the packed mold =
in a thermal oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"83337219-758f-4285-bfb1-d224615dda68">
<p local-id=3D"6dcc5c57-3dfa-4a15-b499-3e10200d49e9">Heat to 85-90=C2=B0C f=
or 60-90 minutes to activate the AIBN</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a894e517-f8af-4ca9-9229-55b8fff9bf64">
<p local-id=3D"ceec1cf5-29c9-4f1a-b45d-96bd20bff979">For thicker sections (=
&gt;10mm), extend curing time to 90-120 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"06d15763-fef0-4ef4-be97-184afe954d4f">
<p local-id=3D"b7d0a4bb-e29f-46e0-b28b-cea4cda47030">This ensures complete =
crosslinking throughout the entire part volume</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"8c1398ce-65c0-4524-a9b2-354d546295be">
<p local-id=3D"87184966-a11c-4f17-8d6d-6ce255849bf2">Allow the part to cool=
 gradually to room temperature before proceeding.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"a29bad76-4fdd-4e8f-b099-d5cef47de931" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.DissolutionandGreenPartRecovery.3">F. Dissolution and Green Part Recov=
ery</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"e33bffc8-ec57-428c-886a-ee2ef0d3dabe">
<li local-id=3D"20273690-52e5-4465-9cfc-724169ac2a12">
<p local-id=3D"871a437d-4ed2-4c2f-84f5-56a1bb6fbd37">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in warm water (40-50=C2=B0C) to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"2cf1c3a3-9ff1-4705-9ad5-9524f0f0557c">
<p local-id=3D"4d9bb9d5-f0ac-467a-87f9-1b22649a2355">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh water as needed until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2d0416fa-9e23-4ac6-904f-2de1d7c3a61b">
<p local-id=3D"6b6432a8-e391-4c0e-a60f-29e20cfc5c84">Carefully extract the =
green part from the water bath and allow to dry completely.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f56f1317-c94b-4517-a1c2-19a6bd47e067">
<p local-id=3D"33ea74b6-7ea7-48b3-9f95-ea87c3629ef5">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to the standard protocol for yo=
ur specific metal alloy (17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr).</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"7162875a-ab74-45a7-a439-550dac5f7f4b" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-TechnicalNotes">Technical Notes</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"08d25c39-eeab-4b06-a706-c153f6c5c353" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ThermalInitiationSystem">Thermal Initiation System</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"55dee2d6-e942-409e-90fd-236577d4c954">
<li local-id=3D"b4a2bda2-f3aa-4932-82c6-eed35ea4bd4e">
<p local-id=3D"dd828522-072f-48a2-9a8f-4103f628bd3a"><strong>AIBN (Thermal =
Initiator)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"cc486dd9-15a4-47ea-bb65-fbc6e54f6235">
<li local-id=3D"12e66d5c-3fc1-440b-82ed-630705c3cfbb">
<p local-id=3D"a6ffda05-3226-4bc6-97c2-26c536b968c4">Activates throughout t=
he entire part volume during thermal curing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6426a3ab-ef81-4c13-97c7-81bc56404d44">
<p local-id=3D"47b4883b-6985-4eac-96b1-171d6dd03501">Ensures uniform crossl=
inking in all sections regardless of thickness</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"866ca648-6d1b-4ae8-842e-64d46b1f591b">
<p local-id=3D"55f3017f-ce8e-4606-a23f-1b20697c5baf">Activation temperature=
: begins ~65=C2=B0C, optimal at 80-90=C2=B0C</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"336afd8b-2f24-4a88-bf8e-fad22773d26f">
<p local-id=3D"b20a43f7-0048-4a1f-bc1c-da30286d742c">Half-life at 85=C2=B0C=
: approximately 1 hour</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2d06ba87-6c67-433c-92b6-04fcaeec7b84">
<p local-id=3D"afcc4a9a-dd98-4305-9fd0-3c63bc74ff6d">Generates nitrogen gas=
 upon decomposition (ensure adequate ventilation)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"09e818ae-cf73-4af5-b2e4-01ffd9bc578b">
<p local-id=3D"dfa80ed2-89de-49e8-906d-3a028199fa3e"><strong>Dibutyl Phthal=
ate (DBP) Benefits</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4bd6725f-b324-44e1-a895-400576acdde0">
<li local-id=3D"4491b602-84fb-4a7d-97b3-179ee5251686">
<p local-id=3D"2247f59d-a3a4-48aa-8922-b0bc1b9cdd7c">Functions as a plastic=
izer for the PMMA polymer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"439e8096-7afa-4b6c-b1ae-6438daa280cc">
<p local-id=3D"1f84cb46-51c0-4cda-b2a6-ae9f8551c726">Improves flexibility a=
nd toughness of the green part</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"72e283c0-1f60-4e63-9428-bb5f0805f101">
<p local-id=3D"02a98d17-b5c3-4515-8e35-058717395893">Reduces brittleness an=
d improves handling characteristics</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5e287ac4-6991-4b6c-84ec-1493c95ef445">
<p local-id=3D"834e432a-b49e-4f1a-be57-3f31a00a1c85">Enhances polymer chain=
 mobility during crosslinking</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d6f78baa-edbd-4145-b4ee-2e60044dcf67">
<p local-id=3D"bafbe6b4-884a-4ee4-bfe0-f81500a4696b">Typically improves def=
ect tolerance in green parts</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"d9e64f24-0f67-4e23-bddf-6e834e26116f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ProcessingConsiderations">Processing Considerations</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"bbd81e66-6a92-4992-852d-94566336a068">
<li local-id=3D"3358930e-10ba-4b41-af38-4a4e52ebfa78">
<p local-id=3D"7b927833-3c62-4750-b324-3428655ab073"><strong>Temperature Co=
ntrol</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"57fc0aa5-e7a8-425e-b7de-b30ed371f367">
<li local-id=3D"c686bb36-0674-4deb-b4ca-c7e3e639dd1b">
<p local-id=3D"9804dd34-8dae-4578-a098-d9bc2f280fa4">Keep all processing st=
eps below 60=C2=B0C before intended thermal curing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e47f12ca-2b20-401c-a963-0bd920cfefc4">
<p local-id=3D"a91f7c68-1a64-4ba9-aa5e-5dbdbd56c883">Store materials in coo=
l environments (AIBN below 5=C2=B0C for extended shelf life)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cb55547f-d039-4d4a-9346-f4c8cac6b038">
<p local-id=3D"a21fb9cb-c527-4a91-8dd8-d957d1399e9a">Monitor grinding tempe=
rature to prevent premature AIBN activation</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"eb591054-06c0-471e-8c44-0bf54fc359af">
<p local-id=3D"e7f54d94-65aa-429c-a585-85974088136f"><strong>Thermal Curing=
 Parameters</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"921cf57e-e5c4-41d8-8cb5-cfac6e607761">
<li local-id=3D"83ca07f6-084b-40be-aacb-352418d3d500">
<p local-id=3D"6ca467b5-e988-4457-b2f2-3d56a39c423c">Water-soluble mold mat=
erial must withstand 90=C2=B0C</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5e603562-7b83-4c12-95a1-33ce15e09745">
<p local-id=3D"821d3b4e-bd90-43df-b564-223c9d54f73a">Thicker parts require =
extended thermal curing (up to 2 hours)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2e524553-b8b8-4cec-b140-fea3c1ee8cdc">
<p local-id=3D"64ed14b2-8d53-4229-a962-00cf8a0408c6">Allow gradual cooling =
to minimize thermal stress</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d81a1745-fcb1-4a69-98eb-8c70caf4860d">
<p local-id=3D"1e3f1e20-3d8f-40bb-951c-f5e61d949fb3">Ensure adequate ventil=
ation for nitrogen gas release during AIBN decomposition</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"db29e778-bfba-4b48-a443-c6268e09ac38">
<p local-id=3D"e8d68321-0c5a-4bca-9b76-4220b34a43b0"><strong>Formulation Ad=
justments</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"d8c2acdb-5403-4932-8e06-f17e69df05f5">
<li local-id=3D"974a7f65-f4e7-4b91-8894-a727dd2dcc71">
<p local-id=3D"f5a855a6-bc21-46da-ad65-5b6f225cf2b9">For very thick section=
s (&gt;15mm): Consider increasing AIBN to 4% of binder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"af42147d-db5b-424e-8d3a-7326cff47c24">
<p local-id=3D"70d4bab2-0290-4302-8753-0e61f1e90fbb">For higher green stren=
gth: Consider increasing total binder content to 2.5%</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"630b8ac8-b369-4c96-9645-37cc83019755">
<p local-id=3D"de23078b-f6d3-4336-a55c-c3aba91d231c">For more flexibility: =
DBP content can be increased to 5% (reducing PMMA accordingly)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"81a6c95c-28ad-425b-9604-98ccab6e7e1d">
<p local-id=3D"30dc698d-dd10-40e0-bb68-bd11864977b8">For better flowability=
: Aerosil content can be increased to 0.6g</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"0e521057-cd99-4a1f-a384-76c7864cb28c">
<p local-id=3D"4baba59e-c957-4392-b407-907a75f75971"><strong>Advantages of =
Thermal-Only Curing</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"8649497c-8825-463e-a376-09bfdf989e3d">
<li local-id=3D"24fae40e-a091-49bc-81e4-d4f3bc380c12">
<p local-id=3D"78d451b6-4acd-4155-984b-de788a096a00">Uniform crosslinking t=
hroughout the entire part regardless of geometry</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d2055e1a-0110-47d2-b21b-440a857778d1">
<p local-id=3D"01ae22db-b0e7-4532-9e68-1ff0c442caeb">No limitations from sh=
adowing or penetration depth</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e40b0dad-e3ee-48ed-965e-7076c20f87a0">
<p local-id=3D"c892c82f-1e3b-44c9-ad98-625d3f04a439">Simpler processing wit=
hout need for specialized UV equipment</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d6808862-5888-4036-be12-c1cf6853268f">
<p local-id=3D"f3e4dbef-9772-422a-8157-bea84cea7931">More consistent result=
s across varying part thicknesses</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bd0227da-fad1-47ac-9d92-fed3344395f4">
<p local-id=3D"6b560f5f-fed6-4ccd-aa44-1b37d14fed21">Higher crosslinking de=
nsity in thicker sections compared to UV curing</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"1a47111e-25e8-4cab-ba6b-2a76db58ea35">
<p local-id=3D"07ec44f0-5433-4a2c-8ab4-8c4851c1d54b"><strong>Safety Precaut=
ions</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"de68a0d8-5521-4bf8-9b95-d3bdfd1361d4">
<li local-id=3D"0bd2b69f-764a-4dab-8e6e-673be8860943">
<p local-id=3D"3269d812-0a0e-4d7a-aeaf-b68a7b433730">AIBN is thermally sens=
itive - store in refrigerated containers</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d6afd3c2-2386-42be-a4bf-9a469c5d5e5e">
<p local-id=3D"c5629884-685d-4300-a587-2184a6fdc7b2">Dibutyl phthalate shou=
ld be handled with appropriate PPE (gloves, goggles)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"63fe8e2b-55c8-4e98-903d-3d64c8dfc051">
<p local-id=3D"1403b325-fd22-4010-8d01-afe765b3e0ab">Ensure adequate ventil=
ation during thermal curing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6f18c6f0-9fb7-4ab3-b3ff-d94954d9ff51">
<p local-id=3D"00bbfdff-84d0-45f7-84be-93e1be7b52b2">Handle all chemicals w=
ith proper PPE in well-ventilated areas</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"6727c2fd-caba-4ad7-bcf7-82cb21f3f871"></p>
<p local-id=3D"c6b032e1-6a33-4c35-acf1-4befb5ced9ff">I also deviated from m=
y standard mixing procedure. After preparing the binder, I mixed it with th=
e powder a little at a time using a handheld power mixer with a single whis=
k as usual, then I left the slurry in a cup for an hour, then I mixed it ag=
ain before pouring it through a filter into an aluminum pie tin to dry.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c565538a-f297-409b-aead-61236171ed57"></p>
<p local-id=3D"86aafcb4-324b-4f73-ba3c-2b720c918d5f">2025-05-09</p>
<p local-id=3D"413c504b-4f29-4519-8777-7a9da82ea673">REDRESS: The cake made=
 with a 2% binder load is fully dried after being on the hot plate at 40C f=
or 12 hours. Based on hand-grinding some of the residue of this batch from =
the mixing cup, it seems to be more flowable and less damp/sticky than prev=
ious batches without the dibutyl phthalate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"07c44dee-ff09-494f-a16c-9b97e2815ac7">I broke the cake into =
pieces, added 0.1g of Aerosil R 812 S, ground them, ground up any remaining=
 large chunks in a mortar and pestle, then ran them through the sieve to ge=
t a good PSD. The powder wasn=E2=80=99t super flowable even with the 0.1g o=
f Aerosil. I am also concerned about the heating that occurs during the gri=
nding process.</p>
<p local-id=3D"dbf6e69c-096a-48d8-a4da-8371d187bfde">In case it is not reco=
rded elsewhere, here is the initial version of the recipe for a UV-curable =
metal slurry with a water soluble binder component and a non-water-soluble =
binder component:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"5f61ae39-0646-46a5-aeb0-011a627b97ff" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-UV-CurablePourableMetalSlurrywithWater-SolubleComponent.1">UV-Curable Po=
urable Metal Slurry with Water-Soluble Component</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"3581960e-f62d-4a28-9bb7-b521ece6c6aa" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.6">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"2da89d96-e088-48ba-a61a-34aaf6336f37" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ForMetalPowderPre-Treatment.2">For Metal Powder Pre-Treatment</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"60930016-4d5b-4e00-8a91-351afa67ef61">
<li local-id=3D"f181ab50-92d0-4100-afc8-1ca967e6fc27">
<p local-id=3D"c36aea48-661a-46fa-a0d8-05412764351c">970g of metal powder (=
choose one: 17-4 PH stainless steel, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f0dff885-3904-4052-9f55-a8efeddd4853">
<p local-id=3D"ace587af-1c92-4009-b95b-43a0369534c3">1g of 3-(Trimethoxysil=
yl)propyl methacrylate (=CE=B3-MPS)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"de0b3fbe-4414-4b6f-b98d-d08439c41938">
<p local-id=3D"380279f5-ec5b-465c-8ad3-1023c32a8133">100mL of Isopropyl Alc=
ohol (IPA)</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"64c42260-2c71-48e1-834e-736ab9b7cd06" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalSlurry(97%Metal,3%TotalBinder).1">For 1000g Final Meta=
l Slurry (97% Metal, 3% Total Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"59bf6216-1bc4-4f9f-949b-a9c57ffdd2fa"><strong>Pre-treated Me=
tal Powder</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"2b70cea0-8c33-4957-95b0-539d788150b4">
<li local-id=3D"f56677b0-5fc1-49c6-8f99-b93cc0627a71">
<p local-id=3D"f52c73df-7cdb-41c0-aa67-6668489915e9">970g of silane-treated=
 metal powder</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"104f623c-fd6f-4571-b976-e08f22b0bdb9"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (30g total - 3% of final mixture)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"4139e1d4-f1be-4aaa-9fe3-199aa44540df">
<li local-id=3D"8072f829-767e-491f-a0ef-6d77883b2b79">
<p local-id=3D"6342f8f2-1f04-434e-a826-b1abb8f7c142">9g Polyethylene glycol=
 diacrylate (PEGDA, Mn ~575) (30% of binder) - <em>water-soluble component<=
/em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a52c7877-a78e-4895-9a36-c1e7cd45cf46">
<p local-id=3D"c626f436-fa0d-47ae-86da-26ec229720bf">6g Poly(vinyl alcohol)=
 (PVA, hydrolysis 87-90%, Mw ~30,000) (20% of binder) - <em>water-soluble c=
omponent</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fc14fe96-0864-4da9-be38-840d919c0677">
<p local-id=3D"be564ab0-ced1-475e-8a4e-85ed23b9b83d">6g Triethylene glycol =
dimethacrylate (TEG-DMA) (20% of binder) - <em>non-water-soluble component<=
/em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4950a8bc-7e26-48fa-9425-8ef3d2e06aeb">
<p local-id=3D"c169cd2d-b54d-47c7-af72-dabc5929a76a">7.5g Polymethyl methac=
rylate (PMMA) (25% of binder) - <em>non-water-soluble component</em></p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"6521a225-8ed7-4db6-9a25-9c248db5e0c6">
<p local-id=3D"35e3def1-5f6a-491d-8da5-2343b27e14e0">1.5g Phenylbis(2,4,6-t=
rimethylbenzoyl)phosphine oxide (TPO) (5% of binder) - <em>photoinitiator</=
em></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"98926752-1ef4-48c3-8d0c-cd332add89cf"><strong>Solvents/Dilue=
nts</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"4ec887b1-12cb-473e-aa80-730c59abdd06">
<li local-id=3D"4bbcf1b1-2e6e-48aa-9d16-7b0698512819">
<p local-id=3D"fe2e89a0-3d2f-4200-9a51-492087512d83">30g Deionized water</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a28c56b-f480-4b41-89e0-63530cae186e">
<p local-id=3D"93f2ca79-f546-4892-b956-aa9962107957">30g Ethanol (or Isopro=
panol)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f54bebde-024b-4ed1-9eac-d5bbf0ddd42d">
<p local-id=3D"0170d017-871d-4967-beae-5ce01e499dc0">0.6g Dispersant (e.g.,=
 Darvan C or Dolapix CE64) (2% of binder weight)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"19ca21ff-5439-4790-9ca2-62021c87b419"><strong>Equipment</str=
ong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"0043692b-709e-48a8-b21e-8df7fa71248a">
<li local-id=3D"bf7e361b-c810-4920-ae30-9a534c84f0ef">
<p local-id=3D"edb3a98d-f576-444b-bf77-b1cdb59c1b25">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1b61db29-d46e-4a99-999a-1c809c9836b2">
<p local-id=3D"0e0418d7-d4c0-49b2-8b9f-bcd1080406f1">Glass containers with =
amber/dark tinting or aluminum foil covering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4ff7b450-1d16-4a86-9d1d-03dd71c9d968">
<p local-id=3D"ba020b30-7693-4f74-94b0-db770aa0a0d4">High-shear mixer or ul=
trasonic homogenizer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"14aba444-bd79-41f8-a76a-96cbd34b09f9">
<p local-id=3D"c27d1118-ad44-455c-86da-8636787b5570">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"831f81ee-9954-4cb5-b372-d93839199d37">
<p local-id=3D"cc71a00f-e10c-4260-b4a3-74f44e99d6fa">UV light source (365-4=
05nm wavelength)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"451a545e-68c5-4d0c-b046-ff793234ffd5">
<p local-id=3D"bf692a7c-9810-49ea-8972-5fb6e6d93d11">UV safety equipment (U=
V-blocking eyewear, gloves, covered skin)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fd5d3777-abed-4bc0-8ee3-8f55008c4947">
<p local-id=3D"0378b652-8786-4c9c-aef0-6205364310fc">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"16c43ce7-b3c4-4d2e-9220-d60c085c797f">
<p local-id=3D"42355af9-c0e2-4456-8b7f-b8d84150a9e9">Viscometer (optional b=
ut recommended)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"2cd3ed4d-a3e2-40e4-8370-bc4ed5757fb3" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.6">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"7bbe89c7-3a6c-49bf-bec6-0a9b37a98d4c" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.MetalPowderSilanePre-Treatment.2">A. Metal Powder Silane Pre-Treatment=
</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"88dd3ee2-da59-46cc-b451-ad7e8f03114a">
<li local-id=3D"623815a3-d19a-49fa-93e9-74e8a0abe752">
<p local-id=3D"078871d1-0d6d-4cbf-b5fc-c80b603b1a77">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, add 1g of 3-(Trimethoxysilyl)propyl methacrylate to 100mL of isopropyl=
 alcohol in a suitable container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"85d200f9-511c-4fa5-8b86-48544c13bd44">
<p local-id=3D"a6301355-ad5f-4c98-9d9a-0c71e7d8dd05">Stir the solution gent=
ly for 5 minutes, then let it stand for 30 minutes to allow hydrolysis of t=
he silane coupling agent.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8d6d8a45-cf2c-4317-bdf3-9e5b58c8e628">
<p local-id=3D"f1692a69-4299-4b77-8b37-5ad5baa50e1c">Place 970g of metal po=
wder in a large mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a7a0fc25-8e5c-417f-946a-f64e3eed27da">
<p local-id=3D"c0ab1eeb-d33e-49b3-915f-3fb52d19587f">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the hydrolyzed silane solution to the metal powder.</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"869e1df1-4663-4608-af1f-f8378ce9d74e">
<p local-id=3D"a79af8cb-0c61-4d78-bd74-5467affec085">Continue mixing for 15=
-20 minutes to ensure even distribution of the silane solution over all met=
al particles.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3b1c5362-39a6-4ec5-aa0e-f3c1e27b7a89">
<p local-id=3D"f8a8b5ba-32b4-46c3-8232-c232796aa0d8">Spread the treated pow=
der on drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"255a84a5-e73f-4acd-9d5d-ad871cd39835">
<p local-id=3D"c0a6931e-6040-4103-afdb-409b72fe61c7">Dry at 60=C2=B0C for 2=
-3 hours to remove the isopropyl alcohol.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"26f241dc-ef89-46b6-98bc-3ffa93603a03">
<p local-id=3D"97f87e32-e3a7-4d29-b77e-0b30dbffcec3">Allow the treated powd=
er to cool to room temperature. The silane-treated metal powder is now read=
y for slurry preparation.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"97a42b3d-207b-4967-8ad2-6027d1fb5869" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.Water-SolubleComponentPreparation.1">B. Water-Soluble Component Prepar=
ation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"6de96031-0b39-4cc1-8f39-5d05c3a6ea88"><strong>Work in subdue=
d lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"06329036-dc7f-4473-a8f2-971c5b7d3ee8">
<li local-id=3D"b1f9ff84-f4a9-4900-8ee4-b882d4a7ebf7">
<p local-id=3D"1ceeb6f0-40c2-4b2c-bb5e-6ebd0cbe7d42">In a suitable containe=
r, add 30g of deionized water.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"09ae2cee-9caa-49ff-a62b-5ac1b0555ec4">
<p local-id=3D"dcb70443-35f2-4e38-bc4e-826ec96053bb">Heat the water to 80=
=C2=B0C and slowly add 6g of PVA while stirring.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b7b7f51b-3047-4f86-9e93-f6216aa2d9c4">
<p local-id=3D"55a1f5c0-fe29-43b3-b80d-ab8c59c73c75">Continue stirring unti=
l the PVA is completely dissolved (approximately 30-45 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"14e12939-100b-4063-bd42-cc0cc5dc149f">
<p local-id=3D"ab5326ec-a5b0-4e6a-9e96-69c6be3d038a">Allow the PVA solution=
 to cool to room temperature.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"b270313a-15b7-4dcf-9913-8736bac2a8e8" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.UV-CurableComponentPreparation.1">C. UV-Curable Component Preparation<=
/h3>
<p local-id=3D"9864267e-653c-4c7f-a67a-d24938a9f152"><strong>Work in subdue=
d lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7aaf53c5-ce86-4cbf-aa76-1715f98c0fac">
<li local-id=3D"6b2be0f9-6dd1-4372-88a9-2aa78defe066">
<p local-id=3D"600510b7-b47a-4d29-aa04-5cc88a034414">In a separate amber gl=
ass container, mix 30g of ethanol with 0.6g of dispersant.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"33cc49ca-391c-4534-a3f5-ecb3fc11f464">
<p local-id=3D"bdacaa51-c43a-4fc7-a4f8-0280e631bf83">Add 7.5g of PMMA and s=
tir until completely dissolved.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"48dbb445-58cc-4b49-a73d-529be24400b4">
<p local-id=3D"15525702-e72c-4b66-bc2d-7295bc276f04">Add 6g of TEG-DMA and =
stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"70058b8b-56a2-496d-9322-09521669fa95">
<p local-id=3D"5b3f1737-f864-40c4-a15e-ae529892d532">Add 9g of PEGDA and mi=
x thoroughly.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"35bd4d92-9668-46b6-9870-88411f1f613b">
<p local-id=3D"3a1ec059-60fc-4b30-9137-960b37c38180">Finally, add 1.5g of T=
PO photoinitiator and stir gently until completely dissolved.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"381e0d02-3852-42c7-8d01-d59259686ce1" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.SlurryPreparation.1">D. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"dada62db-9466-40cf-b1e3-941a9fb15b2a"><strong>Continue worki=
ng in subdued lighting</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"4f582fb2-c1e5-44bf-8d8f-01ad2020c01b">
<li local-id=3D"b6b1fa50-4bed-4a1a-8742-0094a500051c">
<p local-id=3D"4395cf43-8dd9-408b-83ba-e9f495946870">Combine the water-solu=
ble PVA solution with the UV-curable component solution and mix thoroughly.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f0ec6555-b77f-4346-ad37-abfb853fdf22">
<p local-id=3D"36f01478-e11c-4732-9168-05953ced8099">Place the 970g of pre-=
treated metal powder in a high-shear mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a0158af9-eb44-440f-a68b-68913ce4dc74">
<p local-id=3D"3c7cc294-f6bd-4f6d-8311-fd495a231f8f">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the combined binder solution to the pre-treated metal =
powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0a77d172-5a70-4184-8b96-51454018ff50">
<p local-id=3D"8aaa82a4-7011-4c4b-b0f2-0e8b652b9230">Increase to high-shear=
 mixing for 15-20 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder =
throughout the metal powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"edbcd7ed-5863-4a44-9749-a5395346874b">
<p local-id=3D"83336216-e430-4a95-8f7c-c2c1c10e9852">Check the viscosity of=
 the slurry - it should be pourable but not too fluid. If needed:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"97d420dc-f0e3-4606-a91d-36cc7ecd2f78">
<li local-id=3D"1ec3264b-d7d0-40ce-91ed-a0aa33698b45">
<p local-id=3D"ebef957f-4640-4ff4-8016-14f3640119bd">If too thick: Add smal=
l amounts of additional water/ethanol mixture (1:1 ratio) in 5g increments<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"03fe9c59-d771-48c4-a036-f02f2dfb6da9">
<p local-id=3D"31dff008-60ed-4f83-abba-6183bdbb1ad4">If too thin: Add small=
 amounts of PVA solution to increase viscosity</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"682d6504-44f6-490b-a57f-93dd8f32dc1b">
<p local-id=3D"fa219382-9bed-4373-a261-d40fe9c18741">The slurry is now read=
y for pouring into molds.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"37a51f4a-17f0-4565-9528-ee73175f6ecd" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.CastingandUVCuring.1">E. Casting and UV Curing</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"78772aae-ef0e-44d9-bc98-cf9348ccf605">
<li local-id=3D"eb0e2b97-1e14-4c09-9324-7999e8051a3d">
<p local-id=3D"ef94a1f3-dff1-40e3-a6ab-981b3c5f32ef">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1443c3fb-b4de-4b20-9dc6-a8fc69b49a82">
<p local-id=3D"e180f04a-8c34-407e-89f1-7cd7551a9783">Pour the prepared slur=
ry into the molds. Consider using vibration or vacuum to remove any trapped=
 air bubbles.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b9db8ee8-17dd-4e7e-a1f4-20e13aff5218">
<p local-id=3D"58f70852-3ec0-48bc-8804-91c8b606ed45">Allow the slurry to se=
ttle for 5-10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"636c3726-15b5-48bd-9c1e-46f4ed2a1e5c">
<p local-id=3D"daf4250f-5d2d-4f3d-bc61-bf2a6bd7f4f2">Expose the filled mold=
 to UV light (365-405nm wavelength) for crosslinking:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"1ee24125-382d-4c26-803a-9d40c7cc4e40">
<li local-id=3D"4d80d25d-1e95-4a69-9665-92937f2d9c13">
<p local-id=3D"a6bccb93-534e-45b2-9c02-4ce46f1cee82">For thin sections (&lt=
; 5mm): Expose for 3-6 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5e767e96-1130-4554-b72f-234e1b941f71">
<p local-id=3D"e25a9a52-31b4-43c9-b677-8aebb802daec">For thicker sections: =
Use a staged approach with multiple shorter exposures from different angles=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c89db47b-5ae2-4c4d-bbf7-9801f5c1d6db">
<p local-id=3D"2f970d7e-2a33-4706-b857-993230dcb695">Allow 30-60 seconds be=
tween exposures to prevent excessive heat buildup</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"f9072936-cfb0-4282-a60f-82144a37efa8">
<p local-id=3D"b5e70d65-1f83-4ad7-963b-329c1fc6d7bf">Allow the part to cool=
 completely after UV curing.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"800e0350-cbc9-4765-ad6c-14d94f5c8d84" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.PrimaryDebinding(Water-SolubleComponentRemoval).1">F. Primary Debindin=
g (Water-Soluble Component Removal)</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"8f71d84f-7ebf-4d4c-bea5-c1287e81e6ad">
<li local-id=3D"e73b5ff5-2bd7-4a01-8b90-025ce51f361e">
<p local-id=3D"987e674c-cd8f-485a-86f8-842f2e4cb31b">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in warm water (50-60=C2=B0C) to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"cecf8013-30ef-4252-afaf-e0a4cbdedf9d">
<p local-id=3D"41d0fa58-03f9-4ae3-ad7b-cf0f093b152f">After the mold is comp=
letely dissolved, continue soaking the part to begin dissolving the water-s=
oluble components of the binder (PVA and PEGDA).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2620ef9b-7470-4ce2-8c4f-4c2c2a4ff65f">
<p local-id=3D"5c3bb07a-67f1-4f4d-9b63-bc01499f4782">Change the water every=
 2-3 hours to facilitate faster dissolution.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"eb0a9b56-55c3-475c-ae74-929627218c7c">
<p local-id=3D"0347ea34-d0e5-4b76-9eaa-642c7255f2ba">Total immersion time w=
ill depend on part thickness but typically requires 12-24 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c8c6c323-e9e5-4e7d-83ee-abd1e97c9417">
<p local-id=3D"61a69f39-3698-4e8b-b5e5-d9e70e9be0b3">Once the primary water=
-soluble components are dissolved, carefully remove the part and dry it at =
room temperature for 12 hours, followed by gentle heating at 40=C2=B0C for =
2 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fbc60ee9-3ba6-4d02-89bd-86d629dda259">
<p local-id=3D"32726c10-7349-4be7-b649-43f2ae0ffe5a">The part is now partia=
lly debound but still held together by the non-water-soluble components (PM=
MA and TEG-DMA).</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"59abbbe3-5fcb-4c61-b148-bb7ff4b9e971" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-G.SecondaryDebindingandSintering.1">G. Secondary Debinding and Sintering=
</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"062b01e2-e3bb-46f2-ace4-c091880514b8">
<li local-id=3D"6ef5efa0-8255-4b8f-b26b-a36118f8e7e8">
<p local-id=3D"73ed21ea-3749-4531-aaf7-7a9f4a85441d">Follow standard therma=
l debinding protocols to remove the remaining organic components:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"dc1e02a5-cf3c-4434-a036-15a570626f9a">
<li local-id=3D"b268a9cb-b744-4aa8-92dd-40216e023af8">
<p local-id=3D"89bc4e90-5d2a-4d64-997a-f9b6654921da">Slow heating rate (1-2=
=C2=B0C/min) to 300=C2=B0C with appropriate hold times</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"edd92ec8-ce38-4b73-900e-49f7394d1f08">
<p local-id=3D"0923d65c-ad3f-4214-8756-1117e73cf40b">Continue to final debi=
nding temperature based on the specific binder components</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"db719559-6f42-4a23-83bf-f97056a14b23">
<p local-id=3D"83a64625-f398-4d96-900e-77e273555459">Proceed with standard =
sintering protocol for the specific metal alloy (17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or C=
uCrZr).</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"b4f21006-bd6a-4586-a942-ad03d8549d4f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Notes.5">Notes</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"2fcc52e2-da03-4833-8d1a-7ad1efedb2f9">
<li local-id=3D"b1682599-9241-47bc-89cf-9886155a44fc">
<p local-id=3D"6215ea98-b095-45b9-a2f8-c6ed0cb2dd6d"><strong>Dual-Component=
 Binder System Benefits</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"0005c1b5-e4fb-4f35-8045-796816e23491">
<li local-id=3D"9df257c5-ca68-4b47-8c8c-f7cb188a20ea">
<p local-id=3D"0c48c4c2-af88-4c89-b9ae-e4797641a3e8">Water-soluble componen=
ts (PVA and PEGDA) allow for primary debinding via water immersion</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"833ff104-9d2b-4cb6-bae7-0e61c474e640">
<p local-id=3D"3fd3ea63-9550-4cc1-83e3-be28fdbe85a3">PMMA and TEG-DMA provi=
de structural integrity during the water debinding step</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2cac4715-7a3e-4810-8648-00ad593eb9d1">
<p local-id=3D"172791a8-f54a-45d0-9d63-29c4686f708a">The combination allows=
 for lower total organic content during thermal debinding</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"560b11e6-c965-45e7-bc64-3b43797604df">
<p local-id=3D"93f9ab99-7968-44c9-a829-da2e8ff2cb2d">Reduced risk of defect=
s from rapid gas evolution during thermal debinding</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"f0050d97-a951-461c-8c4e-d3553518d14f">
<p local-id=3D"38c38b52-6135-4494-a42e-2d242ff45812"><strong>Slurry Propert=
ies</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"fa81d15c-d516-45ad-9bd2-164ef9d65d66">
<li local-id=3D"443f4138-9334-444f-9c3d-bbb7d3fdea58">
<p local-id=3D"e99e82ae-aba0-4ad8-b628-aa37a693369f">The ethanol and water =
create a homogeneous system that will evaporate slowly, giving good working=
 time</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"34d598ad-d18e-4cba-bb1d-da5155b29f8d">
<p local-id=3D"456da5cc-dc69-4771-aba3-962367c56ad4">PVA acts as both a bin=
der and a rheology modifier</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c3f11d75-eece-4e0b-b885-57047cf876d7">
<p local-id=3D"007d4290-4030-4d61-8339-41b3d8b2c982">PEGDA provides both wa=
ter solubility and UV-curability through its acrylate groups</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"eba740fe-93a0-4e4d-9bd5-25b952ae4988">
<p local-id=3D"f8a9f777-b03d-4800-bee1-a401a650f807">The dispersant is cruc=
ial for preventing metal particle agglomeration in the slurry</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"d1afec51-f4ed-4f28-816e-eae01d0e2a09">
<p local-id=3D"bbf59b7b-7448-4b1a-869c-45d1abc0bf8e"><strong>Key Process Co=
ntrols</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"cdc1411e-3727-452e-bd7f-c1eae93e580f">
<li local-id=3D"2a2316a1-6672-4147-b782-b6b52ed8aae0">
<p local-id=3D"c9c4ab9a-5c52-4a0d-81ba-12fd49dc5062">Viscosity is critical =
- too thin and particles may settle before curing; too thick and pouring be=
comes difficult</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"91f1d911-0e1f-48c5-89c2-33f3c0f7a513">
<p local-id=3D"add7cf37-fe7d-4101-91aa-082c2bc2bbce">UV exposure time must =
be sufficient to cure throughout the volume, not just the surface</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4bbedb04-5c0d-4478-9455-e6a5f7bf3d28">
<p local-id=3D"ad45de09-cd08-4fe8-96b1-598807762c91">Water temperature duri=
ng primary debinding affects dissolution rate and potential distortion</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"c4cea545-ab01-44d4-b814-2650d2561bc5">
<p local-id=3D"2eb6d517-5084-4569-a052-649ad50a046c"><strong>Metal Loading =
Optimization</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"b8012e9a-7da0-4e14-b38d-b8ec7f400914">
<li local-id=3D"2cbadb7a-a439-4882-aa77-af4559bdfab6">
<p local-id=3D"0e2860f9-8721-4484-a4d6-56d460107a21">This formulation uses =
97% metal loading, which is high for a pourable slurry</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"acd25672-387c-4571-be7e-3c574abf1d3f">
<p local-id=3D"4eff8a76-9328-4dbc-8194-c3b530679eeb">The silane treatment i=
s essential for maintaining flowability at this high metal content</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cd3cbf06-7bb9-430d-ac9f-3eeb930fefbd">
<p local-id=3D"65d93b74-0ef1-4fb3-8cdb-31ee8aa2b930">If pouring issues occu=
r, metal content can be reduced to 95-96% by adjusting the formulation</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"2660d918-56f6-4c59-8941-787ac01ab782">
<p local-id=3D"53a49108-3ac2-49a8-9470-c94b1c3a1fdf"><strong>Potential Chal=
lenges and Solutions</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f47ea802-edc7-44a4-9e36-abeb39fced23">
<li local-id=3D"47eb172e-911d-430e-a82d-d85ed0fbfa62">
<p local-id=3D"3fe4e3a5-77fe-4237-a727-681bc03fb9d7"><strong>Sedimentation<=
/strong>: If metal particles settle too quickly before UV curing, consider =
adding 0.1-0.2% xanthan gum to the water component</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"81f3887c-f6a1-47b4-9b60-f057a81d3290">
<p local-id=3D"90b26780-5d8b-44cb-b262-e97062b8f167"><strong>Incomplete Cur=
ing</strong>: For thicker sections, consider adding a secondary thermal cur=
ing step at 80=C2=B0C for 30 minutes after UV exposure</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"54957d78-2859-4aba-ad2e-b3586bd664d0">
<p local-id=3D"a0ff8ce3-eac1-410c-9768-36da1f761677"><strong>Poor Surface F=
inish</strong>: If surface definition is insufficient, increase the PVA con=
tent slightly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"937bdd4a-2407-44e7-af2d-6261b92df70c">
<p local-id=3D"58613bad-1b35-4d25-82e3-67ff1b426225"><strong>Cracking Durin=
g Drying</strong>: Slow the drying rate after water debinding by using a hu=
midity-controlled environment</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"242b02e2-19ef-416b-9d0a-87084218181c">
<p local-id=3D"aee8d422-97d1-4682-8207-7d9b10b72382"><strong>Storage Consid=
erations</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4e458062-16d5-4f46-9edd-c71f7612b552">
<li local-id=3D"e479a6e9-e2a5-4773-b682-b67b77b56311">
<p local-id=3D"1284c14c-f6e8-41a5-b17b-369ea9c55619">The prepared slurry ha=
s limited working time (4-8 hours) and should be used promptly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bb9cba59-1190-494d-8307-6aa5cc5a684c">
<p local-id=3D"5d024cd1-dc84-4977-96d4-d3bedccce13d">Store any unused slurr=
y in light-proof, sealed containers in a refrigerator (4-8=C2=B0C) to exten=
d working time</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e186b6b2-6a1a-4390-a245-5227b56c5278">
<p local-id=3D"24e5116a-3a59-40ad-abb9-1cd0bd9233b0">Allow refrigerated slu=
rry to return to room temperature before use and check viscosity</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"e1391433-9d3f-4fb7-af76-4eaf66d3bb98">
<p local-id=3D"41397bed-618f-4b73-9104-ecabfdb8bddf">Perform all steps invo=
lving solvents in a well-ventilated area away from ignition sources</p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"bc3f0263-1f2d-4da1-ac46-8a01ac0762bf">
<p local-id=3D"26015489-88d6-4f69-bf71-09fc5c99cac1">The water-soluble comp=
onents also make this process more environmentally friendly</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"69920176-3d12-422f-82f5-cc6457ca6470"></p>
<p local-id=3D"715d331f-4f62-43be-aae5-44cec46c76a8">I have tasked Mahmood =
with making that recipe work so it can be dispensed from a needle as a slur=
ry then cured in a layer-by-layer 3D printing process, particularly focused=
 on making ceramic parts, although it should be compatible with metal powde=
rs as well, possible with some changes to the binder formulation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5c870113-39f2-42fb-b63d-32bb6f78548e"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1216acc6-a791-4b6e-a873-67a435d2cf4e">PILOT: I have printed =
and installed heat set inserts in the new version of the Micro Drop mount t=
hat will have a limit switch mounted to it.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5054ece7-87ab-4a32-8545-d46d64971f7f">Completed printing and=
 post-processing window frames for 3X laser safety windows, and also cut of=
f 4mm of the acrylic windows to reduce the length from 204mm to 200mm (the =
nominal spec is 200mm, but they seem to always be cut slightly long). Windo=
ws and frames were given to Ben to install when he has the time.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ecb84354-4109-4102-94af-5af41e6009ba">R&amp;D Weekly Meeting=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"b19a2b7d-5ce0-4b32-b59e-7771c9f8e786">To do:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"1dc48e00-cb80-4d0f-ba6a-9965d94f8773">
<li local-id=3D"b66e3590-8cf0-439c-bc93-03077107145e">
<p local-id=3D"1c3709e6-ee4a-412f-b818-f01ca38fc8e9">Reinstall stepper tapp=
er</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3a16a7df-b7c8-4097-b0aa-f5552460416d">
<p local-id=3D"497f379e-e77e-487b-8606-58a60e893ebb">Switch back to steel s=
haft, print new roller to be compatible with steel shaft</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c6f0ce66-eacd-4209-8528-0ee94417b1b5">
<p local-id=3D"4d2ce6ad-f045-43ff-a62d-2e479e70ee12">Make another V4.0 HOPP=
ER system for benchtop testing</p>
<ul local-id=3D"91e74452-be9d-4546-a374-f0661a5c760b">
<li local-id=3D"03617519-04ea-48d2-afc2-7554f271d237">
<p local-id=3D"61cfde92-9d64-4d4e-a8b0-42fc3cd5ba35">Order NEMA 11 motors</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"06413cd7-a225-489e-9ed2-3d85d8c35782">
<p local-id=3D"4cec7c72-02c9-4eab-acbc-49927f2ebcc3">Order springs</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"b17b674d-28f1-404b-bdda-90026202dcde">
<p local-id=3D"5cb60111-6632-4b03-9d1e-cb8b68a2ed62">Reinstall heater on PI=
LOT 2</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"270b55b1-47ef-4b6d-9ec4-4d41d08d707f"></p>
<p local-id=3D"ba0ac9eb-a0cc-4775-9374-b8ec06c6186a">2025-05-12</p>
<p local-id=3D"284abb61-5bf2-4f65-8009-a163c0db81b0">REDRESS: I came in ove=
r the weekend and added 0.3g of Aerosil R 812 S to the latest batch of powd=
er (2% binder load) for a total of 0.4g of Aerosil in the batch, which made=
 it significantly more flowable. I then filled a water-soluble mold and cur=
ed it. The part seemed quite strong when pressing it with a toothpick, but =
it fell apart when dissolving the mold. I dissolved off the mold by immersi=
ng that green part entirely, which historically has caused the part to fall=
 apart more readily so it may be worth running the same experiment again wi=
th a staged mold dissolution process. I am also working on a new binder rec=
ipe that should be easier to grind and produce stronger green parts:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"2e04de1d-e964-41f2-907c-266929271810" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-EnhancedThermal-CurableAquaMold=E2=84=A2BinderRecipeforImprovedGreenPart=
Strength">Enhanced Thermal-Curable AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Binder Recipe for Impr=
oved Green Part Strength</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"4531e2c4-21a2-458a-8c97-d33954548b33" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.7">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"31a75442-1e0f-47e5-9908-9b3a172f5337" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalPowderMixture(98%Metal,2%Binder).1">For 1000g Final Me=
tal Powder Mixture (98% Metal, 2% Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"bdbfe427-0019-45b8-9544-05e23c5e63fc"><strong>Metal Powder</=
strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"520ff0d9-db74-403a-bc37-9137300c77af">
<li local-id=3D"f90df501-3df2-4f0b-b6da-464aed3c4246">
<p local-id=3D"25ffbfc6-25ac-41a8-bda4-b68d00c369cd">980g of metal powder (=
choose one: 17-4 PH stainless steel, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"3b494fcd-091d-4cb4-9fd2-7b77c3effe0a"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (20g total - 2% of final mixture)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7b21b3f3-42af-4450-a6f5-d6d9ed9d56da">
<li local-id=3D"bc214829-a9e1-4523-a0c3-bda4dd4060a1">
<p local-id=3D"d7f80088-3b81-4045-ac42-e98472d4f0c5">12.0g Poly(methyl meth=
acrylate) (PMMA) (60% of binder)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d26aebc1-6eb5-4db2-acc7-23563abac8db">
<p local-id=3D"dc7cae37-b4a5-434b-8317-6e6bc25e30c8">5.0g Triethylene glyco=
l dimethacrylate (TEG-DMA) (25% of binder) - <em>increased</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3eaf3905-41f0-427a-9429-56e08a7f9674">
<p local-id=3D"f766f013-1d30-4f07-bd7b-e935736d254c">0.8g Azobisisobutyroni=
trile (AIBN) (4% of binder) - <em>increased</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cb3e7a5f-2264-4031-8ae4-49ff1cc05ec6">
<p local-id=3D"b962b41a-93dc-478a-9501-9dddc2e0544a">1.0g Dibutyl phthalate=
 (DBP) (5% of binder) - <em>increased</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4064ae85-ecb3-44c1-a14d-ed2a830d0961">
<p local-id=3D"9c2a9f6b-9504-484e-a965-f59134e2cea8">0.2g Polyethylene glyc=
ol (PEG 4000) (1% of binder) - <em>added</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"699a3c98-b734-4347-aeef-fcb56b9dc66e">
<p local-id=3D"6d5f8fd5-fb2c-46f1-8a0d-b533aed0847a">0.6g Stearic acid (3% =
of binder) - <em>added</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"505019ca-bb01-4a32-9e40-aabc8c91e871">
<p local-id=3D"9a49081a-e6b6-4d6b-a579-7f953f637fcb">0.4g Aerosil R 812 S (=
fumed silica) (2% of binder)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"ae2621c5-82f1-4fe4-bc45-f670d47963c4"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b28d3bd7-df94-494a-86b0-b49a9ccc8a58">
<li local-id=3D"be6972c3-98f6-45e2-aaae-3e47351177cd">
<p local-id=3D"fd2cad5b-a28a-45dc-a990-762172872c6d">200-220g Acetone (10-1=
1:1 ratio with binder solids) - <em>increased</em></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"84d8007d-7dc9-4165-bc75-ba4fd0c413e3"><strong>Equipment</str=
ong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7249a2bd-bf5e-44c5-955a-f3db65bddf2e">
<li local-id=3D"697b3b0f-ae21-435f-a24a-72600c63fedb">
<p local-id=3D"316565d1-4ba0-435d-a516-1283ab0a7fbd">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"77d81bff-59da-4ee6-91be-e7921f2288df">
<p local-id=3D"f4235599-13c1-49b0-91dc-1dee206c777a">Glass containers with =
amber/dark tinting or aluminum foil covering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"083b19ae-7e27-4d8b-8744-3d1306a92f4f">
<p local-id=3D"dc86ae16-3e20-44d5-b2fb-3fe8a329d7f0">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"58ea8ed4-3aa9-408d-a50a-fa77a17b75a9">
<p local-id=3D"7b1699b5-3295-4ddd-8636-a37208ace956">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"56509e11-f7a7-4aeb-9d96-309796bfc517">
<p local-id=3D"1bf4690c-6cb3-417e-be2e-28ab1b8196f4">Controlled temperature=
 oven with precise temperature control</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"38a0ae81-274c-4342-9683-4d7e4eb6b73e">
<p local-id=3D"41793984-11cc-4994-9b36-552a7ece7057">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a72f313c-a6d7-4803-a38b-ddcf89cc79ae">
<p local-id=3D"cc5a93e8-34aa-46d8-bbd9-8c60d72c2f61">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0b7f3401-61f2-4ec3-bcbf-9136d9c937cf">
<p local-id=3D"7ef3037f-b9e0-4e88-96e0-8730fbad6915">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5c8bf5e2-c03f-4c33-8dd1-01cdd1226440">
<p local-id=3D"40da979e-e3aa-49a6-bcb9-325a069b1a38">Thermal curing oven (c=
apable of precise control from 60-120=C2=B0C)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1b015df2-180c-4b8f-8519-c1afb7c5c1d9">
<p local-id=3D"f6ba3495-03a5-49da-b5c5-a2c25ed16261">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"f92f2f72-94eb-4233-9ec1-c3d91b899f00" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.7">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"e7077c02-e9d9-4c7a-9f2b-d4a202487e9b" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.BinderPreparation.4">A. Binder Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"0ffe160d-b7a1-4a6a-ac4e-821e224e617d">
<li local-id=3D"233649ca-bb27-4fde-a9af-84bc33bdef88">
<p local-id=3D"ce987b2b-9444-48c8-aadf-1e2c8b841e36">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 200g of acetone into a suitable container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"31da8764-1c30-49c3-ba24-13fdc818ba9c">
<p local-id=3D"eb463ea1-4abb-46d3-b6e0-5d25c47924bf">While stirring, add 0.=
2g of PEG 4000 and stir until completely dissolved.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f20d8f51-1ed1-4c59-952f-d62e5ac71b21">
<p local-id=3D"39959efb-fbe6-4771-8aa5-370f2cf47355">Add 12.0g of PMMA to t=
he acetone solution. Stir until completely dissolved (approximately 30-60 m=
inutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c512df80-7717-43d6-acae-9e45e48f67da">
<p local-id=3D"15b09000-2de5-4916-a2aa-81ac3553c0a7">Add 5.0g of TEG-DMA an=
d stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3eddf0cf-2375-4275-9ce3-9f2a77b74fed">
<p local-id=3D"3e766344-0909-4188-8d2c-17c3f91342ac">Add 1.0g of dibutyl ph=
thalate (DBP) and stir thoroughly for 5 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dd407d65-618a-42d9-a9cb-a8a7fbc3be73">
<p local-id=3D"4ff8a030-85e8-4dcf-a816-3dd02bfb6580">Add 0.6g of stearic ac=
id and stir until completely dissolved.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9e1263b2-fb5e-4b84-8212-5016779fef23">
<p local-id=3D"49dce18c-30b9-4b2f-9167-90dc21119942">Finally, add 0.8g of A=
IBN and stir gently until completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e1cd4b0f-a842-4470-bb0d-212c653e1c22">
<p local-id=3D"98fdf5e1-aad2-431c-a801-81b5e77a2ed0">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation. The binder solution =
is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"55aa794e-455f-4f34-82b0-33297c799016" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.SlurryPreparation.4">B. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5ede7911-5d17-420e-8b4b-24465b981006"><strong>Maintain tempe=
rature below 30=C2=B0C</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"79a2e0cd-6977-4203-a953-f2d748a9fbe9">
<li local-id=3D"fbdd1222-e028-49a7-b0ca-49872be81e40">
<p local-id=3D"f9070ac7-43e5-4c4d-a688-e88027c7d800">Place the 980g of meta=
l powder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"057e3c7a-4416-4e54-9c23-000a3a08843d">
<p local-id=3D"6958f659-6ef0-423a-9d92-1ad0c26793dd">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the metal powder.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"f3fa93c5-be14-4e32-b72a-62e7a0e3a846">
<p local-id=3D"579ae323-c3ea-4521-93a2-d2f8dbd9cc35">Continue mixing for 45=
-60 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder throughout the=
 metal powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"19650a1e-a466-4a4b-b541-d50dd95f877c">
<p local-id=3D"629a52ef-81d9-453c-abd3-0dad4362ae9a">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 20g) to achieve p=
roper consistency.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cec4e936-1353-4f42-be17-53ded39ff78d">
<p local-id=3D"58d0e9b0-1a7f-40d3-9402-6a5f4bdac255">Keep the temperature b=
elow 30=C2=B0C during mixing to prevent premature activation of the AIBN th=
ermal initiator.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"440ee058-32c0-45f1-8ae2-29d3a4de4260" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.Drying.4">C. Drying</h3>
<p local-id=3D"b8bd1595-7485-43d5-995d-4216843f1f00"><strong>Maintain moder=
ate temperature with gradual drying</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"ec73350e-24fb-4bb5-aa77-4abd7d5c48a3">
<li local-id=3D"6ceb14ba-203e-4b84-88d2-27018fa52198">
<p local-id=3D"282c7625-46c6-40d1-9fff-cc8ec4ae2f88">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ddc588c1-bcde-4884-8e3d-a5ac767435dd">
<p local-id=3D"1e664508-b7a5-4e56-bb07-565e8e0e0879">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature (20-25=C2=B0C) in a well-ventilated area for 12-=
16 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"94ce75c9-5d05-4792-9ae2-f982551ea2ab">
<p local-id=3D"7232652c-fb68-4fd2-92fb-edd557c2ccb7">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 35=C2=B0C for 6-8 hours (temperature must remain well below=
 AIBN activation temperature).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ed7933ac-7381-4b1b-83f0-c8f81771c3cc">
<p local-id=3D"0c2bc5d2-a66a-479b-b695-6338b9391d28">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 45=C2=B0C for 2-3 hours to ensure complete solvent removal =
without activating the AIBN.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fae7a5b8-ac6a-432a-a33b-d1ce93ff6ed4">
<p local-id=3D"02508c54-b005-4af5-a2df-625473ad7f38">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid but somewhat friable cake due=
 to the modified formulation.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"7795bd46-82a6-4eea-bada-ba2fc876bbe0" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.GrindingandSieving.4">D. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<p local-id=3D"0bdcf650-ed5b-42f3-97fa-65da709d0a61"><strong>Maintain cool =
conditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"38c09707-8dea-4b9b-894d-2a124cbd6365">
<li local-id=3D"5b31860a-38e8-4b22-9750-ac979a99e2b3">
<p local-id=3D"a31fa5a2-a063-42f1-8c7a-e1cb98092409">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces (should be easier with this formulation).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2cf5e70f-0c84-4411-9f3b-bbf6121c67be">
<p local-id=3D"e12d35c1-5923-4155-8ea4-14483f14efc4">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill at a moderate speed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"060486f5-f3ed-41e1-8474-d859a2f42904">
<p local-id=3D"f38ff93d-2d4f-4a7f-aa65-757a7b71fc12">Monitor temperature du=
ring grinding to stay below 50=C2=B0C to prevent premature AIBN activation.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5bc04333-1e4f-4647-a9cd-0ad5ca92dba7">
<p local-id=3D"ebba13a6-e909-49ad-8543-c58c510ec236">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
 for metal powder applications).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"64a44123-87c7-4dbf-a0bd-feff0a9475b0">
<p local-id=3D"0fccab48-a1ec-4769-9fb2-19eaa5e0e86b">Add 0.4g of Aerosil R =
812 S to the ground and sieved metal-binder powder mixture. Mix thoroughly =
to ensure even distribution and improved flowability.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1c18edbb-ef9b-4600-a9fc-595a1860d405">
<p local-id=3D"e60f4e69-ee91-4886-9dc7-710feab46471">Store the powder in ai=
rtight containers at cool temperature (below 20=C2=B0C) until ready for use=
.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"61434cac-323f-470e-90c5-35b8df5d67a5" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.EnhancedThermalCrosslinkingProcess">E. Enhanced Thermal Crosslinking P=
rocess</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"ecf0447c-334d-4a21-a11f-efd9d4dbd979">
<li local-id=3D"92489712-a0a1-44c8-8aa6-c5f3ac5b8420">
<p local-id=3D"f3ba50a4-60cb-4d7b-804a-567028f4783c">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology (PVA, specialized PLA, or other water-so=
luble polymer that can withstand 120=C2=B0C).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3caf5b46-a49e-4c0b-922a-e6b5ddc4f667">
<p local-id=3D"ee7fa1ed-ffad-46ad-9cdd-56f5d52880d2">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2cec4423-bc4a-4ca9-807f-71c5b46d2fac">
<p local-id=3D"0657573a-fd69-45dc-8576-49b7e2d1c8d8"><strong>Two-Stage Ther=
mal Curing</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"33932c79-57f2-456b-93d0-fb698842449e">
<li local-id=3D"fb319cbe-86fb-40d7-b7d8-5d67348d4633">
<p local-id=3D"ef096b09-3c76-4575-8243-1c7153726285"><strong>Initial Curing=
</strong>: Heat to 70=C2=B0C for 30 minutes to begin gradual AIBN activatio=
n</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"58b8ac69-c968-421a-94ed-3545788799db">
<p local-id=3D"0a9c7b6d-35d7-449e-80dc-412f64e0a47e"><strong>Primary Curing=
</strong>: Increase temperature to 90=C2=B0C for 60 minutes for TEG-DMA cro=
sslinking</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"032c5e08-3328-450e-9a46-b23bb7551913">
<p local-id=3D"94bf9e54-40cb-4a49-a4eb-df4b5a4b1942"><strong>Final Curing</=
strong>: Increase temperature to 110-120=C2=B0C for 30 minutes to maximize =
crosslinking density</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"752c275d-4357-49a8-b59a-fa1c31d11a6b">
<p local-id=3D"5edd4995-110f-4006-a27c-5e36aec75f7a">For thicker sections (=
&gt;10mm), extend the primary curing time to 90 minutes</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"7d0851f7-7ea4-47d3-8957-20bed94be4b9">
<p local-id=3D"b7205d56-0a25-48c3-b436-8d5c75f7e19a">Allow the part to cool=
 gradually to room temperature before proceeding (ideally cooling at 2-3=C2=
=B0C per minute).</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"b0c2fa7a-7d54-4a85-ae45-3cf30fe38194" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.ControlledDissolutionandGreenPartRecovery">F. Controlled Dissolution a=
nd Green Part Recovery</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"6c4654db-ddb5-41c8-b5dc-d46911a11a3f">
<li local-id=3D"af4232f7-af6c-47b6-aae4-2fea92612da3">
<p local-id=3D"2ba1b452-ab81-4834-8e0e-8b917b1e891e">Allow the thermally cu=
red part to rest for at least 4 hours after cooling to ensure complete cros=
slinking.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"242391e1-e150-4ff3-9805-cba2e19182cc">
<p local-id=3D"26704496-69ba-418a-af93-1d0f65e4ac5d">Prepare a warm water b=
ath at 40=C2=B0C (not hotter) with 1% table salt (NaCl) added to reduce wat=
er activity.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ca32976a-fc26-4030-a9df-68609504125a">
<p local-id=3D"90a2448e-97ad-4abd-a6b5-a06e857fe121">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in the warm water bath to gently dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"c1a18151-f630-49ba-b410-20a8bc4a6385">
<p local-id=3D"48b3a915-3bd5-44b6-be08-0de0ce329886">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh the water/salt solution as needed until mold is completely remove=
d (may take longer than previous formulation).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1f7b49a0-e994-40bb-b308-0cb9b47e7718">
<p local-id=3D"2555f414-8d01-423a-b1a4-1e883fbe394f">Do not agitate vigorou=
sly or use mechanical means to speed dissolution.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"66bed436-cb0d-4534-833a-120f2f098df8">
<p local-id=3D"a2e42d0b-6fff-4455-b268-6e920cef0873">Once the mold is fully=
 dissolved, carefully extract the green part and allow to dry at room tempe=
rature for 12 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5837ea0d-2d36-4330-9557-9bc445dc39d7">
<p local-id=3D"20707686-bdce-4094-a3bf-de9151ffef86">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to the standard protocol for yo=
ur specific metal alloy (17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr).</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"dc7229e0-3bc3-499a-bbb9-7480d090ea3a" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-TechnicalNotes.1">Technical Notes</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"9a2e1904-c123-4314-9dba-16e7bbc29814" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-FormulationEnhancementsforImprovedBalance">Formulation Enhancements for =
Improved Balance</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"deefc141-5040-4b8a-81e4-7075f1958e90">
<li local-id=3D"34832a67-7352-4212-be7f-169d635380b1">
<p local-id=3D"31325211-5a7f-4554-8733-9d94ffc414a6"><strong>Increased TEG-=
DMA (25% vs 15%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a4236af1-20fe-4f33-981d-98d5f4f21583">
<li local-id=3D"a1421b86-d3d0-4115-a376-07855d9eaa1b">
<p local-id=3D"9b6ef97a-89fb-478d-966f-0a9e79a663cf">Higher crosslinking mo=
nomer content creates a more rigid, stronger polymer network after curing</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"05dee155-932b-4d8f-b296-8eb355df5678">
<p local-id=3D"4c09241d-68f9-48c4-8dc5-1424b2e1a889">Significantly increase=
s green part strength after thermal curing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bf730047-e54f-4c52-ad9c-b1ef86f050a5">
<p local-id=3D"c80c35bb-10ac-423b-9580-66e23e700abf">Creates a more resilie=
nt structure that resists breakdown during water dissolution</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"cb2c4e32-eb51-43b1-9d0f-5f5dde0ed4fa">
<p local-id=3D"c1992f7d-755c-41da-8e3e-3a2115c01e2c"><strong>Modified PMMA =
Content (60% vs 77%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"0a96ca66-4939-460b-a266-499070f815c4">
<li local-id=3D"08c2f2e4-8178-40da-b181-ac7bd5fa5c42">
<p local-id=3D"1ebc7f9b-67d1-48d4-b279-6e59eb0c36d0">Reduced to accommodate=
 other additives while maintaining 2% overall binder content</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ee5f2279-0240-4bb0-9934-02e8e71fbdbd">
<p local-id=3D"cba37a47-d731-4751-8a15-1e28d25ebd15">Still provides adequat=
e base polymer structure but relies more on crosslinking for strength</p></=
li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"1181f84f-8cda-45bd-96da-c84652d9d555">
<p local-id=3D"72e5fea6-cb69-4d78-be71-53ea83c531f9"><strong>Increased Dibu=
tyl Phthalate (5% vs 3%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"60a720dc-c538-4bde-a267-6ca98fbd88bd">
<li local-id=3D"cae26beb-cccf-429c-80ad-fdaabf614d6b">
<p local-id=3D"aaa0d652-34b0-45b1-b335-2bafde1212e7">Enhanced plasticizer c=
ontent improves initial flexibility</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"95705235-20b8-401f-b2d4-aadba10c01a2">
<p local-id=3D"a0b9d8fd-d4ba-42b3-af7b-b107739fa5e6">Makes the dried cake s=
ofter and more friable for easier grinding</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6d6579db-bd2c-42a0-9986-23f7ee22057c">
<p local-id=3D"a350fb53-8351-42c5-88ce-5d53588010cc">Provides temporary pla=
sticity that is eventually "locked in" during the final high-temperature cu=
ring</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"7c779977-ca84-4c87-96cc-6d2492d3d45d">
<p local-id=3D"56e272be-37c3-4a6e-90ed-4aaae98f5ea8"><strong>Added PEG 4000=
 (1%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c513343f-c925-4cef-ab50-1ce855ca30c8">
<li local-id=3D"376233d4-4ab5-47b3-be7a-5f384c5ede59">
<p local-id=3D"0d8f976c-e4ae-4485-90a2-dc9f405c9cec">Acts as a temporary bi=
nder during the green state</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"942ea15a-c69c-475a-a971-071254c9159e">
<p local-id=3D"b2b999fb-6ede-45e7-b2b2-297cc6e87ee2">Improves particle cohe=
sion before thermal curing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b575bd06-9e70-41c9-98a9-7f4d97fe8c2e">
<p local-id=3D"f035e69d-2c6f-4684-b26b-3fda6626a5a4">Creates hydrogen bondi=
ng interactions that help hold the part together during dissolution</p></li=
>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"6787631c-7d82-4d09-aeee-56a49a8504c6">
<p local-id=3D"64e8251d-5abf-4b9e-8567-9e3a587c6eca"><strong>Added Stearic =
Acid (3%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"eab8d86d-1ff6-4d63-827b-b02830c093a2">
<li local-id=3D"fcd76dfa-88f4-457e-9308-33487ed72e89">
<p local-id=3D"071326bd-804f-42c8-af8d-cba437ca30ba">Functions as an intern=
al lubricant to make the initial cake easier to grind</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"93b16a3d-1c84-451f-85a1-12326602ff9a">
<p local-id=3D"01f60458-e7a7-494e-8289-6d0051e37b42">Improves powder flow p=
roperties during packing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"64418dc1-1c43-41b6-8bb1-b871efa24f64">
<p local-id=3D"0d3ee13b-4984-424f-9e0c-76727ffe5d68">Creates a more homogen=
eous distribution of binder throughout the metal powder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c809078a-b745-4b6f-b3d1-e669332b3390">
<p local-id=3D"95cdeb94-c751-48ec-8629-8747cdc4f3ca">Helps prevent clumping=
 during grinding</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"e90811a6-6fbe-4ac0-bc32-f038aca1412b">
<p local-id=3D"bc2dcfba-d0bc-42c3-919e-b839c1986c31"><strong>Increased AIBN=
 (4% vs 3%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"40da061a-30dd-410e-a40f-468a1a9f27fc">
<li local-id=3D"8293551e-427e-4cdd-941c-81545d6a33eb">
<p local-id=3D"862d8556-8f58-4061-a7a9-3d3fedb47087">Higher initiator conte=
nt ensures more complete crosslinking</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1d9168fd-cdbb-4b16-ad53-f01eb89d6809">
<p local-id=3D"e4591220-cf51-4977-981b-e1ef4595cb83">Provides better initia=
tion throughout the part volume</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c278e742-bb53-4394-91b2-90eb196c78ee">
<p local-id=3D"d0ebbcae-745a-4204-9633-aa7cd74fa368">Compensates for potent=
ial inhibitory effects of additives</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"379ed97c-79ba-419f-934d-be0879dc9d1e" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Two-StageThermalCuringBenefits">Two-Stage Thermal Curing Benefits</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"b5c0eeef-5c6e-4001-a7aa-678387d69c64">
<li local-id=3D"7c5c1af5-bdf9-4c0b-8a26-68fb99f4529e">
<p local-id=3D"020aeaa5-a73c-4eb6-9680-fca90044c82b"><strong>Initial 70=C2=
=B0C Stage</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"8d6554f6-4ffa-4c9c-85a1-cc9b2b2ddf5d">
<li local-id=3D"0f84bbcd-cad6-4139-90ef-dac5b9c48160">
<p local-id=3D"99d0b861-ee82-4ac5-aaa5-6724de8c9477">Activates AIBN gradual=
ly to begin polymerization without sudden gas evolution</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"61e37a2a-5142-450a-82f9-b1bbf92262e8">
<p local-id=3D"de6925a6-74b9-449d-abf7-1cc675575787">Creates initial polyme=
r network structure at a controlled rate</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cbfcbd1f-be2a-48b1-aca4-390dff413263">
<p local-id=3D"9cacab22-2cfc-4647-a37c-4dc902fa2c88">Helps prevent defects =
from rapid curing</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"adaf77d1-11ca-428a-91dc-eb979062a07a">
<p local-id=3D"20524242-7ef7-418d-b667-8b0f396f5a28"><strong>Primary 90=C2=
=B0C Stage</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"1e4fe2be-d51c-40bd-b55a-bd33d43ebfa2">
<li local-id=3D"f897fba0-47f4-4516-b495-101d95af773f">
<p local-id=3D"39b9140f-1146-47af-8776-8a3c01747f60">Accelerates crosslinki=
ng of TEG-DMA</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ad9d17c4-25d8-4be0-a848-8e4c58011931">
<p local-id=3D"d623f6f5-26fb-4ebc-89ad-efab36d51f50">Creates substantial po=
lymer network structure</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ce70090e-91e9-45a0-abc7-2896b8319ba4">
<p local-id=3D"ab507c8e-bbf0-4b4c-991a-620f51779d53">Optimal temperature fo=
r AIBN decomposition and radical generation</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"5482f084-1ffb-4230-be32-64dc2ff22ba8">
<p local-id=3D"1a80e923-ae34-4e31-8e85-72d0df365eac"><strong>Final 110-120=
=C2=B0C Stage</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"68611474-8858-49bb-bbb2-b281862f9a43">
<li local-id=3D"6c9117a4-1eed-4d88-84f1-d3e6aad26950">
<p local-id=3D"31555d7b-56d6-431c-8d6a-1382072fd431">Maximizes crosslinking=
 density</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a4f3c8e5-77a8-47da-b7f0-0d190b6f4b8c">
<p local-id=3D"e9a31e03-c3fd-4c38-955f-1fe4aa769929">Enhances final mechani=
cal properties</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"41025885-ae97-4e91-b165-6c72f17a4edb">
<p local-id=3D"f9a6f796-2081-408e-ad4f-8874121d6857">"Locks in" the plastic=
izer effect of DBP into the polymer structure</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"41a0099a-9448-4139-ba8d-26c2439e3cfe">
<p local-id=3D"35be304f-2899-46ae-b5a1-16aa2dde249b">Creates the most rigid=
, water-resistant structure possible</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"2229a6e1-416d-4021-a0af-760a8eb269ef" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ProcessingConsiderations.1">Processing Considerations</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"a11e8f71-a0ba-4b85-8f34-d3662aaed14f">
<li local-id=3D"e5a8d810-2666-47fd-ad43-f24b0b545a8e">
<p local-id=3D"2413e32a-1934-4b97-99d4-c8580f5ab39e"><strong>Gentler Dissol=
ution Process</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"b2e5f3f1-5f2a-45fc-aad2-d31fb80f3c94">
<li local-id=3D"54b4597a-6a35-47dc-9ecf-af875fabbbdc">
<p local-id=3D"dc16d222-d95f-4ddc-8844-7775d4ee97ae">Lower water temperatur=
e (40=C2=B0C vs 50=C2=B0C) prevents thermal stress</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aa874247-ea60-4eec-83c2-2e569bcee9f7">
<p local-id=3D"a6cc450a-6848-4a8e-b0fe-ffb1acd17813">Added salt reduces wat=
er activity and slows dissolution rate</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8bc3045d-c343-43ea-a7d9-7e8f6c29604b">
<p local-id=3D"f6b7a9f5-ebf9-4f96-988f-becc2a405818">Longer dissolution tim=
e trades speed for part integrity</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"91f7fbd2-462f-42ac-b82d-ae86348e48a6">
<p local-id=3D"59b66b26-61dc-4c45-a29b-b1ea2a8fb222">Avoid agitation that c=
ould stress the green part</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"e349789f-b521-4d76-afb6-15cc50a27d24">
<p local-id=3D"c755115a-cc0a-4775-8e6c-1d27635db60e"><strong>Formulation Ad=
justments for Specific Issues</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"0e293f90-6b9a-4518-b941-94ed92cad8b4">
<li local-id=3D"d60ca9f3-f059-4786-9c8f-5322f90c86aa">
<p local-id=3D"d3fa63a4-49d9-43ef-9f31-9bd961b12c34">If grinding is still d=
ifficult: Increase stearic acid to 4% (reduce PMMA to 59%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"250b3aba-432b-465f-9228-0dbafc57a6f2">
<p local-id=3D"e713b906-4d7b-403d-aa37-0fc632acff40">If green strength is s=
till insufficient: Increase TEG-DMA to 28% (reduce PMMA to 57%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7d1ef0a7-1934-4b63-810b-ecf958decac2">
<p local-id=3D"da57954d-2085-43e7-9287-e04ec0dafc59">For extremely thick pa=
rts: Consider adding 0.2% hydroquinone monomethyl ether to prevent prematur=
e polymerization during mixing/drying</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"05e080ee-0618-4087-96f3-8442b8b78c0e">
<p local-id=3D"5f5fa867-5c9f-41b6-b05c-026c3095327c"><strong>Additional Tip=
s</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a8ec1f8d-c663-4d0c-9b26-0fed1d59b58d">
<li local-id=3D"9d810033-276e-4596-a222-3983f8751895">
<p local-id=3D"1387b3f5-b0ee-4c18-843d-4d2fed8e80e3">Ensure uniform packing=
 density to prevent weak spots</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8506b2dd-76c6-4526-8113-dc2549ec34ed">
<p local-id=3D"644259f9-2878-4358-89da-735559646389">Consider using vacuum =
assistance during packing for complex parts</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1d6ac663-57c0-47fc-8cb2-a5cd82d0f8b8">
<p local-id=3D"54f95cc3-6de8-4a56-816b-32a9ea6c5df1">The water-soluble mold=
 must withstand the higher final curing temperature (120=C2=B0C)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"11958d19-18e7-4f47-8405-827b56aecd42">
<p local-id=3D"1eb926c1-67ac-4c9f-9c06-bba9ff711eb0">This formulation may b=
e less flowable during packing - tapping or vibration can help</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"bf4bb67a-bb7c-4fbd-bfc2-3bbf6c1cb27e"></p>
<p local-id=3D"cf75ed05-3425-4aa6-9e35-b149e8bf5489">HOPPER: I am working o=
n creating a duplicate HOPPER V4.0 for reliability testing outside of the p=
rinter as well as designing a new gated-style hopper that uses a sheet of s=
pring steel as the gating material. Mohsen found the stepper tapper I assem=
bled last week and I tasked Ben with moving around the components in PILOT =
2 to fit the heater in with the HOPPER. Ben has successfully installed the =
heater in PILOT 2 along with the HOPPER, so it should be ready for full pri=
nt testing once we have a formal test protocol developed tomorrow.</p>
<p local-id=3D"588ecaf4-015b-4362-a1a9-4d1b7e02175e">PILOT: Continuing to w=
ork on the new Micro Drop mount. It is almost all complete, I just need to =
drill some holes in the aluminum piece and assemble it. Completed the alumi=
num part and gave to Pourya to test out the assembly when convenient.</p>
<p local-id=3D"47201677-02b3-4564-84d6-10a4d772e7e2"></p>
<p local-id=3D"9694f640-184a-46a4-a8d6-2f6166ec2077">2025-05-13</p>
<p local-id=3D"b52dedee-011a-4787-81c3-381b2fab5281">HOPPER: Mohsen is havi=
ng issues with the hopper on PILOT 2 being too wide to drop down through th=
e PILOT base plate, so he suggested reducing the timing belt pulley width. =
They don=E2=80=99t sell timing belt pulleys of that style on McMaster, but =
one thing I can do it slide the roller motor towards the center of the hopp=
er and print a hubless pulley with flats in its hole that correspond to fla=
ts on the 3D printed roller so it can rotationally couple without needing a=
ny screws.</p>
<p local-id=3D"26ae839c-33a8-4a83-99b0-32c6f73b2ac1">ULTRA: The gated hoppe=
r design as is is not workable because the spring steel is wrapped around t=
he roller several times, and the roll tends to expand outwards and jam agai=
nst the sides of its cavity as it is rotated. After discussing the issue wi=
th Payman, I have a new idea to reduce the gated opening width and replace =
the roller with one that only slightly bends the steel sheet as it rotates =
to retract or extend it. I half completed a design with that approach, and =
I am tossing it and starting over with a new design that is conceptually si=
milar but is based on the HOPPER V3.1.2 that is mounted to the ULTRA printe=
r right now.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eaaa496f-ab8b-46cc-9bd9-3aa2c5480561">REDRESS: The powder ba=
tch from yesterday did come out much more friable but was damp. I ran it in=
 the v mixer for 2 hours with 0.4g of Aerosil R 812 S, removed it, and grou=
nd up ~30g of it manually using a mortar and pestle, and loaded it in a cer=
amic crucible and cooked it at 275F using the fastheat cycle and let it soa=
k for ~1 hour. The powder was completely unbound when it came out. After dr=
ying the batch of powder in the drying oven in the materials lab for ~3 hou=
rs at 113F, however, it seems much drier and sticks to my gloves well where=
 it did not before. It may be worth drying it overnight and going through t=
he formal grinding and sieving process if it seems usable tomorrow morning.=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"c07da51a-990c-4c18-91b1-e11db4a1bf69">I also mixed up a new =
batch of powder using a variant of the last successful recipe:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"b2f80a1a-b70b-4243-a349-666b739bf478" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ModifiedAquaMold=E2=84=A2BinderRecipeforImprovedGreenPartStrength">Modif=
ied AquaMold=E2=84=A2 Binder Recipe for Improved Green Part Strength</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"61aa6d23-92f6-4ce2-945f-38c4a18fbd74" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.8">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"13e0b32b-3d72-48c9-9f1e-9bd2b43c4cc7" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-For1000gFinalMetalPowderMixture(97%Metal,3%Binder).2">For 1000g Final Me=
tal Powder Mixture (97% Metal, 3% Binder)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5319af76-4fad-4ef1-a2bf-fa84f8bde53c"><strong>Metal Powder</=
strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"1c07fdaa-dd4c-451b-b755-e1358d114205">
<li local-id=3D"1b28381f-73d5-4cf3-9ca6-0ebb1f5521b1">
<p local-id=3D"0307fcd6-f54c-41f7-8a29-b8cf4de3f5ab">970g of metal powder (=
17-4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"93ec0c4d-548c-4805-81e1-23c4195e9d11"><strong>Binder Compone=
nts (30g total)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"354499e2-3e7d-4629-9d9d-f1d0f21c26b9">
<li local-id=3D"d6da8d84-5a0f-49a2-82cb-2f4671dab106">
<p local-id=3D"ef3cde4b-18e7-4cc7-af3d-03e9def8d3e8">23.7g Poly(methyl meth=
acrylate-co-ethyl acrylate) (79% of binder) - <em>reduced from 88%</em></p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"9b2f7ada-f015-4379-a81a-213f816757c0">
<p local-id=3D"bcdbdc7b-6351-4ee1-a466-c645f9fb09eb">4.5g Triethylene glyco=
l dimethacrylate (15% of binder) - <em>increased from 10%</em></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"79ec8710-4dc7-4fad-8ad6-08b85c6f682b">
<p local-id=3D"1d008645-b0de-427f-b83d-8d2b321a0770">0.9g 2,2=E2=80=B2-Azob=
is(2-methylpropionitrile) (AIBN) (3% of binder) - <em>increased from 2%</em=
></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fa69e381-7759-4555-a5f9-3d64caf2c929">
<p local-id=3D"ae9c9fc0-3963-407e-8a39-caa5e746d4b7">0.9g Dibutyl phthalate=
 (DBP) (3% of binder) - <em>added as plasticizer</em></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"aae8a9b1-d9b2-4220-8530-01cae89f27ce"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"09ec6bae-fb4d-4e44-a73e-0628072d416b">
<li local-id=3D"cac5ebd9-3f67-48fd-bdae-a8237033d9b4">
<p local-id=3D"2da289dc-2bf8-4716-b059-9915efa54924">270-300g Acetone (9-10=
:1 ratio with binder solids)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"cefe6932-53cb-4545-8e6e-2b39639b84fe" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Equipment.3">Equipment</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"951a1d74-fce1-4472-8fd1-30ef559e67bb">
<li local-id=3D"aee40d89-c842-4bbe-8627-f7ec04342347">
<p local-id=3D"f821bb31-d2c8-4010-81f0-60d425eedc61">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5740bdf3-11e9-4c30-8f44-5dd4928f9b0f">
<p local-id=3D"9b9b83a9-dcc0-4051-8c3a-0451c49a413b">Glass containers with =
tight-fitting lids</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ab01bc27-d10f-42f2-89b9-fb1d0b6bdd5c">
<p local-id=3D"b303e389-a5b1-49a4-8fd8-8fb00e86c13d">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9ead462b-3281-4b8d-818f-04dd8c775044">
<p local-id=3D"06bcab0d-0c05-4af1-90c6-e0bccea03580">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"487c04c3-a2bd-4fb2-b8d0-00e182baf860">
<p local-id=3D"0da7e122-45e6-496e-9490-f0a6cc6c2858">Controlled temperature=
 oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"562c4cd3-c8f9-460b-ae41-1eb37d935c90">
<p local-id=3D"871eacf3-2b67-4234-be88-3d7b42e993bc">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"87997ef4-e382-4614-b1b4-ff3d383d4fb3">
<p local-id=3D"86a57dc1-449d-4a45-906b-ffb1f9d07e9b">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"de29cf5f-e0a2-4982-a4d4-eb8e3d2a8f4a">
<p local-id=3D"534d2948-4a86-475a-8e00-530a27b4c4a8">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0c5222c6-5de9-4bad-8f23-71fadb1dc808">
<p local-id=3D"f03c6ce7-c7a1-4dc9-ae4b-e5a3c60f5025">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"e8a7994b-8abe-4ae7-ac40-8d48d62c1731" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.8">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"e0b02f9e-e640-4da1-854b-290997e4d528" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.BinderPreparation.5">A. Binder Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7a3cc4d9-8265-495e-a1a6-73387b2429ea">
<li local-id=3D"ceffb24c-1233-4c60-b0b3-15f7872b2fca">
<p local-id=3D"d97d611f-cf4a-427e-a2b7-6728402a2cc6">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 270g of acetone into a glass container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"822f3c1e-756d-4837-babd-970ec2a24f1c">
<p local-id=3D"19947bbb-65b9-4433-99a5-985e27c71907">While stirring, slowly=
 add 23.7g of PMMA-co-EA to the acetone. Stir until completely dissolved (a=
pproximately 30-60 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b9d039fc-8fff-4572-a41a-53d620a2c686">
<p local-id=3D"192315ab-cfe9-41a6-bdc4-df1659ac82e7">Add 0.9g of dibutyl ph=
thalate and stir thoroughly for 5 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7c1a593a-6d7b-4525-af31-c8ff8308eecd">
<p local-id=3D"dc106304-cd96-49cd-8748-2c5e77983c46">Add 4.5g of TEG-DMA an=
d stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ec2d4b27-9191-4547-a3eb-e388bf133e8c">
<p local-id=3D"d48e2125-86a3-41b2-adef-b4cf70d359b8">Finally, add 0.9g of A=
IBN and stir gently until completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"70c50691-5959-4ab6-90e0-4bc8206a46be">
<p local-id=3D"7b916d2d-5efc-4beb-8bc3-304dcbbad5ad">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation. The binder solution =
is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"d2f2d855-ee7c-476f-8099-a1a073f45959" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.SlurryPreparation.5">B. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"023abce8-b161-407b-85d1-5fd38ebb48da">
<li local-id=3D"957a1c04-366c-4388-be78-72e4cc0aed3f">
<p local-id=3D"d8974231-cbf0-42e6-a830-fdbb74f20fa4">Place 970g of metal po=
wder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5d8b2fcb-6bc6-4780-9a73-0901e1846d73">
<p local-id=3D"a1a9ec8d-90de-4a55-9336-a51c858c68b5">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the metal powder.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"9e01798e-0f35-4879-a058-3e53380759b1">
<p local-id=3D"b3a81d76-9114-49b6-91bd-c11efc5b0b3b">Continue mixing for 45=
 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0fc0bb2a-5d24-4d03-8ac8-1acdd52120a1">
<p local-id=3D"073c7716-001a-42d1-95af-236e251aa09a">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 30g) to achieve p=
roper consistency.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"57c9e413-85d0-4d0d-8868-3a134d2fa89e">
<p local-id=3D"e18cc545-545c-4b7f-b0a7-f7a649ce42c3">Keep the temperature b=
elow 30=C2=B0C during mixing to prevent premature activation of the AIBN.</=
p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"bc1a56bf-de5e-41d3-964d-037257dc2b6f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.Drying.5">C. Drying</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"d32d8f47-47e0-4198-b747-52cd6fbb4df7">
<li local-id=3D"f2006f04-60f2-43b3-8530-8e6ba4c133d1">
<p local-id=3D"a3101f39-7249-4dca-8f30-dfe16b6cbcf6">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"71dbbdf6-0a6f-497a-98e1-13d307873a04">
<p local-id=3D"f8dadb17-2cb9-4324-9fc4-a9ada2e9e376">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature in a well-ventilated area for 16-24 hours.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"2f13a5a8-e66b-440b-bc97-ba74c41db69a">
<p local-id=3D"74bb9f0e-df3d-49e1-820e-e9a26448a365">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 45=C2=B0C for 6 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"93996a1b-a140-4eb0-81c7-38fe8a749d79">
<p local-id=3D"a947d911-42ad-4aa1-b081-2c4ecacc0c28">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 60=C2=B0C for 2-3 hours to ensure complete solvent removal.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e49d7512-f795-44ef-8da6-6c2120c3a8a1">
<p local-id=3D"3c7d9100-b0f3-4398-8f8c-55d31272cf77">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid cake with moderate hardness.<=
/p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"ede07b83-5d41-45a4-8334-25739c6a0da9" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.GrindingandSieving.5">D. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"ee91eaab-0031-498e-a4c4-e9c4fc2d50bd">
<li local-id=3D"decb09fa-2a9a-4ac8-ad44-c790e39e22bc">
<p local-id=3D"fbfedb48-ba75-4e91-82ea-d0202c20c1dc">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1db7911a-1946-488c-b339-e91422d02772">
<p local-id=3D"c4b2043a-272f-4892-be17-b05497ae8ec7">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill under controlled temperature conditions (below 40=C2=B0C=
).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2182ad39-4d08-4038-981f-7e44457be922">
<p local-id=3D"1919f0dd-231b-49e2-b932-ad6bce578e7a">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f8c0231a-eec9-472f-890c-9ba964c617b7">
<p local-id=3D"1d039b3f-88fb-4708-8209-a0789d2010dd">If needed, add 0.1g of=
 Aerosil R 812 S (0.01% of total weight) to improve flowability.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"271952b2-3f04-458e-92f0-80ab45016917">
<p local-id=3D"7eb2489c-cfa4-4c1f-85ea-761396dda8ad">Store the powder in ai=
rtight containers until ready for use.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"09f233cb-c29a-4202-ad7d-f2de7a1e115d" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.EnhancedThermalCuringProcess">E. Enhanced Thermal Curing Process</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"e2a32e45-70ed-4b2c-90ff-bf9adf81c282">
<li local-id=3D"2843c5a1-5aef-4ee7-bd9e-9fb07b505807">
<p local-id=3D"46cc9d97-064f-4262-9b94-7f7cd43cc2b2">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"67edaf86-790e-4bdf-98e5-ae28b7fdffc2">
<p local-id=3D"0fa628bc-a687-4aae-93d2-3cf0ba827753">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"73d2b99f-b695-4afd-abcf-f7e04a696a22">
<p local-id=3D"9091b3db-61e8-4f80-9a0a-863636c7018f"><strong>Two-Stage Ther=
mal Curing</strong> (simplified from previous version):</p>
<ul local-id=3D"1b47068c-eda5-408f-9b2f-198ada68a269">
<li local-id=3D"dc6d7b8b-267c-461d-a455-fab3315c2bd7">
<p local-id=3D"9d51378c-ddf8-4463-9310-34d1db4bc764"><strong>Primary Curing=
</strong>: Heat to 80=C2=B0C and maintain for 90 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0db7ea37-e19a-417a-b39b-43248e013837">
<p local-id=3D"17244ac4-b3c1-4d8d-a8ea-c0edf86d4e78"><strong>Final Curing</=
strong>: Increase temperature to 95=C2=B0C for 30 minutes</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"724c224e-4400-4a5a-be67-1d75a33b88a9">
<p local-id=3D"31dbd141-2602-4d3a-8fbb-7772f3668ebf">Allow the part to cool=
 gradually to room temperature (cooling at 2-3=C2=B0C per minute).</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"fc5f28f5-b8a5-4896-914d-1b71e335f3a5" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.DissolutionandGreenPartRecovery.4">F. Dissolution and Green Part Recov=
ery</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"3ef782ef-4292-4448-b01b-10a82afb4627">
<li local-id=3D"10942028-f3a3-4ce2-8a86-daa1ff92bb89">
<p local-id=3D"7e75eaf4-aa69-4916-a509-a23ea99329e7">Allow the thermally cu=
red part to rest for at least 2 hours after cooling.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0ed94164-22cc-430f-a2f4-3fc315fd037e">
<p local-id=3D"e83fe39e-7e50-41af-b142-b6e05de7c28f">Prepare a warm water b=
ath at 45=C2=B0C.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c5f54dfe-44fd-4ac7-b457-ba904ee6ca78">
<p local-id=3D"7d21751f-9ef7-44e4-b857-b2a7e732b346">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in the warm water bath to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0f410992-5df2-404d-b099-5d8d3899df0a">
<p local-id=3D"5ab18068-3ddc-4f3d-9274-8b747130b1f5">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh water as needed until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"12ff7751-df5b-4d07-bc90-4a37ff9a6ca1">
<p local-id=3D"913c96fe-18b4-4477-95f7-152f1d0973f2">Carefully extract the =
green part and allow to dry at room temperature for 12 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ff0dc773-1a88-4330-ad92-dda404af08c4">
<p local-id=3D"920417b2-46a5-4321-97c7-ea0253f4306a">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to your standard protocol.</p><=
/li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"bc039bf6-50ad-4898-bb03-1857b5600282" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-TechnicalNotes.2">Technical Notes</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"b934fa34-78e8-4da7-9cc1-44a69944c342" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-KeyModificationsfromOriginalSuccessfulRecipe">Key Modifications from Ori=
ginal Successful Recipe</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"bfb12804-af2b-4238-ad87-5e4d127afaf1">
<li local-id=3D"3eb4ddee-a675-4018-b4c4-7850d4201009">
<p local-id=3D"6533bca7-5db0-4e30-9ed5-d3940d89967e"><strong>Retained PMMA-=
co-EA as Base Polymer</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"8d280788-6844-4280-a560-d1340a8547dc">
<li local-id=3D"c0059560-eb72-43e6-807a-bb500073b9df">
<p local-id=3D"de886723-b8b5-44f5-b015-395b300328c2">Provides better adhesi=
on and flexibility than pure PMMA</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"caffa17a-392d-4ec9-8673-c0ade206ee96">
<p local-id=3D"e6bfad0b-ec2e-4a92-97e7-0ea6496ec5e4">Lower glass transition=
 temperature makes for better green part handling properties</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"551eb611-697a-472f-8ab3-375db8a5672d">
<p local-id=3D"b2c69a4d-fead-4034-b880-1c443890313e"><strong>Moderately Inc=
reased TEG-DMA (15% vs 10%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"38981340-d4a9-4c20-9299-cde44b37d74a">
<li local-id=3D"2be37d29-287f-48ff-8a6a-d81cfbfacb0e">
<p local-id=3D"0ef3b5ee-33e3-41b4-845c-29fef7eae480">Creates stronger cross=
linked network for improved green strength</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"eb22eaf9-3bb6-40ab-ac77-999747de4a09">
<p local-id=3D"bd70b387-d564-4dc7-8459-d66d010652c5">Still maintains compat=
ibility with base PMMA-co-EA system</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"a6ceec0c-29d3-4b1e-90de-9db2252ada41">
<p local-id=3D"09a89e2c-3c56-4a05-b4c3-5eab378cc7ba"><strong>Slightly Incre=
ased AIBN (3% vs 2%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f788c532-92c8-4507-9c95-5436568aab18">
<li local-id=3D"27ee452d-0a68-429f-bacb-e1849dedd26c">
<p local-id=3D"4a2d96ee-7dcd-44bf-bc9e-339a58d06765">Ensures complete cross=
linking throughout the part</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"78733219-1e94-4598-bf8e-1e6e3b34bdac">
<p local-id=3D"5eda9fde-1e60-4cc2-ac3c-0dc12868528f">Helps compensate for a=
ny inhibitory effects of additives</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"d2ef46c0-fcca-4c8e-b18b-5599183fab56">
<p local-id=3D"8377652b-5266-41c9-a354-a15c8a57d7d9"><strong>Added Minimal =
Plasticizer (3% DBP)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"daf8828f-4a69-4e74-a830-d7a3e327e6b5">
<li local-id=3D"5d8f53f0-d142-4aad-8073-da8def288b6f">
<p local-id=3D"72243f61-ba2d-4a8d-8d2f-2c54088fbd34">Makes the dried cake e=
asier to process</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7375a4e2-76f6-47d2-9bf4-59a4882c0870">
<p local-id=3D"5b6eabba-6fda-4f73-9f42-bfdec374d45e">Improves flexibility o=
f the green part</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b1c82e56-a1f7-4724-bc66-6e65393e14e1">
<p local-id=3D"4977e45e-5555-4a89-a846-3a500d47676c">Amount carefully limit=
ed to prevent excessive softening</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"09d2f2ec-6f5c-4060-8579-be1401fc535b">
<p local-id=3D"4b4eb179-c11b-43de-8b44-557b0d9fc505"><strong>Added Small Am=
ount of Stearic Acid (1%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"30472313-b868-4e85-9fa7-765cf1c69ee3">
<li local-id=3D"8d97cc0e-c281-49d3-bf8a-e741de8dcd03">
<p local-id=3D"2b94241f-a33b-4667-962e-d65346db7534">Acts as lubricant to i=
mprove powder flow and packing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4828fa11-2cd3-4b1b-97e6-b15712976f27">
<p local-id=3D"17ad944e-bb1f-4a54-a893-cc2bbdcb5119">Helps with mold fillin=
g</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d580dbc8-b25a-44b4-8819-3bcb5098d9a9">
<p local-id=3D"c993ceb1-a6ae-4a57-b3e0-9ad5b82719db">Minimal amount to avoi=
d interference with crosslinking</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"f6f567f8-adf4-4763-932b-7b56e03cb744" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ImportantProcessingConsiderations">Important Processing Considerations</=
h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"4d1966c6-7a12-4a83-a6b2-6d721cfaf1e5">
<li local-id=3D"c3efcb2c-c096-452c-bf8d-976b06002d6e">
<p local-id=3D"30deec3e-f078-47c7-8754-ba85109b8134"><strong>Thorough Dryin=
g</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"956ada83-17cb-489a-a58d-8515c136ddeb">
<li local-id=3D"8bf17234-adc8-445c-a10f-e54c2288998e">
<p local-id=3D"8e6648a8-f8b5-4003-87f1-5ada7172a19c">Complete solvent remov=
al is critical</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7b0abac4-78d5-4d47-85a7-903d8f5f3137">
<p local-id=3D"d82caebf-c307-4b47-be23-684282995556">Final 60=C2=B0C drying=
 step ensures residual acetone is removed</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"6584a8ec-9a06-415e-8338-07e0b24a1151">
<p local-id=3D"07d6122a-b4b1-4b7a-9429-ca20cc0cebfc"><strong>Two-Stage Curi=
ng</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"083d0325-c3df-4b2d-8172-03b5594c51d4">
<li local-id=3D"0254347d-8229-4d82-b4c6-2b44081b357e">
<p local-id=3D"ed29767f-ed31-4036-b194-853f7c7bdef5">Based on proven parame=
ters but with additional high-temperature phase</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2858b280-e6b2-498d-97ef-6147bcc63bd5">
<p local-id=3D"e81f100c-96e9-4d89-9b5f-17e70dfc089c">80=C2=B0C primary cure=
 matches your successful formulation</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f0560bd6-ef10-4742-9969-f042606929c2">
<p local-id=3D"005f642f-88e4-4e8e-bbaa-4e647a0ed52c">Brief 95=C2=B0C phase =
maximizes crosslinking without excessive complexity</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"16f296d6-0c95-461a-bc9e-17df27161130">
<p local-id=3D"c098e2ec-1723-4f8d-b32f-26396ae46a1b"><strong>Flowability Co=
nsiderations</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3a542368-23ae-4eaf-800c-c2e33ba067a2">
<li local-id=3D"0fa09add-97bc-428d-aa70-8f3b3f5e4278">
<p local-id=3D"e12ffdf3-014a-4186-9291-b263742b6f2d">Without stearic acid, =
flowability may be slightly reduced</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9fdd6da7-62a1-4e73-a531-411bc1005053">
<p local-id=3D"6f2adde5-15ee-48e3-9d31-6f96a34b8c9f">If needed, add 0.1-0.2=
g of Aerosil R 812 S (fumed silica) to improve flow</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3b3272a5-0b52-4c1d-a01f-44fbd81ba731">
<p local-id=3D"34c90f64-ce9f-4f2f-9bff-f103718ee4ce">Gentle vibration durin=
g mold filling can help achieve uniform packing</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"da34632b-6127-4332-9637-ff3769bf0b73">
<p local-id=3D"13a436bd-2059-4196-9e54-2761f6b2275a"><strong>Quality Contro=
l Checks</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7155ce87-1588-428a-ae2d-618e08924a11">
<li local-id=3D"65587b11-d863-418b-b2a8-53f179b32134">
<p local-id=3D"698d7dbd-219b-4ac2-81b4-c254191fec8a">Test AIBN reactivity i=
f using from previous batches</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"83008c53-dd84-4d13-bdf0-45b4319cf549">
<p local-id=3D"f7765937-b515-446b-922a-60cc1320a1d2">Ensure PMMA-co-EA is f=
resh and properly stored</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"88a14b35-e617-42b6-b01e-e8ce70961fce">
<p local-id=3D"253e4686-cd80-45b9-b99f-16a68978ac1f">Verify oven temperatur=
es with independent thermometer</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"d0526392-bdda-4405-a03c-0b429dc2ae5b">
<p local-id=3D"185002fc-41eb-4c2f-bc2c-9ae9f3382ab7"><strong>Troubleshootin=
g Options</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"9734361f-377c-4ba9-b2f5-ea9223059f28">
<li local-id=3D"4e44334b-007e-4ddc-b73b-2350f8ee207f">
<p local-id=3D"f59e15c4-0e9f-4e29-9e5f-3203149474a7">If dried cake is still=
 too hard: Increase DBP to 4% (reduce PMMA-co-EA to 78%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1e261080-e707-42fa-97f9-67b80b2ebbeb">
<p local-id=3D"5b9d8cbe-9765-443d-8442-16cc9067519b">If cake is too soft: R=
educe DBP to 2% (increase PMMA-co-EA to 80%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ece2e133-719d-49bc-9e20-c9065089f66a">
<p local-id=3D"81d03e90-f4e1-49d2-b216-d0b59ae8ebf5">If green strength is i=
nsufficient: Increase TEG-DMA to 18% (reduce PMMA-co-EA to 76%)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"7c7d25e0-54bd-4926-a5d0-d07c3558e65b"></p>
<p local-id=3D"13ca16bc-43d4-4562-b5e2-a28de11a8357">2025-05-14</p>
<p local-id=3D"aef5faf0-4d23-4831-b8ce-bb38dd811cfe">Bagel Wednesday: The b=
oard meeting last week went well - per Scott we are on track for getting th=
e next tranche of funding, but the Fall funding raising round will be focus=
ed on getting a larger tranche to increase our runway to the point that we =
can plan more long-term. They are also working on replanning our product ro=
admap with a possible focus on no depowdering technologies, a faster spread=
 and spray in one pass, and using the laser ablation process to produce sma=
ller features and speed up layer cutting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7c35bab5-a0ca-4350-b4de-35eb17fb307e">HOPPER: Continuing to =
assemble the desktop copy of HOPPER V4.0. Had to switch out the filament on=
 the Bambu printer while running the print for the newest gated HOPPER desi=
gn. I had to use a different color and brand of filament so the print will =
be two-tone, but an order was placed several days ago for two new rolls of =
Bambu PETG filament that I plan to use for similar prints in the future. I =
am also continuing to work on the design of the gated HOPPER.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9db5cbd1-1d87-4ecc-b408-116b22a7290a">REDRESS: I dried the 3=
% binder load cake last night in the welding area at room temperature; when=
 I broke it apart by hand this morning it was still wet and flexible so I f=
lipped the material upside down to dry and placed it in the oven in the mat=
erials lab. After drying the 2% binder load powder batch with stearic acid =
and PEG 8K added, I ground and sieved it and used it to fill a mold. After =
drying it was quite flowable, so I am very curious to see how the green par=
t comes out after the curing process tonight. I am going to dry the 3% bind=
er load batch without stearic acid or PEG overnight, then grind, sieve, and=
 test it tomorrow.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6acf08a0-b360-4fd2-8da0-5b3a7c5440c7">PILOT: Track down lapt=
op mount used on PILOTs 2 and 3 and order another one for PILOT 1. There ar=
e some 3D printed parts associated with the mounts that also need to be pri=
nted. I placed an Amazon order request for an equivalent laptop/keyboard bo=
ard, and I have started printing 3X mounts that hold it to the control cabi=
net.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bb4f2d73-b690-4e88-9e00-262b28c46fdf"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1c99286c-9199-4a1c-8e75-11362df49c2c">2025-05-15</p>
<p local-id=3D"304aa77b-3120-4254-8f13-2439d340f1ff">HOPPER: Continuing ass=
embly of benchtop V4.0 copy. Because the stepper tapper does not seem to be=
 working well (uneven dispense along line of dispense) I am working to reve=
rt to the former design of a steel shaft down the center of the roller. I h=
ave decided to use an 8mm keyed shaft; d-profile shafts on McMaster are onl=
y available in 10mm, and that would require some design tweaks and reprinti=
ng of the HOPPER components, while switching to an 8mm keyed shaft will onl=
y require new rollers and pulleys.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4dd0016b-1251-4571-b249-ed97d2b73677">Making some design mod=
ifications to Payman=E2=80=99s gated hopper design.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5f061741-c199-406c-b5c4-7804479a19d9">REDRESS: The powder in=
 the mold filled with the 2% binder load with stearic acid and PEG powder w=
as completely unbound upon removal from the Keith furnace this morning. Aft=
er drying overnight, the 3% binder load batch chunks were quite hard, and a=
fter grinding and sieving the powder was flowable enough that I did not nee=
d to add any Aerosil. I filled a water-soluble mold and a ceramic crucible =
with the powder and put it in the upper Keith oven to thermally cure. I am =
also mixing up a new batch that I intend to completely dry with no heat, ba=
sed on the theory that when any heat is applied during solvent removal it l=
eads to some crosslinking.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9ac40706-b954-42d4-9763-41cdd6749dda">High-level meeting tri=
ggered by asking for a meeting to discuss ideas that came out of the board =
meeting. Slide deck from board meeting. Last board meeting: strong differen=
tiation from other metal AM for small parts, but narrow commerical window. =
50/50 focus on commercial execution and tech. Tech focus on commercial appl=
icability: reduce DFAM costs and turnaround time. Strategic shift: tech nic=
he and competing against conv. methods, growth constrained w/out tech impro=
vements, new project structure working, new tech demo'd. Strategic shift pi=
tched to 75/25 tech/commercial to accelerate productization. Projects statu=
s: HOPPER goal to reduce overflow, reduce density variation, enable thinner=
 layers and powder flexibility, Copper project to transfer copper from R&am=
p;D to production, Inconel goal to implement IN625 printing at 3DEO and IHI=
 site. Aid IHI in implementing 3DEO-based mini factory at IHI site. IHI cur=
rently deferring DFAM and mini-factory projects. Still planning on working =
with ORNL consultant to develop binders even though our current binder seem=
s to work OK with IN625. Hot fire test deferred. PXL project: developing pr=
ocesses independently of AEM, including electron beam welding, vacuum impre=
gnation, and in-house brazing of larger area vertical braze joints. No depo=
wdering: eliminate the need for depowdering, enable previously impossible g=
eometries, and simplify DFAM by filling cuts with a material that can be re=
moved during the debind and sinter process. Did random testing initially th=
en selected Micro Drop system for deposition of paraffin. Discussed using a=
 laser to define part geometries. Sold mainly as a way to accelerate proces=
s due to eliminating need for curing and accelerating the cutting process. =
Also mentioned the speed increase from the new mechanism to spread and spra=
y in one pass. Also highlighted ability to make very small features using a=
 laser. Pitched a product we could sell with some estimated specs and compa=
risons with competing technologies.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3d1f34bb-902f-4cf0-a6c3-36ce6c5d0bba"></p>
<p local-id=3D"f4249570-5325-47b0-919d-5550bbdfc0d3">2026-05-16</p>
<p local-id=3D"2cc8c8fb-2ad3-4ab4-9a59-8180dfbbf8c0">HOPPER: Completed asse=
mbling the benchtop V4.0 HOPPER; it needs to be changed to use a keyed stee=
l shaft so that project is ongoing. Focused on the gated HOPPER design; fin=
ished assembling HOPPER V3.3.4 and delivered to Payman. After initial testi=
ng he suggested that the 3D printed guide strip on the bottom be replaced w=
ith a steel strip so I have been working on updating the design to a V3.3.5=
 that includes that modification as well as moving the spreader bar closer =
to the dispensing gate to reduce the powder wastage for each spread.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5b92e965-31fc-48f8-9d71-7affb4b0c2be">REDRESS: I pulled out =
a block of powder in a ceramic crucible from the oven yesterday right when =
the oven turned off, and it seemed fairly strong and was unaffected by wate=
r, however the green part in the 3D printed mold fell apart when I dissolve=
d the mold.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d32ba9be-65ad-4e9f-aa0a-996666c978f6">I pulled out a block o=
f powder in a ceramic crucible from the oven yesterday right when the oven =
turned off, and it seemed fairly strong and was unaffected by water, howeve=
r the green part in the 3D printed mold that was left in the oven while the=
 oven cooled down slowly fell apart when I dissolved the mold.</p>
