 (DBP) (3% of binder)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"70e1925e-b931-4522-bc2f-bce346b497b2"><strong>Optional Stabi=
lizer</strong> (recommended based on latest observations)</p>
<ul local-id=3D"cfa98f55-c09f-4fde-bc48-4d089aca5de2">
<li local-id=3D"bd86c6d4-56fb-42ef-b8da-dce38f092230">
<p local-id=3D"eb9a40ca-e837-4e76-84e6-1d6cdcc61a70">0.03g Hydroquinone mon=
omethyl ether (MEHQ) (0.1% of binder)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"ad8908a1-8cc2-4f3a-b12d-755e10435b26"><strong>Solvent</stron=
g></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7bd4aa0b-d243-453e-9734-d330e85553c9">
<li local-id=3D"66824733-16be-4a22-890d-c8a1097d2bac">
<p local-id=3D"89282a98-cf1b-4599-a80c-6c85e1b3a876">270-300g Acetone (9-10=
:1 ratio with binder solids)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"f2632e78-f99f-45a1-aa82-ee62e13a95dc" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Equipment.4">Equipment</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"e7f42581-8ffe-4469-911f-18b113810f87">
<li local-id=3D"c3c35685-124d-4acc-899b-361d0e3a281c">
<p local-id=3D"565f0ab9-2c22-4306-9e24-17761aa41f2b">Chemical balance (0.01=
g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"471c6734-4456-4fc4-8c9e-8568ee1a192e">
<p local-id=3D"c83bdb06-9b14-4fc8-aa5c-16ecda6e4061">Glass containers with =
tight-fitting lids</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ba9a3c7b-3335-4810-a037-e271fc1ad39a">
<p local-id=3D"ab31b43c-80e5-4553-bc1e-f1530d483623">Mechanical mixer or hi=
gh-shear mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f1aab6bd-3fa0-4c1f-acaf-39d80890f800">
<p local-id=3D"0a0b091c-f846-4abd-9162-c0cfc7417ca2">Drying trays</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"430eb420-2aa9-4a18-8653-656275c9e55a">
<p local-id=3D"670ec9f0-574e-4526-8b4c-83a11408c97b">Controlled temperature=
 oven</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ee898fae-ae43-422c-b6ac-376531c37a4f">
<p local-id=3D"d00cda28-1e4f-444e-941e-fcf64b784286">Grinding equipment (ba=
ll mill or attritor mill)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8fa34c73-c4f5-416f-a564-2d9a216d77ab">
<p local-id=3D"2f85fa77-22c8-42c2-8bd7-2fbf608d685d">Sieves (appropriate me=
sh size for your application)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"83841939-77ee-4e8c-b953-a3dc3f3cb272">
<p local-id=3D"b4d4a163-e340-4aa4-8017-e18264adf218">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"df53a185-9a4b-4579-b585-bab6682537e4">
<p local-id=3D"c0873b77-a7b6-4d8f-b96a-178925efd88b">Safety equipment (glov=
es, goggles, ventilation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"eda06840-78dd-44c4-802f-baee4924b1d6" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Procedure.9">Procedure</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"048af3ee-8f8f-46b8-8aac-b28633df1304" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.BinderPreparation.6">A. Binder Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"76d93ccb-7e19-4b01-925e-7195c723d5a6">
<li local-id=3D"4b6ca6aa-38d7-41c1-97f2-2dcd4b225eed">
<p local-id=3D"b8432cdb-d8ae-4cf7-9374-ba40cb9c37fd">In a well-ventilated a=
rea, weigh 270g of acetone into a glass container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ccdd4b91-99ba-4178-b932-a0222fed268d">
<p local-id=3D"3d93e478-e2e6-4a44-9dc9-ec7e295808f5"><strong>(Optional but =
recommended)</strong>: Add 0.03g of hydroquinone monomethyl ether (MEHQ) an=
d stir until dissolved.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0b81cfa5-ca34-4f43-a94f-847e74e2640b">
<p local-id=3D"c52bda09-ec3a-4a0a-8b20-b31afb3293a6">While stirring, slowly=
 add 23.1g of PMMA-co-EA to the acetone. Stir until completely dissolved (a=
pproximately 30-60 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a3529f30-1fd6-44f9-b116-80b8b008668d">
<p local-id=3D"181a5183-7b3e-43b0-ae8c-5423cc733450">Add 0.9g of dibutyl ph=
thalate and stir thoroughly for 5 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bb86d8f0-d57f-4f6f-90f4-85ec43fb1b61">
<p local-id=3D"80bb8be5-07fa-4bd8-b3c9-ab3b9555d7e2">Add 4.8g of TEG-DMA an=
d stir thoroughly for 10 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"acca166f-3262-4959-96b0-3b92c3ff69f3">
<p local-id=3D"a2bb7aa9-6c60-4b94-b797-2877b71ef651">Finally, add 1.2g of A=
IBN and stir gently until completely dissolved (approximately 10 minutes).<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3930e4d1-eb02-454f-9f57-dc86478791fe">
<p local-id=3D"cb0c13d0-e398-40f7-a09c-4780cd0b11ab">Cover the container wi=
th a tight-fitting lid to prevent acetone evaporation. The binder solution =
is now ready.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"760be1ed-64d9-45eb-b69c-5f81d2dce823" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.SlurryPreparation.6">B. Slurry Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"4bb46e26-e62e-4995-82cd-44f2a5d5ec4f">
<li local-id=3D"0b1f629b-dc80-4b2b-b0c2-6c0d8901f7c3">
<p local-id=3D"f97e4116-53c0-475e-87a1-81a509e327ca">Place 970g of metal po=
wder in a mixing vessel.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9ae20160-e10d-40d5-a484-ac7468bc4fb2">
<p local-id=3D"6d93d274-1669-4b5c-84ae-f36b0815b1e0">While mixing at modera=
te speed, slowly add the prepared binder solution to the metal powder.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"9eddcf4a-ad3d-4522-a2d3-098f5120e477">
<p local-id=3D"5a5f6934-d04e-46bb-87fd-c05aa4570abc">Continue mixing for 45=
 minutes to ensure homogeneous distribution of the binder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f856238b-4aeb-41af-81bf-4a464ea26e95">
<p local-id=3D"078b4d91-fa2b-46ba-a18c-f2fbcf774bfe">If the slurry appears =
too thick, add small amounts of additional acetone (up to 30g) to achieve p=
roper consistency.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"be1df77f-a2c0-421d-a616-306f9e300c8e">
<p local-id=3D"495879a9-6a06-421e-81e5-3f8e2085156c">Keep the temperature b=
elow 30=C2=B0C during mixing to prevent premature activation of the AIBN.</=
p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"e0767e63-a3ba-4c1e-a1e7-238fa47e3ce1" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.Drying.6">C. Drying</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7306e60a-363b-4ae8-a32a-c0c4f256f36b">
<li local-id=3D"0b122be7-dc6f-4972-9697-7ca174a6f709">
<p local-id=3D"d4303e47-1e9a-45ac-8f70-fc077e797393">Spread the slurry even=
ly in drying trays to a thickness of no more than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e0c42f0f-343d-4cac-9123-f2844c515fcf">
<p local-id=3D"a498a309-5d8e-4955-af0f-f3127a18036a">Initial drying: Allow =
to dry at room temperature in a well-ventilated area for 16-24 hours.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"b1315866-515b-49a6-b8ab-d71b5386127d">
<p local-id=3D"4572666d-0451-4ff9-8e5f-d67681b570f1">Secondary drying: Plac=
e in an oven at 45=C2=B0C for 6 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1b3728bd-97d8-4d3c-b0f3-b9d6ce7dd70b">
<p local-id=3D"e3157282-1adc-49d4-9e53-c86d5c7170bc">Final drying: Increase=
 temperature to 60=C2=B0C for 2-3 hours to ensure complete solvent removal.=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e7c40ec4-dbb9-479b-b1c8-352cb326a405">
<p local-id=3D"d484d01e-a58c-412e-86ff-e822b7b3dc60">Allow to cool to room =
temperature. The material should form a solid cake with moderate hardness.<=
/p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"6c0d500b-645b-45d6-baf0-63755c252ec1" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.GrindingandSieving.6">D. Grinding and Sieving</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"aec7f67a-52f1-4f02-9026-d7875afdfd79">
<li local-id=3D"6ad8a047-257e-4dd9-9e08-12dbabaad584">
<p local-id=3D"b0597427-dc49-4e56-8be9-fcbc33d84f56">Break the dried cake i=
nto smaller pieces.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b5a2f45e-86d0-499b-863a-982d0ecc68e0">
<p local-id=3D"1c4690c0-02b3-4a6c-a0da-837ff397189a">Grind using a ball mil=
l or attritor mill under controlled temperature conditions (below 40=C2=B0C=
).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3029996f-49e9-4cb3-982c-7a8d488d4935">
<p local-id=3D"adadfd47-fbfc-48b3-9cab-6fa352a04167">Sieve the ground powde=
r to obtain the desired particle size distribution (typically 45-150=CE=BCm=
).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f974bf1a-eccc-4dd7-81f1-edc3fe72ec77">
<p local-id=3D"ef4daa30-b89d-4786-951b-adb9cc147a5f">If needed, add 0.1g of=
 Aerosil R 812 S (0.01% of total weight) to improve flowability.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a3d2e7cb-82c5-4776-a334-5506998ee5c2">
<p local-id=3D"789981d2-6696-4c49-a458-3181beca0b64">Store the powder in ai=
rtight containers until ready for use.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"cc616785-a71f-4f1e-9861-f927db782cb0" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.EnhancedThermalCuringProcess.1">E. Enhanced Thermal Curing Process</h3=
>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"8120a09e-06b0-41eb-b763-ed3aae6305df">
<li local-id=3D"0253ed87-d674-42da-9742-977808d01565">
<p local-id=3D"53629eb4-2274-4ea3-abe6-9c18cd3eaeb4">Prepare water-soluble =
molds using 3D printing technology.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7fb9741d-1725-4668-8c42-c4892a86ae3c">
<p local-id=3D"24cf6a70-80d4-495d-a2a6-d246c6d49aac">Pack the prepared flow=
able powder into the 3D printed water-soluble molds, ensuring uniform densi=
ty.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ad4f6a3c-5c31-4482-aeab-349d37aa5592">
<p local-id=3D"6d248b26-467b-46a5-bf01-7ecd23a45a2e"><strong>Optimized Ther=
mal Curing</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c62506e7-3993-43a8-b311-4afe9d42d3ea">
<li local-id=3D"8406e2d5-4965-41bf-a7b2-789e44002afd">
<p local-id=3D"d1bdbe1e-a884-422a-9e78-6d3b94c46fda"><strong>Primary Curing=
</strong>: Heat to 80=C2=B0C and maintain for 90 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5ed8c434-2c13-4862-9b42-d6b82f8e714d">
<p local-id=3D"71f56fb0-7d95-4f9b-9acd-ffa1de26d458"><strong>Final Curing</=
strong>: Increase temperature to 95=C2=B0C for 30 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ee4997bf-0246-4cc6-8bb1-f8d496de669d">
<p local-id=3D"45d73875-7e5f-4e1d-a7c5-ac028cae26a5"><strong>Critical Step<=
/strong>: Once curing is complete, remove parts from the oven while still h=
ot (use appropriate heat protection)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3ae16ee5-f42b-4a59-9699-6b14f91853f7">
<p local-id=3D"02e2b5fe-68fe-4d23-957a-31d1a23546f7">Do NOT allow parts to =
cool slowly in the oven</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"156cd329-54d2-4dd5-8b5c-c95fc6fae2f2">
<p local-id=3D"e2edbe34-5a48-4b7b-a598-c8a08f938978">Allow the parts to coo=
l at room temperature (will occur more rapidly due to removal from oven).</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"665039fe-dec2-4895-9a9c-a47d48d88dab">
<p local-id=3D"cbcb3164-7ed8-468c-afe0-6f2fb8e3a362">For larger parts, imme=
rse in room-temperature water bath after removing from oven to accelerate c=
ooling.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"a26c9a88-fa29-4a0a-9b56-b9a460b8cc6e" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.DissolutionandGreenPartRecovery.5">F. Dissolution and Green Part Recov=
ery</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"d8bfec8b-51aa-4c3e-9a9a-a83e3e143de0">
<li local-id=3D"c2bcaf10-4553-4b6c-897a-f3eb6b540f18">
<p local-id=3D"b03326a7-569a-4f79-8028-c46c31fb21dd">Allow the thermally cu=
red part to rest for at least 2 hours after cooling.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ba65e4bc-731d-438a-afaf-0afe3af740dc">
<p local-id=3D"bccf7dee-58c5-455e-b0c3-68c6c0c4525c">Prepare a warm water b=
ath at 45=C2=B0C.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e47d6ca8-b092-4dbc-ac12-7541c8c98bad">
<p local-id=3D"257d5b06-3a20-45f4-b788-427d80b99f3b">Submerge the entire as=
sembly in the warm water bath to dissolve the water-soluble mold.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a69fd987-ed36-47af-8ae8-512c86f1ff30">
<p local-id=3D"5b9cb8e0-ed11-4687-826c-59d53116f32d">Monitor dissolution an=
d refresh water as needed until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6c280d5d-105b-4c7e-8ff3-21eb2d033750">
<p local-id=3D"16560794-2303-4118-b58d-4efd11cce0d8">Carefully extract the =
green part and allow to dry at room temperature for 12 hours.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"56191874-484e-487d-ae99-e3ddfeb0b764">
<p local-id=3D"42485a97-0e84-47f4-b187-3a6c2fcfc21f">The green part is now =
ready for debinding and sintering according to your standard protocol.</p><=
/li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"2d9ecc4e-3213-4b60-b912-d0ede1ab1d1a" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-TechnicalNotes.3">Technical Notes</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"f7dad3c8-ffe0-4d9c-a62c-d132af5eda06" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-KeyModificationsfromOriginalSuccessfulRecipe.1">Key Modifications from O=
riginal Successful Recipe</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"834e9e58-607c-4dab-9d36-09bb4aeda94c">
<li local-id=3D"2adbc061-ae37-4594-b071-c294947af22b">
<p local-id=3D"200bb451-939d-43b8-aeca-c07d4635c571"><strong>Retained PMMA-=
co-EA as Base Polymer</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"78d2118c-8848-447d-aa4d-49fb2bb61db9">
<li local-id=3D"ed979618-77b3-49cd-abd1-f35175896687">
<p local-id=3D"6308618c-1b02-400f-b831-6658d4d835ee">Provides better adhesi=
on and flexibility than pure PMMA</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6ac41302-4fad-4468-9e84-51874ed90cc1">
<p local-id=3D"f3da92d9-5ed4-4cec-86c6-b918e30a0265">Lower glass transition=
 temperature makes for better green part handling properties</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a8f5cbd-f160-4560-a3ed-f92b3fb11683">
<p local-id=3D"3cab644d-c789-4a70-a0a0-f8601a8d9f31"><strong>Moderately Inc=
reased TEG-DMA (15% vs 10%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"b81c2bc6-4b8a-4b99-a2b5-dde2ab8e8beb">
<li local-id=3D"36f233b9-3aee-444f-a2cf-452fc61e78d7">
<p local-id=3D"65454e64-0cdc-422c-9be0-cb23d9c9c6e1">Creates stronger cross=
linked network for improved green strength</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dd33d061-cf92-4b9c-94a4-f064016f8b0d">
<p local-id=3D"80a70550-d00f-404c-bfec-b6b86593fabf">Still maintains compat=
ibility with base PMMA-co-EA system</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"33c74d14-296b-4ca1-b8a8-9941603e254b">
<p local-id=3D"193bb590-2ccc-42ff-9a45-30f751e1eea5"><strong>Slightly Incre=
ased AIBN (3% vs 2%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a07f8644-1c2a-4ab4-89ae-b1a0d8048532">
<li local-id=3D"4d6513c5-af66-484b-9020-d5c7c6f019cd">
<p local-id=3D"7fbdf8b6-f906-4fcd-b5e2-3909e32a9f38">Ensures complete cross=
linking throughout the part</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"37bb42b1-fc9d-48b4-b357-f81d9882e5d7">
<p local-id=3D"6c150e5b-bd4a-48d1-98e0-84ab269a8af8">Helps compensate for a=
ny inhibitory effects of additives</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"f2549734-35e6-4555-879d-359d36197e85">
<p local-id=3D"a802a0d9-d384-4d98-aa9d-d83cbc4f1758"><strong>Added Minimal =
Plasticizer (3% DBP)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"5d4b04c0-fcf3-43cc-aa71-40416e166e55">
<li local-id=3D"486c4537-d52c-47b8-aa43-034c83b494d2">
<p local-id=3D"c911df03-6696-4536-b79b-d87378ee518b">Makes the dried cake e=
asier to process</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"42ab3687-4ca5-4ea6-9242-303134b993a0">
<p local-id=3D"5a051517-3431-48b5-81fa-9e37e25e59f6">Improves flexibility o=
f the green part</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e22ee1e7-7f5a-4514-ba48-e29f5ffa84d5">
<p local-id=3D"1137bfa8-58bd-443a-ab71-614a8e1051b8">Amount carefully limit=
ed to prevent excessive softening</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"d12c002a-3170-4426-80f9-764404eb6af2">
<p local-id=3D"560f8966-58b3-4dd5-ada2-a18a0082c499"><strong>Added Small Am=
ount of Stearic Acid (1%)</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"85b484f1-9c4f-4858-ab03-eca68d726895">
<li local-id=3D"957777ed-95d3-4a68-966b-04e4ddf66c80">
<p local-id=3D"c6dbe0b9-7182-4737-a26f-14ff4db3e2f9">Acts as lubricant to i=
mprove powder flow and packing</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d40e5c0f-5e34-43ee-8f0c-4147526af236">
<p local-id=3D"3a3832da-4854-43e9-948c-58ca26592e01">Helps with mold fillin=
g</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4b42770d-2252-4650-a6f0-e2d89d8793a4">
<p local-id=3D"d4340a8f-7e93-45c1-a6f0-cdea44556c26">Minimal amount to avoi=
d interference with crosslinking</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"8c56accb-25cd-4ed4-aecb-94d88471b2cb" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ImportantProcessingConsiderations.1">Important Processing Considerations=
</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"eae9bd34-821d-4d03-90b0-53fdfd6a4194">
<li local-id=3D"a0abc69f-1596-435b-9661-4434c520cd6d">
<p local-id=3D"50019fd4-3e37-443e-b866-5893b6d1b7f2"><strong>Thorough Dryin=
g</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"b75a2116-6144-43c9-820a-723f1c793423">
<li local-id=3D"39e6860e-e551-488e-96f7-af37b033b59c">
<p local-id=3D"c4fc36d3-9b18-428e-95f7-2f7fee24a343">Complete solvent remov=
al is critical</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c5d6eefa-2c89-4072-9237-327c0f579d80">
<p local-id=3D"cda73426-29f7-4e5b-93c7-397ab68cac96">Final 60=C2=B0C drying=
 step ensures residual acetone is removed</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"a28cb647-609a-46f6-a739-e0bd91ae8f46">
<p local-id=3D"d158abbe-8d4b-4d62-9ffa-84aa7021078a"><strong>Critically Imp=
ortant: Thermal Shock Cooling</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"f2fa7d4e-99b1-4283-8caa-009416e90d08">
<li local-id=3D"f770916b-7337-41ca-a9f4-9be1cad32578">
<p local-id=3D"110d7f0c-00ab-4ea9-a9e0-671d7887b72c">The observation that p=
arts removed hot from the oven were strong while slow-cooled parts failed i=
s key</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7e32e8c4-897a-49f1-8b4b-b6ff13c430d3">
<p local-id=3D"90cb7e92-bfc4-47bb-b2a0-d8173230ea20">Always remove parts fr=
om the oven immediately after the final cure stage</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e35f1be1-4b41-4128-9475-450d56f522ce">
<p local-id=3D"a14b1d29-0a49-412f-b737-37cdf9381651">For larger parts, cons=
ider quenching in room temperature water</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8270a320-f484-4985-bfb2-c248cd4bfd53">
<p local-id=3D"28af4853-956e-42c6-bbac-00ac11a22bdf">This cooling step is j=
ust as important as the heating protocol</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"903eb4da-7db8-46e2-9b72-412b39867b74">
<p local-id=3D"f5d2899d-8840-47df-b778-8ccef557ee6c"><strong>Flowability Co=
nsiderations</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"44e68595-dba6-4bdd-ade5-6ad2f24fc369">
<li local-id=3D"a60b7940-2670-4e52-9663-ad818f9821ba">
<p local-id=3D"d0f6e00d-003d-420a-928a-48e051665346">If needed, add 0.1g of=
 Aerosil R 812 S (fumed silica) to improve flow</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"890fd85b-1a3a-41c4-be6c-7146a3e693cd">
<p local-id=3D"6e7a91b7-18af-470b-961d-a5e8b8939e94">Add to the dried and g=
round powder, not the liquid binder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3f2f8c2b-8d7c-4c22-83ec-f115fac17519">
<p local-id=3D"b21a67b2-e10e-4643-af04-422e37fda1be">Gentle vibration durin=
g mold filling can help achieve uniform packing</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"4624ca0b-d82f-4b78-b8e7-2ab5079b5d61">
<p local-id=3D"bf558db0-0d36-4e80-8c2a-e482bceba366"><strong>Quality Contro=
l Checks</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"d981bbea-54b2-4ba7-a885-916e5985ca40">
<li local-id=3D"f1c6e3f9-d998-47a6-92ce-91fff4c58628">
<p local-id=3D"0e395881-8234-4538-bacd-31ed93cae9f6">Test AIBN reactivity i=
f using from previous batches (store in refrigerator)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"81d60e5d-cfd4-4146-870c-6822e254e8a9">
<p local-id=3D"3b653b02-b208-4c4d-95fa-fca01a181c5f">Ensure PMMA-co-EA is f=
resh and properly stored</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"097faff6-fcee-4015-97db-2d1038d3ae00">
<p local-id=3D"354ad42f-aaa2-461d-9f6a-81cb7eb75008">Verify oven temperatur=
es with independent thermometer</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"df1b0cda-8803-49d8-b54c-5f1f1f6d7ee8">
<p local-id=3D"36d920c1-b388-4fbe-bf94-f12f5ea44090"><strong>Troubleshootin=
g Options</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"fe6ec71b-5f8c-43b9-88f9-848855b00477">
<li local-id=3D"cd840357-4f48-4992-a7f8-9f2212025122">
<p local-id=3D"937242c1-bbce-4662-8282-45c084a57b71">If parts still degrade=
 during cooling: Increase MEHQ to 0.06g (0.2%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a0fbea8-3d98-4352-9119-9e41ce3cf6f3">
<p local-id=3D"df1e4bf8-762a-4a49-b6b7-6c207fe2f923">If green strength is i=
nsufficient: Increase TEG-DMA to 18% (reduce PMMA-co-EA to 75%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e9c4f3c6-e731-4dd9-9d6a-05266f0d6eaa">
<p local-id=3D"1ce6fc2d-f8e6-4ed8-a629-70793a274c8d">For extremely thick pa=
rts: Consider extending final cure time to 45 minutes</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"638d3daa-168d-4665-8f66-f9642768ec11"></p>
<p local-id=3D"ee6c9ca4-6cab-4094-98b5-eabb52eb9249">I am trying a few diff=
erent approaches to improve the green part strength. With the most recent p=
owder batch, I added .1g of Aerosil R 812 S to the bottle and mixed it by h=
and for several minutes, loaded it into a mold, and put that in a furnace t=
o heat to 275F at a rate of 500 F/hour. I also took an old bottle of powder=
 labeled =E2=80=9Cadvanced binder formulation, 2X TEG-DMA=E2=80=9D and adde=
d .5g of 1000 mesh PMMA powder, and sieved it for 10 minutes, then poured i=
t into a ceramic crucible and tapped it for a while. I put that in the same=
 furnace run as the water soluble mold.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2c7e206c-6cd8-4649-8f02-4403bd6c21f7">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting=
:</p>
<p local-id=3D"5f7597bf-415d-4bdf-9617-c78baef49ae8">To Do Next Week</p>
<ul local-id=3D"66ad4d5b-b504-4df6-bad8-7c1ffbee0d8e">
<li local-id=3D"cd164047-6905-4e89-91eb-d834ec9238af">
<p local-id=3D"8df4135b-9699-4600-ac8b-f6b089b3cc30">Complete assembly of b=
enchtop V4.0</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d432c98b-b64a-49dd-b169-f771aa4523aa">
<p local-id=3D"b8a2ef6c-4423-4a44-9c44-9f718c0caa55">Convert both V4.0 HOPP=
ERs to steel shaft core roller</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"24ef58c7-0c4b-4e94-b759-a983c7998f10">
<p local-id=3D"36b25e22-95c7-4766-b0f6-5ff7ba307e8e">Assemble gated HOPPER =
V3.3.5</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6e304ad3-c6ef-4a10-a990-1d09c094ccd4">
<p local-id=3D"63fa22db-1ecd-41f1-a804-4d43e0b55c42">Stepper tapper control=
ler</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"106c64bc-4ef2-4d5f-94de-0653c56a138a">
<p local-id=3D"a0845846-0953-44f4-a98c-ea59ea4e282f">Gantry laser mount</p>
<ul local-id=3D"14c2fb65-956a-42b3-9400-86bd6f131f84">
<li local-id=3D"d5613654-3d12-4938-8f70-0d7c9cc5373f">
<p local-id=3D"c60afb90-e8eb-4337-82a5-26f49d59167a">Vacuum connection and =
compressed air input</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"45c4dfa0-5e08-454c-85bf-d43c32f215d5"></p>
<p local-id=3D"74882aec-9c27-473b-a6ee-23018685b688">2025-05-19</p>
<p local-id=3D"9cd09232-acd4-4bcb-9f64-92fee113be93">HOPPER: Made a spreade=
r bar for the gated hopper design (10mm OD, 128mm L) as well as the two req=
uired spreader bar retainer clips. I also made two steel roller bar core sh=
afts by cutting 8mm OD keyed shaft stock to 180mm L. The keyed pulley that =
I printed to work with this shaft was too tight of a fit; I was able to pre=
ss it onto the shaft without damaging the pulley but when I pressed in a pi=
ece of key stock to lock the pulley to the shaft, the pulley cracked. I red=
esigned the pulley with larger shaft hole and key way dimensions, and am cu=
rrently printing 3X pulleys with the new dimensions. Because the print of t=
he gated hopper and the gate mechanism failed over the weekend, I reran the=
 print today with the Bambu printer set to its highest speed setting so it =
would be done before the end of the day. I cut a piece of spring steel to l=
ength and drilled and countersunk two holes in it to screw it to the bottom=
 of the gated hopper; it will act as a guide for the hopper that will be mo=
re robust than the thin 3D printed guide previously used.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7f039ef3-e931-468d-8bfd-5ca276471936">PILOT: I need to made =
a mount for the 40W (input power, optical power likely closer to 10W) laser=
 diode module for PILOT 3, so I am currently working on making a CAD model =
of the module. I have completed CAD models of the 40W and 80W laser diode m=
odules (it turns out that they have different mounting tapped hole patterns=
 on the back, so I made two CAD models).</p>
<p local-id=3D"f46c8e1e-ff49-42ea-ab88-de142e857752">REDRESS: I am pursuing=
 two separate avenues to solve the issue I saw last week with the green par=
t falling apart when dissolving the mold. First, I am creating a new batch =
of powder following what I believe to be my most successful waterproof reci=
pe to date, a 3% binder load recipe made using only PMMA, TEG-DMA, and AIBN=
. Second, I am making a green part using powder that I had coated with PVP-=
VA after a silane pre-treatment. This part may actually already be waterpro=
of; I have not tested that formulation of powder coating, but if it is not,=
 I am going to post-treat the green part with a waterproofing process using=
 the silane coupling agent I already have around:</p>
<h1 local-id=3D"a01abb2c-e6f1-452e-841e-03a457a646e8" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-MetalPowderProcesswithPVP-VABinderandTMSPMAWaterproofing">Metal Powder P=
rocess with PVP-VA Binder and TMSPMA Waterproofing</h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"a885462e-650e-4409-94a7-2614902433d5" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Materials.10">Materials</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"b1a4692c-14d9-4a57-b240-1f6700d19540" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-MetalPowderComponents">Metal Powder Components</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"464b32e9-6f4c-413a-b265-9f9db4f44af4">
<li local-id=3D"05437f1a-51b7-44b6-91d8-6b5bc9719194">
<p local-id=3D"9a0e4888-9827-44dc-9856-e228b9e32403">970g Metal powder (17-=
4 PH, Inconel 625, or CuCrZr, 45-150=CE=BCm particle size)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"535417f2-0c85-457e-b4d2-ef9b8e9789c7">
<p local-id=3D"d5643222-ef4d-434c-aa80-92e1a2005fcd">30g PVP-VA copolymer (=
polyvinylpyrrolidone-vinyl acetate) (3% binder load)</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"0e763a4f-eb6d-4862-a514-b40c129d27b4" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Solvents">Solvents</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"69d30137-1ac1-4692-9e7b-e9384b5ac197">
<li local-id=3D"3cc7417b-c236-42d5-9940-bea4dedca213">
<p local-id=3D"82632c0b-4e03-46d4-9e39-e3632906836e">350-400g Ethanol (reag=
ent grade, &gt;99.5%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"df1ff7c0-4304-492b-aed3-21910313309a">
<p local-id=3D"8258256f-97c2-4d3c-acac-d6acde5dff26">100g Acetone (reagent =
grade, &gt;99.5%)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c9d031fd-c40a-4789-8f54-07bde6f76d47">
<p local-id=3D"0f313c36-e23c-40a9-875b-03894c48bef0">10g Distilled water (f=
or PVP-VA solution preparation)</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"42c5b63c-23bf-4170-946f-f88e395950bd" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-WaterproofingComponents">Waterproofing Components</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"10e52f6b-4863-488f-9fa9-c29e68743e77">
<li local-id=3D"7e9e7333-ff88-49d5-a3b3-64fccc7c36e0">
<p local-id=3D"e232df83-0c16-4273-b1a0-7d3180af704b">12g 3-Trimethoxysilylp=
ropyl methacrylate (TMSPMA)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"67586949-0144-4194-b9d2-a6c7bbaa0b4f">
<p local-id=3D"0e2ebe75-567e-4055-8cf8-28edb1d7123d">0.6g 2,2=E2=80=B2-Azob=
is(2-methylpropionitrile) (AIBN)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c806aa4c-6a1e-4623-89e9-9c5caefa6ea8">
<p local-id=3D"1b5c7230-0ae9-4b2a-b784-b43b656fb580">0.12g Acetic acid (opt=
ional, as catalyst)</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"845922d2-6710-4e4b-86c2-72bfb96f2bd0" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Equipment.5">Equipment</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"21f987f3-801d-4014-8f3d-b90dcc8c991b">
<li local-id=3D"462bf153-4b46-4608-b9df-9d926929112c">
<p local-id=3D"c0452ae5-1ab7-46cf-8690-051cb9f2f06c">High-shear mixer or pl=
anetary mixer</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"13175f45-1c11-438d-9b51-edeca56af9b6">
<p local-id=3D"49177bea-b819-4ae2-9094-940c991128b2">Drying oven with tempe=
rature control</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3128074b-b65b-4555-a77a-dfb2415de6c2">
<p local-id=3D"297aa060-daab-41f0-b31a-dcda6d14f90e">Vacuum chamber (option=
al but recommended)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6d418713-ca0e-489f-a8ef-931192a7a7cf">
<p local-id=3D"fd2bb811-67b6-4302-9da9-e98d2d09cac0">Water-soluble 3D print=
ed molds (PVA or similar)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"311a984a-4228-48bf-b6b3-5853f1a9a85d">
<p local-id=3D"a725c04b-53bd-4813-a792-670b17d4d9af">Stainless steel or gla=
ss containers</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"699e74e7-7f73-44f9-9f1d-c74e7b5bb245">
<p local-id=3D"6c6afdfd-5f8d-4906-a59b-780e8bd2ebce">Personal protective eq=
uipment (gloves, goggles, respirator)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4b73b534-8df4-41f7-a168-090141048217">
<p local-id=3D"85c9e241-319e-4083-b7b8-33eca4ecd55c">Analytical balance (0.=
01g precision)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dd290899-9629-459d-8262-4b882dba6065">
<p local-id=3D"c31e869b-c766-46d6-a5bc-842d8a282e1a">Temperature-controlled=
 sintering furnace</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"4cfd4a37-40b2-4603-b086-ccf885806aa0" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Process">Process</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"5e5d7680-32d6-48c2-a1d6-c4ad5cffec50" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-A.PVP-VASolutionPreparation">A. PVP-VA Solution Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"198f7c53-7206-40af-ae14-ecae3cb6bc8d">
<li local-id=3D"53f6c3ff-2e4e-4b5c-9c06-c665096786bc">
<p local-id=3D"b24764a9-7f61-4574-9e26-61b10763f30f">In a glass container, =
add 10g distilled water to 350g ethanol and mix thoroughly.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"16f35538-07b4-457b-9245-545040f75104">
<p local-id=3D"77e63c7e-0e3b-4561-a63d-b86fa9b8f64d">Gradually add 30g PVP-=
VA to the ethanol-water mixture while stirring.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ae9e27a0-8a07-400a-9abf-a937957fd49f">
<p local-id=3D"2b334de4-8308-448c-afbf-4290ca55c433">Continue stirring unti=
l completely dissolved (approximately 60-90 minutes).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a1777af5-2f82-4de0-93aa-fe8f4bcbac54">
<p local-id=3D"13d53591-928c-41a3-ac46-47e949d27eb3">The solution should be=
 clear to slightly cloudy with no visible undissolved particles.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"bca5dec8-1cdb-4caa-ac62-58a82e7a094b" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-B.MetalPowderCoating">B. Metal Powder Coating</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"a6575f3c-2b55-4487-941f-570c3f39f098">
<li local-id=3D"0fa43571-4899-4240-84c7-910499927bb0">
<p local-id=3D"8ec978ca-39f0-4b48-8336-e9b8027fd2ea">Place 970g metal powde=
r in a planetary mixer bowl.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dff78910-4cbf-448b-a94e-4eedd18d5346">
<p local-id=3D"f2e01578-5c85-482c-8892-d95d6a44694e">While mixing at low sp=
eed (100-150 RPM), slowly add the PVP-VA solution.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"37e2269c-21f6-4816-a0dc-bc3512ef43b3">
<p local-id=3D"51cb5ac0-6d41-4df6-a979-7927f685827d">Increase speed to medi=
um (200-250 RPM) and mix for 30 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4d9dc32e-cf4a-4048-987a-3c9dcba529d8">
<p local-id=3D"72520e89-301a-417e-b2e7-6642f4732026">Reduce speed to low an=
d continue mixing while heating gently to 40-45=C2=B0C to initiate solvent =
evaporation.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2d1e6a57-5e58-4f55-9528-dabb64706be4">
<p local-id=3D"49145767-fe60-486e-adab-973c6dcabf4b">Continue mixing until =
the powder achieves a semi-dry, flowable state (approximately 60-90 minutes=
).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"23a67c3d-ccea-4ee8-980b-cd9fd65a25af">
<p local-id=3D"20e5b7ca-f56e-406b-be1c-4d2f3934f3e6">Transfer powder to dry=
ing trays in layers no thicker than 1cm.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9a39783e-b22f-45cc-9a2a-82a090898bd6">
<p local-id=3D"54bc0ca2-66e3-42c4-bfaf-2011b8ec0871">Complete drying in an =
oven at 60=C2=B0C for 2 hours, stirring once halfway through.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3f2e4d90-78a5-4805-bb0f-7b06343144fd">
<p local-id=3D"136ac7f9-d38d-4c9c-a89e-4b7be46fa106">Allow to cool to room =
temperature.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9c6033a4-5140-4fb0-b8df-51101fdb00b3">
<p local-id=3D"fdf66565-b86c-48a2-9c21-c55358f05e34">The powder should be f=
ree-flowing with no agglomerates.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"81277d5b-f3c0-4774-ab5b-3ba73127bd07" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-C.MoldFillingandPrimaryCuring">C. Mold Filling and Primary Curing</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"eb7c2aaa-2121-4d5a-9fe5-ece88b32a079">
<li local-id=3D"3339507d-61b9-4516-bd64-eada229b835a">
<p local-id=3D"7176e5e3-f119-4f34-b87a-d0efdbfcf9e5">Fill the water-soluble=
 3D printed mold with the coated powder.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1e5e031f-6e04-4fd6-8de1-19f057db011d">
<p local-id=3D"828c9b98-fe2f-41e7-8d88-f580fd4f45ba">Apply vibration during=
 filling to ensure uniform packing density.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ac4db43b-3db4-4f5e-bf89-ba3a63dd056a">
<p local-id=3D"d0e27886-87c3-495e-ba4d-f5f6ef0c8b58">For complex geometries=
, fill in multiple stages with light tamping between layers.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7c8ef054-171b-4d0d-b667-556486797061">
<p local-id=3D"e7faf949-84d7-4bac-a198-533438eb0842">Primary thermal curing=
:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"5e9c6bc6-6a3d-4f32-be50-12080bcaf5e0">
<li local-id=3D"b3e4c371-f0aa-47c3-8e40-2d69b5167aac">
<p local-id=3D"333cef4a-87ba-43ab-8f1c-7bf00f5917a0">Heat to 75=C2=B0C at a=
 rate of 2=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9e9a53d0-8225-4575-b94a-9f20195e49e9">
<p local-id=3D"630f80ea-8d5d-4116-9c0a-cbd86716c9c5">Hold at 75=C2=B0C for =
60 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c2ed96ef-e4b8-4d4b-bc0b-d25ddf003999">
<p local-id=3D"4f60ee12-1d2d-4f60-8f76-5383bec79778">Increase to 85=C2=B0C =
at 1=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"af2836ca-1100-4858-bafa-b60f146e9129">
<p local-id=3D"24f69772-169a-49df-a104-5b23da3e6157">Hold at 85=C2=B0C for =
30 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"47d38c56-81b5-4609-b54f-4393c106b3b2">
<p local-id=3D"60cc830f-a9f8-41d9-a7e6-df6fac5185f6">Cool to room temperatu=
re at 2=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"4e5cb3a5-7aca-4041-8845-781ba900a1da">
<p local-id=3D"57e9fb7a-9f28-4145-9b87-f8650f0bfeac">The result is a PVP-VA=
 bound green part inside the water-soluble mold.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"14a53335-3ba2-487b-98f2-8da93d4e3fb9" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-D.TMSPMAWaterproofingSolutionPreparation">D. TMSPMA Waterproofing Soluti=
on Preparation</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"ddd9ed3e-08e3-4874-b197-4a038cbfe644">
<li local-id=3D"92d80741-ae6a-4988-9f42-11dcc4a6c18e">
<p local-id=3D"8c64adcd-a55a-46fa-b9e1-b3fc52df00de">In a glass container, =
combine:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"14fff4dd-eb5f-4511-88ef-ee901569e1df">
<li local-id=3D"128ea121-5c62-4eee-a0b5-ff173b9ed698">
<p local-id=3D"55be60da-15c7-48fa-9e46-d41bcc575212">100g acetone</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bb16ca57-1791-43a0-bad4-018ee5ab7ec6">
<p local-id=3D"768caeb3-578b-4099-b48c-6cf83682edd3">12g TMSPMA</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"de2da5bb-c96f-4438-9bc4-4ec1463cbfd4">
<p local-id=3D"818d4831-8e37-4cb8-bdbd-c843c69272d9">0.6g AIBN</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cac462a6-f7ec-4bd3-b63a-0ccf4783fda6">
<p local-id=3D"4352e25d-4a94-4a3a-880a-4563daab4a14">0.12g acetic acid (if =
using)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"2d37d738-7629-4072-b991-2307c836051b">
<p local-id=3D"364b066a-da47-4c01-908d-8b575b465b41">Stir gently for 15 min=
utes to allow partial hydrolysis of the silane.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6e020e96-350c-44dc-abd9-c5ea19076b4f">
<p local-id=3D"7031ec3e-8e98-40b8-8836-23fe343b662a">The solution should be=
 used within 2 hours of preparation.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"08fefa39-80f3-438a-951b-3068f43bff04" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-E.WaterproofingTreatmentApplication">E. Waterproofing Treatment Applicat=
ion</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"f71587d0-867e-42fb-a419-69372dbea27b">
<li local-id=3D"8f8eba0e-a816-469b-9979-cb1c61f0c746">
<p local-id=3D"2ede2589-961c-4d0c-ab02-087581328f3f">Place the green part (=
still in water-soluble mold) in a clean container.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"73eb06d9-7e9a-4dcb-8574-354a5374d7e6">
<p local-id=3D"715e2e56-f174-49dd-87b7-b80a0b37ef63">Method selection (choo=
se one): <strong>Standard Method (Immersion):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"e5db1237-ec15-48fe-a865-4c0125f167d1">
<li local-id=3D"2f48ba55-6727-44ca-96a2-b54c17cf50cf">
<p local-id=3D"a7a3fa41-8702-4a8f-b5fd-a1587a3f01f2">Pour the TMSPMA soluti=
on over the part until completely submerged</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"60f8cfd1-bc86-4ba3-b14a-79c402a6235f">
<p local-id=3D"d4c3c90f-a868-4da6-8596-b1e7d750129c">Allow to soak for 20-3=
0 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d285eb3d-956e-4d12-8f3f-7353b9642680">
<p local-id=3D"8380ae31-5add-4eb8-903a-d95454fd6a6d">Drain excess solution<=
/p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"a93e0c22-0dd6-4133-8317-c823d5d51e1c"><strong>Enhanced Metho=
d (Vacuum Infiltration):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"71d3dc6e-5acc-45f4-9608-4e30c945525c">
<li local-id=3D"8c381230-e42c-4095-b5ff-6ae22902b077">
<p local-id=3D"4137eba6-56c0-4d8a-83b2-88a1e57c72cf">Place part and TMSPMA =
solution in vacuum chamber</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ae2764c3-7996-4e22-aa82-5d63089cb68c">
<p local-id=3D"a39ebfa0-bd51-4796-9735-a86ca97fc441">Apply vacuum (20-25 in=
Hg) for 5 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"44b478aa-11c3-467a-a899-13bfba603d4e">
<p local-id=3D"385a8e6e-95a1-4943-bc68-d348fdfed10e">Release vacuum and mai=
ntain immersion for 15 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4a912d05-e4e1-4745-abc7-8fb16354dffc">
<p local-id=3D"9a44daa0-607c-43e5-ad99-e725e6101d9e">Drain excess solution<=
/p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"d4da946c-18a6-40c5-be81-26d0468ea060">
<p local-id=3D"04eaf0c7-65bb-4123-b3db-ee6737a917fb">After draining, place =
the treated part on a non-stick surface.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fe063f32-f6fe-49ff-b5c6-3d071499a6c9">
<p local-id=3D"599f3fe7-9617-459d-8e85-01b215f7d10b">Allow to stand at room=
 temperature for 25-30 minutes for initial acetone evaporation.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"62c15eef-a867-4e99-ac53-a86f80cad9ad">
<p local-id=3D"aa37b8e7-0b82-45da-b4dd-e0d829ee7500">The part should reach =
a "tacky but not wet" state.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"c86258e1-7352-466b-8cc2-b681bea72cf3" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-F.TMSPMACuringProtocol">F. TMSPMA Curing Protocol</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"99f9bcc7-397b-4c4d-8215-40e5b93ec649">
<li local-id=3D"813b2d10-55ce-4a77-820b-4ddac0ea7571">
<p local-id=3D"dd98bd06-1ad6-4bae-a876-25f21cf31517"><strong>Stage 1 (Solve=
nt Evaporation):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"26831a79-231e-4980-9912-5cf8bf6217aa">
<li local-id=3D"1f704c2a-9f26-4eb0-afb2-f7201fd55b09">
<p local-id=3D"6120aedc-4c62-455f-af65-e5f066048394">Place in oven at 40=C2=
=B0C</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8dd1a3a9-346b-4b94-b1d9-053e1eecb85f">
<p local-id=3D"ac11f2a2-514d-4853-810c-8d8d99d7c79c">Hold for 30 minutes wi=
th slight ventilation</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"643e5fd3-1956-40d7-a3ba-9297a006efb5">
<p local-id=3D"9ac4196c-dd95-483c-a654-be2ce0c18163">Part surface should ap=
pear matte rather than glossy</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"0a49a7bb-976c-4ff1-b483-6e1195d2f89f">
<p local-id=3D"1bf166e6-9abc-4c1d-95e1-cb7279c22189"><strong>Stage 2 (AIBN =
Activation):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"04c91e41-5094-415f-b48d-7c92ae517bce">
<li local-id=3D"fa20200a-92bc-4e3b-9837-e5fc8cef6213">
<p local-id=3D"192561a1-7be3-4c3d-8ae6-67a98a6c42af">Increase temperature t=
o 65=C2=B0C</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5ae7b634-fd80-46a4-a80c-309263ca93e1">
<p local-id=3D"f75c3393-e402-41c8-abe0-2d19dcc43611">Hold for 60 minutes</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"4fbc404f-0c19-4337-a7d7-b4a1126cfdae">
<p local-id=3D"03b63041-2068-4f09-ad22-b0dcff08ab5e">This initiates methacr=
ylate polymerization</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"6ce2173f-5193-40ba-8c9b-aa6ca82b54c2">
<p local-id=3D"eefe35a6-182b-4630-954b-b7880790db58"><strong>Stage 3 (Silox=
ane Network Formation):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"f4aa0d8c-9c4d-4bbe-8168-cbb7680153c3">
<li local-id=3D"53d3e189-7aca-457e-a68e-f8f1c21f847f">
<p local-id=3D"17211774-e1dd-4773-966a-b3668b54e973">Increase temperature t=
o 85=C2=B0C</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1282e3fe-744a-4cbd-80a4-997c6430f080">
<p local-id=3D"db330128-356a-4408-bf6c-21f49a695d9f">Hold for 30 minutes</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"9e86a60d-098e-4571-a5e4-5f5b940eead7">
<p local-id=3D"7dd80db8-058a-474d-8ba3-b585b8258072">This completes the wat=
erproofing layer formation</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"cab5411f-2c43-4fb7-930e-0683ffaaf205">
<p local-id=3D"caa676a2-b994-43ba-89ee-072e6cdeb887">Cool to room temperatu=
re at 2=C2=B0C/minute or slower.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3d5a3061-700b-4c7e-b806-c5f8b6118aff">
<p local-id=3D"6a349fde-a373-451e-ae8e-20e043725a41">The part is now waterp=
roofed while still in the water-soluble mold.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"9d06b5a2-c977-45cd-bf7f-4d2b94533bed" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-G.Water-SolubleMoldRemoval">G. Water-Soluble Mold Removal</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"66f89aeb-f216-4d1d-bbe4-9439ed91a5af">
<li local-id=3D"2d12b3a7-0d52-4fef-9fb6-ec7f6d444c72">
<p local-id=3D"01a65f4b-91d2-4c38-aaaf-15b777687c50">Prepare a water bath a=
t 45=C2=B0C.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"041dac9d-ba44-454b-8ec1-ba3264ee139c">
<p local-id=3D"dfcdbb26-7b70-4a3f-a768-57f6aa513421">Fully submerge the wat=
erproofed part and mold in the water bath.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1bb00205-a1e7-4791-9624-bda7ed7e5454">
<p local-id=3D"ad64815e-6ea8-47df-99f9-dd4be9db791e">Allow dissolution to p=
roceed without agitation for the first 30 minutes.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"420bc517-6441-4d55-8f69-75526d01b02c">
<p local-id=3D"e318cb3e-a683-4331-b0f7-ca1907b9982c">Gently agitate water a=
nd continue dissolution until mold is completely removed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"91cc3b6e-93a6-4e61-91b2-8e8084528198">
<p local-id=3D"f3622c87-16b4-4f77-adb0-5bb894cdd523">For thicker molds, ref=
resh water as needed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9851312a-1ac0-4336-a839-606a724721a4">
<p local-id=3D"dac10dd2-e090-415a-970a-e9ca0e17236a">Total dissolution time=
 may range from 1-4 hours depending on mold thickness.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"418d29cf-85f5-4033-8a40-64becb5531f8">
<p local-id=3D"6651d7b2-3e59-42f7-8cc2-c95d479402d5">Once mold is fully dis=
solved, carefully remove the part from water.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5149a9b1-18a1-4a81-aa2a-b0fa681f4565">
<p local-id=3D"a7e683e0-4106-42bd-944c-a8775c0ac2f1">Rinse gently with fres=
h water.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8fddf9e6-51ed-4acd-8b54-9104b506b932">
<p local-id=3D"f42c1025-6f93-4fbf-a6dc-556eafe130e9">Allow to dry at room t=
emperature for 24 hours.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"875927d9-0576-47c1-901c-c39c41f827df" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-H.DebindingandSintering">H. Debinding and Sintering</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"dbc1087f-3a2d-4eb8-a80c-8ece1b63a2cb">
<li local-id=3D"3012aaeb-79e2-414f-bf17-c28d4121d95b">
<p local-id=3D"7d1a9214-5380-41aa-8263-f84d29a3dfff"><strong>Primary Debind=
ing (PVP-VA and TMSPMA Removal):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"59d55e4b-a6c6-4288-889e-ecc78aab46f1">
<li local-id=3D"9dd55efa-572f-4b71-9d6d-16ca0f493d9e">
<p local-id=3D"1f209dfb-9fe0-479d-8d35-7931d2061c3d">Place part in debindin=
g furnace</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"61c36525-540b-4457-99b2-10659848275f">
<p local-id=3D"e81282ca-427e-4b5d-9b36-af55937f5ff8">Ramp to 200=C2=B0C at =
1=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3058ff4a-5716-452e-bfc4-c2660f8d4747">
<p local-id=3D"59095222-25e4-4813-afe2-ae8e54baaddf">Hold at 200=C2=B0C for=
 60 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"dd3098a5-87ba-4ba7-86b7-afeb04267f35">
<p local-id=3D"7e90587d-c199-4e9a-b7e5-daeef2c7ec28">Ramp to 350=C2=B0C at =
1=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b84accb6-93af-4ebb-86bc-fa424c6596bf">
<p local-id=3D"e40283c3-ea07-4421-8041-bd7e612591d5">Hold at 350=C2=B0C for=
 120 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3fe0a735-904f-4258-af37-8f251b27f1c7">
<p local-id=3D"8a068c97-2d62-46a2-88f5-034e80940999">Controlled atmosphere:=
 flowing air or nitrogen with slight oxygen content</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"5ffd24fb-db28-42c1-b2c7-38fdc17237cd">
<p local-id=3D"ab55caa1-79ef-423f-8600-162ad4f69606"><strong>Secondary Debi=
nding (Complete Organic Removal):</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"eefab748-745a-42a7-b7e6-abb5b62a157a">
<li local-id=3D"ab557c6d-8b89-4be5-86d1-2aa9f2a370cf">
<p local-id=3D"e4f22632-a3fa-4e7a-bb30-c882eae5057d">Ramp to 450=C2=B0C at =
1=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aa594264-d0e4-4fe2-8d28-49024dbda356">
<p local-id=3D"99d40886-873b-42b8-85dc-2d1a0413db7b">Hold at 450=C2=B0C for=
 90 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"48f623fe-b624-45f9-bfa4-0ce04faa48ce">
<p local-id=3D"750ea7f8-4fd4-4394-b68d-e8220e6a472f">Controlled atmosphere:=
 flowing hydrogen or hydrogen/argon mixture</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"07df5a5a-b254-4aa0-8a47-e2492847d457">
<p local-id=3D"ffb31dab-a028-4b20-ac4c-f39f9ece0c99"><strong>Sintering:</st=
rong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"a3b4735e-9be3-4d12-be69-85b3f23f6fe7">
<li local-id=3D"df68dbfa-3493-4207-939b-7ecbc12f64c9">
<p local-id=3D"b69af1a4-85f7-427c-a944-ec92c811b240">Proceed with standard =
sintering protocol for the specific metal powder</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9cb922ae-449e-452d-ac19-02e194ddb3b1">
<p local-id=3D"cc6d44fa-1f4a-427d-90e7-54c78dbf36e4">For 17-4 PH: Ramp to 1=
360=C2=B0C at 5=C2=B0C/minute, hold for 120 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"10a5e5b9-0f51-419b-9743-a7dcbf4d84ec">
<p local-id=3D"b56ab8b0-f276-460c-96ab-f56508c5215d">For Inconel 625: Ramp =
to 1290=C2=B0C at 5=C2=B0C/minute, hold for 180 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f6a91c14-158d-4236-b47f-2a6e12c6ebfb">
<p local-id=3D"efc5a975-ef9c-4370-a1b0-61faf5453520">For CuCrZr: Ramp to 10=
40=C2=B0C at 5=C2=B0C/minute, hold for 90 minutes</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"676cecb4-5700-473d-aad5-8ffef46058cb">
<p local-id=3D"2d517f39-c4aa-4694-a1ca-0a0a6df32593">Sintering atmosphere: =
high purity hydrogen or vacuum</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"b378e425-127a-4912-aabc-cd512e35821d" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-TechnicalNotesandTroubleshooting">Technical Notes and Troubleshooting</h=
2>
<h3 local-id=3D"a7e089aa-1a7a-4621-afce-8dea50b907b4" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ProcessOptimization">Process Optimization</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"21001395-66a6-4466-8c3e-293ccb020e6a">
<li local-id=3D"a47bde96-5468-4093-810d-77527b69b46a">
<p local-id=3D"8c0784b6-6f6b-4013-8dda-ebfc9d300f0f"><strong>Powder Flowabi=
lity:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"0cb3463f-7b10-4944-95aa-33989740dad5">
<li local-id=3D"9279ef85-de94-4dbf-bc03-1e052655d38b">
<p local-id=3D"74002f5a-862d-485d-8800-b58b7728a0e9">If powder is not flowi=
ng well after PVP-VA coating, add 0.1% fumed silica</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"224f0f16-93de-4c17-9517-2eb4f3cca35e">
<p local-id=3D"ad9db501-f85d-421e-9358-35b8b6feaff0">Alternatively, reduce =
PVP-VA concentration to 2.8% and repeat drying step</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"61c5fe77-179e-4b52-a5e3-5173320f92d5">
<p local-id=3D"050dd7ad-8b7a-4c9e-8fc8-33f6fc94cd59"><strong>Green Part Str=
ength:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"12985fcb-eb6b-45f7-a7fa-0f88b59fb344">
<li local-id=3D"8f580099-4040-44ac-ad6d-d41b64fa7f59">
<p local-id=3D"f9881f6f-a9fe-422f-b06b-6f0b90ef0177">If green part strength=
 is insufficient, increase initial cure temperature to 90=C2=B0C</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a387950f-6a7e-4409-b29a-dc5a7d0c93ff">
<p local-id=3D"e6cd309e-06d6-4663-9494-8d467e9756c2">Hold time can be exten=
ded to 90 minutes for thicker parts</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9d22f993-e602-4e3c-b2b9-3c0da4d80f97">
<p local-id=3D"bef47f90-f21a-449d-a867-c96953a58be8">Consider adding 0.5% c=
ross-linking agent to PVP-VA solution</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"61574581-b6f8-4c6d-bed9-539a2f369d8d">
<p local-id=3D"a00a369d-5010-46b6-8c7b-4ba6e3ef36ae"><strong>Waterproofing =
Effectiveness:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"69494f3b-eeed-45a2-881e-5c9d387fd052">
<li local-id=3D"1f5d85b5-3114-4fa8-9c24-f3a148e25e40">
<p local-id=3D"c3b7e622-e99d-4676-8272-9488563eadae">For enhanced water pro=
tection, increase TMSPMA concentration to 15%</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5a1eaab1-1a76-43de-aa07-8c39be69d440">
<p local-id=3D"5a4679c9-2384-4712-8e72-4c6cafa69145">For very complex geome=
tries, consider multiple TMSPMA applications with partial curing between</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"de3a7012-9df6-454f-82a0-f58464f17030">
<p local-id=3D"a59531a1-c714-419d-9f4d-61a466a03116">If water penetration o=
ccurs during mold dissolution, reduce water temperature to 35=C2=B0C</p></l=
i>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"07b13e95-6924-4c39-b0a3-5cf228b9470d">
<p local-id=3D"81854a89-99c1-4e97-863e-e4ebb423d8d7"><strong>Mold Dissoluti=
on:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"fd06fddd-2046-4e6c-9a93-3e80d1354888">
<li local-id=3D"08eaf015-26fd-44e9-b3ce-162f4e4a2afc">
<p local-id=3D"676b8167-a350-455e-8877-7c4f1ea8c52a">For faster dissolution=
, use circulating water bath</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"649a5664-2cf5-4053-93f3-2c7a8e0afe27">
<p local-id=3D"297bd057-54c1-4551-b7f2-6aff5011f183">For delicate features,=
 use static dissolution only</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e359c522-e3f9-4bac-a4fb-427dddf3dfdc">
<p local-id=3D"a218e9b7-b249-4606-b3a2-9ed4a39f83f9">If green part shows an=
y softening, immediately remove from water and dry</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"b7f1a938-b734-4634-b540-4202c912add1">
<p local-id=3D"5bbef114-6f92-479e-a455-1ef57236d7f5"><strong>Debinding Opti=
mization:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"690abc7c-a53a-4243-b78a-1bbce7301287">
<li local-id=3D"407579ec-68d0-4475-ab21-d4d777518e96">
<p local-id=3D"3e0bc91a-fcf1-46b4-8561-a776ebdfddac">For large parts (&gt;5=
0mm in any dimension), reduce heating rates to 0.5=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1f82b5fb-f006-4ec8-b72b-9f198387abe1">
<p local-id=3D"063bb64b-c6ca-407e-9287-bf274a2c35f3">For very small parts, =
standard rates can be increased to 2=C2=B0C/minute</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b78ada0c-9d01-4df9-9056-54396f5ebba5">
<p local-id=3D"48dde0b8-99f3-4908-9ad6-73bb08d0e885">Monitor for cracking o=
r blistering and adjust accordingly</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"07df3645-c20b-40fd-a0ef-0891f21fd3ca" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-QualityControlChecks">Quality Control Checks</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"5543d3f0-9065-4f33-b75e-c284f6f3e795">
<li local-id=3D"ee29b1a8-839e-4a29-990e-e5a79cdbb770">
<p local-id=3D"b4973fbc-413c-46f5-8a25-c6c7de3f09e5"><strong>After PVP-VA C=
oating:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"a57e2fa0-c157-4eca-9391-68f139511417">
<li local-id=3D"99739bdb-7ea9-4b1c-9397-20296dac63ad">
<p local-id=3D"fc49f7ab-5e92-43d9-983e-7d662768283b">Powder should flow fre=
ely with no large agglomerates</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d1874bf0-badd-418c-b88e-edd54f09393b">
<p local-id=3D"7aad835c-2e29-4612-9aa2-62b535281ae9">Binder distribution sh=
ould be uniform (check with methylene blue dye test)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"6c19fe7f-dbce-4a1c-a88e-970ad2e2dffb">
<p local-id=3D"9d4bd1a7-780b-41e4-b3cb-69c816bc8035"><strong>After Green Pa=
rt Formation:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"cbd4cb19-4878-44de-8365-40948c2c3a5e">
<li local-id=3D"416dc4e2-973b-4e92-830d-212544b197a1">
<p local-id=3D"1cb1aaed-4da2-484d-87f5-3ac6e822cb67">Part should have unifo=
rm density (check with caliper measurements)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a481fac6-a7a9-4784-ae09-bd802e206f0d">
<p local-id=3D"a6e748eb-11be-41b8-b38b-18ac47c3a3cd">Surface should be smoo=
th with no visible defects</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"9b5a6e7e-f413-4ab3-bca2-39180ebae935">
<p local-id=3D"4c754cd4-18c5-494b-a1c3-ed275154716b"><strong>After Waterpro=
ofing:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"a9428853-1fc5-4fdf-8de5-ed0f8417918e">
<li local-id=3D"86a23f92-4a30-4f5e-9908-0b30ecbc760c">
<p local-id=3D"dc60e23b-f7fc-4b0d-b013-7de15bc74af8">Water drop test: Water=
 should bead up and not penetrate surface</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"99abcfd3-fec3-4f9d-9ebe-27673b71421b">
<p local-id=3D"fc6b4af8-047a-4482-b1f9-fc540759d7b0">Weight gain should be =
0.8-1.5% compared to untreated green part</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"4b37093e-e4b3-4633-866a-8ec88c7ac55e">
<p local-id=3D"91f8e50a-82e5-4fdf-9f37-c190c4e533fc"><strong>After Debindin=
g:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"0bb11ed7-09d0-4997-872c-c29552da95c7">
<li local-id=3D"5759a5c4-3d57-4e99-a80a-de4737d1d609">
<p local-id=3D"e4d4e3ba-26f6-4743-9950-241fc2064c85">No visible carbon resi=
due should remain</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6919bc62-9222-4734-8c3b-3fd9c6358e8d">
<p local-id=3D"9221c9e8-8a8f-4d09-a0df-b4dbbdf5ef19">Parts should maintain =
dimensional stability (within 0.2-0.5% of green dimensions)</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"4e3f5245-0ead-4d61-9358-1d1b41a5ce2f">
<p local-id=3D"c9eba346-7fbb-439b-aeb2-b8e9862247db"><strong>After Sinterin=
g:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"4ba5d6b8-53ad-4947-8df7-f2a8e8255d47">
<li local-id=3D"5255afae-f054-46da-be06-d3346d0b9161">
<p local-id=3D"ab920b83-092c-4675-a158-7aa8ea46168e">Density should reach &=
gt;96% of theoretical</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fb69f32e-40ca-49bd-9d65-2e79d830e086">
<p local-id=3D"7ca23eb6-ddea-4969-b076-4fcdfe435264">Surface finish should =
be consistent with no visible defects</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h3 local-id=3D"3d38f528-d43f-4a08-81bb-f0badb2b3e7c" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-StorageConsiderations">Storage Considerations</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"33c7935e-9041-4ef8-b217-1a4b0dfd0b9e">
<li local-id=3D"08ac0c51-95e9-497a-b495-d542ed373c5f">
<p local-id=3D"bce43500-7818-40c4-98a9-b18510a7121c"><strong>Coated Powder:=
</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"707687f2-31aa-4838-bc9a-ffe97f07b247">
<li local-id=3D"38a9a2be-470e-4ae2-b442-579f5366f1cc">
<p local-id=3D"6a62da64-1b91-4c7d-97b2-2772066f1b94">Store in sealed contai=
ners with desiccant</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d040d8c8-adb1-4589-908c-2470dc6e7d8e">
<p local-id=3D"b2a9ba33-807b-4864-8117-176d2559c284">Use within 2 weeks for=
 optimal results</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"e6efb98b-7946-4de9-8a5e-1c6600719b96">
<p local-id=3D"e205a45b-dbe6-475a-a654-103558b91622"><strong>TMSPMA Solutio=
n:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"b62ff698-32f5-437b-a793-352e6259d639">
<li local-id=3D"e6393558-cebe-4fb4-a3f5-d94877397070">
<p local-id=3D"d69b7e9b-3168-4e31-8e88-4f7fb2ea447d">Prepare fresh for each=
 use</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ee0b7cd3-6867-4574-b46b-91b1ad0b9514">
<p local-id=3D"32e7d154-4be3-4bc0-b825-bf1bee67d8a1">Do not store mixed sol=
ution</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"064628d2-7201-4065-a290-c3b6b686340f">
<p local-id=3D"e08f7105-8b19-4861-a069-92da016a7a6f"><strong>Waterproofed G=
reen Parts:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"d2213943-9530-4f4b-9ec3-720121b86c02">
<li local-id=3D"f4ec3065-9abc-4863-ba03-bd04150a71ef">
<p local-id=3D"706fc1ba-19c2-4075-ae5c-add4e463d183">Can be stored for up t=
o 30 days in sealed containers</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"849cc083-4680-4687-b038-1d8740abe958">
<p local-id=3D"d5f66f56-3cd9-407b-856d-0a08ca8a3ed6">Avoid humidity fluctua=
tions during storage</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"6782004c-7635-49e3-a96e-80c7ce1e332f"></p>
<p local-id=3D"85ec33a9-4a26-4ff3-a8bf-ae65bff8ddfd">2025-05-20</p>
<p local-id=3D"ad38deaf-235b-4298-8368-fc1cb3f6cd50">HOPPER: Finished assem=
bling gated HOPPER V3.3.5. There were issues with the belt slipping when tr=
ying to close the gate even without powder loaded, so per Payman=E2=80=99s =
suggestion I switched the 0.010=E2=80=9D thick stainless steel gate to 0.00=
5=E2=80=9D thick stainless steel shim stock, which seemed to resolve the is=
sue. It seems that the motor shifts when it is trying to apply a large torq=
ue to the belt, which I believe is due to either lack of rigidity in the mo=
tor mount or, more likely, the hopper itself flexing where the motor mount =
is mounted to it, since it is mounted to a particularly thin region of the =
hopper. The hopper is printed from pure PLA, which is more rigid than PETG =
but less rigid than PLA-CF, so one thing I will do is reprint the hopper fr=
om PLA-CF. I also plan to reinforce the motor mount and the region of the h=
opper that it is mounted to.</p>
<p local-id=3D"112821cf-876f-43c1-8cbb-8458e029eaf4">The keyed roller print=
 last night failed, and the PLA-CF showed up from MatterHackers, so I am pr=
inting a new roller from that new material. The roller finished printing, a=
lthough there is a noticeable discontinuity in the print where I switched f=
rom 100% to 166% speed to accelerate the print, and I also want to print th=
e key into the roller so I don=E2=80=99t need a separate metal key, so I am=
 going to reprint the roller. I am also printing a new impact arm for the N=
EMA 17 motors that I received from <a href=3D"http://StepperOnline.com" cla=
ss=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">StepperOnline.co</a>m with 5mm shafts=
 and a shaft flat.</p>
<p local-id=3D"397c7e19-dfd6-492e-bc18-5e311d55e46f">PILOT: I printed the d=
ovetail mount pair for the laser diode module and gave them to Mohsen/Ben t=
o be installed on PILOT 3. I am also designing a vacuum connection for the =
laser diode module to suck up any residual burned binder or metal dust duri=
ng the laser process.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b9eb4668-38e2-4a5c-9f76-5c77212d67f4">Biweekly Clean Up Meet=
ing: There is a presentation for the board planned for mid June to present =
a pitch for new technologies. We are allegedly close to getting a contract =
from Epson for $1M for a PILOT printer (unclear whether Scott actually mean=
t a PILOT printer, or the Saffron that has been customized for Inconel). A =
C-suite person from Embraer is visiting at some point, which may lead to de=
velopment of new technologies or materials.</p>
<p local-id=3D"349c453b-763e-49bb-90a6-c4d29eae28c9"></p>
<p local-id=3D"42ef929a-81d7-4019-9388-2dce4b32b819">2025-05-21</p>
<p local-id=3D"0a330c33-ad52-4449-8d49-800431693f27">HOPPER:</p>
<p local-id=3D"3e8845b7-186f-4f36-aadf-0b18085dfdb5">New rollers were succe=
ssfully printed with PLA-CF and fit on the keyed shafts without a separate =
key needed. Working on design of dovetail for quick replaceability and heig=
ht adjustment. Need to confirm with Mohsen that the new layout of component=
s on PILOT 2 does not cause the heater to be heating the build plate during=
 cutting but is also able to reach the entire build plate while curing the =
layer. Components look like they=E2=80=99re probably OK but there is still =
an issue with increased porosity towards the -Y side of the build plate.</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"55873427-cac1-4d2b-bb36-8416aca79bc4">Hopper Qualification T=
est Plan Meeting</p>
<p local-id=3D"ed599d95-66e2-476a-aad7-92d7d6368b70">End of Q2: Fully quali=
fied Hopper implemented on at least one PILOT. Nominal qualification plan i=
s to run prints with HOPPER and tank-to-tank system and compare them.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"22cb157a-588b-4746-ae46-66383237f8aa">
<li local-id=3D"e177f9eb-abf7-424f-b1cf-77aaa8bfcd8b">
<p local-id=3D"4a6c69ba-52fb-45cc-b9e9-c6afc55e36bd">Quantifiable performan=
ce specs</p>
<ul local-id=3D"825b48b2-1301-448e-806d-e6ee70600d3c">
<li local-id=3D"af31d0e0-3d57-4369-89a6-1f6adfa7463a">
<p local-id=3D"518182c6-776f-455b-b5e0-f7fe163444c2">Maximum overflow perce=
ntage tolerable</p>
<ul local-id=3D"fd789e7d-751d-4c15-88ed-f6fb3d530bf6">
<li local-id=3D"da5bdeab-e4bd-4575-91c6-eb9417915089">
<p local-id=3D"420439a2-a090-467c-a1b8-7200b3ee10f4">Below 50% want</p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"c9e3b1d6-4823-4f32-8852-163880a96c3b">
<p local-id=3D"e84d706f-104e-4df8-b227-14a73304eeb4">Less than current 150-=
250% req=E2=80=99d</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"48d343c3-2743-408a-99a2-ed8f51bb4a81">
<p local-id=3D"a05b8836-2db9-446f-a4eb-a8b1012caeaa">Powder compatibility</=
p>
<ul local-id=3D"1a8b63ab-c3e1-4a21-80e3-5ee35edd3041">
<li local-id=3D"62cace9e-1c7b-4f83-bbc9-b81aea366ab0">
<p local-id=3D"bf63af69-49af-4d43-97df-919433b452e9">Flowable req=E2=80=99d=
</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"12fd8c25-4dca-420a-b1b6-106ce7af0a06">
<p local-id=3D"dd7e8f74-4f76-4f9b-9b64-46132149587f">Non-flowable want</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"09b470a6-61b0-4c15-bfe6-3aa466c905df">
<p local-id=3D"065d497b-fe22-4b9d-bd98-2bf9a16c2a95">17-4 PH SS</p>
<ul local-id=3D"bcfa4c5e-ace3-44bf-83e3-abdb029bfcc4">
<li local-id=3D"97b7b64f-7200-4a13-a537-3576e94dbd3f">
<p local-id=3D"df449da6-b7f7-4a02-a926-182c518d10de">Atmix (untreated)</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"4d66123f-0538-4391-9c7a-117eb3e38181">
<p local-id=3D"ee87b091-d307-4e2c-bd88-921595af92d3">Sandvik (treated)</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"3c530e28-1b12-4b8e-9b76-0e704e8e8ae1">
<p local-id=3D"284c83a5-55b1-4ada-9c7f-7b501b5c8035">Cu</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5833b017-d385-4181-9eee-a7da7fb05bd2">
<p local-id=3D"1426eaae-09b8-4d58-88c9-80f77478ea52">Inconel 625</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"203c405a-0598-4948-a266-71fb5f2237fb">
<p local-id=3D"b91fd02e-7ba7-4e96-9f48-6f93063a8c6b">Weigh powder dispensed=
 per rotation of doser roller with controlled amount of powder in powder. U=
se this data to adjust dispense depending on cuts.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2ccc801e-a2a7-4fc6-ac38-4119c24ac014">
<p local-id=3D"89fc0e4b-9db0-4903-bc02-fc685d0f72b8">Measure particle size =
segregation with stacked TRS coupons</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"eb82c635-49f8-4915-9adc-d8baaf43d8cb">
<p local-id=3D"57168fa4-212d-4f15-8779-20fd8a6c5b36">Green part density var=
iation</p>
<ul local-id=3D"fc4f52d2-e922-4e01-9b55-3576db347ea1">
<li local-id=3D"8b37961f-b77e-47e0-abd5-1f9d052f972a">
<p local-id=3D"7bf568fa-e2e1-404e-97fd-a4304725d64e">Reduce by 50% versus p=
revious benchmarks want</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cc8a6a66-30fe-4c62-a104-985fa07e8fb6">
<p local-id=3D"e0176973-0d50-409a-b85d-891c899d075f">TRS coupons</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"d028e473-9900-4214-8d4b-65179713e4cc">
<p local-id=3D"4186e50c-2725-44df-82c3-b80835959520">Layer thickness</p>
<ul local-id=3D"0552df7a-3075-4969-888b-acdc846b05f4">
<li local-id=3D"b0a07d74-dff3-4e6b-ae8c-dbad9eb99722">
<p local-id=3D"063fb05f-f2f5-4a21-853b-31fcb727b055">100 micron req=E2=80=
=99d</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5298b748-9bec-4bb3-9d6f-f9ce97a84ae3">
<p local-id=3D"e55cb986-7871-40b3-8afe-74d3972a10aa">Down to 30 micron want=
</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"36d7f4d0-6fbd-49ea-99a8-a3873933aaba">
<p local-id=3D"9ca54e46-af24-4da2-903e-88f434dab036">Powder volume without =
refilling</p>
<ul local-id=3D"bc87afbb-85fd-4697-aced-aca0be8ae691">
<li local-id=3D"7416d8c2-7f7a-4be7-a283-8bbc9c59c605">
<p local-id=3D"9e09e00c-c560-42ca-9997-8156ad4eb8ed">Refilling system want<=
/p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"28c542a6-d535-42b2-bd18-f34de89abc8f">
<p local-id=3D"7019d177-da59-48fd-93b8-5d4629aa7df3">Functional life</p>
<ul local-id=3D"2783f99e-a8f7-403c-8058-072e1f40e97f">
<li local-id=3D"5ce0a67d-a2a9-4c73-b4ef-3ebb0283a68c">
<p local-id=3D"a0bd7f2f-be8d-43d1-b8e9-883206bb6b00">Roller and hopper body=
 could wear over time</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"72d075f1-0794-424f-bfd8-80ae2034dcd2">End of Q3: HOPPER repl=
icated to all PILOTs and proposal developed for extrapolation to Saffrons</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"7f3ea6b5-603a-44c6-9237-7232f61e6931"></p>
<p local-id=3D"0a71ccae-e21c-4746-938a-acf51ef6f66b">PILOT: Project to make=
 2X updated PILOTs is tentatively going to start soon. Goal at this point i=
s to make 2X PILOTs with safety modifications for operation in Japan and de=
signed from the outset for HOPPER, laser, and micro drop systems. One is to=
 be dedicated to Copper and one is to be dedicated to Inconel. They also ne=
ed to be sealed. According to Marcus, Scott wants at least one of these pri=
nting with Cu by December.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2bccd6ef-e182-486e-8484-e3fab3f9bac4">REDRESS: I filled two =
molds with a batch of powder coated with the most successful recipe I have =
had so far, which is PMMA, TEG-DMA, and AIBN, and cured them overnight in t=
he standard cycle. This batch of powder had been dried in the oven overnigh=
t before grinding and sieving, and did not have Aerosil added. I also poure=
d and tapped some of the powder into a ceramic crucible, and after curing t=
he green part in the ceramic crucible had noticeable cracks, which I attrib=
ute to poor packing density. After removing them from the oven, I put a few=
 drops of TEG-DMA along the top of the parts to hold the top together (hist=
orically it tends to fragment more readily than the rest of the part). One =
of the molds was uncoated while the other had an internal coating of waterp=
roof binder. I immediately put the uncoated mold part in water to dissolve,=
 and it partially fragmented, although the parts that held together look go=
od. For the one with the coated mold, I put it in a fast heat cycle to heat=
 it to 275F at 500 F/hour along with a ceramic crucible filled with some of=
 the same batch of powder but with Aerosil added, and the green part in the=
 ceramic crucible was noticeably less cracked than the previous one. The gr=
een part in the coated mold was soft on the top, but I put it in the water =
wash tank to dissolve off the mold anyway. The coated mold green part compl=
etely fragmented during mold dissolution, which suggests to me that the bin=
der I used to coat the mold (which was a blend of random binder mixtures, i=
ncluding one with a photoinitiator) inhibited the proper curing of the powd=
er.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c53f0fe4-4c17-4f9c-8d93-9b6995113b81"></p>
<p local-id=3D"a5c52a57-b5ca-4573-8c9d-fc9f987db2c8">2025-05-22</p>
<p local-id=3D"4fb24ca9-8462-4c7c-88df-913b666693b0">ULTRA: Printed the dov=
etail machine side mount and 2X dovetail hopper/mist box mounts and install=
ed them. The mounting holes on the mist box were not centered like I though=
, so I had to install the dovetail mount with two of the M5 screws and supe=
rglue. Other than that, the mounts seem both adjustable, well aligned, and =
rigid, so Payman is currently testing them out on the ULTRA printer built o=
ut of the silver and blue gantry.</p>
<p local-id=3D"585900a2-8038-4383-9a2f-3ab483e15b31">PILOT: Designed a new =
mount for the laser diode module for the PILOT 3 that moves the laser diode=
 module as close to the nominal position of the spindle in Z and Y. Z is OK=
, but Y is still 5.25 mm off because of the larger dimensions of the laser =
diode module as compared with the spindle.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d76a60cd-e386-4848-9117-0fa2bf75673c">HOPPER: The HOPPER V4.=
0 benchtop is fully assembled other than the vibrator motor; since the moto=
rs I ordered from <a href=3D"http://Stepperonline.com" class=3D"external-li=
nk" rel=3D"nofollow">Stepperonline.com</a> are longer than the previous mot=
ors, there is not enough space to fit the vibrator motor mount. I will need=
 to order a motor from McMaster that is shorter, which is unfortunate becau=
se the cost is $100 but the motor is closer to the stepper tapper motor cur=
rently being used on PILOT 2, so there are advantages and disadvantages the=
re. I have modified the design of the gated HOPPER, incrementing from V3.3.=
5 to V3.3.6. The new design includes: gate stepper motor mount strengthened=
 and integrated into HOPPER print to increase strength and improve rigidity=
, adjusted position of steel guide strip and guide channels to reduce powde=
r wastage, added a non-structural 3D printed guide strip to further reduce =
powder wastage. I am printing it now on the Bambu printer from PLA-CF, whic=
h should have comparable print quality with improved material properties as=
 compared with the pure PLA design.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c68ca9f2-8bf6-44c2-9a2b-32c3467bd695">REDRESS: The green par=
t made with an uncoated mold is falling apart in dissolution, while the one=
 made with a coated mold is holding together but the powder did not fill th=
e mold well. The binder I used to coat the mold was quite thick because I m=
ixed it with the same acetone proportions that I typically use for making a=
 metal powder slurry, so I diluted it to a total volume of 350 mL where the=
 original volume was 150 mL. I then completely filled a 3D printed mold wit=
h this binder, poured it out, placed the mold upside down on a paper towel =
to let excess binder flow out, returned it to its original orientation, and=
 am now drying it in the FormLabs cure chamber for 15 minutes at a temperat=
ure of 40C. I plan to build up the layers of binder to a total of 3. These =
binder layers will add strength to the green part by helping to bind the ou=
tside of the green part where the mold contacts the powder, they will prote=
ct the green part while the mold is being dissolved, and if the binder laye=
r is thick enough this will also improve surface finish by filling in imper=
fections in the 3D printed mold. Since my latest batches of powder have bee=
n performing worse than previous ones, I am looking back through older reci=
pes and changes I have made. The recipe I have that I believe worked the be=
st so far is a batch with 3% binder load, with 26.4g PMMA-EA, 4g TEG-DMA, a=
nd 1g AIBN, dried in a pie tin overnight on the hot plate set to 40C withou=
t stirring the cake. I am also using untreated Sandvik powder for this new =
batch.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b54b7d57-1ee1-410f-b7b5-2a943c00327b"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1b51d615-8e7a-4bb1-ae69-2f4461e6f82f">2025-05-23</p>
<p local-id=3D"0acd2041-e206-4533-af64-f786b2db706d">HOPPER: Finished assem=
bling the benchtop HOPPER V4.0 and gave it to Ben to install in PILOT 2. It=
 uses a keyed steel shaft with a 3D printed roller to spread out tapping fo=
rce. It also uses a 3D printed timing belt pulley to reduce the width of th=
e HOPPER assembly. I tried to print a new design of stepper tapper impact a=
rm that is prevented from rotating fully by being lengthened to the point t=
hat it stops against one of the dovetail mounts. I also</p>
<p local-id=3D"06899565-c848-4430-9b43-44512c92c871">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting=
:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"ba0cd970-b9e5-41a6-8f61-a85eff30f71c">
<li local-id=3D"c675f71e-862a-48f7-96e0-a8777e9dfc48">
<p local-id=3D"385bf38c-9095-4a5a-b347-111d9c1bc24a">Doser hopper worked wi=
th non-flowable powder, but the powder did not spread well. Possible but ch=
allenging to spread on sprayed glass, but not possible to spread on a bound=
 layer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"c155226c-d69a-4714-be02-5c70e03c4373"></p>
<p local-id=3D"e4e462a3-0158-4333-8152-9baad67d2559">To Do Next Week:</p>
