<p local-id=3D"e168f2d1-2afc-440c-9b54-416ebe45d1ea"></p>
<p local-id=3D"a1c7c726-6f13-4e8d-8da6-75d51fa624d0"></p>
<p local-id=3D"d046f4a7-9b02-407a-a9ae-894305093b4e">2025-05-27</p>
<p local-id=3D"221b35a1-cdc1-4f1e-9415-92fede262cb3">HOPPER: Working on des=
ign of V3.3.7 gated hopper to fit on PILOT 2. I am making a new body model =
from scratch because the V3.3.6 model had been modified so many times that =
it had many unnecessary features in the feature tree that made it difficult=
 to change the design as necessary. The design of V3.3.7 is complete, and I=
 am running the print overnight</p>
<p local-id=3D"fdc800c4-bf18-4a1a-a187-451527c70417">PILOT/NEXTGEN: I desig=
ned a vacuum connection part for the laser diode module on PILOT 3, and it =
is currently printing from Clear 4.1 resin on the Formlabs. The clear resin=
 is stiff and prints and cleans well, but is brittle. I am printing two, so=
 if one breaks there is a spare that can be used until a stronger part is p=
rinted. Wrote up the recommendations from the Epson engineers about upgrade=
s to the PILOT printers while they were here, as well as some upgrades I th=
ought up.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9f3ca225-d8c5-40f8-9e33-c7d698adb9fb">REDRESS: I filled a mo=
ld that had been precoated with 3 layers of my typical V14 binder with powd=
er coated with the same binder and cooked it overnight with the standard cy=
cle. I also filled a ceramic crucible with copper powder I had gotten from =
Nick a few months ago and put it in the upper Keith furnace running the For=
mLabs resin burnout cycle; I want to try filling some FormLabs Clear Cast m=
olds with uncoated copper and the latest batches of coated 17-4 powder; thi=
s would eliminate the issues I have been having with dissolving off molds b=
ecause the FormLabs molds can be thermally decomposed.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2c185575-912b-4901-9fb2-420d0712045b"></p>
<p local-id=3D"00921710-2fca-41a9-a898-7dc765318b42">2025-05-28</p>
<p local-id=3D"109a9c81-a1df-4b9e-a591-2ce667a1f3b0">HOPPER: Waiting for th=
e print of the PILOT-compatible HOPPER V3.3.7 parts to finish on the Bambu =
printer. Parts are finished printing and ready for post-processing and asse=
mbly, but there are parts missing that I planned to scavenge from the V3.3.=
5 HOPPER on the blue and silver gantry that Payman is using on the V3.3.6 H=
OPPER (that I assembled today) so I will need to buy new bearings etc. for =
the V3.3.7 HOPPER.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8dd4fea3-cc77-4f10-ab58-a56dce95a367">PILOT: The laser diode=
 module mount on PILOT 3 hits the Z stage limit switch mount, so Mohsen Dre=
meled the one on the printer, and I modified the CAD and am printing a new =
one. The laser diode module SVP was printed overnight, so I ran it through =
the IPA wash cycle and cured it, then Mohsen removed the supports and insta=
lled it on the laser diode module in the printer. It appears to work, altho=
ugh sparks are visible traveling through the SVP while it is operating, lea=
ding to concerns about erosion of the SVP over time and risk of fire. At so=
me point it would be a good idea to reprint the SVP from high-temperature S=
LA resin. I would also like to change the flow path to a tangential outlet =
for more even flow and expand the inlet holes for greater flow.</p>
<p local-id=3D"646e9053-53db-4981-997b-92014cc9ee6b">REDRESS: The latest gr=
een part with the coated mold fell apart during mold dissolution. I am prin=
ting two new molds from FormLabs Clear Cast resin to try a process that doe=
s not require dissolving a mold with water. I tried making another green pa=
rt in a water soluble mold by vibrating it while I filled it with powder, t=
hen heating it in a fast heat cycle to 275F, letting it dwell for 30 minute=
s, then pulling immediately placing it in the water dissolution tank. It al=
so fell apart.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1138ae80-2835-41e4-b80e-0570dd534032"></p>
