<p local-id=3D"7140e583-2d06-4694-bc40-efedf5691af0">PILOT: Continuous tapp=
ing works on PILOT 2. It seems that the roller axis was moving in the negat=
ive direction, and the negative limit of the roller axis was set to -100 mm=
, so once it hit that limit it would stop rotating.</p>
<p local-id=3D"40cc79f0-1dcf-435d-b996-ea800b8ec476">HOPPER: Finished assem=
bling gated HOPPER V3.3.7. I asked Mohsen to try and run a test print with =
the doser-style hopper tonight now that continuous dispense is working, but=
 he may not have time to do that because he also has to document some of hi=
s laser experiments from this week. Payman has been pushing to switch from =
the doser-style hopper to the gated hopper in PILOT 2, so my plan is to swi=
tch them out tomorrow morning, but once that has been done I suspect that w=
e will not be reverting to the doser-style hopper anytime soon.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2c800708-12be-42a8-bb40-3f6f67480dc7">REDRESS: I post-proces=
sed some FormLabs Clear Cast resin molds and filled one with V14 coated 17-=
4 and one with copper (I think Ultrafine, but I=E2=80=99m not sure). I also=
 did some research on AIBN, and it=E2=80=99s possible that I have been over=
heating the powder when I thermally cure it; the typical decomposition temp=
erature of AIBN is 80C or so. It has a half life of ~80 hours at 50C, 7 hou=
rs at 70C, and 9 minutes at 100C, while I have been curing the molds up to =
135C (275F). I filled up a regular water-soluble mold with V14 17-4 powder =
and cured it to 80C (176 F) with a dwell of 1 hour; immediately after the d=
well I pulled it out and the powder was somewhat cured but still quite soft=
 and powdery. Claude=E2=80=99s suggestion was 2-3 hours at 80C, and looking=
 back at the numbers now I think a more appropriate time would indeed be ~3=
 hours at 80C.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7b4d94c5-e319-49d0-bbc8-eceef485a42d"></p>
<p local-id=3D"5f357b46-e8e3-4a3d-a05d-c6cc2648cc23">2025-05-30</p>
<p local-id=3D"22e20e08-b81a-459e-b08d-5b03814f0649">HOPPER: Mohsen ran a T=
RS coupon print last night with the doser-style hopper V4.0 on PILOT 2, and=
 is going to try running it with non-flowable powder this morning. The gate=
d HOPPER V3.3.7 is ready to be installed as soon as testing of the V4.0 HOP=
PER has been tested.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b06f9fed-d0ed-4713-bfb9-6d115f7e4ca9">REDRESS: The green par=
t water-soluble mold that was run at a lower temperature in the lower Keith=
 furnace was still not bound completely, so I am running it through another=
 cycle with a 1 hour dwell at 200F (93C, ~20 min half life) to try and comp=
lete crosslinking without burning off the AIBN. I am also experimenting wit=
h using TEG-DMA as a single-component binder. Historically I had good resul=
ts with using a 10% binder load of pure liquid TEG-DMA with no added solven=
t to make a slurry; the green parts were completely waterproof and extremel=
y strong, but also completely solid and so would be difficult to debind. I =
am trying something different today where I use a 3% TEG-DMA binder load bu=
t with 150 mL of added acetone blended with the TEG-DMA before making the p=
owder slurry cake. There are two approaches I am trying with this slurry: o=
ne is to pour it directly into a water soluble mold, while the other is to =
dry the slurry and try to use the cake to make pourable powder. One thing o=
f note is that the powder is not held in suspension with TEG-DMA blended wi=
th acetone; the powder particles settle out in the water-soluble mold. This=
 has the disadvantage of the top of the green part being lower than the top=
 of the mold, but it may prevent the issue I have seen previously of part s=
hrinkage causing the green part to fracture as the solvent vaporizes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8034c340-e1fc-4cb1-b718-74a39a168854">R&amp;D Meeting:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c939018d-ddf7-4dc2-86ab-f16b7aa67a52">
<li local-id=3D"eeca33c6-355e-433f-9494-790e02e7f2b0">
<p local-id=3D"cbcd24fc-4989-49d9-87d1-bd50ed2d38a2">Abandoning doser-style=
 hopper for time being in favor of gated-style hopper</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ec58190f-5a9b-432c-9598-c65fa2e04739">
<p local-id=3D"a922e375-af6a-4f2d-aac4-bddb0011025c">Ignoring overflow for =
time being</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"036b8232-5642-4269-afcf-39a2c943099d"></p>
<p local-id=3D"97bc0554-f696-4eed-af54-4fc5bf150556">To do next week:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3a7f1232-a567-43e3-884a-37f88147b293">
<li local-id=3D"42870b42-9b5a-4bbe-ae3e-40b9a5e5896d">
<p local-id=3D"75a0d6b8-39ee-4fdd-85d5-cdf30d462f30">Install gated-style HO=
PPER V3.3.7 in PILOT 2</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7af71f11-720f-4363-a6d0-addf99bab116">
<p local-id=3D"08ef39be-89a5-4dce-a77e-97cb12887ecf">Work on reducing powde=
r wastage further with V3.3.8</p>
<ul local-id=3D"51d2965e-b559-4690-9dc5-57ec1c07b1eb">
<li local-id=3D"e7a26f7a-c083-47c4-b963-51cc9122d12a">
<p local-id=3D"a0707c2f-62a9-4689-a48c-4a1273e4c980">Linear driven wedge</p=
>
<ul local-id=3D"dc727b7d-ed8e-46a3-9583-960e9271fdb8">
<li local-id=3D"3fb2b420-2ace-4e11-a277-ea53bae874f5">
<p local-id=3D"a391f2e8-bb9b-4e17-887e-24526a5fcf4a">Will need linear guide=
s and sufficient force to lift all powder in HOPPER</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"f069b446-1b47-46c5-865d-7fc1cbabd346">
<p local-id=3D"069da47a-919a-4e2f-b0de-43a3d6c34a35"></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"80035b09-430b-476f-a1a6-e3116aaf74c3"></p>
<p local-id=3D"7082017c-acb4-4b25-a38e-2d68472d2fc3">2025-06-02</p>
<p local-id=3D"aa7cee6c-3e73-48f6-a7f4-ef1e57a12bd6">HOPPER: Redesigned mou=
nts for HOPPER V3.3.7.2 (gated HOPPER designed to be smaller than previous =
version so that it fits in the PILOT printer better). The new mounts enable=
 the HOPPER to be adjusted using the Edmund Optics X axis lead screw drives=
 that we have a bunch of around, previously used for manual adjustment of s=
pindles in the Beta machines: <a href=3D"https://www.edmundoptics.com/p/sma=
ll-x-axis-leadscrew-drive/11767/?srsltid=3DAfmBOoryJPdkpyVvvN1iGDV3bU26lyMM=
bUz7qOLgMmHSB7j4N8H3ThlU" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://=
www.edmundoptics.com/p/small-x-axis-leadscrew-drive/11767/?srsltid=3DAfmBOo=
ryJPdkpyVvvN1iGDV3bU26lyMMbUz7qOLgMmHSB7j4N8H3ThlU</a> .</p>
<p local-id=3D"feaa58c4-f054-4fc5-9123-a36b36c7f2fd">Designed and printed a=
 new machine-side dovetail mount plate with a dovetail added 90mm to the le=
ft of the current mist box dovetail</p>
<p local-id=3D"8424283e-9852-46ff-871f-eea5d7d3536a">Beginning design of HO=
PPER V3.4.0, the latest version of the gated HOPPER, that in theory will ha=
ve near-zero waste.</p>
<p local-id=3D"42104355-003b-4a28-bb48-28fdef87c253">REDRESS: I am working =
on a new binder formulation that uses Benzoyl Peroxide as the thermal initi=
ator instead of AIBN. AIBN has a much shorter half life, leading to faster =
decomposition at curing temperatures, but possibly more critically it may d=
ecompose over time at room temperature. It really should be stored in a ref=
rigerator, but I have kept it stored at room temperature, which may have le=
ad to my inability to recreate earlier results. It also has a very short ha=
lf life at the curing temperatures I have been using, which could mean that=
 it decomposes before it has a chance to fully crosslink the binder. My ins=
tinct, though, is that it has been degrading in storage over the several mo=
nths that I have had it and that is at least one of the factors leading to =
my recent poor green part quality.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-fi=
le-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=
=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"image-20250602-194543.pn=
g" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"bbe2dc5dfc690a6523707302100cde33e2=
522e44863d1428f40f934e271e2925" data-image-src=3D"https://3deo.atlassian.ne=
t/wiki/download/attachments/867500072/image-20250602-194543.png?version=3D1=
&amp;modificationDate=3D1748893547622&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" da=
ta-height=3D"456" data-width=3D"821" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" da=
ta-linked-resource-id=3D"962166787" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data=
-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"=
image-20250602-194543.png" data-base-url=3D"https://3deo.atlassian.net/wiki=
" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-cont=
