<ul local-id=3D"691e1821-e15f-4296-b6e9-a0664dc8e64c">
<li local-id=3D"4d507f77-e407-46b2-b2d5-feb18d796a0a">
<p local-id=3D"2e53a4ee-8fb3-4453-a2b7-e3346808c336">Localized curing of bi=
nder</p>
<ul local-id=3D"f93c8bf4-a797-4133-89fa-1c6e7202e365">
<li local-id=3D"bdcf9dee-977e-4445-b97f-51deec5e9a50">
<p local-id=3D"a2819f11-279f-4995-aacd-5a409ba44df2">Powder pre-coated with=
 binder (photosensitive or thermally cured)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a908ed15-cb7f-479b-9afd-b131fc1970c0">
<p local-id=3D"3cda4403-eb39-45ea-a5b3-d4d68714dac6">Photosensitive sprayed=
 binder</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"95ec34c6-6827-47ec-8d2c-98b45c170024">
<p local-id=3D"7faf40a1-91f5-41ce-b9f8-3780ca95966d">Pre-sintering of part =
to increase green strength, dimensional accuracy, and control warpage durin=
g sintering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"774b2c83-0de1-493a-911e-259b963a28c2">
<p local-id=3D"486c5a7d-49f0-4e7c-a39d-e7b2bb3b0feb">Selective oxidation of=
 regions of parts</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5e07783f-30ff-4f90-82c6-c8f79463790d">
<p local-id=3D"ead5955e-98c5-403d-acff-767a8b7d922b">Controlled porosity at=
 different regions of parts</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d006afaf-78fa-463b-9f79-73b8308219cb">
<p local-id=3D"594d9fd4-59f3-4c47-865d-9cf5a597fa30">Laser sintering or mel=
ting combined with binder jetting</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"cc833f1c-e130-4461-b74c-98796e15902f">Biweekly cleanup</p>
<p local-id=3D"2b1d0c4b-22d8-46e4-9ae4-e03df4e70359">REDRESS: I finished dr=
ying and ground and sieved a batch of V15 coated powder and loaded some int=
o a low-temperature water-soluble 3D printed mold, then put it in a thermal=
 curing cycle that heats it to 250F and dwells there for 7 hours. This is b=
ased on Claude=E2=80=99s graph, which suggests that at 120C the half life o=
f Benzoyl Peroxide is 7.7 hours. Considering the time to ramp up to peak an=
d time to cool back down to room temperature, a dwell of 7 hours at that te=
mperature should roughly decompose all the Benzoyl Peroxide. However, the c=
hart from Sigma Aldrich suggests that the decomposition half life of Benzoy=
l Peroxide is ~30 minutes at 100C, and so is presumably shorter at higher t=
emperatures, so a dwell that long would be inappropriate if that chart is c=
orrect.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3a3685c7-a88e-4c4b-be91-c9de968ee29e"></p>
<p local-id=3D"3fc65636-3dbf-4bc2-b5ea-33e7d3efc521">2025-06-04</p>
<p local-id=3D"d71cfe16-518f-4bee-a9c3-15cfc2519c9e">HOPPER: The gated HOPP=
ER V3.3.7.2 is functional and installed in PILOT 2. The pulley printed from=
 FormLabs clear resin on the keyed shaft shattered, so I replaced it with a=
n aluminum pulley. I also wrote some macros to open and close the gate, alt=
hough there is no mechanical feature preventing the gate from opening too f=
ar, which is a pain because the stainless steel sheet needs to be carefully=
 threaded back into its guides. The hopper is not operating on PILOT 2, and=
 seems to be able to successfully spread layers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eacf5cce-ca5f-414c-a2a2-794126c72ee2">REDRESS: The most rece=
nt test was unsuccessful; the part broke apart during mold dissolution. I a=
m considering moving back to using PVP-VA coated powder and adding a chemic=
al to waterproof it before dissolving off the mold.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9df1bbb4-95c0-41a7-926a-9eee05878684">PILOT:</p>
<p local-id=3D"ba8ae272-2e52-4820-9bbf-b50abd7c506b">Meeting with Manjun to=
 discuss PILOT BOM.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"d5e58975-921a-44c9-a28c-8574fbdc76ff">
<li local-id=3D"9aa17a41-8fad-4428-9057-ff99fa11109e">
<p local-id=3D"7433c99b-d83c-4ac5-ac36-5a9dbdcdc7bd">Quote for extrusion le=
ngths from Vention</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a7632b2a-916e-40ce-bc7f-a400a46c7f48">
<p local-id=3D"97352b3a-0cd6-4431-98f3-8b2b233b1d44">List of 3D printed par=
ts</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"ae77770f-0757-4d8a-b060-19a5a0cf0ba1">
<p local-id=3D"798c7f16-c371-41c9-aedd-084dd4d88837">STEP file to Manjun</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e82a4119-e3b3-4091-a69a-838f3d3821b9"></p>
<p local-id=3D"8d8b0419-463c-48b8-8af8-0606f431cb92">2025-06-05</p>
<p local-id=3D"ae0b749b-da84-4139-af51-61740de63f51">HOPPER: Gated hopper b=
eing tested in PILOT 2 by Mohsen. Continuing work on design of zero-waste g=
ated hopper.</p>
<p local-id=3D"44607c92-b3a2-4062-8f5a-a49df3821df6">Slicer Meeting: 1 hour=
 40 minute meeting on features for the slicer ZZ is currently developing. T=
he meeting was mostly very low-level focused on specific instances and part=
 features that have caused issues in the past. From a high level, the slice=
r ZZ is developing is not based on a commercial 3DP slicer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c4bab61a-6815-4e0c-8cf5-9be67e3c5e63">PILOT:</p>
<p local-id=3D"5e39f3c9-ec65-4c9e-b23c-1b35ff1e3f75">PRD Meeting</p>
