<p local-id=3D"d23ee7e7-e7b2-40dc-9ee6-d8f02616cf1b">Build plate and tank s=
ize 5.5=E2=80=9DX5.5=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d9fd5f95-ad3c-4257-8a2a-7911320cd552">
<p local-id=3D"ba43de44-0c6a-416e-b7e4-1bf7819ab7e4">3/8=E2=80=9D bridge be=
tween powder and build tanks</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"89b634e6-8540-4797-a479-bd01d3c1d0b9">
<p local-id=3D"cd89a250-89b8-4b7e-9d9e-58053d2081b8">5.5*2+.375=3D11.375, r=
ound up to 12=E2=80=9D for powder/build module</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9ee5add3-a5c8-495a-95d6-55852cfe395b">
<p local-id=3D"86532177-f9ec-49f2-bf71-46c101051abd">Nordson Asymptek (larg=
est component protruding from X axis): 4.5=E2=80=9D</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9c8287d8-02c9-4dd9-ba83-3d3d091f2a1f">
<p local-id=3D"eca2b455-10ea-4a87-bbf8-a80666fbabec">X axis length in Y dir=
ection with mount:</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"18cee9e4-7646-43b9-8c64-38c881bb55a5"></p>
<p local-id=3D"5364373f-e156-481d-bc87-654e1f9cc970">PILOT: Working on esti=
mating the Y axis gantry travel required for the worst case of the Epson PI=
LOT printer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"95d56f1f-e22f-40c1-b764-71f5cea96afe">HOPPER: Installed a li=
mit switch on the hopper on PILOT 2, but I don=E2=80=99t like how the desig=
n came out. Because the gate holder is able to shift along the keyed shaft,=
 and because of how I oriented the limit switch, it would be possible for i=
t to trip at different points depending on how the shaft shifts. I will red=
esign it so that it reliably trips in the same gate holder position and pri=
nt a new mount tonight.</p>
<p local-id=3D"62c57059-e77d-4596-aaa9-e230e1089f59">REDRESS: I am dissolvi=
ng some ParaPlast paraffin in some N-Heptane to test whether they are compa=
tible for cleaning the MicroDrop unit that Pourya is working on that has be=
come clogged, and also to use as a possible waterproofing agent for green p=
arts produced using the REDRESS process. I received a new roll of AquaSys 1=
20 filament (the higher temperature water-soluble filament) and filled it w=
ith some V15 powder that I am now cooking in the upper Keith furnace with a=
 30 minute dwell at a peak temperature of 275F.</p>
<p local-id=3D"07646ef8-8f19-46e2-8b33-a298da438b90">NEXTGEN: I made an alu=
minum plate with holes drilled in it to be used as a mount for the Nordson =
Asymtek head on PILOT 1. I have concerns about the extra torque being appli=
ed to the X axis stage because the Nordson Asymtek head is about a 1 K, whi=
ch is applied cantilevered about 75mm away from the stage, but it remains t=
o be tested whether that is indeed an issue. I am also working on a documen=
t summarizing various available laser types: <a href=3D"https://3deo.atlass=
ian.net/wiki/pages/resumedraft.action?draftId=3D966983683&amp;draftShareId=
=3Debf5b9ac-c5a3-4585-b95a-b93097dfe908" local-id=3D"52186646-b5c7-48ff-80b=
9-e58ad271c576" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" rel=3D"nofollow">https://3d=
eo.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/resumedraft.action?draftId=3D966983683&amp;draf=
tShareId=3Debf5b9ac-c5a3-4585-b95a-b93097dfe908</a> .</p>
<p local-id=3D"d3605c7d-1fa7-4cb2-9f9c-6ed5929c5d3e"></p>
<p local-id=3D"6697912c-210c-4996-8efe-5f06a7e0b0a1">2025-06-10</p>
<p local-id=3D"aba7dc66-b822-4ead-9fcb-f5cbc25d1c7e">NEXTGEN/PILOT: The alu=
minum mount I made yesterday works, but because the Nordson Asymtek dispens=
ing head is mounted to the side of the spindle it takes up enough space tha=
t the spindle and dispensing head cannot address the same area of the bed. =
I am pursuing two approaches to resolve this: one is printing a new spindle=
 mount that is mirrored from the original and so has the vacuum line attach=
ment point on the side of the spindle mount opposite from the dispensing he=
ad, and the other is to make a longer aluminum mount that places the dispen=
sing head in front of the spindle.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8a259eaa-0f6a-4bde-92f1-6fb5935048e7">I am working to dissol=
ve 15g of PE-CVA in 100g of ParaPlast paraffin. I have them on the heated m=
ixer plate set to 80C and 800 RPM mixing speed. The paraffin melted in a fe=
w hours, but the PE-CVA is taking a while to dissolve. Historically I have =
seen that it first swells as it absorbs the paraffin and eventually dissolv=
es, but the process will likely take overnight.</p>
<p local-id=3D"88b6a1e6-3a84-42b8-a174-9d8c1ca3bb04">HOPPER: Test fit the v=
arious limit switch mounts printed last night. It seemed that the limit swi=
tch would be triggered before the gate is fully open, so I printed 3 more l=
imit switch mounts with the limit switches mounted at different distances f=
rom the gate holder in 1mm increments. The middle one seemed like it would =
work OK, so I installed it and placed the hopper on the blue and silver gan=
try that Payman has been using for testing gated hoppers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"cee8ae16-7e83-4bc2-9c81-3a3127d55e69">REDRESS: I treated a g=
reen part with paraffin dissolved in N-Heptane and let it dry overnight, th=
en tried to dissolve off the mold and it completely fell apart. When I put =
several drops of the N-Heptane/paraffin solution on a surface and let it dr=
y out for a few minutes, the solution did not seem to reconstitute into pur=
e paraffin. It is possible that a thin layer of paraffin is formed on the s=
urface of the drops when the surface solvent evaporates, and this thin laye=
r prevents further evaporation of the solvent.</p>
<p local-id=3D"56f26268-8fbe-48fc-9746-b9e9d79f6b8e"></p>
<p local-id=3D"235dd6c1-f9eb-46e0-b84e-464c1c19a40b">2025-06-11</p>
<p local-id=3D"033b0cd5-5040-4b5b-abe9-621f7c66bea6">NEXTGEN: The PE-CVA pe=
llets have swollen more overnight, but they have not dissolved completely, =
so I increased the temperature to 90C. The extended aluminum mount I made y=
esterday for the Nordson Asymtek head on PILOT 1 seems to be usable, but I =
am still working on a print of a mirrored spindle holder. It printed last n=
ight mostly successfully, although there are cured resin fragments in the t=
ank that suggest it is not printing perfectly. I have seen this happen befo=
re when the slide and leadscrew of the Formlabs printer are not properly gr=
eased, so at some point I will grease those components and clean out the To=
ugh 1500 tank.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fb56ae3e-d35e-445e-9cfc-2556592f64bb">HOPPER: The print of t=
he HOPPER V3.4.0 (zero waste gated style) body failed last night, but the m=
iscellaneous greebles did print successfully. HOPPER V3.3.7.2 is currently =
being tested on PILOT 2 by Payman.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bd307e34-7715-40f4-a925-a3a6f362ed0b">REDRESS: The water-sol=
uble mold filled with TEG-DMA slurry bulged outward during the curing cycle=
 last night, despite the peak temperature being set to 250F. I filled a wat=
er-soluble mold and a ceramic crucible with powder coated with PMMA and TEG=
-DMA without a free radical initiator, and the green part formed in the cru=
cible seems fairly waterproof. When the green part is first immersed in wat=
er you can see that bubbles come out of the green part all over it, so clea=
rly water is able to flow into the interstitial spaces between bound partic=
les, but the part still holds its shape. I have a theory that one of the ca=
uses of the part formed in a water-soluble mold breaking apart is that it a=
bsorbs water and swells, but because the water-soluble mold prevents it fro=
m swelling outward, the swelling force causes the part to fragment. I cut t=
he bottom off the water-soluble mold that I made last night with powder coa=
ted in PMMA/TEG-DMA and soaked the bottom with PVP-VA binder and the part s=
tarted to break apart. I also soaked the top 1 cm of the part with paraffin=
 with PE-CVA</p>
<p local-id=3D"aed04082-81eb-4a5c-8ad0-f93a7736db1c">PILOT PRD Meeting:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"480d4a29-73b4-455c-b2b1-811a25805ecb">
<li local-id=3D"c97040b0-a6c5-415f-ad80-d26c4f0351e8">
<p local-id=3D"943ca6bc-89da-4412-9753-8151180a94f1">Options are to replica=
te current PILOTs with minimal electrical upgrades, or to take longer and d=
o the same changes with additional upgrades for beautifying and enabling fu=
ture upgrades (laser, wax, etc.).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"649e8d4a-4aa2-415b-8df2-916ed8c98dc5">
<p local-id=3D"fbdba805-5ca0-45cd-ad94-c003a14c5bb5">Still waiting on respo=
nse from Trak; seems unlikely that they are interested in this project</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"a8acdedf-068b-4975-8aa4-cd739d8cbc7d">
<p local-id=3D"40c18c40-3a7d-40a3-83ca-464b80639b0e"><strong>To Do: Spec ou=
t and price a stage for Y axis 48=E2=80=9D stroke and X axis 18=E2=80=9D st=
roke</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"fe0911dc-317d-4226-a32b-bd865d89309c">
<li local-id=3D"430333fa-cecf-496e-b08e-0782e2fe0a1a">
<p local-id=3D"d2e7eac2-3eb3-4bd5-8323-d24f30763638"><a href=3D"https://www=
.tolomatic.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/3600-4222_08_TRS_cat-1.pdf" class=
=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.tolomatic.com/wp-content/up=
loads/2022/05/3600-4222_08_TRS_cat-1.pdf</a></p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"4fae368c-7ccc-4240-8d1f-cc06cc1c8345"></p>
<p local-id=3D"74540a34-f086-429a-8be5-503bfe4a9eca">2025-06-12</p>
<p local-id=3D"42c0dabe-1814-496b-ba1a-9f3d9577c066">NEXTGEN: Gave a mist b=
ox catch for the ULTRA Mist Box V2 to Payman, and redesigned and reprinted =
it based on his experience with it. Gave a hopper side dovetail mount print=
ed last night to Payman. Entered an order for two types of polymer for incr=
easing wax viscosity: <a href=3D"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product=
/ambeedinc/ambh9a9ac98a?context=3Dbbe" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofol=
low">https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/ambeedinc/ambh9a9ac98a?cont=
ext=3Dbbe</a> (Ethylene-vinyl acetate copolymer) and <a href=3D"https://www=
.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/437247" class=3D"external-link" rel=
=3D"nofollow">https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/437247</a>=
 (Poly(ethylene-co-vinyl acetate)). The second polymer is one that I have d=
issolved in paraffin previously in order to reduce shrinkage and act as a b=
inder when the wax is melted out for the REDRESS process.</p>
<p local-id=3D"92b272b7-fd4e-46c0-8bfd-c22b884c3cf6">HOPPER: Printed out th=
e body of the zero-waste free-flow hopper, but I noticed that the motor mou=
nts will interfere with the Y axis stages so I will need to redesign and re=
print the body.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ca8c7af8-1f52-4b1d-aae5-8d981bcd33ef"></p>
<p local-id=3D"9ab6ba19-b5f4-4afd-a3d4-560fbaadec6b">2025-06-13</p>
<p local-id=3D"077c1b06-905c-4a58-89ad-180060efe241">HOPPER: In process of =
redesigning zero-waste hopper body to enable it to fit within the PILOT pri=
nter.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0a2d5d91-5735-4327-b5d8-7f0d770b0ff5">REDRESS: In process of=
 melting paraffin/PE-CVA wax out of a vacuum-impregnated green part. Vacuum=
 impregnated another green part (binder V15) with hard microcrystalline wax=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"973d8061-281f-4923-bf77-a9a58ff4ea88">NEXTGEN: In process of=
 mixing a wax formulation that is 95% hard microcrystalline wax and 5% PE-C=
VA to make a higher viscosity wax for the Nordson Asymtek dispensing head. =
The wax formulation completed mixing and I poured it into a pie tin to cool=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eb6b4e14-79a5-4fc8-a2c2-03560af20019">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting=
:</p>
<p local-id=3D"5de83c0b-62a5-402e-bb54-6815a1d8000d"><strong>To Do Next Wee=
k:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"177d76be-6118-4cf8-ae9c-d30ccba6bb84">
<li local-id=3D"57ac8355-a376-411b-a553-897700f8d01b">
<p local-id=3D"2a40030a-64ac-420d-8429-94009abc0a6a"><strong>Integrate tank=
-to-tank spreader bar into free flow hopper and increase opening</strong></=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f202f7fd-07b5-459a-8cec-42e9ebc97eaa">
<p local-id=3D"42220f56-e2e7-4312-8ae2-cac1f452ca5a"><strong>Print another =
SVP</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e8332491-8b72-4eed-b0c9-fe53ea576603">
<p local-id=3D"22a6d753-778d-477c-98c7-3df97f0eb398"><strong>New LVP</stron=
g></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d2a83342-4d15-4947-8eac-bdb73fe9e50a"></p>
<ul local-id=3D"5550ea37-d552-4e6e-b4b6-7e217b316a7d">
<li local-id=3D"7d86e489-26a7-421d-a864-cb3d328a35ae">
<p local-id=3D"ca731cea-161e-42d4-ac83-2b428284c0b4">Free flow hopper gave =
better density uniformity of TRS bars as compared with line dispense of dos=
er-style hopper, but lower density than the tank-to-tank system (~57 vs ~51=
).</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"b170d5dc-21ec-4c54-ad9b-9e10be8a0189"></p>
<p local-id=3D"d87289cb-a0b6-4d27-b3f8-bf6add3169ed">2025-06-16</p>
<p local-id=3D"e74b9703-38b0-4555-8a01-b96d10714fd9">NEXTGEN: Mixing up a n=
ew batch of 95% hard microcrystalline wax / 5% PE-CVA in a (loosely) closed=
 jar for Pourya to test. The batch I made previously seemed to have some vi=
sible FOD in it, so this one will hopefully have less contamination because=
 it is sealed. At the same time, Pourya is trying to filter out the contami=
nated batch using some 5 micron syringe filters from McMaster.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ebd7f8d5-37d1-4b55-92ae-f373df4d7cd2">REDRESS: I have a tota=
l of 5 green parts I am running through a modified furnace cycle to melt ou=
t the wax; there are four nozzles with one partial nozzle tip. The new furn=
ace cycle goes to a peak temperature of 300F in several stages with 2 hour =
dwells at each stage. I believe the three temperatures are 198, 250, 300. T=
hey were made using various binders and different waxes, but look fairly eq=
uivalent. I am also making a new batch of V15 coated powder to compare with=
 the V15 batch I have been using.</p>
<p local-id=3D"90dcb356-b470-40b1-b767-61b7239b3522">HOPPER: Mainly working=
 on the new hopper design (V3.5.0) that uses the same spreader bar as the P=
ILOT printers. The design intent is to have a hopper that is as similar to =
V3.3.7.2 as possible, with the only difference being the larger spreader ba=
r. Also continuing to work on the zero-waste free flow hopper (V3.4.0).</p>
<p local-id=3D"3aa73ea6-7092-4e0a-9758-1004e847a1cc">PXL: In the process of=
 thermal interference fitting copper parts to stainless steel bases in prep=
aration for electron beam welding tomorrow. There are three geometries, so =
I assembled one of each geometry without processing the parts other than th=
e acetone cleaning last week, and I plan to assemble one of each geometry w=
ith copper parts that have been acid descaled. Supposedly surface oxides in=
hibit electron beam welding, so I will quickly assemble the parts and vacuu=
m seal them in nitrogen with a desiccant packet to preserve them for testin=
g tomorrow.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3352c930-c892-4082-95b2-80e8e92e41a6"></p>
<p local-id=3D"69f589b8-0308-4b33-974b-6c7c3013a14d">2025-06-17</p>
<p local-id=3D"434365bb-f0e9-49d2-b99a-7516de43d1ee">PXL: Went to Electron =
Beam Engineering in Anaheim with Marcus to run test EBW welds on some PXL t=
hermal interference fit parts. There were chronic issues with weld cracking=
. The cracks were small enough that they were not visible to the naked eye =
or on pictures taken up close with a phone, but they were detectable with t=
he helium leak test used at EBE. The cracks were also highly localized, gen=
erally no more than 5mm in length along a weld that is a total of ~80mm. Th=
ere was one unit that was completely sealed, so the process can work, but i=
t may take some part modifications to make the process more robust. The wel=
ds completed on the lift pin holes where the copper was ~1mm higher than th=
e level of the stainless steel, however, came out well. This suggests that =
it may be possible to make copper parts that are 1mm higher than the stainl=
ess steel and form welds robustly. Because copper is so much more thermally=
 conductive than stainless steel, it is necessary to direct most of the hea=
t into the copper, but because of the thin copper flange there is a tendenc=
y for the weld to melt through the flange. With a thicker copper part, it i=
s possible to melt the copper and roll down the edge to the stainless steel=
, where the heat from the copper is conducted into the stainless steel, mel=
ting it, and joining the two parts.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a92e3a27-6e3c-4cf4-96f0-4ad704eb0bbd">REDRESS: Filled a mold=
 with V15 powder and cured it overnight.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7f4a5b74-4785-4310-972b-10a21c43a6a2"></p>
<p local-id=3D"3b7dfe9f-595f-4380-a206-a1e81a4dd34e">2025-06-18</p>
<p local-id=3D"1f708e28-a27f-4e39-a241-0261a0f324ec">HOPPER: Worked on asse=
mbling hoppers V3.4.0 and V3.5.0. Noted that the side mounts are shallow en=
ough that the M3 screws protrude too far into the carriage of the Edmund Op=
tics adjusting stages, causing them to lock up. I redesigned the mounts and=
 will print new ones.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f17f2468-6bd6-4ba7-a279-c8883cd40dc6">REDRESS: Impregnated g=
reen part made last night with 85% ParaPlast paraffin / 15% PE-CVA solution=
 and in process of dissolving off mold. Began mixing up binder in preparati=
on for making a 1kg batch of Inconel 625 coated powder using Inconel powder=
 waste. Printing a new water soluble mold that has internal channels.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fbed9748-3ae2-455b-809d-2d1e00a0377b">Call with Techcon, a c=
ompany based in Cypress, CA that makes wax dispensing heads similar to the =
Nordson Asymtek system. They offer free applications testing, are open to u=
s visiting their facility to test our paraffin in their system, offer nozzl=
es in sizes from 50-400 micron, and have a dispense rate of up to 1500 Hz b=
ut recommend keeping it around 150 Hz for production applications because t=
he piezo actuator tends to heat at higher frequencies.</p>
<p local-id=3D"29a145fb-da3d-4c46-ab63-5bd4b5c4cfe7">PILOT: Based on discus=
sions with Will, I looked back at the PILOT CAD and found that the stroke o=
f the Y stages is actually closer to 615mm and the stroke of the Saffron st=
ages is close to 670mm, so a 48=E2=80=9D stage would be WAY oversized for w=
hat we need.</p>
<p local-id=3D"95e851bf-42a8-4f97-9cc9-45cd59298b06"></p>
<p local-id=3D"46838791-ec70-4398-85a6-933a75fa75ce">2025-06-19</p>
<p local-id=3D"de786671-4e9f-49cf-ac7c-6f24bf65a3fc">HOPPER: Mohsen removed=
 the hopper from PILOT 2 because it had been having issues with not closing=
 completely. This seems to be due to a buildup of powder on top of the meta=
l gate strip, likely as a result of powder leakage out of the hopper. I am =
working on scavenging parts from it for the new hopper I am working on that=
 uses the standard PILOT spreader bar. In the meantime, Mohsen is going to =
run baseline tests with the tank-to-tank setup.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f32f387b-02d8-424c-8fdb-dbd1e07a14d7">PILOT: 2.5 hour meetin=
g to discuss Epson PILOT program. Sounds like the goal of the program right=
 now is to make 2 PILOTs to send to Epson that are as similar to PILOTs 2 a=
nd 3 as possible, with several safety upgrades and a larger chamber volume =
to enable use of the full stroke of the current X and Y stages. The plan is=
 to have these complete by October, with some number of similar PILOTs read=
y for internal use by December.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7bd5202a-3fdb-482b-b06e-7a76e8d9a221">2025-06-20</p>
<p local-id=3D"dc0923c3-9fc2-426b-92c6-df6c8e5ecd33">HOPPER: Continuing to =
work on larger roller and zero-waste free flow hopper.</p>
<p local-id=3D"80be95ca-7fbd-498a-8a56-d20e0e78907a">PILOT: Talked with Man=
ju for ~1 hour to help him with inventory.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bc8003a3-73b2-4cdb-8903-3330d7ea8dcb">R&amp;D Weekly Meeting=
:</p>
<p local-id=3D"bc0a946c-1f3f-4a57-a3de-edc57f612c45">Green density generall=
y indicates distribution of powder, green strength generally indicates dist=
ribution of binder.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6443cd8a-9ec8-47c0-a5a9-f6966a20d1e7"><strong>To Do:</strong=
></p>
<ul local-id=3D"71a73ec8-8bc5-4476-b0b5-0f242c1a9c08">
<li local-id=3D"0caf5c56-9050-4c17-80d9-1ff2f23c6c75">
<p local-id=3D"a05d8ac9-b915-4fc0-9087-849cb815f31f"><strong>Complete and i=
nstall updated free flow hopper with larger spreader bar</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9e1deb84-a7cc-4566-b96e-0d03fd8f45ab">
<p local-id=3D"5fa3b2c1-ef74-47aa-a905-ef6d750c38f7"><strong>Add vibrator t=
o flee flow hopper with larger spreader bar</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"75d1c3c6-29a3-4989-9f31-091a1d6dfda0">
<p local-id=3D"0ae225fa-f224-4a18-a75c-1e3e456148da"><strong>Look into meta=
l safe compact vacuums</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"85d3f83c-4fc6-47ac-aeca-66f901c92ce5">Epson Project Update M=
eeting:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"9e296dd1-fc44-4b7d-98bc-078ee4fe2e26">
<li local-id=3D"d355b4c8-6f03-4fc8-b010-6b13f43595f5">
<p local-id=3D"3f29a3f2-e5c7-4264-be9d-56c27fcd82a2">October 15 date is cri=
tical, not sure if that means machine completion, machine testing completio=
n, or ship date</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d4003d00-ae55-4926-94b7-b5548cfbf4ad"></p>
<p local-id=3D"e183da17-2b00-41de-9e1c-07757af1ae61">2025-06-23</p>
<p local-id=3D"48641c77-009f-4471-842a-9b901102387b">HOPPER: Finished assem=
bling gated hopper with two limit switches to detect open and closed state.=
 I had redesigned the side mounts to work with 6mm long M3 screws, but in r=
edesigning it I made the side mounts 1mm thicker which meant the hopper wou=
ld not fit within the Y gantry cutout, so I reverted to the older side moun=
t design and gave the hopper to Ben to install in PILOT 2.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a866f4e3-4c47-4310-b27b-e234c17fc8c8">Continuing to work on =
zero-waste hopper design. Figuring out how to integrate limit switches into=
 the design to ensure that the gate opens or closes when commanded to do so=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a8755227-cca8-4c72-8a50-98c7471146dd">PILOT: Working on modi=
fying design of PILOT base plate and frame for the Epson PILOT printers.</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"56366ead-4008-49b2-b61f-fb6bdfa61215"></p>
<p local-id=3D"cd03d065-e08d-46eb-8229-540a9fde7a0d">2025-06-24</p>
<p local-id=3D"9d08f2e0-4c33-4672-8ae7-6ff1c25fab6c">PILOT: Continued work =
