<p local-id=3D"667cb4dc-c90f-472c-952b-1612f8aedfb6">HOPPER: Completed gate=
d hopper with larger diameter spreader bar. It seems to be having issues wi=
th incomplete spreading after several layers, so Mohsen is adding a vibrato=
r motor to it. It also has two limit switches now, one that detects opening=
 and one that detects when it is closed, so operation should be more robust=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"00282979-bf88-4b76-882f-d6c1ffce4c02"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1c5361c1-19a2-4c1e-b3c0-3b9c5a322f18">2025-06-25</p>
<p local-id=3D"ac9a0ac0-a6fe-45e5-96ba-0922aacdc294">PILOT: Continuing to r=
efine the design of the PILOT-E. Discussed machined parts with Manjun to co=
nfirm which parts are needed and which are obsolete.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a3f11d29-618a-4249-b379-2ad0b402bda1">HOPPER: I accidentally=
 started the print last night with the red PLA-CF instead of the brown, so =
the print did not complete because it ran out of filament and was the wrong=
 material anyway (Payman wanted to try the brown PLA-CF because it seemed t=
o work better on past free flow hoppers).</p>
<p local-id=3D"8c78a9fc-22bb-4d2e-a705-bf98b4821f22">2025-06-26</p>
<p local-id=3D"3088fafc-ae33-4d6c-82c3-c98e8403be49">PILOT: Continuing to w=
ork on CAD and design details (vacuum etc.).</p>
<p local-id=3D"b24e8d00-f013-44b9-b3a2-c62e0ab2f8ad">HOPPER: Installed heat=
 set inserts in new hopper V3. The zero-waste hopper is assembled and able =
to open and close with a 3D printed blade. It is very slow with the stepper=
 motor controller I use for testing, but should be able to run faster in th=
e pilot printers with the Duet board running it. I have the two motors just=
 wired in parallel so that they can be run with a single stepper driver; it=
 seems to be working so far.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bfa38cca-a060-493e-b63b-49f67eee96c4"></p>
<p local-id=3D"9ede5205-d804-4877-a9a9-852e6159d529">2025-06-27</p>
<p local-id=3D"e14a7ff7-4cfa-4442-b0ec-5e07de75a3ef">PILOT: Refining CAD fo=
r design review on Monday (finishing sizing of frame and doors so that the =
side extrusion of the doors does not go higher than the top of the enclosur=
e, added in new larger cable carrier, etc.)</p>
<p local-id=3D"b419034c-ae43-4cb2-9f66-f3e3c9744b72">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting=
:</p>
<p local-id=3D"b0cb5fc5-c7ad-4e13-8f6a-61a515eca5a7">HOPPER: Working on upd=
ated version of zero-waste bladed-gate hopper based on learnings from the t=
esting Mohsen ran this week (larger diameter spreader bar, in-powder vibrat=
ion).</p>
<p local-id=3D"a74f7d1c-daf0-443c-a8ab-3f41d74f41fa"></p>
<p local-id=3D"a1ba3ae0-048f-4026-bc0d-881b2adc3ce3">2025-06-30</p>
<p local-id=3D"c7b75e1e-74af-4148-9d4b-fcdc364255b9">HOPPER: Ben and Mohsen=
 assembled the brown PLA hopper V3.5.0 and are currently testing it in PILO=
T 2. I am working on designing a way to apply vibration to the powder direc=
tly with some sort of structure that is inserted into the powder. This will=
 hopefully replicate and automate the manual stirring process that Mohsen u=
sed to get good density results in testing last week. Mohsen and Ben are pu=
rsuing an alternative design that vibrates a thin sheet of spring steel (~0=
.010=E2=80=9D) inserted vertically into the hopper aligned with the X axis.=
 I drilled several holes in the sheet they selected to mount a vibrator mot=
or and to install screws to act as stops to prevent the sheet from falling =
into the hopper. I am printing the part that holds the 4X pointed rods that=
 insert into the powder in the hopper. The part will be vibration isolated =
from the hopper by silicone rubber strips.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e113fabb-6118-4c07-b967-fd1caa85900b">PILOT: CAD update meet=
ing. I raised concerns about decreased rigidity and increased vibration wit=
h the larger base plate and frame. Since the Y stages are farther apart, th=
e Y gantry needed to be widened, which will result in less rigidity and pos=
sible sagging of components. I also have concerns about whether Epson will =
be happy with a printer that is considerably larger than the first 3 pilots=
, but that is ultimately more a business decision than a technical decision=
. We also discussed the design of the new mist box; Sean is working on a de=
sign that is made from machined aluminum instead of the current 3D printed =
PLA.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6df72432-f32b-4a47-800a-a95edb502f00"></p>
<p local-id=3D"88aaee0c-28cd-4fec-95aa-89a5b96fdb57">2025-07-01</p>
<p local-id=3D"750a5250-a961-409a-9964-6eb1d282ac5b">HOPPER: Al finished ma=
chining the blade for the zero-waste hopper, and I installed it for Payman =
to conduct benchtop testing. The bladed gate is able to open and close, but=
 it appears to have difficulty spreading a flat layer without being mounted=
 to a rigid gantry, so it needs to be tested on one of the pilot printers. =
Continued working on the vibrating rod insert. I have cut rods to roughly t=
he right length and ground a small chamfer on them; machining them to a poi=
nt was deemed too difficult with the available equipment. The orientation I=
 used for printing the vibrating rod insert plate was correct for the motor=
 mount but incorrect for the rod mount, so I have separated it into two par=
ts that I will print tonight.</p>
<p local-id=3D"08a0d467-8a73-4afb-b0f2-de481e58f42f">PILOT: Spent a few hou=
rs going over the current pilot printers with Rajan and Manjun to finalize =
the current components list. Discussed which parts will be 3D printed vs ma=
chined (all parts that are currently being printed will continue being prin=
ted, other than the mist box). Had a meeting with Will, Rajan, and Manjun t=
o discuss CAD, drawings, and timelines. Per Rajan=E2=80=99s request I am go=
ing to reduce the width of the cutout in the Y axis gantry to the original =
width in pilots 1-3. I repeated the point 3 times that this limits space to=
 install wider components and also limits access to components from the top=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6a29d422-ca0a-45fe-830e-2fcd00a86bce"></p>
<p local-id=3D"4ecc209f-d2c9-4979-a3de-5a2d09a14ea2">2025-07-02</p>
<p local-id=3D"a942d0c5-3211-4cd1-8674-4403a9f5ece2">3DEO Technical Team Sy=
nc: Current &amp; Upcoming Tech Improvements</p>
<p local-id=3D"e56b9c54-bc40-4a2b-a09b-2af401bd6b87">1.5 hour meeting with =
Scott, Rajan, Payman, Marcus, and all of the technical staff at 3DEO. It en=
tailed Scott and Rajan discussing their various philosophies of business an=
d product development and their view of the future of 3DEO and the technolo=
gies we are currently pursuing. At two points Scott asked if anyone had any=
 questions; there were none.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2513c4ac-7ddc-42fc-8455-b818077fb907">Part Benchmarking Meet=
ing</p>
<p local-id=3D"3d29dd2f-841f-4452-9b33-d635715f0911">Four different geometr=
ies were printed by Xometry and Protolabs using DMLS and binder jetting and=
 compared with 3DEO=E2=80=99s parts and pricing structure. 3DEO has a lower=
 per-part cost and higher quality parts, but also has a significant minimum=
 order quantity based on the build plate size (51 for the parts benchmarked=
).</p>
<p local-id=3D"cdb1bbf5-7c83-4822-b77b-877312157c4f">PILOT Printer Discussi=
on W/ Payman, Marcus, Rajan, Mahmood (informal):</p>
<p local-id=3D"744bec38-1aa9-4e9f-84ab-88124d2abcc9">It sounds like the pla=
n as it is right now is to make 2 pilot printers to send to Epson by mid oc=
tober then make 2 identical printers for in-house use by mid december. I wa=
s pushing to purchase off-the-shelf glove boxes and recirculating gas manag=
ement systems for the two in-house printers, such as systems available from=
 <a href=3D"https://lctechinc.com/" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow=
">https://lctechinc.com/</a> . This would give us precise environmental con=
trol, a completely inert internal environment, and complete operator safety=
 without investing significant internal resources. My pitch was ultimately =
rejected; inerting the pilot printers is not a requirement for the foreseea=
ble future, it is thought that it is not possible to develop a workflow whe=
re the printers can be operated without regularly opening large doors to ac=
cess the mechanical systems, thinks it would be easy to make the pilot prin=
ters airtight as they are right now, and inhalation of stainless steel powd=
er is deemed an acceptable risk for machine operators.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f8880ebe-7c03-432f-a8b2-3b6a636dbfdb">R&amp;D Weekly Meeting=
 NEXTGEN:</p>
<p local-id=3D"7a02e1f8-8bc8-401b-9082-e1f93cb73d4b"><strong>To Do:</strong=
></p>
<p local-id=3D"ea32f180-70b1-4b93-974e-ed4bd9da6cb5"><strong>Burnout test o=
f different waxes - done</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"6d8b934c-78c9-4f9f-9747-1ab0a4ab69c0"><strong>Order/test 2 f=
lute end mill - Mason testing various end mills, trying to get a single flu=
te .020=E2=80=9D cut diameter end mill</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"06ae9110-3167-4909-a8ff-33b793e075b9"><strong>Filter custom =
wax blend - done</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"7ecadcf7-0e84-4ddb-a7a1-15103d805f76"><strong>Increase hoppe=
r size - hopper extension printed</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"6eadbf9d-2924-4bcb-b489-012ef5ecab6e"><strong>Add limit swit=
ches to zero-waste hopper - 1 limit switch added for closing, hard stop pre=
sent for opening</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"344d9a24-e398-4852-be39-a5241c69ddaa"></p>
<p local-id=3D"5d5c7e58-603c-4b97-b4db-1e4e2ef8ff55">2025-07-03</p>
<p local-id=3D"ce54827d-f343-4fa0-ad19-d20b2b15c04f">PILOT: Discussed power=
 supply requirements with Manjun. One issue that I had forgotten about is t=
hat the heater needs to be converted to DC power; this will necessitate a &=
gt;500W 12VDC power supply to be added that is dedicated to the heater. Als=
o, I need to spec out some lights for the printers. Per Pourya=E2=80=99s re=
quest, I will select lights that are external to the primary machine chambe=
r to minimize heat input to the chamber.</p>
<p local-id=3D"85063164-7dff-4c2d-bb69-08bac2beade9">HOPPER: Ben is in the =
process of installing the zero-waste gated hopper into Pilot 3. I accidenta=
lly printed two of the same modified side mount brackets, but there are dif=
ferent versions for each side, so I am in the process of printing 1 of the =
correct brackets that are needed.</p>
<p local-id=3D"011ae06a-037d-418a-a136-53a779aa51c9">I am also in the proce=
ss of assembling the vibrating rod - based powder vibration system.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9ddf88eb-70a9-4953-bc80-e403a54dd4e2"></p>
<p local-id=3D"1acfba30-8bcc-4816-8d0f-a01dcad2cb97">2025-07-07</p>
<p local-id=3D"165f91ec-9f7c-44ee-908a-b1d91bde7d83">PILOT: Working with Ma=
nju and Pourya to spec out wires and cables for the Epson pilot printers. T=
he color code I used on PILOTs 1-3 is compatible with the Japanese color co=
de: <span class=3D"ap-container ap-inline" id=3D"ap-com.bilith.lref.conflue=
nce-gdrive__lref-gdrive-file7091013934519500804"> <span class=3D"ap-content=
 ap-inline" id=3D"embedded-com.bilith.lref.confluence-gdrive__lref-gdrive-f=
ile7091013934519500804"></span>
