<p local-id=3D"a9be713b-c916-4697-b819-bf7397495ae8">2025-07-11</p>
<p local-id=3D"ebeeb3d8-9141-4f2b-9bd5-ecfe73ae55f6">HOPPER: Completed asse=
mbling latest iteration of zero-waste hopper. It now has a limit switch to =
detect when it is fully closed, which should prevent overdriving the gate, =
which can cause the gate to bow outwards and, at best, cause a poor layer, =
and at worst, cause the gate to crash into the machine or build plate. The =
hopper is ready to be installed into the machine, but the machine needs to =
be wired to detect a limit switch input. I asked Pourya to do this whenever=
 he has a chance and I asked Ben to install the hopper in Pilot 3.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b1684398-c049-4f8b-9630-80ea4bbdef5a">Designing a new blade =
for the zero-waste hopper with a much sharper angle (20 degrees vs the curr=
ent 45 degrees).</p>
<p local-id=3D"66777544-7173-4c24-9d2a-6647039ffe86">NEXTGEN: I removed the=
 two ceramic crucibles from the upper Keith furnace that had gone through a=
 burnout cycle last night, testing the burnout properties of hard microcrys=
talline wax and the 85% paraffin/15% PE-CVA blend. The results were promisi=
ng; the microcrystalline wax showed very minimal residue and the blend show=
ed a slight amount of residue.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ebd4f224-51ef-4e43-9185-eed2b5716200">I also learned about a=
 different kind of wax that may be useful: it is called Synthetic Fischer-T=
ropsch (FT) Wax and is a synthesized wax that in theory has a more standard=
ized chemical structure than paraffin, since there are so many variations o=
f paraffin available.</p>
