<p local-id=3D"77b07508-f60b-4a5f-88e7-f23462dcac9c">NEXTGEN: Working on ma=
king a wax that is 75% hard microcrystalline wax and 25% PE-CVA. It is diff=
icult to keep the mixture liquid because of the high melting point of hard =
microcrystalline wax; I currently have the hot plate in the wax testing fum=
e hood set to 160=C2=B0C to keep the mixture liquid for mixing with a PTFE =
magnetic stirrer, but I have not checked whether that is sufficient to keep=
 the whole batch liquid (it tends to stay liquid towards the bottom but sol=
idifies towards the top). The batch is a total of 100g. I had to bump the t=
emperature up to 180=C2=B0C, I=E2=80=99ll see if that is sufficient.</p>
