<p local-id=3D"41e4cbc6-813f-448d-b3b7-7edd2501dcac"></p>
<p local-id=3D"44b8593b-4c4e-4670-bbcc-d55d47e19d19">PILOT: Continuing to w=
ork on the Epson pilot electrical system and CAD. I am still on hold for st=
arting fabrication of the electrical control cabinets until the schematic i=
s complete. I sent Manjun several items that needed to be added to the BOM =
and the schematic. Pourya is going to do some benchtop life cycle testing o=
n the TEC power supply (Mean Well UHP-1000-48) because the current rating i=
s slightly lower than the startup current of the 48V TECs. I have ordered a=
 replacement power supply so that one can be dedicated to life cycle testin=
g while there are two for the two pilot printers. Apparently the Delta TEC =
has an integrated control system that turns it on and off depending on the =
resistance of a thermistor; since we want to be able to control it directly=
, Pourya is going to try replacing the thermistor with a fixed resistor to =
tell the TEC to be on continuously.</p>
