<p local-id=3D"64c40bcc-37c9-4a70-8c6f-706ca99125d3">PILOT: The smaller Ven=
tion parts showed up (~1m extrusion sticks, angle brackets, etc.). Manjun i=
s looking into where the longer extrusion parts are currently. Continuing t=
o work on the design of the electrical control cabinet. I opened up one of =
the door lock solenoids, and am in the process of figuring out how to wire =
it. I am in the process of printing the Duet and Raspberry Pi board mounts,=
 and am also working on designing the Arduino Mega mount. I printed out 2 R=
Pi mounts and installed Pis to them, but I realized that the ribbon cable c=
onnecting the Pi to the Duet board needs to wrap underneath the Pi, so I am=
 reprinting the Pi mount with increased height to give enough clearance for=
 the ribbon cable underneath the board. I sent the latest CAD of the electr=
ical control cabinet to Manjun. It is largely complete, but it is missing s=
ome of the breakers and terminal blocks (depending on the final electrical =
schematic) and the cabinet is missing some cutouts for electrical cord plug=
s and the buttons/switches on the operator side of the cabinet.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a65ccb9e-7913-48ec-95b9-26ddbace6815">Performance review wit=
h Marcus. It went pretty well, I think. I got a bunch of 3=E2=80=99s, but M=
arcus seems to view those as reasonably positive scores.</p>
<p local-id=3D"04c699bf-3103-47dc-aeb1-ac20171d9af5">2025-07-25</p>
<p local-id=3D"4fcfe9db-3e1b-4483-9051-854fb71030c2">PILOT: Working on the =
design modifications to the new heater design. Got formal quote for, and ad=
ded to the purchasing request Jira page, an order from SendCutSend for the =
heater sheet metal components and acrylic windows for the machined mist box=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f6945a82-5d02-4119-a115-86a5633feb40">NEXTGEN: Meeting to go=
 over results of and issues with recent no depowdering wax filling experime=
nts and discuss solutions.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f198f586-4229-4e1a-a50a-1aa19b491ed6">2025-07-28</p>
<p local-id=3D"b12eba0c-fb67-4c25-aa90-996f240b6e82">PILOT: Showed the CAD =
of the latest version of the Pilot printer and the current control cabinet =
electrical CAD to two Epson visitors (no idea who they are, nobody tells me=
 anything).</p>
<p local-id=3D"c50dec28-5135-4f85-a3ba-132509eff79a">HOPPER: Continuing to =
work on the blade for HOPPER V3.4.2, the latest iteration of the linear gat=
e zero-waste hopper design. The design direction I am going in right now is=
 to use a thin, flat blade (2mm thick, 15 degree angle blade) with machined=
 side mounts to give it structure. I am also considering a reinforcing stri=
p along the back of the blade, which would give it increased rigidity but c=
ould cause issues with powder buildup jamming the gate from closing fully.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"f7ca1354-cdf3-4828-b9c2-a35b5373b142">R&amp;D Weekly Meeting=
: Held on Monday because Payman was out last Friday.</p>
