<p local-id=3D"786808e8-0283-4d95-99fa-e36bac2faf68">2025-07-29</p>
<p local-id=3D"bac32f46-5070-4db5-8949-2768847bec1f">PILOT: Showed Fernando=
 how to assemble the Vention frames and got him started with putting togeth=
er the two frames. Finally got permission to start work on the electrical s=
ubpanel. Completed layout, completed cutouts, drilled holes for and install=
ed 16X rivet nuts for large PSU sheet metal mounts, riveted in the DIN rail=
s on one of the panels.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e372f7fa-637f-4fd5-a4f3-dd96b3b44ebb">HOPPER: Working on des=
ign of side mounts for the 15 degree blade for HOPPER V3.4.2. Printed body =
of HOPPER V3.4.2.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f909f813-d11a-464d-8449-75a6f01a36e5">2025-07-30</p>
<p local-id=3D"350e394e-6074-4ad8-afd1-9a91c47890b6">HOPPER: Gave hopper bo=
dy to Mason to assemble. Received machined flat spreader bar from Al and ga=
ve him the drawing and stock for the new thin blade. I forgot to design the=
 mount for the limit switch for HOPPER V3.4.2, and there are no heat set in=
sert holes in the hopper for the limit switch mount, so I will need to add =
that in later.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7ab32ccc-ca3e-416b-a0fb-b325e0981753">PILOT: Finished attach=
ing DIN rail and wire duct for the electrical subpanel for PILOT 4.</p>
<p local-id=3D"42db6529-b0fc-474f-b3df-9c73804a4ce2">2025-07-31</p>
<p local-id=3D"088b1e44-c7b1-49ac-8ca0-ff75fb528b5a">HOPPER: Printing new E=
dmund Stage Y Plate Mount brackets for the hopper in Pilot 2 because the pr=
evious ones broke. The previous ones were made from PLA-CF with an infill o=
f less than 100% so I have added reinforcing material to the design and I a=
m printing replacements from PETG-CF with 100% infill. Beginning to work on=
 the external hopper refill system. The current approach I am taking is to =
route a hose from the top of the print chamber to a connection point on the=
 hopper. This hose will remain attached throughout the print, and powder wi=
ll be added to the hopper as necessary.</p>
<p local-id=3D"acba67ad-be6f-4790-bbab-0fa91dc24134">PILOT: Began populatin=
g the electrical subpanel for PILOT 4. In process of attaching the wire duc=
t and DIN rail to the PILOT 5 subpanel. Fernando is still working on the fr=
ames; he also looked up the torque spec for Vention aluminum extrusion moun=
ts, which is 13 Nm. This sounds a little low to me, but apparently Fernando=
 initially tightened them to a lower torque so possibly it is higher than I=
 might have tightened them initially. He said that there is a possibility o=
f distortion of the extrusion if the screws are tightened too much, so he i=
s using a torque wrench to install them.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a5bf528d-561c-4611-9849-1ff6ccfd668a">2025-08-01</p>
<p local-id=3D"003b87a1-1490-4e6b-92eb-628cc73e8263">HOPPER: I reprinted th=
e blade side brackets for hopper V3.4.2 because the older ones were too thi=
ck to be able to slide the hopper through the opening on the Y gantry. Al f=
inished the new steel blade, and Mason is currently installing it on hopper=
 V3.4.2.</p>
<p local-id=3D"559d2e58-cd47-483c-8ba4-08188656711f">PILOT: Connected AC wi=
res to the 12VDC power supply to be able to mount it to the subpanel; the c=
onnection points are inaccessible once the sheet metal mount has been screw=
ed to the subpanel. Fernando is continuing to work on the frame for PILOT 5=
; he had put two of the cross members in the wrong location so I showed him=
 where they should be and gave him the drawing of the frame that I generate=
d. Working on a redesign of the heater for the Epson pilots. Due to limitat=
ions with SendCutSend=E2=80=99s bending capabilities, I need to redesign th=
e sheet metal parts so that they are manufacturable. I finished a new desig=
n and uploaded it to have them look it over to see if it is more manufactur=
able than the previous design.</p>
<p local-id=3D"298c717f-0129-440c-aa57-a9fff415d3bc">2025-08-04</p>
<p local-id=3D"f2ac3a93-c8bb-42c1-8112-e5f19210de97">HOPPER: Mason has asse=
mbled and installed hopper V3.4.2 on pilot 3. Ben cut himself on the blade =
on Friday, that new blade may be a serious safety issue that needs to be ad=
dressed. Working on a part to interface to the hose to be able to fill the =
hopper from a hose connected to the top of the pilot printer. Designed and =
printing a limit switch mount for hopper V3.4.2. Printing a funnel to conne=
ct to the hopper refilling hose through the top acrylic panel of the pilot =
printer. I need to redesign and print a hopper-side interface because the c=
urrent design is incompatible with the vibrating sheet metal plate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"933c6171-e2ec-41bf-8849-da2069d7466e">PILOT: Talked with Wil=
l about some of the 3D printed parts required. Went over 3D printed parts w=
ith Manju again. We also have a meeting tomorrow to go over the 3D printed =
parts again.</p>
<p local-id=3D"87a1156a-f31f-4f5f-a577-d329db081d4a">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"78aca1a5-4642-4bfe-ab0a-7a908c2c8fe9">2025-08-05</p>
<p local-id=3D"cb3dcf4e-6357-4d2c-87d0-6ba6b3b1c826">HOPPER: Printed a new =
limit switch mount and it was installed on the V3.4.2 hopper on pilot 3 by =
Mason. Printed a funnel for the flexible fill hose that looks good, althoug=
h I need to redesign and print a new low-profile adapter that will feed pow=
der into the hopper with the vibrating sheet metal in place.</p>
<p local-id=3D"17f12726-e202-4fb3-bfa2-5f5e419cf4f1">PILOT: Working on wiri=
ng and installation of final electrical components on 2X electrical subpane=
ls.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6ffae247-f073-44aa-973b-11f9b511ab17">2025-08-06</p>
<p local-id=3D"909e380f-a661-4966-8d0f-cb3f58d31443">HOPPER: Asked Mason to=
 help out with the design of hopper hose filling adapter.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b48aa8a1-3505-4461-8e41-418a5a92e9c6">PILOT: Installing Duet=
 boards and Raspberry Pi boards with 3D printed DIN rail mounts. Duet board=
s and Raspberry Pi=E2=80=99s are installed and connected with a ribbon cabl=
e. I am currently working on installing the Arduino Mega=E2=80=99s for envi=
ronmental control. I asked Pourya, and the only two boards that need to be =
installed on the electrical subpanel are the Arduino Mega and Adafruit I2C =
multiplexer board (PCA9548). Soldered the screw terminal shields for the tw=
o Arduino Megas.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1ccca705-86f9-4ad5-8e3b-2086b91d9390">2025-08-07</p>
<p local-id=3D"46258415-c292-4302-90ef-6341a9cfc80c">PILOT: Arduino Mega mo=
unts are printed and ready to be installed. The low voltage rail is getting=
 crowded so I am considering moving the USB hub to an alternate location. T=
he Arduino Mega has been installed. I have moved the USB hub to the lowest =
rail (safety controller, USB hub, motor cutoff relays). Three power supplie=
s are connected to AC power, although the primary 24VDC power supply is con=
nected through the safety relay so it will need to be bypassed for initial =
testing. The two acrylic windows that are sandwiched between the control ca=
binet and the Vention frame arrived. Assuming that they have been cut corre=
ctly, I can use them as a template for marking out the M8 clearance holes f=
or bolting the cabinet to the frame. I still need to finish the CAD for the=
 cutouts on the control cabinet. It is also confirmed that we will be makin=
g 2 more carbon copy PILOTs for internal production use, and there is inter=
est in making a PILOT for printing with copper so there may be a third (the=
se would be PILOTs 6, 7, and 8. The PILOTs in progress are 4 and 5, and the=
 ones already build are 1, 2, and 3.) Wired up all 5 DC PSUs and energized =
them on subpanel 4, resulting in green lights across the board. Subpanel 5 =
will be tested tomorrow. Once the PSUs are tested successfully, I will proc=
eed to connect the remaining components to power.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3f47dd52-d42f-46df-ab91-f360d0934e9d">2025-08-08</p>
<p local-id=3D"9a52729d-127e-488a-9cc4-fe2f34b76ca0">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"6ae5f459-6c3d-427e-bc70-784c4f9210cf">PILOT: The subpanel is=
 fully populated and the control boards are powered.</p>
<p local-id=3D"99a61b37-c11c-42b1-9912-4932234acd3c">2025-08-11</p>
<p local-id=3D"3c2af322-6451-4410-9c9c-517b69875e6a">PILOT: Showed Fernando=
