<p local-id=3D"78c7a3c9-d1d8-4911-ac7c-3be855264fd1">Drawings of the cutout=
s to be made in the control cabinet are complete. Engineering printer is no=
t printing well so I had to order some more toner cartridges; it turns out =
that the front office printer uses 054 toner cartridges while the engineeri=
ng printer uses 045 cartridges</p>
<p local-id=3D"afaf0f76-89c1-4389-8bd5-057c620b6ea3">2025-08-12</p>
<p local-id=3D"c9d13fa1-63d0-40a5-aff2-be2e44140657">Bagel Tuesday. Switchi=
ng to Clockify for time tracking. Hired a new Director of Sales, Steven Riz=
zo.</p>
<p local-id=3D"88efce25-590a-40d1-8880-9a1024c69227">PILOT: Reviewed safety=
 system options with Rajan. The decision was made to include the safety sys=
tem as designed but add a safety system defeating keyswitch on the front of=
 the control cabinet which will override the safety system when active and =
allow the doors to be opened for machine setup. Completed cutouts on top, l=
eft, and bottom of control cabinet. Rear cutouts and final cleaning are pen=
ding, after which the control cabinet can be installed on the frames.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9dc8dfb4-8eba-4f61-8a2c-7033e45fc25b">NEXTGEN: Payman brough=
t up an interesting concept for me to work on: making a pourable substance =
that, when sintered, will act as a porous material that liquid can be pumpe=
d through for transferring heat.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b904028a-9574-44db-8688-f86b22786c7d">2025-08-13</p>
<p local-id=3D"e3fddaba-516a-4b51-9e8b-4a69723e8fa4">PILOT: Completed cutou=
ts, cleaned cabinets, mounted cabinets and cabinet-side acrylic panels to P=
ilots 4 and 5 with the assistance of Fernando, installed both Roxtec block =
cable glands on each cabinet, and installed 3X power outlets on each cabine=
t, as well as the NEMA power input socket.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6d97551d-02d9-4a51-91d6-973c13b269e8">2025-08-14</p>
<p local-id=3D"a9929434-c9e0-4f33-a8e2-b67c40ff6a4d">PILOT: Added tapped ho=
les to mount the 3D printed parts that clamp onto the keyboard and monitor =
mount. Pushed for us to buy a dedicated Bambu printer to just go ahead and =
print the non-resin 3D printed parts in-house; the process of getting them =
quoted and ordered from an outside vendor is taking up more time than we wo=
uld spend just printing them here. The main advantage of having them printe=
d outside is saving our time, but the process of ordering them is taking to=
o long. Installed the electrical subpanels in the control cabinets. Install=
ed the stack lights, power disconnects, and cabinet cooling fans. Installed=
 one E-stop; we only have one currently available but more are being ordere=
d. 2X anodized base plates were received. Installed threaded inserts in bas=
e plates and began installing one base plate in a pilot printer. The base p=
lates seem flat but they are definitely quite flimsy.</p>
<p local-id=3D"107794e8-52f0-4769-88e9-cfcfd450afc4">2025-08-15</p>
<p local-id=3D"d8299a52-6b87-44b3-a5bf-df494d05be27">PILOT: Fernando develo=
ped a test protocol for testing the flatness of the base plate by mounting =
a dial indicator to one of the Y stages and moving it along the direction o=
f travel. When the plate is in the machine (without being bolted down to an=
ything) or resting on a bowed table, it is up to .015=E2=80=9D out of flat,=
 and can be warped by .005=E2=80=9D by pressing on it, but it is flat withi=
n .001=E2=80=9D when it is fully supported by a granite surface plate, so t=
he base plate was machined flat, it just needs to be supported well in the =
flat position. I laser engraved labels for the switches and the Raspberry P=
i USB bulkhead fitting and installed them on the control cabinet. I realize=
d that I had forgotten to install the pneumatic system components, so I am =
working on adding them to the control cabinet CAD and will drill two holes =
today for installing the bulkhead fitting. Received Bambu printer for print=
ing PILOT printer parts and began setting it up.</p>
