ting with the new Bambu X1E by loading the sliced print file onto a microsd=
 card and installing that in the printer. I have been having issues with co=
nnecting to the printer over wi-fi. Using an SD card is a little slower tha=
n wi-fi, but it has the advantage that it is possible to rerun prints from =
the printer touchscreen directly without needing to send them from a laptop=
 every time. Working on installing the keyboards and monitors today. The mo=
unts are printed, but I think it will be necessary to order a new pipe beca=
use the mounting rod is likely too short for the height of the new cabinet.=
 The Bambu X1E is up and printing; I ran a Benchy with CF nylon and now am =
running two overflow blanking inserts. Assembled 2X pneumatic system regula=
ting assemblies. These each have a 1/4=E2=80=9D quick disconnect, a pressur=
e regulator, and a flow regulator. The pressure regulator used is no longer=
 available, so the system will need to be redesigned at some point to accom=
modate an available regulator. I successfully powered up one of the machine=
s (I need to number them individually so that I can keep track of which is =
which). Drilled hole, and installed pneumatic pressure/flow regulator stack=
, in one of the pilot printers. Set up the FormLabs printer for printing pa=
rts with ESD safe resin and started two spindle cleaning troughs printing. =
Running a print of overflow chutes for the 2X pilot printers on the Bambu X=
1E.</p>
