ront of the machine</p>
<p local-id=3D"340e84a0-f780-4891-89c3-2bc657e7096c">2025-09-10</p>
<p local-id=3D"293fa95d-e020-4362-915e-7bbb389bf8f0">Bagel Wednesday: Emily=
 acknowledged that many people are leaving at the same time. There are many=
 positions they=E2=80=99re hiring for, mostly high-level engineering and R&=
amp;D positions, as well as one R&amp;D technician and one cross-trained te=
chnician. Most interestingly, Scott was surprised that many people are conc=
erned that the company may shut down soon. To the best of my knowledge, we =
have operating capital for 3 months and are dependent on another funding ro=
und to stay open beyond that. Two people have been fired and four have chos=
en to leave within the past month. Epson seems to be pushing to get access =
to all of our IP and technology before the end of the year (PILOT printers,=
 slicer, their engineers are going through training to transfer knowledge f=
rom 3DEO to Epson). The job listings have been posted several times over th=
e past few months, with only one hire so far. Scott was recently in Japan a=
nd said that Epson seems excited about integrating our technology into thei=
r portfolio, although it occurs to me that once they have the PILOT printer=
s in hand, have been trained on their use, our approach to DFAM, and softwa=
re, they have much less need for 3DEO at all.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7f1a3675-52b9-49ed-ab99-0d5409263dd8">PILOT: Modifications t=
o printers per Epson recommendations. Pushbuttons added to outside of contr=
ol cabinet to reset safety system, bumpers added to vacuum tray, labels add=
