<p local-id=3D"7f359ffe-4dfc-419d-93a8-42e454846243">2025-09-17</p>
<p local-id=3D"6e4e6ea4-7584-4f47-b168-2c4061bf0324">PILOT: Designed and pr=
inting new door latch mounts. Designed new pull handles for vacuum support =
plates that do not interfere with the new lower front doors. Added M8 lifti=
ng eyes to design of vacuum support plate, modified the drawing per the new=
 design, and ordered 4X straps for holding the vacuums in place. These stra=
ps are added per Epson=E2=80=99s request. Tested and redesigned door latch =
mount and printing the new version to test before mass producing them. ZZ s=
eems to have added several terminal blocks to the control cabinet so I aske=
d him for the connection points so I can update the schematic. Updated the =
schematic with a new power supply for the nebulizer driver; I am using a 12=
V boost converter powered by the USB hub. It may be possible to power the n=
ebulizer driver with the 12V power supply that powers the water detection s=
ensor, but because the output of that power supply is not connected to any =
terminal blocks but is instead connected directly to the water detection se=
nsor, I would have to add in terminal blocks and rewire the sensor to those=
