<p local-id=3D"19085c0c-598c-4002-a136-48431e496bef">For machines, are we f=
ree to use any printing process, or do we need to use 3DEO=E2=80=99s proces=
s? How much flexibility is there in machine design (such as replacing the m=
ist box with a binder jetting head, eliminating the spindle in favor of a l=
aser, using pre-coated powder instead of spraying binder, etc.)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c88fa479-bafe-4c18-bd83-4ac0fd48faca">
<p local-id=3D"512a1c0b-c012-497c-a7e1-1fb3625fe21f">Are there equipment re=
quirements based on funding requirements or based on current contracts?</p>=
</li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"ca7483e3-7904-4085-ac3c-59b737335b7a">
<p local-id=3D"022c7a20-124c-4863-bb6c-b1be580fb88a">Once we have a framewo=
rk for the manufacturing services we want to provide and the machine design=
, we need a timeline for figuring out the precise details necessary to star=
t any work. If there are any details that need to be figured out as we go, =
they need to be written down and have dates and action items assigned to re=
sponsible individuals.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"be02158e-37f2-44b3-8b3c-e09b420bbb17">
<p local-id=3D"867bd8bc-324f-46ab-80ce-9c8aa4ae9a7a">This is not a democrac=
y, it is a consensus-based process derived from the Wikipedia process. If a=
nyone disagrees with a detail, they can submit changes to a single Confluen=
ce document, which the original writer can then approve or change. Any intr=
actable disagreements will be elevated to an elected triumvirate. If they a=
re unable to come to unanimous consensus, the final decision will be elevat=
ed to me. The final document must be one that everyone has contributed to a=
nd at least can agree with.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e6210a1e-e473-44c6-8c2f-3f37461325c0">
<p local-id=3D"d5ad5957-4593-42bd-bda9-01391e50e52f">Once everyone in the c=
ompany has signed off on the plan, an organizational structure would be est=
ablished based on the skills, experience, and interests of everyone at the =
company. Consensus would also be established here.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0616233b-2d71-4af2-8ec3-45d069100b24">
<p local-id=3D"c178817f-c7ce-4382-933d-5db2eefe1ad4">Tasks would be broken =
up between responsible parties, with clear responsibilities and required ac=
tions assigned as necessary.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3a8be197-5b92-4550-9ddb-8ac251cfa32f">
<p local-id=3D"486c9a6d-1ea3-47e7-875a-2c436bddc3e6">The status of projects=
 would be assessed regularly and compared with the target timeline, with th=
e particular timeline milestones and scope of projects adjusted as necessar=
y.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"502e9921-01fa-45ad-889c-5907bbce6d4d">2025-11-12</p>
<p local-id=3D"dc82fafd-0406-4d9a-88f4-119dee79ce50">PILOT:</p>
<p local-id=3D"133c076a-8b4c-4220-8ae3-63a3643cc3c2">&nbsp; The electrical =
control cabinet standard in the United States is UL 508A. The PDF documents=
 from Siemens and Eaton related to this standard are attached for your refe=
rence.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p local-id=3D"96a4a774-d0f6-43fb-ac6d-6d6be0173b99">&nbsp; Detailed explan=
ation of the second electrical control cabinet:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"12b679c0-6307-4527-9471-7541020ac3d4">
