<ol start=3D"2" local-id=3D"4d185ca3-7f5a-4988-ac6b-992c07e60c41">
<li local-id=3D"d8b05fa5-cbe9-4123-9d35-df4807c01f62">
<p local-id=3D"01cee731-4950-43bf-9300-c26fe5503913">The original design us=
ed a software-controlled safety controller, but in this new design it has b=
een changed to a industrial standard hardware-controlled safety relay.</p><=
/li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"1f0785b2-a1d7-4bb2-9c54-b5336963e103"><a href=3D"https://www=
.amazon.com/750104-PILZ-Safety-Channel-SEMICONDUCTOR/dp/B07JHRMHFW" class=
=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.amazon.com/750104-PILZ-Safe=
ty-Channel-SEMICONDUCTOR/dp/B07JHRMHFW</a></p>
<ol start=3D"3" local-id=3D"8dd7f3ec-2292-481f-8bfb-8ea0696531d7">
<li local-id=3D"ab8cc2ac-140f-4675-85bd-e1a8c6dbc356">
<p local-id=3D"eb772b5c-406e-4050-a062-cfbadef2d617">This new design still =
uses the original controller and software, with modifications made only to =
the safety controller section. I have already discussed it with ZZ, and he =
agreed.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d1615433-30b6-48fa-a9a3-e1c7f3476780">
<p local-id=3D"93bf514a-21f4-4c7f-a276-04db7d6e4738">Except for components =
powered directly by the Duet, all other components are equipped with fuses,=
 providing individual switching and overload protection for easier daily op=
eration and maintenance.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"ca39a144-59b5-4b72-b435-2c0562a5d2ba"><a href=3D"https://www=
.digikey.com/en/products/detail/wago-corporation/2006-1681-1000-449/1552271=
1?gclsrc=3Daw.ds&amp;gad_source=3D1&amp;gad_campaignid=3D17336967819&amp;gb=
raid=3D0AAAAADrbLljPwA2XJrgC7x_FQViVQo6G6&amp;gclid=3DCjwKCAiA_dDIBhB6EiwAv=
zc1cP0j5I0YZiQWDwFzloWrrKjTFMzgrjEQ6S2vHLO_lgvb4GwrzgwhVxoCKCQQAvD_BwE" loc=
al-id=3D"8082a998-a274-454c-9a19-cbf906e8437f" data-card-appearance=3D"inli=
ne" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.digikey.com/en/pro=
ducts/detail/wago-corporation/2006-1681-1000-449/15522711?gclsrc=3Daw.ds&am=
p;gad_source=3D1&amp;gad_campaignid=3D17336967819&amp;gbraid=3D0AAAAADrbLlj=
PwA2XJrgC7x_FQViVQo6G6&amp;gclid=3DCjwKCAiA_dDIBhB6EiwAvzc1cP0j5I0YZiQWDwFz=
loWrrKjTFMzgrjEQ6S2vHLO_lgvb4GwrzgwhVxoCKCQQAvD_BwE</a></p>
<ol start=3D"5" local-id=3D"0e3d0357-5a44-41bd-b8d3-9e80e3fc4207">
<li local-id=3D"0e8c4e4c-b7b0-4da1-84f2-830b2d21f3d1">
<p local-id=3D"01e879f4-4af0-4f07-ab9b-c791a98cd26f">The original safety do=
or switch used a mechanical locking mechanism: the door could be opened whe=
n powered on, and was locked when power was off. The new design uses an ele=
ctrically locked mechanism: the door cannot be opened when powered on, and =
can be opened when power is off. IDEC&nbsp;HS5L-VD7Y</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"bdc382a2-6957-4d41-a35f-61f4ba57d3be">chrome-extension://efa=
idnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/<a href=3D"https://us.idec.com/idec-us/en/USD=
/medias/B-1715-7-E.pdf?context=3DbWFzdGVyfGRvY3VtZW50c3w3MDk1MjM2fGFwcGxpY2=
F0aW9uL3BkZnxoMjYvaDViLzkzNjg2MzI5ODM1ODIvQi0xNzE1LTctRS5wZGZ8ZmIzOWI2ZWE3Z=
GVhZjdlMzI0ZWIzOTcxNDA0ODkxMWFkZWFmZTQwMDRjOTUxNGEyNzc3NjUxZGY5Mjg4NDA5Nw" =
class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://us.idec.com/idec-us/en/USD=
/medias/B-1715-7-E.pdf?context=3DbWFzdGVyfGRvY3VtZW50c3w3MDk1MjM2fGFwcGxpY2=
F0aW9uL3BkZnxoMjYvaDViLzkzNjg2MzI5ODM1ODIvQi0xNzE1LTctRS5wZGZ8ZmIzOWI2ZWE3Z=
GVhZjdlMzI0ZWIzOTcxNDA0ODkxMWFkZWFmZTQwMDRjOTUxNGEyNzc3NjUxZGY5Mjg4NDA5Nw</=
a></p>
<ol start=3D"6" local-id=3D"166d3f42-806b-45e5-90a6-75225f01646f">
<li local-id=3D"0f9ecfea-a10f-47fc-b6bf-d88365dfda0d">
<p local-id=3D"67f03d5f-f12e-4b4e-b64d-184d8463bd0a">The exhaust fan and in=
take fan were originally designed to operate when power is supplied and sto=
p when power is cut off. In the new design, a mechanical thermostat has bee=
n added to control the fans=E2=80=99 operation. When the temperature inside=
 the electrical cabinet is too high, both fans start running; when the temp=
erature is not high, they remain off.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"637eced6-809c-4616-bbf1-faf206bb1581"><a href=3D"https://www=
.automationdirect.com/adc/shopping/catalog/enclosure_thermal_management_-a-=
_lights/thermostats_-a-_hygrostats/111010-00" class=3D"external-link" rel=
=3D"nofollow">https://www.automationdirect.com/adc/shopping/catalog/enclosu=
re_thermal_management_-a-_lights/thermostats_-a-_hygrostats/111010-00</a></=
p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"98aec0c5-668d-4306-af42-1ceee0b0c83c">
<li local-id=3D"5bebe9ea-c0d1-43ea-b346-e52d09855ec0">
<p local-id=3D"8a4c08cc-175f-4a0c-afca-75ed5e279467">It should be fine to r=
eplace the bulbs with 24 VDC equivalents. The PTC heater works differently =
from our current heater so we probably wouldn't want to swap it in; the PTC=
 heater works by forced convection of hot air and our current heater works =
by radiation heating of the build.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4719a5bf-6814-48a7-b74e-8c184ac5bf05">
<p local-id=3D"75d1459f-9f5c-413e-ba3f-768bff745231">The current safety con=
troller is programmable but it is&nbsp;ISO 13849-1 PL e certified and along=
 with the attached safety relay meets the Epson requirements for a safety s=
ystem, but if the alternative safety relay meets the same certifications an=
d has the same functionality for our needs, feel free to switch to it.</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"0c7b68d1-dca0-47fb-ac47-d596536151b7">
<p local-id=3D"a3083c0d-b8bc-4690-a1fa-eefb1eada5d7">I personally prefer to=
 put circuit breakers on every power supply instead of fuses so that they c=
an be switched on and off without having to pull components and if they tri=
p they don't need a fuse to be replaced, and I've never seen fuses used on =
modern industrial machinery, but from a safety perspective single-use fuses=
 should be equivalent. We'll just need to make sure to keep a stock of all =
the different fuse values around. The particular fuse specified from DigiKe=
y is also only UL rated to 12V, so you may need to specify a different mode=
l depending on the component.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"75989cf7-9fd8-4438-8265-a64c5c7e2ea2">
<p local-id=3D"61388233-9ab9-40e6-b4d2-82838cb8902a">The current safety int=
erlocks use an electromagnetic solenoid which unlocks the door when powered=
, which means that if there is a power loss of the safety circuit or if the=
 wire to the safety interlock is cut, the door will automatically lock, pre=
venting the operator from accessing any moving machinery. This is inherentl=
y safe but inconvenient because it is impossible to access the machine if i=
t is turned off when the doors are closed. The suggested safety interlock w=
orks in the opposite way, so that any time the safety system loses power or=
 if the wires to the safety interlock break, the door will automatically un=
lock, so the operator can access the inside of the machine. This would be m=
ore convenient because the machine can be accessed when the machine is off,=
 but is less inherently safe.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e8502102-85f0-4ae8-94e3-fd9344e4678f">
<p local-id=3D"7e9e3654-7f8f-4dbe-9251-893929d4dba0">Because the fans are p=
owered with AC they will see a current spike and increased wear if they are=
 turned on and off repeatedly instead of running continuously, so they will=
 have a shorter lifespan when connected to a temperature controller, and th=
e components in the control cabinet will see fluctuations as the fans are t=
urned on and off instead of have a continuous flow of air cooling them, but=
 the total energy usage might be slightly reduced by keeping the fans off s=
ome of the time.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"8c6765d2-b494-41f8-aeb5-22ac13041040"></p>
<p local-id=3D"a8a4ce22-f9fb-4cc3-8a73-d07bdc4ad778"></p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"61ec3f64-e135-468d-a79d-484f9917820d">
<li local-id=3D"d667bb56-9dd9-4225-8147-42e91efdf735">
<p local-id=3D"8a3aa719-b2c9-4166-8d5e-b2464c9ff55e">I follow the method yo=
u mention: the heater=E2=80=99s structure remains unchanged; just replace t=
he bulbs from 12V DC to 24V DC.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b5503e4f-c5ee-4300-a128-714c2188f993">
<p local-id=3D"eb0e1398-8383-4100-a077-8156a8c81e05">The new safety relay c=
omplies with the&nbsp; safety system equipment Code, I will try to assemble=
 it and you can test after installation.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2cda6b6f-1964-4eab-81ec-b24c8b228809">
<p local-id=3D"78abaa2a-1b0c-412b-af1a-b240d21d3017">I will follow your sug=
gestion to replace the six Fuses of the power supply with circuit breakers.=
 The other fuses will remain as per the new design.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7b60ceee-2db2-4450-b48b-39fbf397acb7">
<p local-id=3D"e0064242-e8ef-44d6-9999-c388ad24770e">The current safety doo=
r switch is installed inside the door, and if the power is off, the door ca=
nnot be opened from the outside. I suggest replacing it with a new safety d=
oor switch. Let=E2=80=99s try using this new one =E2=80=94 if you think it=
=E2=80=99s not suitable, I can revert to the original design.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b1ef1db5-2219-4341-ad7c-49bfbab17e40">
<p local-id=3D"d55707fa-c11f-466b-8766-9ae6e6049461">This mechanical thermo=
stat only costs 23 dollars. Let=E2=80=99s buy one and try it out =E2=80=94 =
if you think it=E2=80=99s suitable, we=E2=80=99ll keep it; if not, we can r=
eturn it. The circuit requires almost no modification.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"8ef0f690-e162-4197-8ead-ec54493990d8"></p>
<p local-id=3D"a019e23d-0daf-443f-a714-5f7e08b1af5b">Can you create a formu=
la of a paste for this application?</p>
<p local-id=3D"8ba3aa37-ec84-4ab5-ad21-3e8f13b4559f">I can provide a genera=
l formulation framework, though I should note that optimal recipes require =
experimental refinement for your specific preceramic polymer, printer, and =
target application.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"82042313-1c6a-4a04-9913-6abf1cd95943" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-BasicSiloxane-BasedPasteFormulation">Basic Siloxane-Based Paste Formulat=
ion</h2>
<p local-id=3D"162ee0ea-5a74-48f6-b732-d2b1c7c80dfa">Here's a starting poin=
t for a DIW-compatible paste:</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"f65c6aa7-25c9-459c-a34c-61be06d68143" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Components(byweight)">Components (by weight)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"f12e8dc4-d68c-4838-8658-e9df7ba27bd3"><strong>Preceramic Pol=
ymer (40-50%)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"1e1c71b3-1061-4a84-89fc-98a205883726">
<li local-id=3D"f64a09a6-95f2-4ebe-9c6b-af2ea1ab9b4c">
<p local-id=3D"18e03b7e-5e8f-4fd0-8b9f-8646a96622e5">Polysiloxane resin (e.=
g., methylphenylsiloxane or polymethylsiloxane)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fd356bdf-06f4-4ab0-ad6c-f5726a887959">
<p local-id=3D"91799b79-0114-479d-9243-10a4d2ea0ab2">Should be partially cr=
oss-linked or reactive to allow further curing</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"4322c05e-dffb-4e47-9cb5-996ab0a9b752"><strong>Ceramic Filler=
 (30-45%)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"2a851092-974c-494e-b78c-7c7dccdb2ea0">
<li local-id=3D"0e0a1589-13ae-4c72-955f-2ff361775fd8">
<p local-id=3D"13c287ee-095d-4cba-a4eb-c19a8df59a19">SiC powder (submicron,=
 ~0.5-5 =CE=BCm particle size)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d336c5e7-52cc-43ba-bcd8-5b5e9f507d49">
<p local-id=3D"7c1706ad-24c7-40f6-9970-2e0486d1739b">Purpose: Reduces shrin=
kage, improves density</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c6991eb0-2ad3-4e34-9a84-13005b3e06d8">
<p local-id=3D"fc97f6af-0266-4b9c-b25e-96bd98f1e288">Can substitute with Si=
O=E2=82=82, Si=E2=82=83N=E2=82=84, or other compatible ceramics</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"f6f0a8cc-fd90-42ec-89d1-ae78c18f8f8a"><strong>Rheology Modif=
ier (3-8%)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"1a137e5a-64fc-4513-8839-7b8b1d42c03c">
<li local-id=3D"11311179-d6f7-49e7-bac3-3ab611b2673f">
<p local-id=3D"146c9d97-b577-468c-9edc-eb29c023b5b1">Fumed silica (e.g., Ae=
rosil 200) - most common choice</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"99a5ef50-7168-4b5d-b43b-1c3f21bde5d6">
<p local-id=3D"39137394-724c-421d-9649-780d395f0b98">Or: bentonite clay, hy=
droxyethyl cellulose</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4eb8ad94-a295-4aca-9ad8-9577ae2f4b2d">
<p local-id=3D"7b442606-1c30-4bd7-b62d-37b319e0baca">Creates shear-thinning=
 behavior and structural recovery</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"b944db06-822e-4414-9fe5-b47d408f06ba"><strong>Solvent (5-15%=
)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"8c4d8ea9-8975-417b-a75f-7ec99b8c2b7e">
<li local-id=3D"8effc4b1-de7b-419e-8957-f725cdd66a5c">
<p local-id=3D"8b37784f-edd4-486c-afa7-632e60a748fe">Toluene, xylene, or pe=
troleum ether</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"39a57869-fced-49da-bf25-7302f29c7004">
<p local-id=3D"8d9941fd-0427-44a1-9b40-814e90aeb56b">Adjusts viscosity for =
printability</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e7ed5e92-381a-46e5-a448-1965efbfb87b">
<p local-id=3D"3b939167-0702-4bb2-a82c-dfe8c4c93dfb">Lower amounts =3D thic=
ker paste</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"936c37eb-7736-4f9e-8998-31fcae8aed59"><strong>Cross-linking =
Catalyst (0.5-2%)</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"8f5598f2-62ea-46dc-8a58-74a8f277bdeb">
<li local-id=3D"5dc7d48c-2e91-46da-a35c-2314f6572f7d">
<p local-id=3D"9e8f75a8-2201-4123-86b3-6b724bf02311">Platinum catalyst for =
hydrosilylation (if using Si-H functional groups)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"564ecee0-e5c6-4ea2-8e8b-63276c20eb8d">
<p local-id=3D"21f92d86-5c62-4f91-b264-f0e91b1c0dec">Or: peroxide initiator=
s for free radical cross-linking</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3f5f1ca7-234a-4748-842c-a71ab12a3019">
<p local-id=3D"6c208aec-d44d-4a49-89e1-efb9851d8635">Enables curing after p=
rinting</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"9edb93fd-40cd-4b8f-9841-ea568546ea52" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ExampleStartingRecipe">Example Starting Recipe</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">- 45g p=
olysiloxane resin
- 35g SiC powder (1-3 =CE=BCm)
- 5g fumed silica
- 10g toluene
- 1g platinum catalyst (Karstedt's catalyst, 2% Pt)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 local-id=3D"6c41b67b-9adf-4f7b-87b1-31cd6ae45927" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-MixingProcedure">Mixing Procedure</h2>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"e39d9796-0401-4d6e-a0fa-af7c2afc795b">
<li local-id=3D"32dc6838-f4d0-4deb-a01a-5526b1311158">
<p local-id=3D"6d02119f-966f-432a-a933-04dccc37896a"><strong>Dissolve</stro=
ng> the preceramic polymer in solvent if needed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e218b1e5-ed11-46e0-830f-763305cf87cb">
<p local-id=3D"fcd82cdd-6e78-4869-b019-52f07d66abcc"><strong>Add filler</st=
rong> gradually while mixing (planetary mixer or high-shear mixer)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a5db8cc9-931a-4158-be73-af3134062303">
<p local-id=3D"98c1152c-9a43-4398-a882-754c98d2f474"><strong>Incorporate rh=
eology modifier</strong> - mix thoroughly (30+ minutes)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6254c503-a0c6-4270-8852-2a800b476a3b">
<p local-id=3D"ab0812b5-9088-45c1-a6aa-71f8e7b5d6c5"><strong>Add catalyst</=
strong> last, mix briefly</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"25f4b284-96ce-49fc-92c6-92a2de6cea31">
<p local-id=3D"12b48cb5-403b-4982-beec-61dbd1deb5d3"><strong>Degas</strong>=
 under vacuum to remove air bubbles</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"794647ed-39c1-4c35-928d-8217243078b7">
<p local-id=3D"6108c381-9cd8-4dfa-a8c3-4207f7f86d0f">Store in sealed contai=
ner (shelf life depends on catalyst reactivity)</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"69ba5076-83f6-4805-9c1a-bdbe3058ff19" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-TargetRheologicalProperties">Target Rheological Properties</h2>
<ul local-id=3D"28b55391-e761-4c8e-b794-73ab16ddc65f">
<li local-id=3D"457718ea-c026-41b4-b909-4832aec5a6bd">
<p local-id=3D"817c2048-90b7-4cb1-ba18-50a260dfa95d"><strong>Viscosity</str=
ong>: 10-100 Pa=C2=B7s at rest</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"412875ae-79d2-44e8-839b-6d5781d0b4a9">
<p local-id=3D"64f7f45c-ade0-49c8-96d8-c17d03510430"><strong>Shear-thinning=
 index</strong>: 0.3-0.6</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5d5d4a68-7c63-4d32-bd0e-14df56b56aed">
<p local-id=3D"ce9e78db-672e-4ba8-8e32-ac1877a866d6"><strong>Yield stress</=
strong>: 100-1000 Pa</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6c7a888d-b384-4043-8e3c-84ac6533edc3">
<p local-id=3D"bebbf3b3-0c70-4e35-96be-200f36a15a9d">Should extrude smoothl=
y but hold shape immediately after deposition</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"a9c5d0ef-77bf-49ca-b028-07d7d7064e9f" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Curing&amp;PyrolysisProtocol">Curing &amp; Pyrolysis Protocol</h2>
<p local-id=3D"0122c691-ac82-4325-9af6-29f677e30a7d"><strong>Curing</strong=
> (green part):</p>
<ul local-id=3D"78696656-4bcd-48df-ae2a-e1d09595f027">
<li local-id=3D"4f3f6c31-91fc-478e-8945-0735c9fbe827">
<p local-id=3D"c82d3e8f-c1c5-452c-8ba7-99b5845998fc">80-150=C2=B0C for 1-4 =
hours (depends on catalyst system)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fe3ba6b3-98c4-46e6-94f0-e6c7c925ec38">
<p local-id=3D"2f3a1632-4096-4717-a4ff-9ab50f451cc1">Can also use UV-curabl=
e systems with appropriate photoinitiators</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"2234707e-b657-4ef0-ad84-2c9eaaaff932"><strong>Pyrolysis</str=
ong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"68e9e02d-ee28-4122-b206-84c4d6ba34e4">
<li local-id=3D"14fcced1-0ab4-4337-8b0c-f163e84e85e4">
<p local-id=3D"e5997b1d-4e7f-4587-b5df-1ccf4a623b1b">Slow ramp: 1-5=C2=B0C/=
min to 800-1200=C2=B0C</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"15a661e9-9ce8-48fd-aefb-849f1d9f8205">
<p local-id=3D"bf76feff-724f-44c2-a854-8dd7887772df">Hold time: 1-2 hours</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e6b4c924-dee9-4a6e-9aba-bda6b32bd255">
<p local-id=3D"7e0c4dc6-5354-4e0d-a0c8-7fc3dfeed3ad">Atmosphere: Argon or n=
itrogen</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6b04173a-f666-4d2e-b7cb-43a609571b58">
<p local-id=3D"e16a98ab-5a48-459a-aed5-ba2ef3e4e8df">Expect 25-40% linear s=
hrinkage (less with high filler loading)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"8d9f2eca-9a1e-48ed-994f-f505b1dfceb2" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-ImportantConsiderations">Important Considerations</h2>
<p local-id=3D"e98b027e-7fa8-4274-8455-f24e43de834d"><strong>Safety</strong=
>: Work with adequate ventilation - solvents are flammable and toxic, pyrol=
ysis produces volatile organics</p>
<p local-id=3D"c49ea4ee-4464-49e1-bea6-3e82109b1c63"><strong>Adjustments ne=
eded</strong>: You'll need to tune this empirically by:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"44e35769-e2c5-429c-b23c-bcfd66dbdb88">
<li local-id=3D"f641c32f-3cf1-4293-81f7-ae21d6518301">
<p local-id=3D"40bd61d9-a20c-4622-8b9c-6059c1ff5a3c">Adjusting filler loadi=
ng (more =3D less shrinkage, harder to print)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2e9a87db-f3f0-4727-bdb4-1cb387285606">
<p local-id=3D"b62876e8-a6ea-4513-80eb-ee6b23e14805">Varying rheology modif=
ier amount (more =3D stiffer paste)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5e29c54a-f446-47b2-aef8-975c393c1281">
<p local-id=3D"94addd0c-78f6-4b5e-827d-0e7cf03c7a4a">Testing different nozz=
le sizes (0.4-1.0mm typical)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"26f4538f-20d1-4c9f-9f1d-4f7ad4b56b80">
<p local-id=3D"ba47d329-2018-4c9f-b4ca-b49064c343ac">Optimizing layer heigh=
t and print speed</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"ce87595e-21fa-472e-aa72-ae193fe7ea06"><strong>Commercial alt=
ernatives</strong>: Companies like Tethon3D and Lithoz sell proprietary cer=
amic/preceramic pastes if you want a more proven starting point.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c7d4247e-2310-48aa-b0bb-0475ee8b586a"></p>
<p local-id=3D"966af87e-298f-4595-951e-0d78df1fb559">2025-11-13</p>
<p local-id=3D"d73fb781-57aa-404e-8f51-dea397362aed">PILOT: Printing 1 set =
of powder catch boxes. Went over next steps for assembling PILOTs 6 and 7; =
I recommended installing the components inside the machine chamber that wil=
l need cables run to them, such as the IR camera, TEC, and the 3X BME280 se=
nsors.</p>
<p local-id=3D"da6ab19b-2741-4030-808f-5f602103c9a5"></p>
<p local-id=3D"ca000d7e-edf1-4dcf-90dd-d563ec292fff">2025-11-14</p>
<p local-id=3D"158c6b9a-d487-4602-a352-e11318ef676c">PILOT: Continuing to r=
un 3D prints for the 2 PIP printers. Maintenance on Mahmood=E2=80=99s Bambu=
 X1C printer in the R&amp;D lab. Ordered rubber seals and nylon washers for=
 installing the acrylic panels on the PIPs. Repairing the CAD assembly of t=
he new model heater; many of the parts had been moved to a PILOT folder Wil=
l had set up a while back, so I copied them to my active folder and fixed t=
he assembly.</p>
<p local-id=3D"73cff06b-f0ce-45af-8f4e-4522ef387f86">2025-11-17</p>
<p local-id=3D"54db5427-7060-4b5d-aaa2-a8d63cc55458">PILOT: Plan is to crea=
te the necessary square cutouts in the cabinet for PILOT 7. Ning is current=
ly marking out the cutouts and drilling the pilot holes necessary for inser=
ting the jigsaw blade to start the cuts. Really the only time consuming par=
t of the square cutouts is placing the blue masking tape that protects the =
cabinet powder coating from being scratched. Modified design of the door la=
tch mount to align with and be supported by the slot of the Vention extrusi=
on; it currently is supported by the outermost 2 flat surfaces that are adj=
acent to the slot, which means that when the screws are tightened they have=
 a tendency to crush the part into the slot.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2be57f6d-5048-49c8-bc23-d5589d70293e">2025-11-18</p>
<p local-id=3D"3fc9a427-f906-4d96-9f4b-473e62e74a61">PILOT: Printing Duet b=
oard mounts on Mahmood=E2=80=99s Bambu printer. Need to design and print bl=
anking plates for the opening in the top of the cabinet for an industrial g=
rade monitor mount that will no longer be used.</p>
<p local-id=3D"43ed8300-23a3-4efa-8219-081e25e86739">CERAMIC: Got approval =
from Marcus to dedicate 15% of my time to ceramic printing experiments. Sin=
ce I have not been too busy with the pilot printers because most of the act=
ual assembly and wiring is being done by others, I am working on some side =
R&amp;D, such as considering the architecture of the next-generation printe=
r design, as well as experimenting with pre-coating 17-4 powder with PEG as=
 a companion experiment to the PEG no-depowdering approach.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9eb3b4b4-0cb5-4a90-b616-16eca5245a03">2025-11-19</p>
<p local-id=3D"c04dffe0-c607-46fe-91a3-5f08a254f1ec">PILOT: The 50X Vention=
 zip tie mount print last night failed (layer shift?) so I am running the 1=
0X zip tie mount print that I believe was successful.</p>
<p local-id=3D"49a5b3a4-9216-401b-8ccb-69955e3cfd1e">CERAMIC: I received 5 =
lb of 8 micron silicon carbide powder from McMaster; it is intended to be u=
sed as an abrasive medium for lapping compounds, so the particles are quite=
 sharp and angular rather than rounded as might be desired for 3D printing =
and sintering. Mahmood and I looked at it with the Keyence microscope, and =
the particle size did indeed seem to be 7-8 micron. This is also how I foun=
d out that the particles are very sharp. I mixed up a binder recipe that is=
 20g of Poly(vinyl alcohol) 87-90% hydrolyzed, average mol wt 30,000-70,000=
 and 10g of colloidal silica along with DI water for a total volume of 100 =
mL. I then mixed 50 mL of this binder recipe with 250g of the silicon carbi=
de powder for a binder load of roughly 6%, although I discovered during the=
 mixing process that the PVA had not fully dissolved in the water after mix=
ing at room temperature overnight, so the actual binder load is likely clos=
er to 5%.</p>
<p local-id=3D"400b8f48-7c67-4884-a693-f82f8f19255f">2025-11-20</p>
<p local-id=3D"b3043c72-f0b5-4b5f-bdeb-0de6e2f467e2">PILOT: Showed Devin wh=
ere the monitor and keyboard mounts need to be installed and gave him the d=
rawings generated by NEMA custom cabinets. Continuing to printed and assemb=
le the USB and HDMI pass throughs for replacing the RoxTech blocks.</p>
<p local-id=3D"58dedf1e-6455-46a9-ae9d-5e29ac2ca0c2">CERAMIC: Marcus did no=
t want to place my order for ceramic precursor polymers from Sigma Aldrich =
(<a href=3D"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/mm/818063" class=3D"=
external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/=
mm/818063</a>) so I need to alter my approach. I am exploring the possibili=
ty of making a binder recipe to pre coatedp owder using a combination of PV=
A and Boric Acid, which fortunately Payman bought a packet of for his binde=
r experiment.</p>
<p local-id=3D"250d16c6-d70a-493c-ad8c-6bea40b005d9">2025-11-21</p>
<p local-id=3D"0b6f1b12-418f-4a0a-a2c8-10ec1fe3cbd3">PILOT: Printed and ass=
embled the pass-though plate with 2X USB and 1X HDMI bulkhead pass-through =
components. Cleaned 2X U and V tank endstop mounts printed from ESD safe re=
sin on the FormLabs printer. Placed them in the curing chamber but forgot t=
o start the curing process so it is currently running.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3c1824df-a6c5-442c-92b3-167fb042f4f5">CERAMIC: The ceramic c=
rucible that I filled with coated silicon carbide powder and heated to 300F=
 did not form a strong green part, when I inverted the crucible to drop the=
 part onto a ZTE setter the part fell apart. This may be due to heating to =
too low of a temperature, or because the binder does not adhere well to sil=
icon carbide, or the particle size is too small, etc. etc.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4759c1cb-b95d-434b-9f44-3b40f30eb25b">2025-11-24</p>
<p local-id=3D"d8eb4c0e-bd58-44f0-b2ab-1cc2271a4c1f">CERAMIC: My latest bin=
der recipe is:</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"cf0e6b45-ec63-4d21-a84a-2ab28b350526" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-Recipefor1000gCoated17-4Powder">Recipe for 1000g Coated 17-4 Powder</h2>
<p local-id=3D"15d8762f-e57e-48f1-a809-60831a19c390"><strong>Target:</stron=
g> 1000g coated powder (1.5% binder by weight)</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"31dcd25c-3466-4509-8bf2-9f69890c5264" id=3D"JaredHumphreysL=
og-IngredientQuantities">Ingredient Quantities</h3>
<p local-id=3D"df317d2a-158b-4852-a85f-63a7643e6fae"><strong>Dry ingredient=
s:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"8f2f725c-9f08-462f-8c38-0040bb1cc48a">
<li local-id=3D"09c1fd83-ea16-486b-82c3-e6441feba4fb">
<p local-id=3D"e7257453-e7e0-4ad8-b648-3a27ebf202c2">17-4 stainless steel p=
owder: <strong>985.2g</strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e72e3485-ad82-47b3-88b3-fada55d82621">
<p local-id=3D"bb698083-b174-4b87-9201-cd5e82221459">PVA (87-89% hydrolyzed=
, medium MW): <strong>10.0g</strong> (1.0% of powder weight)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0cd11d3a-d37c-4af3-910e-ef1285e4f3da">
<p local-id=3D"c0d25e13-e4bd-444b-bea6-a6c796c53f52">PEG 6000: <strong>5.0g=
</strong> (0.5% of powder weight)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e8fca653-0376-4adc-98f0-3f91be7a58aa"><strong>Liquid additiv=
es:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"a01554ad-61fe-415e-9d19-cf2f3f8ed2af">
<li local-id=3D"7d355fda-bf6b-478d-8a0a-d62452ead279">
<p local-id=3D"01b3f243-9c52-48b0-a938-79327596314a">Glycerol: <strong>1.5g=
</strong> (10% of total binder weight)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2c86a39b-7f2c-4bf2-8ec1-10260953d5de">
<p local-id=3D"df9b6ca5-10e9-4c5b-b353-698629ca565a">Deionized water: <stro=
ng>150-200g</strong> (adjust for desired slurry consistency)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"cc256cd5-25b1-47df-a96e-3497ba320e80"><strong>Total binder c=
ontent: 15.0g (1.5% of final coated powder weight)</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"6484d55d-aba8-48dd-bb8e-7667ae604afa">This has a lower total=
 binder content and has PEG 6000 and glycerol added to increase friability =
and grindability of the cake, hopefully without compromising the binding pr=
operties</p>
<p local-id=3D"18cbdce2-1005-43f2-9c72-ff7d17013df8">PILOT: Working on desi=
gn of sheet metal or machined U and V tank endstop mounts. Working on assem=
bling the pressure and flow regulator stack. Showed Senai how to wire and i=
nstall the water leakage sensor. Went over wiring the RTD for detecting the=
 heater temperature with Cisco. Received cables for wiring the safety inter=
locks; they will not be installed to the doors but will be wired to the saf=
ety system so that the safety system at Epson can be troubleshot remotely.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"8a4bf34d-e16c-43b6-b1f1-5128994e250a">2025-11-25</p>
<p local-id=3D"fd9f3fa1-fd54-489d-88d0-29e1a1e66e89">PILOT: Received spiral=
 cord grip for 4X safety interlocks. Began wiring. Assembled and installed =
the compressed air handling stack, which comprises a 1/4=E2=80=9D industria=
l male quick disconnect fitting, a bulkhead pass-through, a pressure regula=
tor, a flow regulator, and a solenoid valve. Began laser engraving and inst=
alling cabinet labels. Engraved and installed printer name labels (=E2=80=
=9CPILOT 6=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9CPILOT 7=E2=80=9D), Raspberry Pi USB labels=
, and Safety System Reset labels.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2ee1ec38-d231-4125-ad75-03250456f993">R&amp;D: Overview meet=
ing with Alex discussing goals and progress so far of the no-depowdering ex=
periments.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b235381f-3e6e-45f5-9bba-6c3cb8447c43">CERAMIC: Mixed up a ne=
w batch of slurry with 1.5% binder load, 1% PVA and .5% PVP-VA. Experimente=
d with crosslinking PEG 400 by dissolving citric acid in PEG 400 liquid and=
 heating it to 100C, which had no apparent effect.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d564f79a-fec7-404b-a839-9c8edf61ffba">2025-11-26</p>
<p local-id=3D"5a084bdd-35ed-4942-b9bf-bb5cc44723c2">HOPPER: There have bee=
n issues with stepper motor failure on Mason=E2=80=99s machined hopper, so =
I am exploring different higher-torque motor options. Requested to order 2X=
:</p>
<p local-id=3D"d7b76b3e-7d63-49e4-ba1d-5a1d635690a4"><a href=3D"https://www=
.amazon.com/100-Planetary-Gearbox-Stepper-Torque/dp/B00PNEQPCU/ref=3Dsr_1_4=
?crid=3D14TF2V207UK3X&amp;dib=3DeyJ2IjoiMSJ9.YGGmFPVHjvqRn2CoyzA3FMyVVmK3gY=
zAz_ppjKJFi7r6FPkPGdNmNVV54J1oqI0ODebg7xz6o_uYFhlIZSLxYNFhIUCYG6pvhdQAvuDbn=
H4Im6w_SdFi9-bPkIDzRqqIol5tQvk5y8OayK0bIOW5zyG1urFuyuqNDuIE386ctTy2zPz7fHb3=
gyGXd1rLwzC_ghPB39-c2SbCVRDoOa1Sj7CV6kug9GkrnS53zH51vDo.jHI98J-uTin-Uzlbgg3=
dWkU6PTMcLkB1alCziF7WIxM&amp;dib_tag=3Dse&amp;keywords=3Dnema+11+geared+ste=
pper+motor+100%3A1&amp;qid=3D1764183114&amp;sprefix=3Dnema+11+geared+steppe=
r+motor+100+1%2Caps%2C148&amp;sr=3D8-4" local-id=3D"ca4cbd29-7a6c-4937-a36a=
-31377115bcb9" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" class=3D"external-link" rel=
=3D"nofollow">https://www.amazon.com/100-Planetary-Gearbox-Stepper-Torque/d=
p/B00PNEQPCU/ref=3Dsr_1_4?crid=3D14TF2V207UK3X&amp;dib=3DeyJ2IjoiMSJ9.YGGmF=
PVHjvqRn2CoyzA3FMyVVmK3gYzAz_ppjKJFi7r6FPkPGdNmNVV54J1oqI0ODebg7xz6o_uYFhlI=
ZSLxYNFhIUCYG6pvhdQAvuDbnH4Im6w_SdFi9-bPkIDzRqqIol5tQvk5y8OayK0bIOW5zyG1urF=
uyuqNDuIE386ctTy2zPz7fHb3gyGXd1rLwzC_ghPB39-c2SbCVRDoOa1Sj7CV6kug9GkrnS53zH=
51vDo.jHI98J-uTin-Uzlbgg3dWkU6PTMcLkB1alCziF7WIxM&amp;dib_tag=3Dse&amp;keyw=
ords=3Dnema+11+geared+stepper+motor+100%3A1&amp;qid=3D1764183114&amp;sprefi=
x=3Dnema+11+geared+stepper+motor+100+1%2Caps%2C148&amp;sr=3D8-4</a></p>
<p local-id=3D"70f281e4-5056-4178-8468-823fc7c2c7b7">CERAMIC: Exploring pho=
tocured binder options. Combined 10g TEG-DMA, 10g PEG 400, and .2g photoini=
tiator:</p>
<p local-id=3D"de1509da-22d4-4a3e-88f1-12be9b25ecd0"><a href=3D"https://www=
.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/511447" class=3D"external-link" rel=
=3D"nofollow">https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/aldrich/511447</a>=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"85ea0ae3-ec39-4457-ab6e-03f1e59718e5">Then exposed it to UV =
light in the cheaper UV curing chamber. It hardened rapidly into an opaque =
white semi-flexible solid.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b9c0305c-cec7-4ba3-8bc2-c1739236426e">Mixed up a batch of 1 =
kg of coated powder with a 1.5% binder load with 1% PVA and .5% PVP-VA to t=
ry drying it in two different ways. I poured a thin layer in a pie tin and =
put it on the hot plate at 100C for several hours, and poured the rest into=
 a pie tin left to dry at room temperature. The thin layer was crispy but e=
asy to break apart, likely because it is so thin (~1mm instead of the usual=
 6-7mm). It would be easier to grind when it starts as a thin layer, but I =
don=E2=80=99t believe it is any more friable than it would be if cured more=
 slowly. I hope that the batch left to dry at room temperature will be more=
 friable, but I don=E2=80=99t have high hopes for it. When I return from th=
e Thanksgiving break I will make a new batch with maltodextrin as a binding=
 ingredient, which will hopefully inhibit PVA linking when the slurry is dr=
ied into a cake but will assist with particle binding when the dry coated p=
owder is heated.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e091ad5b-a0ad-4fb1-a8bb-3d7db88b658d">PILOT: Completed wirin=
g of 2X door safety interlocks.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7347f6e1-80c6-4079-9834-7eae150b693f">2025-12-1</p>
<p local-id=3D"a22fd8eb-857b-44c4-8785-be267021be81">CERAMIC: Ordered some =
maltodextrin off of Amazon. The theory is to make a pre-coated binder recip=
e that is 10g of PVA and 5g of maltodextrin, which will hopefully make the =
dried cake more friable while allowing the final sieved powder to bind when=
 heated more easily.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4d84a45e-27b9-4820-b91e-70aa9fe75428">Trying a new binder re=
cipe with 17-4 PH powder:</p>
