 height=3D"181"></span>
<p local-id=3D"d6507da0-38e1-4f05-b352-1fa3a67303f7">Note the shielded but =
freely rotating hose duct joint on the bottom.</p>
<p local-id=3D"08934b3a-4ebe-4827-9799-d095258f5427">I removed the new thre=
e-pour mold for making the vibrating hat vibration isolator and added a lar=
ge number of pour holes; because the urethane rubber is quite viscous it do=
es not tend to flow well through the narrow channels I am trying to fill, s=
o I have added pour holes with a scalpel and did a urethane pour by pouring=
 into every other pour hole so the others can act as air outlets. That way =
the urethane only needs to flow ~1=E2=80=9D along the inside of the mold in=
stead of ~6=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p local-id=3D"48b1354a-1ac8-41b0-a1de-386b01f6d4f1">I have started a print=
 on the Bambu printer for all the remaining parts necessary for a FLIP prot=
otype.</p>
<p local-id=3D"44d89223-ed57-4ee8-9649-2c7934c8f2b8">I am printing two part=
s for Mohsen, a muffler clamp that I added to my Bambu PETG-CF print and a =
larger box print that I am running on the Ultimaker S5 Thanos because it=E2=
=80=99s not worth using up a bunch of the PETG-CF filament.</p>
<p local-id=3D"852e41fc-9a47-43c2-8a3c-881a64c13015">I am continuing to wor=
k on the design of the rotating hose duct interface. I think the FLIP-side =
interface is pretty solid, so I have moved to the vibrating hat-side interf=
ace.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3d1b69ce-c0d6-486e-8306-f8dae830c42a">2026-01-28</p>
<p local-id=3D"b25ee65b-9ec2-40b2-9efb-93434b10170f">Alloyed Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"ed32b18e-f22b-420b-a05b-73531fc03351">Joined a meeting betwe=
en various people from the company Alloyed and 3DEO.</p>
<p local-id=3D"618c3f61-964a-4491-a6ee-d05b7cbfd2ce">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"cb536e6b-56db-4b76-a78e-c7fff173f2d0">Demolded the vibration=
 isolator for the vibrating hat. It has some voids at the top of the part, =
but for the most part it came out pretty well. I think the voids are small =
and localized enough that it should seal sufficiently.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b7afd90f-af4b-4df9-ace2-7901d9565b1a">I have redesigned the =
rotating duct mounts so that they use a spiral retaining ring instead of pr=
inted teeth; this should be a more durable method for locking the rotating =
duct to the bearings.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ebf2a725-6577-45d8-a48c-da438a8a02f4">2026-01-29</p>
<p local-id=3D"cd4cf3d8-8717-4783-a142-8e2d50cfb301">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"044e3468-03a2-44ec-9d6e-e0f91b685444">Completed print of the=
 new vibrating hat design. Machined 2X splined shafts for the powder cartri=
dge. Machined a short piece of splined shaft and glued it into a splined bu=
shing to make a custom stepper motor-splined shaft coupler. Drilled and rea=
med a 6mm hole for the stepper motor shaft through the splined shaft that h=
ad been glued into the bushing. Tomorrow I will drill and tap two holes at =
right angles to install set screws to lock the coupler onto the stepper mot=
or shaft. Installed heat set inserts in the vibrating hat and the cartridge=
 dock. I test assembled the two rotating duct hose adapters and two bearing=
 clamps, and modified the design of the cartridge dock rotating duct hose a=
dapter and both bearing clamps based on fit testing of the original design.=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"22064fea-d37f-4883-bcfa-897feb030910">Joined Alex=E2=80=99s =
debrief on events in Japan with Sean, Senai, Payman, and Marcus. He visited=
 Epson and the facility where they are running the two pilot printers as we=
ll as some other companies and the two banks Mizuho and DBJ. He said that t=
he visits were generally positive but we did not get any new funding.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b5f64fe2-c8d0-4f3d-9b69-d52730d8d287">2026-01-30</p>
<p local-id=3D"a4301750-8df6-45be-8ae9-86cd6a420067">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"de15276d-4014-4ad7-a10b-8ea1b7c3a39f">The new parts printed =
last night seem good; they hold the bearings in place and shield them while=
 not interfering with their rotation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"511e5a96-9c17-4865-bf9b-a3d6e6af8667">I am starting to work =
on the sensors. I am concerned about the TOF sensors building up powder, an=
d since they claim to be able to detect distances through windows I am desi=
gning a new bayonet style prox switch holder that the board can be mounted =
to and will have a window that the sensor beam passes through. This will ma=
ke it easy to remove the board and clean the window before each print or wh=
enever readings become faulty.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f8aeaf0042ef">R&amp;D Weekly Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"31bbaf5db49c">To Do:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"c6469064a5d5">
<li local-id=3D"84d1aa0a4bee">
<p local-id=3D"69f53178a901">Bring up microcontroller and sensors</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"870b469724cd">
<p local-id=3D"46a3cb47b8ac">Continue prototyping of assembly and start cyc=
le testing of hopper gate</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"de5cd116f19a">
<p local-id=3D"e39d7bda8519">Find large end mill/fly cutter for facing cake=
 after meltable filler has been applied</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"8e4048d7-c656-45e0-9cdb-03c1a66ee945">2026-02-02</p>
<p local-id=3D"c601c6af-355b-43f1-a1fd-916f41daf870">HOPPER:</p>
<p local-id=3D"555ca8b7-8664-4642-a26f-88be5c2f27fb">Need to generate an im=
age of the hopper/dispenser CAD to send to Marcus for the board meeting sli=
de deck.</p>
<p local-id=3D"05874a5d-129a-41f2-a93b-b8b39c542304">HOPPER:</p>
<p local-id=3D"3efaab49-2e29-4a0b-901d-3064725834ce">Prepared the new mold =
for making a vibration isolator for the vibrating hat and did a pour of the=
 Urethane 744 (shore 40A). I forgot to cut out some of the pour holes so th=
e pour did not go as well as I had hoped; even after poking through the pou=
r hole (there was just a thin membrane of silicone where there had been a s=
light gap between the positive and the posts printed as part of the mold sh=
ell) I was still not able to get air to evacuate passively as I had hoped. =
I used a syringe to inject urethane under slight pressure, which seemed to =
push out lots of air through the holes that were fully open, but that is no=
t a super elegant solution and may or may not have cleared the air and is m=
ore difficult to demold because there is a lot of urethane that overflowed =
the mold.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0f65035a-4416-4922-8d7c-e71f4bb6e128">Continuing to work on =
interfacing the ranging sensors with an ESP32; I was unable to get the Wave=
share relay ESP32 to send Serial.println commands back to the Arduino IDE, =
so I gave up on it and am switching to one of the basic ESP32 boards I have=
 around.</p>
<p local-id=3D"31b16e0a-2931-404a-9918-302ec654bf39">I got the new ESP32 bo=
ard to connect to the VL53L4CX TOF ranging sensor. One difficulty I ran int=
o is that one of the ground screw terminals was not directly connected to g=
round; for some reason I read a voltage of 1.6V when measuring from that gr=
ound to the 5V line, so I had to switch to a different ground terminal to p=
ower the board. I also had to add a wire to connect to the XSHUT pin; techn=
ically you can use the board with only 2 power connections and an SCL and S=
DA connection, but the board cannot be reset with software without the XSHU=
T line. Where that is useful is when loading new code onto the ESP32; witho=
ut the XSHUT line you have to power cycle the board (in my case by unpluggi=
ng the ESP32 board from the USB connection) to get the board to connect pro=
perly.</p>
<p local-id=3D"21f660aed7d4">The machined parts finally showed up from Xome=
try (for reference, they shipped Thursday 1/29 and were received Monday 2/2=
). I am going to pivot to working on assembling the machined parts so I can=
 start a cycle life test of the new motion system while I pivot back to the=
 control system and powder dispenser.</p>
<p local-id=3D"106b27081c0f">The aluminum machined parts were fairly clean =
and free of burrs, but the stainless steel parts were dirty with cutting fl=
uid and chips, so I cleaned all of them off with Citrusafe BBQ grill cleane=
r, washed them in the far left-hand sink, and dried them off with air. The =
side panels are missing two M4 threaded holes each, and all of the dowel pi=
n holes are too tight of a press fit so I will need to ream them all out.</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"773b52b58d9a">GENERAL R&amp;D:</p>
<p local-id=3D"614c7a612b93">I am working on printing a new V block for Don=
g to measure the IHI thruster combustion chamber/nozzle. I have removed the=
 endcap and lowered the outer wall height, and it will be printed from clea=
r resin instead of PETG-CF to improve the ability of the Keyence IM to dete=
ct the edges of the part visually.</p>
<p local-id=3D"cc4526e6e690">2026-02-03</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedd=
