<p local-id=3D"9b89304582f3">2026-02-09</p>
<p local-id=3D"439b9c401344">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"172031c4eb7d">I ran the hopper gate cycling over the weekend=
, and it has made it to ~27,000 cycles so far. Granted, it has been operati=
ng under optimal conditions with no powder loaded in the hopper or in the a=
mbient environment. There is also some buildup of black powder, likely grap=
hite debris, below the bushing. I am guessing that there was some bushing w=
ear from the cycle test, but it seems quite minimal.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7a414fa8739b">Since the control system for this hopper and c=
artridge loading system will require reading I2C sensors and operating 2X s=
tepper motors and 2X DC motors (at least), I have decided to use an ESP32 b=
oard as an independent control system that will monitor gate opening and cl=
osing and powder level when commanded to open or close the gate or refill t=
he hopper. It also will have an error line feeding back to the Duet board t=
o let it know if something goes wrong so the printer can pause until the is=
sue is resolved.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e91051110632">Working on an enclosure for the control system=
: ESP32, relay board, 2X stepper drivers, 2X DC-DC converters for adjusting=
 hopper and cartridge vibration.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e62441f65fac">Finished the design of the enclosure and lid a=
nd sent it over to the Bambu printer to print.</p>
