<p local-id=3D"12245bb04ab3">Spread and Spray:</p>
<p local-id=3D"0ec7f31d8154">Sean and Payman discussed how to analyze layer=
 quality. Got vacuum turning on and off automatically. Seeing droplet forma=
tion on the mist box, hoping that by moving the mist box down, droplet form=
ation will be reduced.</p>
<p local-id=3D"92c360a68d24">Laser:</p>
<p local-id=3D"52c2405cd571">Mason developed a new procedure for measuring =
binder penetration by applying a very thin layer to the base plate and chec=
king adhesion. Also developed a depth test procedure.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c9df4a6be003">It seems that the issues seen previously with =
powder spread into cuts would fuse into a solid seems to be due to overpene=
tration of binder; if the previous layers are too wet, the excess binder wi=
ll soak into the freshly applied powder and bind it together. With less bin=
der applied, laser cuts seemed to melt more. Midhun recommends adjusting su=
gar concentration in binder to change the physical properties when it is va=
porized by the laser. Plans to try adding dyes to the binder next week to i=
ncrease its absorption of light. Continuing to evaluate printing skived-lik=
e parts.</p>
