<p local-id=3D"c28fc29e6f6f">I demolded the 70A urethane cast doser ball, a=
nd it looks usable. I installed it in the cartridge base in place of the cl=
ear SLA doser ball, and based on visual inspection it seems like it would s=
eal well while still being able to be rotated.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5f686a15b9bc"></p>
<p local-id=3D"5a03007f8a12">GENERAL:</p>
<p local-id=3D"d3974ddc579f">Meeting with Sorin Dimescu (heat transfer anal=
ysis guy). Goal is to introduce the team to Sorin and talk about our needs =
for heat transfer/flow analysis for our entry into the heat exchanger and c=
old plate market.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b0bd5f7f14b9">Sorin: Has worked with Payman and Sean on the =
AEM projects. Materials science backgrounds (operations, mfg quality, custo=
mer interface) in semiconductor industry for 15-20 years, specifically semi=
conductor testing. Multi-layer ceramics mostly (thick film), multi-layer or=
ganics, elec. packaging, assy and testing, die bonding, soldering/brazing/l=
apping/grinding/polishing. Thermal management is a common thing to many of =
these (I like that he brought this up to tie into things we need him to wor=
k on). Heat interfaces. Designed test fixtures and equipment. Worked on AEM=
 cold plate project between Craig and Don, designed 300mm heater component =
for PXL. Personal interest in 3D printing, called out materials in our part=
s.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4b622a996545">Technical Q=E2=80=99s:</p>
<p local-id=3D"1d24235798f3">Our needs (Payman and Alex)</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4e96c3cfbd32">
<li local-id=3D"75e37fdc3533">
<p local-id=3D"d3ad055120de">We need to level up internal testing capabilit=
ies, internal tooling</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"bafec01ab6aa">
<p local-id=3D"4e6eee1e81b1">Interest in developing our own flexible cold p=
late architecture</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d4d40b852ca6">
<p local-id=3D"4e47d457ec79">Need assistance with some projects currently i=
n the pipeline</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3b62d2cb39ce">
<p local-id=3D"d4998bbf56e4">Want in-house simulation capabilities</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"d054ca3ef22d">Experience working on heatlets like Don? (Marc=
us)</p>
<p local-id=3D"e9c69e94d846">Made ceramic heater, communicated with Don abo=
ut needs, focused on making sure that coolant flow was aligned with heater =
traces. Working on the heat management side of the system while Don was mor=
e on the cooling level side.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6f9ab0d724e2">Experience designing cold plate internal featu=
res? (Alex)</p>
<p local-id=3D"49f6828b6a27">Not much involvement on PXL, worked on integra=
ted ceramic heaters/coolers with similar geometries (?). Monolithic cold pl=
ate/heater device w/ internal microfluidic channels. Very general discussio=
n of requirements for this type of system. Worked on cooling/heating system=
s for semiconductor wafers at Fralock.</p>
<p local-id=3D"08669fdbc13f">Design of cooling stack done iteratively? (Sen=
ai)</p>
<p local-id=3D"e2bd5bf830f0">Was an iterative process designing cooling/hea=
ting systems for Fralock. Used ceramic thermal compression bonding. Used So=
lidWorks flow simulation (haha).</p>
<p local-id=3D"2a11ffab7eaa">Showing an example we=E2=80=99re working on (M=
arcus):</p>
<p local-id=3D"4bcad56ce1c1">Epson cold plate design. He said the main way =
to optimize performance is to maximize surface area.</p>
<p local-id=3D"be43edd8c7a9">How to optimize surface area given a certain h=
eat transfer requirement?</p>
<p local-id=3D"43646f93bcbc">Maximize surface area, sweet spot in level of =
turbulence vs laminar flow.</p>
<p local-id=3D"36892f1ae307">Experience with developing test equipment for =
cold plate and heat exchanger testing? (Marcus)</p>
<p local-id=3D"955b63a6c0ff">Used customer provided systems, has not develo=
ped systems himself.</p>
<p local-id=3D"02ef6af84697">How to size testbed? (Senai)</p>
<p local-id=3D"dca4f650d3de">Heat to remove? Recommends a chiller that can =
reach -70C (why?). 2 stage compression chillers. Instrumentation and sensor=
s? Flow meters, pressure, gauges (did not mention temperature sensors). Con=
trol card, Python, very general suggestions.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3992fc8a4978">Epson slide. How to approach making an improve=
d cold plate? (Alex)</p>
<p local-id=3D"7eb2cc9814bb">Does not show power to remove. Does not know i=
f there is anything better than gyroids or Schwarz P.</p>
<p local-id=3D"92664d8ffcb9">How do you decide what designs to go with?</p>
<p local-id=3D"981f2869f788">Dunno. Best heat transfer mechanism is phase c=
hange. Optimize/maximize surface area and come up with way to implement pha=
se change. Kinda threw up his hands and really focused on phase change syst=
ems.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f070fc82ff84">Fralock project shown: Why do many customers n=
ot integrate the heater into the heatsink?</p>
<p local-id=3D"84fc0e1bf505">Two reasons, one is they don=E2=80=99t really =
need to, one is they don=E2=80=99t know(?). Making the point that thermal i=
nterface between heater and cooler has a low enough thermal resistance that=
 it isn=E2=80=99t necessary, although not articulated clearly. Started talk=
ing about different kinds of semiconductor manufacturing processes and vacu=
um lifter functionality. Heating quickly and cooling enabled semiconductor =
manufacturers to increase memory density. Used ceramics because semiconduct=
or manufacturers are sensitive to what material contacts the wafer. A metal=
lic cold plate would be static dissipative, which is nice. Implied that a h=
eater/cooler with integrated heaters would be useful, but then started ramb=
ling about die bonding, flip chips, etc. etc. A way to insulate a heater tr=
ace from the metal part could be valuable if possible.</p>
<p local-id=3D"512c8128c1a7">Payman and Marcus don=E2=80=99t think he=E2=80=
=99s good for this kind of design, which I totally agree with, but could be=
 useful for semiconductor equipment integration.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7c82bac927ad"></p>
<p local-id=3D"2e36e74e6eaf">R&amp;D Weekly Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"52afab47b90f">No-Depowdering:</p>
<p local-id=3D"d3672dbe35e9">Have not decided what to do on Pilot 1. Organi=
zing wiring.</p>
<p local-id=3D"868ec5337036">Continued effort to make an AEM-style part in =
copper. After spreading a new layer and spraying it, the layer has been puf=
fing up. Cisco noted that he had not seen this behavior previously. The lay=
er generally drops back down, but does not adhere properly and loses precis=
ion. Marcus recommendations: try varying binder volume and investigate root=
 cause.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3a13a4a38f9e">Base layer improvements: almost finished prepp=
ing Pilot 7 for experiments. Right now a 30 minute air cure only base layer=
 is working OK. With heat pass, the layer is 30-40 mins.</p>
<p local-id=3D"29f15eba6ced">Bring up no-depowdering on P6? Remove second v=
acuum (actually second vacuum line), print with heat pass base layer. Tried=
 to print layer 35 repeatedly, failed at 2nd layer due to triggering collis=
ion macro. Disabled collision macro, then next print had an issue with the =
g code where it faced at 150 micron instead of 10 micron. Restarted print, =
made it to layer 5 OK, still running.</p>
<p local-id=3D"69d160c5bd7c">Look into adding humidifier? Mohsen did some r=
esearch but has not ordered anything yet (my recommendation is an evaporati=
ve humidifier instead of a mist-type). Waiting to see if the current P6 run=
 succeeds. Running extreme case to replicate the problem of base layer curl=
ing (due to low humidity per Devin).</p>
<p local-id=3D"2523cccc5f9e">Had base layer focused meeting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bee28be1a65a">Vacuum is still heating. Outlet is not rated t=
o sufficient current (? BS). Is StoneVac rated for continuous operation? (a=
 quick glance at the website do Plan is to take the Festool with a broken l=
atch to use on P6 instead of the StoneVac.</p>
<p local-id=3D"20e92f190cbb">Mason noted that there was an error that left =
the vacuum running overnight and the outlet burned.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c63a2d8ad8e1">AEM wax print had the corner of the cake break=
ing. After running the print again, it is still breaking on Pilot 6. Still =
need to confirm with more prints. If it is still happening, run the same pr=
int without wax to see if the issue still occurs.</p>
<p local-id=3D"124f64ab9e5b">Did not evaluate larger bit or diagnose part s=
ide roughness and delam.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8da52a141d80">Hopper:</p>
<p local-id=3D"59846826b059">Transitioned hopper to Mohsen for print testin=
g</p>
<ul local-id=3D"882eb3ef7fd2">
<li local-id=3D"f3a67da4ec4b">
<p local-id=3D"44900c26610b">Linear gate can drag on layer when hopper is s=
preading</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"22b3827be56e">
<p local-id=3D"6c7516912428">Had to tilt the hopper towards the spreader ba=
r side</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"b772c3ea9a8e">Spread/Spray:</p>
<p local-id=3D"22cac66ecb22">Sean notes that the design of the mist box ten=
ds to promote the formation of droplets on its edge.</p>
<p local-id=3D"abce1a6a71ce">Payman did some preliminary optimization of pa=
rameters. He has implemented a new hopper that is essentially a shaker-styl=
e hopper that has a slit opening that is always in contact with the layer. =
He seems to have poor control of binder penetration, which makes sense beca=
use it is not a fixed-volume binder application approach, it is a flooding =
sheet of mist.</p>
<p local-id=3D"176023ccbfd6">Laser:</p>
<p local-id=3D"8864a95f1d5d">Tried mixing dye with binder at a 100:1 mixing=
 ratio, which seemed to improve cut quality and reduce powder melting. Expe=
rimented with heat curing layers after the cut and before the next spread. =
It worked well for initial layers but in later layers small features would =
break off. It also decreased binder penetration so Mason had to increase bi=
nder volume. He is interested in testing air-curing with fan. For the skive=
-style parts, he tried double line thickness and different binder volumes, =
and was seeing cut connections but still seeing too much debris. Wants to p=
ause this experiment until the basic process has improved.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1ee1c35f4c93">Tried adding water to the layer with a handhel=
d humidifier; when water was used this increased melting, but when binder w=
as used it seemed to yield better results. Binder with increased sucrose co=
ntent yielded better results (not sure if this is with the handheld humidif=
ier or standard nebulizer).</p>
<p local-id=3D"9d72977b1b97">Tried printing AEM-style geometry, but the cut=
s are still not very clean.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d480a74a3e68">Tried testing new LVP design which seemed to w=
ork better. (Recommend implementing a crossflow system fixed to the build p=
late with inert gas injection on one side and vacuum extraction on the othe=
r).</p>
<p local-id=3D"e39069164ebf">Tried spreading powder on a layer of PEG then =
cutting it with a laser as a meaningless simulation of a combined laser/no =
depowdering experiment. the laser was able to cut through but the PEG surfa=
ce underneath was not very even.</p>
