<p local-id=3D"7abefc964dcb">PILOT:</p>
<p local-id=3D"25dc5aa4078c">I used a hole saw to make a 2 1/8=E2=80=9D hol=
e in the metal bottom plate of Pilot 6. The purpose of this is to pass thro=
ugh a large diameter vacuum hose from the vacuum to close to the Z stages; =
Splitting the standard small diameter hose into two equal diameter hoses (1=
X for the standard spindle and 1X for the facing spindle) close to the Z st=
ages was not providing sufficient suction.</p>
<p local-id=3D"88cafff7c259">I went over the BOM that Senai, Adriana, and P=
hilip have been working on, and added comments where appropriate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fd1e78d9ef84">2026-02-25</p>
<p local-id=3D"b76296e20987">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"fd72b375254b">Post-processed the parts printed last night: a=
 new dummy hopper with threaded inserts on the top and bottom and provision=
s added for a manually removable powder gate, the associated powder gate, a=
nd a funnel that screws to the bottom of the dummy hopper and has threads o=
n the bottom for a nalgene bottle to screw to it. The theory is that the po=
wder will mostly be contained when the hopper is filled or emptied.</p>
<p local-id=3D"20262b70a2c7">GENERAL:</p>
