plan next steps in the laser project.</p>
<p local-id=3D"20f3ca91c970">Per Midhun, Marcus said that a far IR laser wo=
uld be better because it is more absorbed by the water and reflects from th=
e metal, but Midhun believes that targeting metal powder heating provides b=
etter results where the metal powder heats and transfers energy to vaporize=
 the water and =E2=80=9Cpyrolyze=E2=80=9D the binder. Midhun supports the M=
OPA laser because of the greater degree of control over parameters. In lite=
rature, people have used NIR lasers (MOPA) and blue diode lasers and gotten=
 good results but have had poorer results with FIR (CO2).</p>
<p local-id=3D"1ea352a7f6af">Mason was started on the XTool, and told to us=
e it until Q2, but after 3 days Payman bought the MOPA laser and told Mason=
 to switch to that.</p>
