<p local-id=3D"646db71421b0">The cable carrier mount for the sheet metal en=
dstop holder broke on Pilot 7. I destructively tested the original part tha=
t had not broken in operation against the spare printed alongside the one t=
hat broke, and found that the one that had broken in the printer was much w=
eaker and had been printed with far fewer walls (I think 2 vs the original=
=E2=80=99s 6), so I redesigned the part to be slightly thicker at the regio=
n where it broke and I am printing it with 8 walls and 69% infill.</p>
<p local-id=3D"434477c2d420">Laser Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"26597d0d30e7">Meeting for discussing results of DOE complete=
d. Midhun has been analyzing the data collected in Google Sheets, and Mason=
 has been analyzing the results in Minitab.</p>
<p local-id=3D"74f31bfa7698">Midhun noted that it is easy to twist statisti=
cal results to fit any narrative.</p>
<p local-id=3D"87aaf9804b5f">Mason measured debris quantity with image anal=
ysis and gave a subjective ranking to level of debris distribution in cut z=
one and a ranking of variation in cut depth in the hatched region.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a233bce0b119">No direct correlation between cut depth measur=
ed on the last cut and whether layers are interconnected. No correlation be=
tween hatch depth and layer connection.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a8f063ec72d0">Strong correlation between debris area percent=
age and debris score.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d9d5780ca8eb">Avg cut width 110 microns, very stable across =
different tests. Hatch depth correlates with cut depth.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c722cd9f2b2a">Response variables Midhun used are debris area=
 percentage for cuts, debris area percentage for hatch, and whether cuts we=
re connected.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a97beaa96900">To measure whether cuts were connected, Ben fi=
rst measured the cut width, depth, and debris on the Keyence VHX microscope=
 after print curing, then used a brush to brush out the cuts and repeat the=
 measurements. If the depth measurement changes, then the cuts are consider=
ed to be connected. For cuts that were down to the glass, the measurement w=
as not done, it was just marked as cuts connected. If the change in depth b=
etween pre-brushing and post-brushing was less than 50 microns the cut was =
marked as not connecting.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0040827f1f14">Mason noted that binder penetration is an unkn=
own, so he wants to do an experiment to measure binder penetration with the=
 different binder quantities used.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2b2d80fae104">Midhun=E2=80=99s recommends adding a step to t=
he experimental protocol where a cut is done on the third layer only as wel=
l as the cuts that are done on each layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f81e779f42ee">Minitab build a 98% accurate predictive model =
that concludes that the pulse width is not a significant factor but all the=
 other variables are important to debris area.</p>
<p local-id=3D"302217dd2855">The model developed for predicting whether cut=
s are connected is weak, but it suggests that the only variable that is imp=
ortant is number of passes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"3c672ec13bfd">Debris percentage for hatch model has a 96% ma=
tch, with all variables statistically significant.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8e363dfa0563">Midhun recommends adding more response variabl=
es to improve the quality of the data.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a44b81a18f09">Midhun also asks what the actual desired cut w=
idth is. Is it possible that the cut will be so narrow that it is difficult=
 to remove the part from the cake?</p>
<p local-id=3D"eb583f2fc0d0">Mason asked Marcus and Payman for hard specs f=
or cut width, minimum feature size, etc. in January and was only given the =
directive to =E2=80=9Cmake a printer that can use a laser to print parts.=
=E2=80=9D</p>
