<p local-id=3D"6ac58542bdd6">It may be beneficial to use Magics or</p>
<p local-id=3D"e9d00cdf2b23">Marcus raised the concept of running the MOPA =
laser in a regime that matches the results of the diode laser as closely as=
 possible, per an email he has sent out previously showing the output of Cl=
aude for this application. Claude=E2=80=99s suggestions were based on match=
ing a pulsed laser to a continuous wave laser, based on adjustment of pulse=
 width and frequency and adjusting the spot size to match.</p>
<p local-id=3D"075a849cb20d">Marcus recommends maximizing frequency and pul=
se width to match Ultimaker Xtool results.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ca5868fc16f6">Payman asked about time taken for running the =
experiment. Mason noted that the bottleneck was a limited number of glass p=
lates; this resulted in the measurement process taking more time than the p=
rinting. It was also raised that only one sample section was run on each pl=
ate, in the center of the build area. Each cut line needs to be measured in=
dividually, so measurement time scales linearly with cut length (5mm to 10m=
m square quadruples measurement time, 1 to 5 squares multiplies measurement=
 time by a factor of 5).</p>
<p local-id=3D"34aee639489a">Marcus suggests that Payman review the results=
 and determine next steps, and Mason will consider comparing the diode lase=
r with the MOPA laser.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e3c10b950e24">Midhun asked about Payman=E2=80=99s success wi=
th using the blue diode laser on the Ultimaker, and Marcus asked about his =
experiments and results. Payman noted that the setup is very different. It =
uses the spread-and-spray system with his hopper design. He started by meas=
uring penetration depth by changing layer thickness until the layers did no=
t adhere. He did a thick layer of unbound powder and bound one layer then r=
an a grid with squares with different parameters to come to a setting that =
cut through the layer without sintering, then ran a 20 layer print with the=
 optimal settings. The straight lines cut seemed good, but where the laser =
path turned around a corner the surface finish was poorer. He wants to =E2=
=80=9Cwork on fundamentals=E2=80=9D first by starting at 1 layer then incre=
asing the number of layers. Midhun asked if he cut 20 layers of joined hatc=
hes, and Payman said that he only cut lines that were joined. Payman did no=
t clean off the layer between cuts and noted that the layers were quite dir=
ty between layers. The laser is the galvo-based XTool used on a roller gant=
ry setup.</p>
