<p local-id=3D"c4c798738f37">Air Drying:</p>
<p local-id=3D"bfebbbd96adc">Mohsen and Ning working on a control system fo=
r the humidifier. It was previously necessary to manually press a button to=
 start the humidifier, but it is necessary to integrate humidifier operatio=
n with the machine. Ning rewired it so it can be run with macros.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b1205591e5c0">Mohsen has been researching airflow uniformity=
. He tried focusing the dry air on the center of the build only, and found =
that he was able to print 30 layers before the layer started cracking, wher=
e before he saw corners curling up after 10-15 layers. NOTE: this is very l=
ikely due to an environment is too dry. I would recommend first controlling=
 the environment in the machine tightly and increase airflow over the cake =
(recirculating air within the machine) to achieve faster layer curing. Actu=
ally, I would recommend improving spray uniformity and optimize layer dryin=
g with the use of a heater, along with a NIR moisture measurement sensor.</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"33527e26aebb">Experimenting with multiple-nozzle setup to tu=
ne nonlinear airflow along the build (i.e. more airflow in the center than =
the sides). Plans to adjust airflow orientation and turbulence and add spee=
d control to the layer drying fan. Also plans to try using the humidifier d=
uring a print to confirm that it is functioning as intended.</p>
