<p local-id=3D"d27b96e2dfad">Laser:</p>
<p local-id=3D"c191f318c989">DOE results analyzed and reported at meeting t=
his week. Tried a new experiment with optimized settings based on DOE resul=
ts. Hatching worked well but is unable to do a single width cut with the sa=
me settings as the hatch. With hatching, the procedure is to raster scan th=
e target geometry in one orientation then raster it again at 90 degrees rel=
ative to the first cut.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4d1e5e7334fd">Parameters used here are within the range of p=
arameters tested during the DOE, but Mason used a low binder volume where t=
he model predicted that a higher binder volume would be better.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2acf17c3cb54">Print shown was 8 layers and had dry powder wh=
ere desired. The dry powder is fresh powder that is applied in the spread, =
laser cuts throw out power instead of drying it in place.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f317b8dee2db">For the base layer, had to make a thick base l=
ayer and raster with 6 passes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ff17cc633883">The different experiments here were run with t=
he same parameters suggested as optimal by Minitab but with different cut s=
trategies. Even with the same parameters, the changing cut strategy had a h=
uge difference: single cut lines were not effective (difficult to remove pa=
rts from the cake), and sintering seen in single cuts was ~10% where it was=
 much less (although not zero) when hatching the parts.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d3fbe8673983">My recommendation would be:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"52cf95d58f95">
<li local-id=3D"c539abbe8f7e">
<p local-id=3D"d0e364179f86">Run another formal DOE on different cut strate=
gies; this seems to have a significant effect even with the same base param=
eters</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8b89e2f201f5">
<p local-id=3D"597ad047168c">Run a formal DOE for depth control</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"04a1122979f3">
<p local-id=3D"6631cc977814">It may be worth exploring LPBF simulation/cont=
rol packages, such as Magics or</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e072a46bb6b2">Mason plans to design another experiment for c=
ontrolling depth and study the effect of different numbers of passes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"45e61d122287">Marcus asked if Payman is still interested in =
exploring different laser technologies; since Payman is currently using the=
 XTool on the gantry Payman wants to defer that to some unspecified time in=
 the future.</p>
<p local-id=3D"373cdbbf3b61">Marcus also raised the concept of running the =
MOPA laser in a regime to match the functionality of CW lasers; Mason plans=
 to try that next week.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c03da975f19f">Payman made some thicker parts but no 3D parts=
, and plans to improve machine robustness before attempting 3D parts.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2a8751fb8c57">Mason raised the concept of trying testing the=
 laser with different materials. Proposal is to try cutting a copper and 31=
6L cake or green part on Pilot 3.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c7b054544646">Spread and Spray:</p>
<p local-id=3D"0f9030eadc20">Payman designed and printed a new mist box wit=
h a vacuum skirt around it. Biggest issue is vibration of system that restr=
icts to 200 micron layers (no thinner). Thinks spray uniformity is good. Ho=
pper unchanged. Goal next week is to make layers with laser.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d1dd357aedce">2026-03-09</p>
