<p local-id=3D"9985f9683db4">Laser Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"056290b1b460">Note: The first mention I have in my notes of =
the laser project is that I designed and ordered sheet metal panels for Pil=
ot 3 on 2025-04-21 . This was for the XTool F1 Ultra, and some laser experi=
ments had been done by Payman with the smaller XTool F1. Presumably the las=
er experiments had started at least a month or two earlier, which as I reca=
ll was done with cardboard panels taped to the outside of the machine, and =
Payman=E2=80=99s benchtop experiments preceded this by a month or two. Base=
d on this, I believe the laser project was started roughly 14 months ago.</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"56e421fed6dd">Midhun, me, and Mason. Mason wants to set up a=
n IR thermometer sensor in Pilot 2 because it provides a more accurate sing=
le-point measurement. System was mostly set up, but was told to stop by Pay=
man and Marcus on Friday. Also was setting up software to make 3D shapes, b=
ut was also told to stop working on it pending discussion at the rebaselini=
ng/project planning meeting this afternoon. Payman and Marcus want to discu=
ss planning or something. Mason wants to set up another formal DOE focused =
on understanding and controlling cut depth. To get the cut depth of a cut o=
n top of a bound layer, he wants to start the print by building up a thick =
base first then doing cuts. Midhun recommends reducing the power setting to=
 reduce the heat input that may be affecting cut behavior over multiple lay=
ers. (Should we cool the whole print to ambient before cutting?). Midhun no=
ted that he did not have success running prints in Saffron printers at temp=
eratures above 85F (binder does not penetrate at high cake temperatures). L=
arger squares may reduce heat transfer between cuts. Cutting in different p=
laces for each layer would help to show whether cut depth varies or not ove=
r successive layers when not cutting on top of previous cuts. Midhun also r=
ecommends testing the blue diode laser against the MOPA laser because of Pa=
yman=E2=80=99s positive results on the gantry. Payman is reluctant to trans=
fer the XTool diode laser off of his gantry, so I would recommend buying an=
other XTool to install on Pilot 3.</p>
