<p local-id=3D"f0b238e3687b">Payman, Marcus, Mason, me</p>
<p local-id=3D"c0d8b5262ee6">Payman had already ordered xTool UV laser, but=
 Mason pointed out that we would be limited in the software control system =
because we would be restricted to xTool software, so he suggested an altern=
ative option from Aliexpress (1 5W UV laser and 1 30 or 60W CO2 laser, ~$3K=
 each)</p>
<p local-id=3D"06a6f7757d80">Mason raised the possibility of inerting the m=
achine, and Payman wants to use less than 1 day for that. Payman is OK with=
 doing one test with an inert atmosphere for each laser technology.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7cad9192eae4">Payman raised the possibility of purchasing a =
high speed camera, and recommended that Mason do research for one that is c=
heap.</p>
<p local-id=3D"88c387f0055e">&lt;Could we just raster everything instead of=
 doing single width cuts?&gt;</p>
<p local-id=3D"d668009347db">Mason recommends using an industrial-grade IR =
sensor from the Saffrons instead of the current hobbyist-grade sensors. Pay=
man wants the ability to record a thermal image/video. Mason points out tha=
t the industrial sensors will be more accurate and provide a trusted temper=
ature value. I also support using calibrated sensors; it is dangerous to dr=
aw conclusions from data that cannot be trusted.</p>
<p local-id=3D"1454621283bb">Payman also wants Mason to do some experiments=
 with the gantry printer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c4377c53fd8e">Payman recommends not printing complex parts. =
Instead he would rather spend 1 week on each laser technology. He doesn=E2=
=80=99t want to get into details in this meeting, but wants Mason to draw u=
p a schedule showing daily tasks for each week of screening for each laser.=
 Payman wants a meeting set up for Monday to go over experiments.</p>
