<p local-id=3D"8db048872040">2026-03-23</p>
<p local-id=3D"0a9a84dc7718">Pilot Baseline Stabilization Project Planning:=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"8904fdb0475d">Goal is to establish that the core Pilot techn=
ology is reliable (start machine and have high confidence that the print wi=
ll complete without operator intervention).</p>
<p local-id=3D"4c243d87a876">Pourya recommends finding the limits of the so=
ftware (i.e. file size). Ben has been having difficulty transferring files,=
 and wants to be able to transfer files wirelessly. Pourya points out that =
this is dependent on wifi network quality.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fa9472ab34ea">Payman raised the point that data logging is i=
mportant to figure out before trying to benchmark the system, including vis=
ible light images before and after the cut. IR pictures are explicitly not =
necessary. Also, he wants pictures taken of the inside of the mist box peri=
odically.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4ff5dd66dfbf">Because the communication between the Raspberr=
y Pi and the THC control arduino has been changed, it is not possible to ad=
just the temperature and humidity offsets (sensor calibration) but the humi=
dity and temperature targets can be adjusted.</p>
<p local-id=3D"be197b1d8f1d">Since there is no way to raise the humidity in=
 the machine if it is too low, Payman recommends increasing the humidity of=
 the room to compensate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7a4f19c13d77">&lt;We have never done testing to optimize the=
 print parameters, such as layer target temperature.&gt;</p>
<p local-id=3D"a7a27ee02a93">&lt;Recommend having ZZ add the environmental =
sensor offset adjustment functionality back into the code.&gt;</p>
<p local-id=3D"e451375135f1">&lt;Check whether the safety system is still o=
perational matching the functionality of the safety system in the Epson pri=
nters.&gt;</p>
<p local-id=3D"0cdb02831095">Goal here is not to ensure the quality of prin=
ted parts, it is only to test the reliability of the print start - finish p=
rocess.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8293330fe08b">&lt;Recommend running repeat prints of TRS par=
ts, breaking them out, sintering them, and comparing part quality.&gt;</p>
<p local-id=3D"95cf04067922">Payman wants to do 50 layer prints with air cu=
tting to ensure that the data logging system functions properly, then switc=
h to 300 layer prints.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a707d3b2ba89"></p>
<p local-id=3D"6fa7e775f665">I asked about making Pilots 8 and 9, and he sa=
id that we are planning on making one more only to save money.</p>
