ce doesn=E2=80=99t impact the layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f6bc85b54af5">I adjusted the design of the cams by decreasin=
g the gap between the cam and clamp components as well as increasing the di=
ameter of the clamping cylinder from 24 to 25mm, which should give more mat=
erial to the outside of the part where it broke previously.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e80762c8aa60">I am printing a modified design of the spreade=
r bar (cutouts added) and the original version of the gate from clear SLA m=
aterial. An SLA printed spreader bar will have improved surface finish as c=
ompared with the FDM version, although still not as good as a polished shaf=
t. It is also unclear whether the SLA part or the FDM part would have impro=
ved powder adhesion properties; I could imagine either one being stickier a=
nd having a greater tendency to hold powder. My sense is that in order of m=
aximum to minimum stickiness it would go: SLA resin - FDM PETG-CF - machine=
d stainless steel - polished ceramic coated aluminum, but frankly powder te=
nds to stick to everything so I=E2=80=99m not sure it matters much. On the =
Bambu X1E with support filament, I am printing a new -Y direction guard wit=
h the improvements discussed above as well as a gate with a cutout for glui=
ng in the 4140 steel part mentioned above. Between this version and the SLA=
 gate I am hoping that I will have at least one gate that is usable for tes=
ting, but it is possible that it will be necessary to have one machined in =
the end.</p>
