<p local-id=3D"1f19f9da9006">Results from UV laser: single cut: 310 micron =
deep, 100 micron wide cut, kerf angle is 7.73 micron over 310 micron. Debri=
s field when hatching seems to be more loose powder than melted material. F=
or single width cuts, he is finding that a single pass never cuts through t=
o the previous layer, but more passes (he tried 2 and 3) always cuts throug=
h. For the single width cuts, before brushing it out he found that the mate=
rial in the cut had variable height, but was fairly even after brushing out=
