<p local-id=3D"91e5b9b79900">2026-04-14</p>
<p local-id=3D"bbf464bd76a3">GENERAL:</p>
<p local-id=3D"9788cc41926c">I asked Rajan if we were going to have enough =
money to make an industrialized pilot (mainly to make the point that I supp=
ort doing so and that the reason I did not do so originally was because of =
cost constraints) and his answer was essentially =E2=80=9Cno one knows.=E2=
=80=9D Mason talked to me after Rajan went to the big technical/strategy me=
eting, and said that it was not a reassuring answer on Rajan=E2=80=99s part=
; I hadn=E2=80=99t really made the connection at the time but Rajan=E2=80=
=99s answer was also about the future of the company. Mohsen also said that=
 there is a board meeting planned later in the month, so this technical/str=
ategy meeting is likely focused on what to show the board to convince them =
to fund us further. This board meeting is likely where they will decide whe=
ther 3DEO will continue to stay in business. I don=E2=80=99t really have en=
ough information to make an informed answer of whether we should or not. We=
 are focusing mainly on the heat sink market, which is indeed a growing mar=
ket assuming that AI data centers are built at the rate that is currently p=
redicted. However, there are many other companies focused on selling heat s=
inks, some 3D printed, some conventionally manufactured, so we will need to=
 provide an advantage over those companies to get some significant contract=
s. This could be in the form of a proprietary heat sink design, advantages =
in material properties, or unique capabilities in terms of geometries that =
can be printed, assuming that the no-depowdering and laser processes can be=
 made to work.</p>
<p local-id=3D"35a460bc8bdc">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
