<p local-id=3D"98ccf103cfb4">No Depowdering:</p>
<p local-id=3D"f2fc9780ad1b">P6 SVP: Originally used StoneVac, but it was t=
oo weak, so Pourya switched to P1=E2=80=99s vacuum, but it was too weak for=
 the facing bit, so he dropped the facing bit height, and redid the hoses. =
That worked, but P1=E2=80=99s vacuum burned out, so he switched back to the=
 StoneVac. The facing spindle=E2=80=99s SVP was vacuuming up powder, causin=
g holes at the edges of the print, so he raised the SVP.</p>
<p local-id=3D"981e9924a305">Marcus pointed out that it may be beneficial t=
o have independent flow and height control. Payman pointed out that they us=
ed to have adjustable restrictor valves on each SVP opening (many years ago=
). I agree that it would be beneficial to have a restrictor valve of some s=
ort on each line, and possibly electrical ball valves to switch the vacuum =
to each spindle on and off.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0cb2c07782bd">Currently the SOP is to have the facing tool b=
it follow the same path as the small end mill, instead of following a stand=
ard facing operation.</p>
<p local-id=3D"5ede620d852f">Ran various tests with varying degrees of succ=
ess; some prints failed, some of the results were meaningless because the T=
HC either turned off or stayed in a fixed state (constant TEC power, consta=
nt dry air injection).</p>
<p local-id=3D"daff7f5ffdd4">Per Pourya, the end mill being used for facing=
 was inspected yesterday and seemed both clean and sharp (inspected with th=
e MicroVu).</p>
<p local-id=3D"c4b18932d2f3">No pen test macro yet, Mohsen is working on it=
.</p>
<p local-id=3D"569192daa4be">In process of sintering some copper parts (sin=
tering run will not be run until Monday). Ran some other copper prints with=
 different parameters.</p>
<p local-id=3D"955fb8c6ec16">Laser:</p>
<p local-id=3D"71300d2469c1">Mason showed UV laser cutting results with AEM=
-like geometry. Features do not seem to be very well defined (looking at th=
e cross section) when a 3D scan is conducted, but visually they seem to be =
present.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7bbb6e068427">Due to the oval shape of the laser spot, cuts =
in the X direction tend be narrower and deeper than cuts in the Y direction=
. This could be resolved with a diode laser with improved optics, only cutt=
ing in the X direction, physically rotating the laser 45 degrees so the X a=
nd Y direction cuts are the same width, or compensating for it within the c=
ontrol system (tricky to do because the number of passes is limited, maybe =
adjust power/speed?) When the laser hits dry powder, it causes much more =
=E2=80=9Csintering=E2=80=9D as compared with the UV laser, although the phe=
nomenon with the UV laser is not completely unknown. He noted that the =E2=
=80=9Csintering=E2=80=9D behavior seems much worse when a cake is left out =
for a while (presumably due to decreasing moisture content of the cake). Th=
e temperature of the cake was increased significantly (recorded temp ~75C, =
~50C increase from ambient) while the UV laser tends to increase the cut te=
mperature by ~5C.</p>
<p local-id=3D"7edf74b83663">When trying to perform cuts in copper with the=
 diode laser, Mason found that it tended to melt/sinter the copper without =
removing the material.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b75195500311">UV laser is being installed on Pilot 3 today.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"bf70e2dee4c8">Misc:</p>
<p local-id=3D"fbc6eb545563">Mohsen working on the pen test macro.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a07cb33bb775">Marcus/Dong/Midhun/Mohsen working with Argonne=
 National Lab to put together a grant proposal for modulating porosity for =
thermal applications. Goal is also to leverage their AI models for some DFA=
M-type stuff on our side.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4b8b2bf5468d">Marcus raised the point that he has been discu=
ssing with Sean the idea of changing the test geometry of the no-depowering=
 process to be closer to geometries seen in real parts.</p>
<p local-id=3D"67ade9dad51b"></p>
