<p local-id=3D"2661f512afbb">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"f948649c5082">Cast urethane seals should have cured over the=
 weekend. After installing those, the SLA steel-reinforced gate should be s=
ufficient for initial testing. The spreader bar is made from SLA material, =
so I may need to machine a new one from the ceramic-coated shaft stock that=
 I received last week. Since it has an OD of 1.5=E2=80=9D it will need to b=
e redesigned slightly as compared with the current spreader bar design; the=
 easiest approach is to machine it so that it has three flat sides and one =
side is left round.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eb36afaaba11">In trying to run some cams and cam clamps from=
 PAHT-CF several times today, I keep running into an issue where the printe=
r shuts down while it is laying down lines for calibration of extrusion. Th=
is is apparently a known issue with X1Es that is commonly due to failure of=
 the power switch; I also did a quick check of the power switch. When the p=
rinter shuts down, the power switch stays on but its built in light turns o=
ff. I pressed the power switch on the =E2=80=9Con=E2=80=9D side, and the li=
ght flashed a bit on and off. This suggests that even when the switch is no=
minally in the =E2=80=9Con=E2=80=9D position, there is a failed connection =
somewhere that is reconnected by pressing on the switch.</p>
<p local-id=3D"232496a51e1c">MOSP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"60e6bb8d6781">I am continuing to work on a metal mount for t=
he Mest unit. My current design approach is to have two machined dovetails =
for slotting into the Saffron spindle stages, along with two bent sheet met=
al components to link these two dovetails and join them to the Mest unit.</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"ebba3aaf534e">Pilot Stabilization Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"7baa9a92fe75">Main question is whether Ning should disassemb=
le and rewire Pilot 7 (estimate is that it will take 2 weeks).</p>
<p local-id=3D"6675d2c291b7">Ning wants to isolate the negative return line=
s of the DC power supplies on Pilot 7.</p>
<p local-id=3D"056f2e761151">THC on Pilot 7 is unreliable and there are iss=
ues with it failing to log data.</p>
<p local-id=3D"80ad5b14aebd">Ning says that one issue is the connection bet=
ween the Arduino and Pi (claimed to be due to non isolated power supplies).=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"0cdbf24d5532">The Pi-Duet connection works on Pilot 6, but t=
he Pi-Arduino has connectivity issues on both printers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a053b1eddf44">Payman asked whether there is a quick way to g=
et Pilot 6 and 7 working.</p>
<p local-id=3D"838076e1dc87">Pourya pointed out that the Pi-Duet connection=
 works on Pilot 6.</p>
<p local-id=3D"aaee35ad11fd">Points I think I made:</p>
<p local-id=3D"d3e5051b4790">These issues do not seem to be present on Pilo=
ts 1-5, which all have the negative lines of the DC power supplies connecte=
d.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d65631991d19">Every industrial system I have made, the Beta =
machines, and the Saffron printers all have the negative line of different =
DC power supplies connected.</p>
<p local-id=3D"898b609ccb49">Relevant Information:</p>
<p local-id=3D"283391f755a5">I have so far not found any industrial standar=
ds that say that every DC power supply should be isolated</p>
<p local-id=3D"cb1f519aa39b">There are instances where circuits should be i=
solated:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7f762e561a32">
<li local-id=3D"db31891f8935">
<p local-id=3D"c28fe6800917">You want systems to be able to be turned off o=
r have a fault without shutting down the entire system</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2a1287fe45e3">
<p local-id=3D"34201d9c4514">You have high voltage systems that need to be =
isolated from low voltage DC circuits for safety reasons</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"035f81a75193">
<p local-id=3D"1582bf52813d">Analog systems that are sensitive to noise</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"393e5fe6803f">
<p local-id=3D"36e035e3de66">Intrinsically safe systems that need to isolat=
ed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9310d823c39c">
<p local-id=3D"f669b43db674">Instances where one negative line is measuring=
 a process potential</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c4fd6e52bbe8">
<p local-id=3D"182dd23913e7">Very long cable runs where a ground loop can f=
orm</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"55423b9a01e7">Ning asked me to make a DIN rail mount for the=
 large relay board that he is working on installing.</p>
<p local-id=3D"251720dfefa7">I designed the DIN rail mount and a cover for =
the board and started them printing on HAMMER.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b8d2041c57bf">The print on HAMMER failed for some reason. It=
 did prompt me to turn on some kind of glob management detection or somethi=
ng, which printed a small square off to the side of the main print. I stopp=
ed the print, cleaned everything off, double checked that the nozzle was no=
t clogged, and restarted the print with standard settings, and so far it se=
ems to be running fine.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6c828ca902e5">Laser Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"ba0b42fdb41b">Payman asked Mason about switching laser devel=
opment to copper only. There is also a meeting tomorrow between Marcus, Ale=
x, and Payman to discuss switching all development efforts to copper. Mason=
