on of the hopper is causing issues with the layer. I recommended reducing t=
he vibration motor power due to the decreased weight of the hopper, but I t=
hink the root cause is the vibrating hat is contacting the stepper motor, b=
ypassing the vibration isolator and conducting vibrations directly to the h=
opper body. I am going to redesign and reprint the vibrating hat, which act=
ually should have been done a while ago because the powder level sensor hol=
der that makes it possible to keep the sensor triggered even if the hopper =
is not full of powder is undersized for the current sensor holder (I design=
ed it for the bare sensor, but the sensor is now screwed into a holder that=
 increases the outer diameter).</p>
