<p local-id=3D"8bfa77ec5e8a">No-Depowdering:</p>
<p local-id=3D"1fef1b8cc936">Tested different tool bit heights (to adjust h=
eight of SVP opening). The goal was to minimize sucking up features (chippi=
ng?) while also removing all PEG fragments cut by the facing end mill.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9c37e60ecee3">To address a chipping issue, he increased the =
binder volume by 10%. Chipping of one part at the end was seen, possibly du=
e to measured low humidity (28% RH).</p>
<p local-id=3D"53fe3d6f05f8">On the copper no-depowdering printer, increasi=
ng the PEG droplet size improved print quality (?) but did not solve the is=
sue (?) completely. The facing G code used previously left some PEG on the =
layer (possibly due to weak vacuum). He is updating the G code to face beyo=
nd the outside of the part boundary, it previously was only facing right to=
 the edge, which may have been the cause of reside seen right at the edge.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"181d00fe01fc">He is going to work on matching the Saffron ha=
rdware to the Pilot hardware: larger facing end mill, matched spindle RPM (=
currently the Saffron spindle is running at ~60K RPM and the dental spindle=
 on the Pilot printers is running at ~35K RPM (I think).</p>
<p local-id=3D"d72558161370">Laser:</p>
<p local-id=3D"2f736eb3c542">Experimenting with copper. Cleaned out Pilot 3=
 along with Cisco and Alex and Ben for copper service. Was able to make cut=
s on copper with the diode laser in the printer when it was not possible wi=
th benchtop testing. Also tried the MOPA laser, which seemed to be a more r=
obust process (a wider range of parameters was able to yield good results).=
 Differences here vs earlier testing: make copper layers on pilot (earlier =
saffron), remove layers more quickly, curing layers less than earlier, incr=
eased binder volume and soak time. &lt;Payman said that there will be a pro=
ject dedicated to copper printing on Pilots&gt;. He was able to make a melt=
ed layer with the diode laser. The diode laser was unable to hatch layers w=
ithout fusing the powder.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eec17fdd9f4d">Plans to redo the screening tests with cakes f=
rom the Pilot instead of the Saffron. Eliminating the diode laser due to is=
sues with hatching. Plan is to test with the MOPA and the UV laser, and pos=
sibly the CO2 laser (unlikely).</p>
