<p local-id=3D"ed42b5e401a6">I am skipping over reinforcing V5.1 to handle =
the heat from the heater and printing a V5.2 from SLA material instead. I a=
m designing a monolithic and lightweighted body that combines the front, ba=
ck, and side panels into one part and has isogrid cutouts to limit the resi=
n used while maintaining adequate strength.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e0039d6cfbb0">MOSP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"3ee8630faddd">Installed the metal Mest mount on the copper S=
affron printer that Pourya has been using for no-depowdering experiments. I=
 had to drill out the mounting holes for the dovetail with compliance (curr=
ently 3D printed from PETG-CF, although I am considering casting it from th=
e harder urethane to get even more compliance). The dovetail was a really t=
ight fit, even after grinding it down with a rotating tool with a carbide b=
urr and aligning it as best I could with the new, larger mounting holes. Th=
e fundamental issue is that the Saffron spindle stages are not spaced relia=
bly, so I need to design more adjustability in the mount to compensate for =
various spindle stage spacing. With the metal mount being as tight a fit as=
 it is, and with it being less compliant than the 3D printed version, I am =
concerned that it will cause binding or increased wear issues with the Saff=
ron spindle stages because their carriages will be rigidly fixed without be=
ing precisely aligned.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9541b579616e">I have designed a mold for casting urethane do=
vetails and am printing 2 of them on the Bambu P2S. Hopefully they will not=
 be necessary, but if they are, I will be ready.</p>
<p local-id=3D"326667524ab3"></p>
<p local-id=3D"5cf166df4621">2026-04-30</p>
<p local-id=3D"92a9577b992f">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"a689d829680b">The monolithic hopper body (front, back, and s=
ide panels combined into one part) finished printing from clear SLA materia=
l on the FormLabs printer and is currently being washed in the Form Wash.</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"e64915ff8739">I populated the CAD assembly of HOPPER V5.2 wi=
th the cast side seals, and I am designing a cast main wiper seal for the g=
ate. My sealing approach with this design is to eliminate all the felts and=
 use cast urethane only; there is a risk that urethane will not seal as wel=
l as felt but there is less risk of FOD getting into the powder (I am worri=
ed about fibers from the felt separating and mixing in with the powder).</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"5d556fc426b3">I designed a urethane wiper with =E2=80=9Cteet=
h=E2=80=9D to act as multiple wiper blades. If it was wiping on a solid sur=
face I would avoid this architecture because powder could get trapped betwe=
en the wipers, but since the surface has cutouts to act as powder drains, h=
aving multiple wiper blades should increase the lifespan of the wiper vs. a=
 single one that could wear out quickly. The wiper will still not last fore=
ver, and since the plan is to glue it down it will be difficult to replace.=
 Urethane is pretty temperature resistant; maybe use a hot melt adhesive so=
 it can be removed by heating the hopper body until the adhesive melts? It =
also might be possible to secure it down with mechanical fasteners in some =
way (maybe a bunch of small flat head screws?) but using an adhesive would =
yield a reliable solution more quickly, even if it makes seal replacement m=
ore difficult in the future.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4c65434f938d">Removed the supports from and manually IPA cle=
aned the monolithic V5.2 hopper body, and put it in the Form Cure to cure.<=
/p>
<p local-id=3D"ce4a6555e9b5">After the curing was finished, I looked at the=
 hopper body and one of the sides (the side that was facing downwards) has =
a lot of sagging issues, so the part is likely unusable.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6f917dc3fb21">GENERAL R&amp;D:</p>
<p local-id=3D"4b7ba227b8cd">Cleaning the Elegoo wash chamber for trying to=
 dissolve the sacrificial filler material out of one of Pourya=E2=80=99s no=
-depowdering green parts.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b5885beb3c81">Replaced the power switch/socket on the Bambu =
X1E. The printer has been having issues with shutting down shortly after a =
high-temperature print is started, which is a known failure mode seen when =
the power switch contacts get worn. After replacing the power switch/socket=
 assembly, I took apart the old power switch and saw significant damage to =
the electrical contact surfaces. Presumably there have been arcing events t=
hat are ablating away the surface of the contacts, which causes them to fai=
l when too much current has been passed through them.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2d5ec5f9c460">I successfully ran a benchy printed in PAHT-CF=
, which came out surprisingly well, even though the PAHT-CF hasn=E2=80=99t =
been dried in a few days.</p>
<p local-id=3D"eeeb5ec77831"></p>
<p local-id=3D"aeca5884e90c">2026-05-01</p>
<p local-id=3D"d65080ca4fcf">3DEO:</p>
<p local-id=3D"1e50cf9c5234">I asked Alex how the board meeting went, and h=
e seemed somewhat equivocal. As Alex said, many of the people at the meetin=
g were Japanese, so they tend not to respond or react in the meeting itself=
; 3DEO management gives a presentation which needs to be translated into sp=
oken Japanese in real time, then the presentation is sent out to all the st=
akeholders, then translated into Japanese, then they will come back with th=
eir interpretation/suggestions. This means that it will take time before we=
 know what their feelings are about the presentation. The focus of this pre=
sentation was the successes of the R&amp;D division, and the major pivot th=
at 3DEO is going through to be a thermal solutions company instead of a com=
ponent manufacturer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"59d144ea7cf7">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"ea14d03b7f39">I demolded three of the gate side seals (the o=
ther three mold cavities did not get fully filled) and they look OK. I was =
unable to demold the wiper seal since the FDM 3D printed mold stuck to the =
urethane; I tried to get mold release into the mold by dousing it with liqu=
id mold release and blowing air into the mold at an angle to try and distri=
bute the mold release throughout the mold, but it does not seem to have wor=
ked. Instead, I need to print a master positive to make a silicone mold, th=
en use that to cast some urethane wipers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"cb31674982c7">I finished designing a positive mold for casti=
ng the silicone mold; it has three thicknesses of urethane wipers so I can =
try different sizes without needing to make more molds. I am currently prin=
ting it on the Bambu X1E (ANVIL) because the print time and print constrain=
ts (6h, needs internal supports) on the FormLabs 3 are restrictive for this=
 part. Not impossible, but I would rather avoid them if possible.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b2cf2fd2c3c1">PILOT:</p>
<p local-id=3D"ee4fda948dca">I discussed some possible approaches for regul=
ating and switching the vacuum on the Pilot printers between spindles; sinc=
e the two spindles are operated separately (one for general part cutting, o=
ne for the facing operation to remove sacrificial filler material left abov=
e the surface of the build) it is only necessary for the vacuum to connect =
to one at a time, and having the vacuum connected to both causes issues due=
 to vacuum loss when one SVP is raised and inability to adjust the flow sep=
arately to optimize the suction for the particular SVP=E2=80=99s needs. To =
regulate the flow, Mohsen bought a Y splitter with a ball valve on each of =
the two outlets, which would make it possible to adjust the vacuum flow ind=
ividually, but has the disadvantage of not being able to switch the vacuum =
flow to each spindle on and off. To have that functionality, the easiest wa=
y would be to add an on/off valve to each line (such as a motorized ball va=
lve or butterfly valve, or a pinch valve on a rubber hose if the ball valve=
 has issues with opening and closing when powder or binder builds up in it)=
. It is also possible to combine the on/off and flow adjustment capabilitie=
s with a proportional ball valve whose position can be controlled with a va=
riable output voltage controlled through the G code.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f48a4a3d2dd6">MOSP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"7e2e07a8c570">I demolded two compliant dovetail mounts cast =
with Urethane Shore 70A, the harder of the two urethanes we have around. We=
 also have a bunch of MOSP sheet metal parts because two orders ended up be=
ing placed from SendCutSend, each of which had two sets to have a spare set=
 if only one order was placed, so there are currently a total of 3 spare se=
ts, and one aluminum dovetail is left over from the original design, which =
was intended to use two aluminum dovetails but ended up using one aluminum =
dovetail and one PETG-CF 3D printed dovetail because the aluminum dovetail =
was A. not designed for the actual spindle spacing seen on the copper Saffr=
on and B. was rigid enough that I was concerned about overconstraining and =
damaging the spindle stages. Even with the 3D printed semi-compliant stage =
that was designed to match the actual spindle spacing, I am still concerned=
 about it damaging the spindle stages. It took a lot of force to install th=
e current assembly, so I am worried that it is putting some side loading on=
 the spindle stage carriages, which could damage them over time.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fc6c5b0ff7dc">Weekly R&amp;D Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"d447c13064be">No Depowdering:</p>
<p local-id=3D"986944fca4ed">Trying to run experiments with printing 17-4 P=
H stainless steel on Pilot 6, but ran into issues with the facing spindle c=
rashing.</p>
<p local-id=3D"55e48bde880a">Switched to InkBird environmental control. Not=
 seeing chipping on prints after switching from Arduino THC to InkBird.</p>
<p local-id=3D"414840d50a13">Reprinted SVP to replace the broken one, but i=
t was the wrong version (2mm shorter than the one being replaced). It was t=
oo short for the 1/8=E2=80=9D diameter facing end mill. A new SVP will need=
 to be printed with modified dimensions to compensate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"72cdb6595b52">Ran experiments to try to improve wall quality=
 by adjusting the end mill stepover distance. There was no variation seen b=
etween experiments.</p>
<p local-id=3D"11ef7b12e983">Ran 1 experiment with the incorrect SVP and 1m=
m stepover for hatching, and the PEG was thrown everywhere.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9be191fcd729">Mohsen looking into modulating vacuum flow wit=
h a valve. His current approach, as detailed above, is a pair of manual bal=
l valves in a Y configuration. The valve was delivered today. He needs to d=
esign and print some adapters to interface the valves to the hoses.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e99d0e6773ea">For copper printing on the Saffron, worked on =
software to generate G code; ran into some issues but should be OK now.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0bbbb31cbf3b">Even with the metal mount installed, they are =
still seeing issues with the XY offset shifting over time.</p>
<p local-id=3D"caa6a4a24718">Question raised of whether or not to switch Pi=
lot 7 over to running copper</p>
<p local-id=3D"645dfc76bd95">Payman recommends continuing to run the copper=
 Saffron with the no-depowdering setup. I raised the questions of whether w=
e want to switch to no-depowdering copper experiments on Saffrons only or o=
n Pilots only, and the answer I got from Payman and Marcus was to keep runn=
ing experiments on both platforms &lt;despite the fact that we are losing t=
he person running the experiments previously, and I am unsure as to whether=
 Pilot will even continue to exist or be replaced with the Saffron printers=
. The Saffron printers are the only one currently shown on our new rebrande=
d website&gt;.</p>
<p local-id=3D"689b8ce70ffa">Metallurgical analysis of a no-depowdering cop=
per print was conducted by Dong, and there was some anomalous porosity seen=
 at the first 10 and last 10 layers, where no hatching was done; the no-dep=
owdering layers seemed to show less porosity.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6eb35da84de6">Laser:</p>
<p local-id=3D"737e5a5e0548">Mason installed the MOPA fiber laser on Pilot =
3 and printed a new LVP for use with copper. Printed 2 10-layer coupons in =
copper with the MOPA laser. Started experiments to determine the binder pen=
etration depth.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d185b804bfaf">Finished informal testing with UV and CO2 lase=
r on copper cakes.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fe5ad4dff504">Plans to continue refining parameters and try =
inerting the printer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e805ee9d64eb">Ran a 9 layer print printing a rectangle in co=
pper, and found the wall surface finish to be ~20 microns vs nominal 6 micr=
ons for our CNC milled green parts.</p>
<p local-id=3D"594d3ce6203f">To measure binder penetration for a layer, he =
would measure the thickness with calipers after curing the layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"06f1b0e3aaa1">Mason asked how the board meeting went. Alex s=
aid it=E2=80=99s hard to say. Half the audience was Japanese, so they will =
need to take time to process the presentation (sorry about the racism!). We=
nt through R&amp;D stuff, commercial stuff, financials, fundraising efforts=
. Talking with two VC companies, including one that funded Alloyed Enterpri=
ses, the other is backed by TSMC.</p>
<p local-id=3D"84e68fed8097"><strong>To Do:</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"baa0aef802b4">
<li local-id=3D"a72ee7c7e75b">
<p local-id=3D"4a0412d8cc00"><strong>Get collets for 1/8=E2=80=9D end mill =
on Saffron spindles to Pourya</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7f980a64e636">
<li local-id=3D"f222e0283b97">
<p local-id=3D"df829645308a">Done, took one from Senai=E2=80=99s desk</p></=
li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"ba533fcb088d">
<p local-id=3D"2ab615ebd32b"><strong>Make sure that Pilot 7 is equipped wit=
h the proper spindle stage and Mest unit mounts</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"7fede83bd28f">
<li local-id=3D"3d1e7542abf0">
<p local-id=3D"ac113c53e3f3">Looking for machined parts I made for mounting=
 three stages and the Mest unit</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"86924da2ee07">
<p local-id=3D"042fac8f7332">Found the sheet metal part and 3D printed part=
 for the three stage setup</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"90b981371e4a">
<p local-id=3D"5a33d2c62cbe">Have the 3 stage mount, which still needs the =
M3 threaded inserts installed</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1b9e84f8726f">
<p local-id=3D"c148b54beddf">Still missing the aluminum Mest dovetail mount=
s. Will need to machine new ones, which should be fairly quick since I alre=
ady have the CNC programs done on the Trak mill.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"fc0054f515d6">
<p local-id=3D"4e118926cfc2"><strong>Install compliant dovetail mount on Sa=
ffron printer, if necessary</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"82ff2dc99ff4">
<li local-id=3D"38c5cc30db30">
<p local-id=3D"0af7cf585021">Compliant dovetail cast, ready to install</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"ce675c55f981">
<p local-id=3D"46fa128cc36b"><strong>Analyze layer quality of spreads with =
metal spreader bar</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"8aac11cc7a4f">
<li local-id=3D"4abc59b86153">
<p local-id=3D"427f7d6525c4">Quality seems OK, still seeing issues with the=
 line on the build where the gate closes</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"c1de830d2569">
<p local-id=3D"ad5e2c30827a"><strong>Get new numbers on overflow waste</str=
ong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"73ce50322a2e">
<p local-id=3D"d0139a48755c"><strong>Install new vibration isolator on hopp=
er V5.1</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"50cbf77ca563">
<li local-id=3D"d0930f565015">
<p local-id=3D"40f2f8f39c88">Vibration isolator cast and post-processed</p>=
</li>
<li local-id=3D"5108bd672e32">
<p local-id=3D"4dfcf7000fc1">Needs 8X M4 heat set inserts to be installed</=
p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"e7863e8c3a3d">
<p local-id=3D"3c6f22c496db"><strong>Run some TRS coupons on Pilot 2 with H=
OPPER V5.1</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"492901164877">
<li local-id=3D"4790280ea3b8">
<p local-id=3D"339daa6192e7">1 print complete to be broken out by Ben, and =
another print started (2026-05-07)</p></li>
