<p local-id=3D"fdf5591a5f7d"></p>
<p local-id=3D"71b36d75a9db">In a discussion with Devin in Jira, he pointed=
 out that we can get more working area on the Saffron printer with the Mest=
 unit installed if the unit is aligned with spindle 7. I had already design=
ed a modified sheet metal bracket to accommodate this, but I had not placed=
 an order on SendCutSend for it. I also had failed to add a slot to access =
the screw on the spindle stage carriage that locks the dovetail to the stag=
e carriage. I added that slot into the design. There are three possible app=
roaches I can take to align the Mest unit with spindle 7:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"75d90925484f">
<li local-id=3D"10a327da8eef">
<p local-id=3D"7e06044fca5a">Order a new bracket from SendCutSend and insta=
ll it when it arrives</p>
<ul local-id=3D"1925d08b33ac">
<li local-id=3D"a6b276217d32">
<p local-id=3D"42f78b80d03c">Best part quality, costs money, takes calendar=
 time</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"50421afe821f">
<p local-id=3D"6ee8407eba61">Make an intermediate bracket to extend the ori=
ginal mount bracket to the side</p>
<ul local-id=3D"71f9d6e68f9b">
<li local-id=3D"8c2962654525">
<p local-id=3D"623d431e09c1">Shifts the Mest unit forward in Y</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b5c0b9fd9e37">
<p local-id=3D"54b5fa216607">Need to machine a slot into the mount bracket<=
/p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"a707d9206ce0">
<p local-id=3D"2af68d5bf03c">Weld the original mount bracket to the U brack=
et, but shifted to the side</p>
<ul local-id=3D"9c2f1e503665">
<li local-id=3D"6e770e01dd7a">
<p local-id=3D"661476f8dc82">Takes time to do</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"cde6a28acf09">
<p local-id=3D"45ef5ecc72c7">Still need to machine a slot into the mount br=
acket</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"45bb8f0526c6">I went ahead and placed an order request for t=
wo of the extended brackets from SendCutSend. If it becomes necessary to ex=
pand the working area quickly I can implement one of the other two solution=
s above, but ordering new brackets is cheap and easy enough to do in prepar=
ation for the most likely eventuality, that we have enough time to wait for=
 the new brackets.</p>
