<p local-id=3D"cf96acf6dc99">2026-05-08</p>
<p local-id=3D"cd714ed9d274">Pourya=E2=80=99s last day. We had a lunch yest=
erday to celebrate Pourya, and Alex talked a bit about the business. He sai=
d that we have money for two paychecks, and since the next paycheck is next=
 week that means that we have 3 weeks of operating capital left. Per Mason =
this morning, it sounds like FusionX is unlikely to give us more funding, s=
o it is down to these two VC companies that Alex has been speaking with. On=
e of them is in the process of discussing investing in 3DEO with their part=
ners, while the other has not gotten to that point yet. It also seems unlik=
ely that Epson or any of the other Japanese investors will invest in 3DEO w=
ithout us bringing in any external funding (I guess they agreed to give us =
some more, but only if we can get someone else to kick in some money to dem=
onstrate that others believe in 3DEO).</p>
<p local-id=3D"3f32e1f7b247">Mason also asked a good question: if we get en=
ough money to operate for 6 more months or a year, will we be able to accom=
plish something, or will we chase our tails as we often have?</p>
<p local-id=3D"100aa9126355">So there definitely is a market for liquid coo=
led heat exchangers for data centers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"fc02c0c5d0ad">Complex internal geometry designs do improve p=
erformance.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e44913e2e9f0">There are several companies making heat exchan=
gers for liquid cooling (JetCool, etc.) and several companies trying to use=
 AM to make heat exchangers for this application (Fabric8Labs, Alloyed Ente=
rprises).</p>
<p local-id=3D"133b7f5180cb">So what can we provide that others can=E2=80=
=99t?</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"52f6ca05273a">
<li local-id=3D"487a67218d10">
<p local-id=3D"a98f873143f7">Complex internal geometry, although this is of=
 questionable importance and the abilities we have here are at risk of beco=
ming less unique over time</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4b4077cba7d9">
<p local-id=3D"68840d5438c9">Single piece enclosed geometry without separat=
e components or joints. This is more important, since it eliminates leak pa=
ths and expensive joint design and manufacturing operations.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3cad1976f1b3">
<p local-id=3D"74a9f5545aa5">Scalability. I think this is the critical diff=
erentiator; our printers are slow individually but our process is optimized=
 for parallelization and simplicity. We can have many printers running in p=
arallel, run large batches of parts through a debinding oven then a sinteri=
ng furnace, then post-machine them onsite (I=E2=80=99m going to be honest f=
rom the start and say that post-machining will be necessary; accepting sint=
ering warpage and post-machining the outside for flatness will be much easi=
er, cheaper, and more reliable than trying to minimize warpage to machining=
 tolerance levels).</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"c62ce09f1b0f">Let=E2=80=99s say we get 6 months of funding. =
What will 3DEO need to look like by the end of the year to be a survivable =
company?</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"47bf6e52defc">
<li local-id=3D"dee28fc24f7e">
<p local-id=3D"369cec5c13fd"><strong>Large, high-volume low-mix contracts o=
f single piece fully enclosed heat exchangers for data center applications<=
/strong></p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6039970bfd4c">
<p local-id=3D"1ba9e9b395df"><strong>All the printers running copper in par=
allel</strong></p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"0d9a78ae11ef">Within 6 more months, all powder waste must be=
 eliminated.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4a6a1913d316"><strong>This is fully dependent on the CleanPr=
int(tm) process working in full scale production.</strong> Without it, we l=
ose the ability to make single piece heat exchangers, and if we can=E2=80=
=99t do that, then we have no advantage over companies that print in pure c=
opper with PBF technologies and braze parts together.</p>
<p local-id=3D"bcaae2dedd2b">HOPPER/FLIP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"74a35988aad9">Continuing to work on the design of hopper V5.=
3 with an active roller spreader bar.</p>
<p local-id=3D"54ef739c8f59">The felt seal on the currently installed V5.1 =
hopper came loose and dragged on one side of the build.</p>
<p local-id=3D"da84d9c469a8">MOSP:</p>
<p local-id=3D"1409b84fd286">Looked at the model of the metal Mest mount in=
stalled in the copper Saffron printer. I think the best approach is to make=
 a new mount that has dovetails that mount to the carriages on two spindles=
 on one side instead of the center two spindles, and design the mount such =
that it does not interfere with the front spindle that the Mest unit=E2=80=
=99s outlet nozzle is in line with in the Y direction. This should maximize=
 the working area of the Mest unit and two spindles (one for regular cuttin=
g, one for facing).</p>
<p local-id=3D"b5bab23c36ec"></p>
