<p local-id=3D"76ecb3627872">COPPER NO-DEPOWDERING:</p>
<p local-id=3D"e34718f29cf4">Last week, Mohsen worked on breaking up the no=
-depowdering process on Pilot 6 printing with 17-4 into different steps to =
understand them independently.</p>
<p local-id=3D"2ef4aca8dad1">Cutting layers - worked fine</p>
<p local-id=3D"e2b832ead23c">Adding filler into channels - filler curled up=
, overfilled which can lead to more debris during facing operation</p>
<p local-id=3D"35c38839712c">Facing - some cracking of cake near to feature=
s, damage to corners of part seen</p>
<p local-id=3D"4285a7dc4b65">Has a flow restrictor on each vacuum line so t=
he flow can be adjusted independently. Even with the feature cutting spindl=
e vacuum line closed and the facing vacuum line fully open, there was still=
 filler debris being thrown around the cake.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d2953c8129c2">Mohsen developed some optimized parameters for=
 end mill extension from the SVPs and vacuum settings (quantified with stat=
ic pressure measurements).</p>
<p local-id=3D"776b78a4ccfa">Marcus raised the idea of adjusting filler app=
lication strategy to fill hatched areas to prevent the filler from distorti=
ng as it cools. Devin also pointed out the length of time that filler is le=
ft to cool in features before the facing operation is started may affect pa=
rt quality.</p>
<p local-id=3D"04fce0de5188">For this week, Marcus wants Mohsen to focus on=
 printing the Epson cold plate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6cc128b41d47">Devin noted that we do have the ability to dou=
ble cut through multiple layers.</p>
<p local-id=3D"52ab312a39c4">Pilot 6 is having issues with the Duet board d=
isconnecting. ZZ changed the SPI communication frequency between Raspberry =
Pi and Duet board.</p>
