s that can be packed onto a Saffron build plate.</p>
<p local-id=3D"366f9d1fd20f">Midhun asked about the impact of thermal condu=
ctivity of the material on the thermal resistance. Sean thinks that his sim=
ulations are based on 400 W/mK, and Midhun and Dong said that we usually ge=
t ~360-380 W/mK &lt;need to double check that exact number, it is at least =
less than pure copper&gt;.</p>
<p local-id=3D"46d66c5a4176">Sean talked about optimizing the design of the=
 heat exchanger. Generally you want high surface area and high flow velocit=
y to maximize heat transfer. &lt;Possible to modify pressure drop with a po=
st-processing process&gt;. A rougher internal surface can improve heat tran=
sfer because it increases turbulence of the boundary layer and increases su=
rface area.</p>
