<p local-id=3D"6e9ac088d1ad">R&amp;D Weekly Meeting:</p>
<p local-id=3D"4649d8e0d9f7">No Depowdering:</p>
<p local-id=3D"727c8f75152f">Mohsen has been running experiments with the M=
est no-depowdering system on Pilot 6. He has switched to using an acrylic b=
ase plate for its reduced thermal conductivity. He added a 180s dwell time =
to allow the PEG to cool before the facing operation. He is seeing cracking=
 in large volumes of PEG used to fill hatches regions and is having issues =
with those same regions of PEG pulling up. He tried doing the facing operat=
ion in multiple passes at varying heights to reduce the likelihood of the P=
EG filler material pulling up, which seemed to help. He also tried slowing =
down the feed rate, which seems to have caused melting and smearing of the =
PEG instead of cutting it cleanly into chips.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e367af32ad4a">Marcus wants to switch away from the Epson hea=
t exchanger geometry that we have been printing in favor of printing a sect=
ion of the microchannel geometry that is present in Sean=E2=80=99s recent d=
esign. The hope is that this geometry will be more successful because it do=
es not have large volumes to fill with sacrificial filler material and does=
 not have tall unsupported pins.</p>
<p local-id=3D"e66a639afb53">A copper print from the Saffron printer is cur=
rently in the dry box.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c31f388c49d5">Midhun is trying to collect knowledge about th=
e no-depowdering process and systems, particularly from Mohsen, Mason, and =
possibly Pourya if we can get him to come in for a bit. Midhun is also goin=
g to get trained up on running the copper Saffron and the Pilot printers.</=
p>
<p local-id=3D"d7e448e74fe2">GENERAL:</p>
<p local-id=3D"17cb8012cdcc">Senai did a print to try and print a wicking s=
tructure with a 100 micron end mill &lt;what gap size is necessary for capi=
llary action?&gt;. Most or all of the end mills broke (at least 3/4) &lt;LO=
C is 300 micron&gt; &lt;feed rate was not updated to maintain the same surf=
ace speed and feed per tooth, the feed used was half of the standard feed r=
ate, which may have been too fast for end mills of this size&gt;. The goal =
is to create parts for two-phase cooling heat exchangers.</p>
