<p local-id=3D"cbdec76572b4">GENERAL:</p>
<p local-id=3D"41101ba27f6b">Senai is working on accelerating the timeline =
of Pilot 8 by reducing the documentation that will be generated in the proc=
ess of building it. I talked with him about whether there is an integrated =
software package that will make it possible to design the electrical and me=
chanical systems in CAD and have those changes propagate automatically to t=
he BOM and also organically feed into build instructions, and he is not awa=
re of any. In theory some of those features are available with various Soli=
dWorks packages (for mechanical CAD the BOM in drawings can be automaticall=
y updated, but that still needs manual population of all the hardware (whic=
h actually doesn=E2=80=99t sound that hard, now that I=E2=80=99m writing it=
 out)).</p>
<p local-id=3D"fb8d77e8982d">One issue is that we have a machine designed i=
n SolidWorks but not fully populated with all necessary components so the B=
OM is incomplete, both due to missing hardware that I left out for the sake=
 of expediency and electrical components that are time consuming to model (=
terminal blocks etc.) or difficult to model (wires, cable harnesses, etc.).=
</p>
<p local-id=3D"bc375ee1c2cf">There is also minimal documentation for assemb=
ly procedures (there are videos somewhere for some of the processes, but ev=
en I have lost track of exactly where they are).</p>
<p local-id=3D"bb2f3d9181cd">And then we have issues with communication of =
information between stakeholders: Ning has information about the electrical=
 system and wiring, I have information about the design and components, Sen=
ai needs to oversee assembly and integration, Cisco needs to do the actual =
assembly, and Adriana needs to do ordering and inventory.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0ebc45a4311d">We need a system that integrates all this info=
rmation to enhance communication but more importantly record everything tha=
t needs to be ordered and how it needs to be assembled without detailed man=
ual intervention (such as needing people to write everything they do down, =
which is too time consuming).</p>
<p local-id=3D"31586fdeedb4"></p>
<p local-id=3D"88cce1cea5ce">Midhun, Mohsen, Dong, and Mason are working on=
 two issues being seen with the Mest dispensers: liquid PEG is building up =
on the nozzle during the print (possibly only some prints?) and dripping on=
 the build, and PEG in the syringe is solidifying and preventing dispensing=
 of the PEG during the print.</p>
<p local-id=3D"f25af2281868">There are some theories as to why this might b=
e occurring:</p>
<p local-id=3D"2352e7880fe4">Nozzle liquid PEG buildup:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"593bd73c80e9">
<li local-id=3D"226aed26dc11">
<p local-id=3D"2672081825f2">Piezo speed or frequency set incorrectly</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"867d7c18703b">
<p local-id=3D"8c866e7d5158">Leakage from faulty o-rings</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b9666964aae1">
<p local-id=3D"1fd65e24fe29">Insufficient air cooling of the piezo system (=
cooled with adjustable compressed air flow)</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"c46c85718c4f">PEG solidifying:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"88e0600be0e4">
