<p local-id=3D"791140593564">Per Alex: Banks in Japan are interested in sup=
porting a reboot of the company built on 3DEO=E2=80=99s IP, focused on vari=
ous thermal applications using the CleanPrint(tm) process. The main value-a=
dd is a fully enclosed high-performance cold plate. Our main stumbling bloc=
k so far is that we have been unable to print a prototype for Japanese comp=
anies to test in-house, which would be valuable for selling to various cust=
omers in Japan. Specific milestone would be a fully enclosed heat exchanger=
 that meets or exceeds the performance of competitors' heat exchangers. As =
secondary goals, the design should be scalable &lt;I am more of the opinion=
 that the overall design should be fully customized for each application in=
stead of built from a series of standardized blocks&gt; and mass-manufactur=
able &lt;this is probably the real value-add of our process if we can get i=
t working&gt;.</p>
<p local-id=3D"b88f793b56b1">Midhun asked about the number of HXs that need=
 to be ready at the end of 90 days, to which Alex responded ~6-12. Midhun a=
lso asked about the required dimensional accuracy &lt;internal dimensions o=
nly matter insofar as the impact the thermal performance, external footprin=
t is somewhat more flexible as long as it fits within the right envelope. M=
ore critical are the flatness of the IC contact face over a range of temper=
atures. Either way, it is all wrapped up in the measured performance of the=
 HX over the target liquid and IC temperatures and flow rate&gt;.</p>
<p local-id=3D"c41bff4e19ae">Per Marcus and Alex, brazing is something that=
