ivergent. He will be here through next week, with next Friday being his las=
t day. This is rather concerning because Marcus was the person who seemed t=
o most believe in the CleanPrint(tm) process. He was also doing most of the=
 high-level coordination of tasks working towards our 30-60-90 plan objecti=
ves. Without him, the most logical replacement is Midhun, although I am not=
 sure how much management and team coordination experience he has, and also=
 whether or not he is interested in that role. Aside from the logistical im=
plications of Marcus leaving, I am unsure why exactly he has chosen to leav=
e. It is possible that it is because he wants something from his role that =
he is not getting here, or that he simply does not believe in the path that=
 the group here is taking, or the technology itself (I can=E2=80=99t say th=
at it is the direction of the company because 3DEO is dissolving and potent=
ially being reformed, but nominally the team should be continuous).</p>
<p local-id=3D"1ffdc4a05760">I talked with Senai about the design of the Be=
ta printers, mainly why they have a linear stage positioning each spindle m=
otor as well as a stage that positions a plate to which all four individual=
