<p local-id=3D"5d38670fe70b">Copper Printing (Dong, Midhun):</p>
<p local-id=3D"b23a37a7c6a1">Tried printing with multilayer sacrificial fil=
ler material filling. Worked on bringing up Pilot 8 and running de-PEG expe=
riments and found that the roof of the parts tended to collapse during the =
cycle. Tried de-PEGing parts with and without drain holes drilled into the =
manifold and found sacrificial filler removal was comparable. Part seems to=
 soften significantly when PEG is melted. When using a hot air gun to melt =
out the sacrificial filler material, it oxidized rapidly but seemed to reta=
in its strength better.</p>
