<p local-id=3D"96573ab00e73">Working on learning more about the math involv=
ed in various heat transfer and thermal resistance calculations. Discussed =
the expected performance of heat exchangers with Sean; for the 20X20 HX he =
expects a thermal resistance of ~0.1 C/W</p>
<p local-id=3D"c6ce6093c383">In setting up the test bench to repeat the pre=
vious 20X20 HX experiment to confirm the results, I found that the pump was=
 not reaching the full 3 LPM flow rate value. I increased the max pump moto=
r frequency from 20 to 23 Hz and it is now able to hit it, with a bit of he=
adroom seen when the flow rate overshoots as the pump is spooling up (this =
happens sometimes due to control system tuning but also because when the sy=
stem is first turned on it takes some time to get liquid circulating throug=
h the flow sensor so it reads the correct value, before which it reads no f=
low regardless of pump speed).</p>
<p local-id=3D"bf9024b80842"></p>
<p local-id=3D"3b54c3ca492c">2026-09-02</p>
<p local-id=3D"1f2c0d36e4ef">Need to design and print a new jig for section=
ing parts on ABSAM.</p>
<p local-id=3D"15d9490a95bd">Designed new jig, and it is currently printing=
 from purple ASA.</p>
<p local-id=3D"a5a8df54c2bc">Did some research on ways we might be able to =
sinter copper parts here for some basic testing.</p>
<p local-id=3D"609b07dc07df">In sectioning the parts with Dong yesterday, t=
he automated bandsaw dumped a lot of coolant onto the floor. I think that c=
an mostly be prevented by leveling the machine properly, but it shows a pro=
blem with the original design; I designed it with a fixed base plate like t=
he standard vertical band saw work surface and mounted the stages to that b=
ase plate. This architecture made more sense with the original design that =
needed various trays and chutes mounted in fixed positions, but even then i=
t had the issue that flood coolant would pool on the plate and flow over th=
e edge, and if the plate is tilted such that the rear edges are lower, the =
coolant will flow beyond the catch extensions that I added to the bandsaw t=
o catch dripping coolant. With the current goal being sectioning parts, it =
would make more sense to make a small, fully enclosed desktop machine with =
a small bandsaw. Alternatively, it would make even more sense to make or bu=
y a purpose-built sectioning saw (typically those use a rotating circular b=
lade instead of a bandsaw to get a cleaner and more repeatable cut).</p>
<p local-id=3D"c5642169cc03">Discussed the design of the stonevac to thread=
ed selector valve adapter with Cisco, and he pointed out that the fit seems=
 a little loose, so I have increased the diameter slightly and I am reprint=
ing two of the updated design from ColorFabb XT blue filament on the Bambu =
P2S. I also engraved the name of the part file into the part to be printed;=
 I think that should be a standard moving forward so that it is possible to=
 track down the original CAD file(s) of the part if (when) it needs to be r=
eprinted.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0d0af6e9085b">HEALTH:</p>
<p local-id=3D"1e4048756d67">Submitted an order request through the new Rei=
ka form for the reference cold plate and chassis resistor.</p>
<p local-id=3D"28047d6e0307">The test I conducted yesterday on the test ben=
ch with the dmc1 20X20mm HX had very similar results as the test I ran the =
day before, which is promising. At least the results are repeatable, even i=
f I do somewhat mistrust their accuracy.</p>
<p local-id=3D"4add6f526bd7">Repeated the same test with the HX clamped dow=
n tightly with M3 bolts instead of compressed by the springs as before; the=
 3D printed clamping part cracked where layers were pulled apart near the b=
olt mounting points, but there was no significant difference from the previ=
ous tests.</p>
