<p local-id=3D"f6ef98593901">Mohsen is seeing variation with dispensing par=
affin. Over the print, the amount of sacrificial filler material dispensed =
increases, resulting in excess overfilling. Since paraffin is being used, i=
t is currently impossible to machine the excess paraffin cleanly.</p>
<p local-id=3D"6725f4db0fb5">I suggested that we could sidestep this proble=
m with a filler material change to one that is more machinable, which seeme=
d to be accepted by Alex and possible by Midhun, however, there did not see=
m to be much interest in changing/exploring materials in the near term. I w=
ould like to use a paraffin/polymer blend to make one that is:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"6bdcde90ea2b">
<li local-id=3D"e9b94dc76129">
<p local-id=3D"5ac1113ceb73">Machinable</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"77bac9101363">
<p local-id=3D"6dfdffff9cac">Stable when held above its melting point for u=
p to 2 weeks</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b51c5b66ba93">
<p local-id=3D"9978ee2a78ff">Interaction with our green parts is favorable<=
/p>
<ul local-id=3D"7a810e28e824">
<li local-id=3D"809717e78bdd">
<p local-id=3D"b9c5b626e5eb">Does not excessively soak into part</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"430e79b672bb">
<p local-id=3D"1591b35f0622">Does not impede part binding during print or d=
ebind and sintering</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"91683ee9b820">
<p local-id=3D"099f3030681e">I would like it to act as a binder to strength=
 the part as well</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"5749ec72a456">
<p local-id=3D"3c5a9ebbb567">Burns out cleanly with no residue in debind (c=
opper is highly sensitive to contamination)</p></li>
</ul>
