<p local-id=3D"92b8ad537afe"></p>
<p local-id=3D"eb20f8b1094a"></p>
<p local-id=3D"6f72c12c9a12">HEALTH:</p>
<p local-id=3D"b66c0c9e4040">I am working on machining the copper heat flux=
 measurement blocks. I am also curious about rerunning the test procedure o=
n the Dracaena cold plate that I bought a while back; now that the coolant =
temperatures are more stable because they are reporting a smaller range of =
values giving better resolution, I would like to repeat the current best te=
st procedure and see how well it works. I am also interested in benchmarkin=
g the cold plates that Ning brought in.</p>
<p local-id=3D"288b6a11e1cc">I have one blank faced on two sides so it is a=
 3=E2=80=9DX3=E2=80=9DX1=E2=80=9D block, where I will leave it unless it is=
 needed. The other blank was faced to the same dimensions, then on the larg=
e faces was milled until the thickness was 24mm. I then drilled 4X holes at=
 the corners matching the hole pattern of the Ohmite chassis resistor that =
I plan to use as the heat source.</p>
<p local-id=3D"04b45166c4cf">I received the two XTP series compression-moun=
t RTD temperature sensor/transmitters that I plan to use for measuring the =
two block temperature points.</p>
<p local-id=3D"13226f3b9daa"></p>
<p local-id=3D"976f0b2b997d">2026-09-16</p>
<p local-id=3D"df5ded5a7942">HEALTH:</p>
<p local-id=3D"07d02bd5e642">Talked with Midhun about possible errors intro=
duced from the lines and fittings on the heat exchanger test bench. I ran a=
 test with a low pressure drop shunt in place of the cold plate to generate=
 an equation for pressure drop compensation at various flow rates, and appl=
ied that to the results collected from the 20X20mm cold plate:</p><span cla=
ss=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embe=
dded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=
